notes={{t="You wake in a crypt. Undertaker Mordo stands just outside its exit.",tp=1},{t="Venya Marthand is inside the Deathknell church.",w=1},{t="Water is 25 copper for 5. Sell your zombie loot here to pay for it.",tp=1},{t="Joshua Kien is inside the building east of the church.",w=1},{t="You start with no money. Sell some loot to Joshua Kien, then come back for Arcane Intellect.",tp=1},{t="Immolate costs a little, and you start broke. Sell some loot to Joshua Kien before you train.",tp=1},{t="Shadow Priest Sarvis is inside the Deathknell church.",w=1},{t="Archibald Kava is inside the building east of the church.",w=1},{t="New characters have no coin. Sell a bit of loot to Archibald Kava, then train Battle Shout.",tp=1},{t="Dannal Stern stands in the building east of the church, at its far end.",w=1},{t="Joshua Kien is inside the building east of the church.",w=1},{t="Mangy Duskbats (level 3-4) drop wings too, but the level 1-2 Duskbats die much faster.",tp=1},{t="Aramis Hammerhand is inside the Deathknell church.",w=1},{t="Dannal Stern stands in the building east of the church, at its far end.",w=1},{t="David Trias is inside the building east of the church.",w=1},{t="Joshua Kien is inside the building east of the church.",w=1},{t="Aramis Hammerhand is inside the Deathknell church.",w=1},{t="Archibald Kava is inside the building east of the church.",w=1},{t="Dannal Stern stands in the building east of the church, at its far end.",w=1},{t="Young Night Web Spiders sit near the cave mouth. The full-grown ones are deeper in.",tp=1},{t="The Night Web Matriarch, level 5, sits in the cave's north end. Keep her out of your pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Joshua Kien is inside the building east of the church.",w=1},{t="Leave Meven Korgal alone for now. He's the target of The Red Messenger, offered after this turn-in.",tp=1},{t="Scarlet Initiates cast Frost Armor, which slows your attacks and movement when you hit them.",tp=1},{t="Archibald Kava is inside the building east of the church.",w=1},{t="Gordo is an abomination who walks the road toward Brill. Look along the road for him.",tp=1},{t="Deathguard Bartholomew walks around the Brill graveyard, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Innkeeper Renee is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Dark Cleric Beryl is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is indoors, in the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Dry Branches lie at the foot of the trees around Brill.",tp=1},{t="Sit by Eleanor's campfire with /sit. Boosted Rest shows after about a minute.",tp=1},{t="No credit after sitting? Abandon the quest, take it again from Eleanor and sit back down.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Priests: keep your Linen Cloth. Tailored greens disenchant into the essence a Lesser Magic Wand needs.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Use the Executor's Motivator on Deathguards in and near Brill. Any five will do.",u=286176},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Each report comes from a dialogue option when you talk to Kristof, Dillinger and Gordo.",tp=1},{t="Dark Cleric Beryl is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Cain Firesong is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Austil de Mon is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Marion Call is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Rupert Boch is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="This needs Lesser Heal (Rank 2). If you skipped it at level 4, Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill teaches it.",tp=1},{t="Cursed Darkhounds roam among the ones you need, and they're higher level. Look around before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Hostile Tirisfal Farmers and Farmhands (5-7) work the pumpkin rows, with Farmer Solliden, a level 8 rare.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="When a Scarlet Warrior drops into a defensive stance, it parries much more for a few seconds. Save big hits.",tp=1},{t="Three Scarlet Warriors stand together on the tower's top floor. Expect all three if you pull one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bareth Dawnstone is on the top floor. Once you accept, stay with him until he's clear of the outpost.",w=1},{t="Bareth Dawnstone not here? Another player has taken this quest. Bareth Dawnstone is back a few minutes after they finish, so wait nearby.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Dark Cleric Beryl is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Deathguard Burgess is inside the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="The Maggot Eye poster is inside the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Dark Cleric Beryl is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Coleman Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="The Captured Scarlet Zealot is in the tavern cellar, toward the back.",w=1},{t="Gretchen Dedmar is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Use the Executor's Motivator on Deathguards in and near Brill. Any five will do.",u=286176},{t="You can destroy the Executor's Motivator once Discipline is handed in.",tp=1},{t="Junior Apothecary Holland walks a loop around the Brill graveyard.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Make bandages in dead time, like waiting for a zeppelin.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only if you have it in your bags.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Coleman Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Doom Weed grows at the foot of trees in the Rot Hide gnoll camps.",tp=1},{t="Only Vile Fin Muckdwellers and Minor Oracles drop the skins. Puddlejumpers never do.",tp=1},{t="Duskbat Pelts don't drop from every bat. Plan on more kills than the five you need.",tp=1},{t="Junior Apothecary Holland walks a loop around the Brill graveyard.",tp=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is indoors, in the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Gretchen Dedmar is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Keep the Slumber Sand from this quest for the day a pull goes wrong.",tp=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is indoors, in the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Ageron Kargal is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Rupert Boch is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Marion Call is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Cain Firesong teaches from the Brill inn's upper floor.",w=1},{t="Cain Firesong is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Austil de Mon is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Priests, Warlocks: Enchanting makes a Lesser Magic Wand from Simple Wood and one Lesser Magic Essence.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ulag the Cleaver is level 11 and hits hard. Call him at full health with food ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Coleman Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Carendin Halgar is in the Magic Quarter.",w=1},{t="Anastasia Hartwell is in the Magic Quarter.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Warriors, Rogues: keep some Rough Stone. Blacksmithing turns it into sharpening stones, +2 damage for 30 minutes.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Perrine's Chest sits on the ground right beside Captain Perrine.",w=1},{t="Deathguard Burgess is inside the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Necrotic Crystal Fragments also lie loose on the ground. Pick those up between kills.",tp=1},{t="Dark Enforcers (level 10-12) hit hard and have an instant strike. Neophytes hit hard too. Fight at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stand on the Summoning Circle, then use the Runes of Summoning to call the Voidwalker.",u=6284},{t="Tomb Weed grows among Bleeding Horrors and Wandering Spirits, levels 9 to 11. Watch for adds by each plant.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gunther's Books sit next to Gunther Arcanus on his island out in Brightwater Lake. Swim across.",w=1},{t="Anastasia Hartwell is in the Magic Quarter.",w=1},{t="Gunther Arcanus stands on his island out in Brightwater Lake. Swim across to him.",w=1},{t="Lillith's Dinner Table is on the smaller island, south-west of Gunther's.",w=1},{t="Lillith Nefara is level 12. Light the candle at full health and mana.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Captain Vachon is inside the Scarlet tower.",w=1},{t="Scarlet Friars cast Lesser Heal on themselves and their friends. Kill them first.",tp=1},{t="Priests, Warlocks: keep this camp's Linen Cloth, the last good source before Silverpine. The wand plan takes about 60.",tp=1},{t="Riptear, a level 13 elite, wanders the west end of Venomweb Vale. Keep to the spiders on its east and south side, and watch for it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Captured Mountaineer is in the inn cellar, in the same room as the Zealot.",w=1},{t="Junior Apothecary Holland walks a loop around the Brill graveyard.",tp=1},{t="Leonid Barthalomew is on the upper floor of Bandarion Keep.",w=1},{t="Stay by Leonid while he and Danitha Morr talk. The quest completes when they finish.",tp=1},{t="Hilda the Breaker stands outside, south of the keep.",w=1},{t="Ephram Barbaro stands outside, west of the keep.",w=1},{t="Hilda the Breaker stands outside, south of the keep.",w=1},{t="Ander Solliden walks the road south of the keep. Look along it if he isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Jorin Croge is inside Bandarion Keep.",w=1},{t="Danitha Morr is upstairs in Bandarion Keep.",w=1},{t="Jorin Croge is inside Bandarion Keep.",w=1},{t="Rudolph Gelhardt is upstairs in his building.",w=1},{t="The Whispering Horror haunts the north end of the Shadowvale Crypt.",w=1},{t="The Whispering Horror in the crypt's north room is an elite of 11 to 13 that hits hard. Bring a partner, or leave it: nothing else needs it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Its drop starts a quest. Pick it up if you come across it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Whispering Horror drops the Residue that starts this quest.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 2 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Glowing Crystal Fragment lies at the far south end of the Shadowvale Crypt.",w=1},{t="The bones come from the level 9-10 Lurchers and Mystics in the crypt's south half.",tp=1},{t="Bottles of Whispering Elixir lie about the Shadowvale crypt, some on the floor, some up on its walls.",w=1},{t="The Lumber Piles lie on the floor of the Shadowvale Crypt.",w=1},{t="Jorin Croge is inside Bandarion Keep.",w=1},{t="Any undead at Agamand Mills can drop the letter. Loot every kill there.",tp=1},{t="Nissa Agamand sometimes stands inside the building. Check indoors if she isn't out front.",w=1},{t="Thurman and Gregor Agamand wander around the Mills instead of standing still. Look about for them.",tp=1},{t="Cracked Skull Soldiers in the Mills are level 9 and packed close. Start in the fields to the south and pull singly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Coleman Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Yvette Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is indoors, in the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Dark Cleric Beryl is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Cain Firesong is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Austil de Mon is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Marion Call is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Rupert Boch is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Captain Melrache and his bodyguards are inside the tower.",w=1},{t="Melrache (level 12) and both Scarlet Bodyguards stand side by side. Expect all three at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The drop from Agamand Mills toward Garren's Haunt is steep enough to hurt. Zigzag down.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The crypt's Ancestors respawn fast. Rooms you cleared can fill again behind you, so don't linger.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Captain Dargol, level 13, waits on the crypt's lowest level. Clear the Ancestors in his room first.",w=1},{t="The four weapon racks are on the floor inside the Agamand family crypt.",w=1},{t="Rotting and Wailing Ancestors (levels 9 to 11) fill the crypt and respawn fast. Loot each rack and keep moving.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Magistrate Sevren is indoors, in the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Coleman Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Danitha Morr is upstairs in Bandarion Keep.",w=1},{t="Hold on to 10 Linen Cloth. Tanis Alderwood's quest after this one asks for them.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 2 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Danitha Morr is upstairs in Bandarion Keep.",w=1},{t="Raise Deathguard Falgan with the Symbol of Life from your bags, then talk to him.",u=6866},{t="Danitha Morr is upstairs in Bandarion Keep.",w=1},{t="Astor Hadren walks the road between The Sepulcher and Brill. Check along it if he isn't here.",tp=1},{t="Andron's Bookshelf stands right behind Andron Gant.",w=1},{t="Deathstalker Erland isn't always at his post. If he's gone, wait for him to come back.",tp=1},{t="Deathstalker Erland not here? Another player has taken this quest. Deathstalker Erland is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Worgs ambush the escort, sometimes several on the same spot. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Eat and drink in each lull between worg attacks.",tp=1},{t="Vile Fin Shredders and Tidehunters on the shore east of here drop Murloc Eyes. Keep 3 for Quinn's Wild Eyes.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) has been seen on the road at the north end of this loop. Keep clear of it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dusty Spellbooks lie upstairs in the house at Valgan's Field. The Remedy of Arugal is in them.",w=1},{t="Quinn Yorick is upstairs in the house at the Ivar Patch.",w=1},{t="Fear doesn't work on the Rot Hide gnolls here.",tp=1},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 25 elite) roams from The Dead Field south to the Moonrage gnolls. Give it a wide berth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) can wander through here. Watch for it and keep clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krethis Shadowspinner (level 15 rare) shields herself and shocks hard. Nothing here needs her, so leave her alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Buy the Wise Man's Belt here, about 14 silver. You can wear it from level 15.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Moonrage Darksouls (level 13-14) enrage when they get low. Keep a cooldown for the end of the fight.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) has been seen among the Moonrage here. Look around before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Quinn Yorick is upstairs in the house at the Ivar Patch.",w=1},{t="Ivar the Foul waits in the barn with two Ravenclaw Slaves. One walks out on a short patrol, so pull it alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ravenclaw Slaves can't be feared.",tp=1},{t="Clear the mobs standing in front of the barn before you go in.",tp=1},{t="Hands of Ravenclaw (up to level 16) stand around the ferry dock and stun melee for 5 seconds. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Corpse Laden Boat is tied up alongside the ferry dock. Click it.",w=1},{t="Dalaran Apprentices (level 13-14) guard the crate. They cast Frostbolt and run when hurt.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Draw the apprentices away one at a time, then open the crate.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 5 minutes. Walk straight to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium, across the slime canal."},{t="Doctor Martin Felben is in the Apothecarium, over the slime canal.",w=1},{t="Master Apothecary Faranell is in the Apothecarium, with Apothecary Zinge beside him.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Grimson the Pale is inside the Deep Elem Mine, past its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine is full of Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls (13-14). Clear the way in one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Moonrage Bloodhowlers (15-16) stand with Darksouls at the mine's mouth. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dalaran Conjurors and Warders (16-18) hold Ambermill's east end. Keep to the Protectors and Mages west of them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Apothecary Berard is upstairs in Pyrewood's inn. The journal is in Berard's Bookshelf beside him.",w=1},{t="Berard is a level 16 elite, and every villager around him is an elite too. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Deathstalker Faerleia waits inside Pyrewood's chapel.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The council is eight elite councilmen and Lord Mayor Morrison, a level 15 elite. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Pyrewood villager is an elite of 14-15. Take them on with a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="In Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium, use the Cantation of Manifestation to reveal the Rift Spawns.",u=7308},{t="Once a Rift Spawn is stunned, use the Chest of Containment Coffers on it and loot the coffer. Three in all.",u=7247},{t="Vile Fin Lakestalkers and Oracles of 18 to 19 walk the lake shore south-east of here. Leave them be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Outside the keep the Rot Hides are 16 to 18, inside 18 to 19 with Thule Ravenclaw (24 elite), and Snarlmane, a level 23 rare, roams the island. Pull one at a time at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shallow Grave is just east of Fenris Keep's walls.",w=1},{t="Dalaran Conjurors and Warders (16-18) hold Ambermill's east end. Keep to the Protectors and Mages west of them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Josef Gregorian is in the tailor shop in the Magic Quarter.",w=1},{t="Mennet Carkad is in the Rogues' Quarter, near the rogue trainers.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Ruins of Lordaeron, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Thork and Darsok Swiftdagger stand at the top of the Crossroads tower.",w=1},{t="The keg spawns in several spots across the Barrens. If it isn't here, grab it when you pass another.",tp=1},{t="Thork is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="The supply crates spawn in several places, so one may not be where the arrow points.",tp=1},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Root Samples come from gathering Barrens herbs: Peacebloom, Silverleaf, Earthroot, Mageroyal, Briarthorn, Bruiseweed.",tp=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Baron Longshore can be at any of the Southsea camps. Check each one.",tp=1},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Thork is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="The Bubbling Fissure is underwater in the pool. Dive down to it.",w=1},{t="Barak Kodobane hits very hard, and the Kolkar Wrangler at his side nets you and shoots from range.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Warriors, Paladins: Vrang Wildgore also sells the Heavy Spiked Mace, a level 14 two-hander, in limited stock.",tp=1},{t="Two of the valves call out Venture Co. guards when shut, two for one and one for the other. Start each at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Tinkerer Sniggles is inside the building northeast of the control console.",w=1},{t="Darsok Swiftdagger is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="Chol'aruk is built for a group of five. Don't take him on alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Thatog is on the upper floor of his building.",w=1},{t="Whuut's the Rush can take about 10 seconds to show up on Yelmak. Give it a moment.",tp=1},{t="Zor Lonetree is inside Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="Migi is out behind Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="Thra paces behind Grommash Hold and may not be right at the arrow.",w=1},{t="The Smooth Boulders are few and slow to respawn, so other players can make this drag.",tp=1},{t="The Smooth Boulders are small orange rocks lying on the ground.",w=1},{t="The Cats Eye Emerald is a rare drop. It can take 25 kills or more.",tp=1},{t="Boulder Lode Mine mobs stand close enough to pull in pairs, and the tunnels leave little room to run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Work the camp outside the mine entrance. Stay out of the tunnels.",w=1},{t="If the shredder isn't here, someone is on The Escape with it, and it's slow to come back.",tp=1},{t="Venture Co. goblins here are 14 to 18, and a few Lookouts and Patrollers of 22 to 23 stand just north-west. Pull one at a time and keep away from those.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supervisor Lugwizzle paces the platform, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Two level 19 rares, Foreman Grills and Sludge Beast, can be up around The Sludge Fen.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The escort starts the moment you accept. Rest to full first.",tp=1},{t="Wizzlecrank's Shredder not here? Another player has taken this quest. Wizzlecrank's Shredder is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Two Venture Co. Mercenaries jump in when the shredder reaches the high ground.",tp=1},{t="The quest completes after the shredder's closing lines, so stay until it's done talking.",tp=1},{t="If he doesn't show or another player tags him, abandon the quest and take it again from Sergra for a new horn.",tp=1},{t="Blow the Horn of Echeyakee at his lair to call him out.",u=10327},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws in the north run up to level 18 and use Thrash. Take your heads from Lashtails and Screechers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Takk the Leaper, a rare level 19 elite raptor, can spawn just east of the Sludge Fen. Leave him be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Witchwing Slayers cast Execute, a heavy hit once you're under 20% health. Keep your health up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Witchwing Ambushers patrol in stealth, so one can join a fight without warning.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Darsok Swiftdagger is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="When Polly the parrot attacks, give her the E.C.A.C. from your bags.",u=7970},{t="The Jewel of the Southsea is on the ship's bottom deck. Opening it takes Lockpicking 70.",w=1},{t="Raise Lockpicking to 70 on the ship's second deck before you go down.",tp=1},{t="The Bubbling Fissure is underwater, on the lakebed in the middle of the oasis.",w=1},{t="Each Kolkar killed at the oasis can bring out Verog. When it's crowded, wait at his spawn point.",tp=1},{t="Laden Mushrooms grow at The Forgotten Pools and at The Stagnant Oasis.",tp=1},{t="Each nest (blue, red and yellow) takes one Sunscale Feather, which the Scytheclaws drop.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws are level 16-18 and Thrash for two extra hits. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Beaten Corpse lies on the ground at a small outpost beside the road south of the Crossroads.",w=1},{t="Mangletooth's Spirit of the Wind costs 10 Blood Shards and speeds you up for 5 minutes.",tp=1},{t="The Grimtotem camp is up a trail that climbs to a bonfire.",tp=1},{t="Kill all six Brutes before you talk to Kaya, so none are left to join her escort.",tp=1},{t="Grundig Darkcloud stands in front of the camp's main tent.",w=1},{t="Kaya Flathoof is indoors, next to Grundig Darkcloud's spot.",w=1},{t="Kaya Flathoof not here? Another player has taken this quest. Kaya Flathoof is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Three Grimtotems attack when Kaya reaches the bonfire. Start the escort at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stay right beside Kaya the whole way.",tp=1},{t="Xen'Zilla is inside a hut at Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Mor'rogal and Tsunaman stand together, up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks is in a small goblin hut, tucked behind a hill.",w=1},{t="Deepmoss Hatchlings can call a level 22 Deepmoss Matriarch into the fight. Kill them fast, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Deepmoss Eggs lie on the ground beside the trees.",w=1},{t="If you have First Aid, keep the Small Venom Sacs for Anti-Venom.",tp=1},{t="Venture Co. Operators are level 19-20. Pull them on their own, away from the Loggers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bristleback Geomancers are level 19-20, the toughest here. Take them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keep the Blood Shards the quilboars drop. Mangletooth at Camp Taurajo trades them for buffs.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws cast Thrash, two extra hits about every 10 seconds. Fight them at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Oasis Snapjaws are in the water as well as on the shore.",tp=1},{t="Humar the Pridelord, a rare level 23 elite lion, can be up among the lions north of Ratchet.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Zhevra drop the Fresh Zhevra Carcass that draws Ishamuhale out. It spoils 30 minutes after you loot it.",tp=1},{t="By the dead tree, use the Fresh Zhevra Carcass. Ishamuhale comes out to eat it.",u=10338},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Grazlix's Mighty Chain Pants are limited stock and a solid leg upgrade.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 45 minutes. The route takes it to Zamah in Thunder Bluff straight away."},{t="Apothecary Zamah is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Clarice Foster is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Miles Welsh is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ruga Ragetotem is inside a building at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Kill Lakota'mani for the Hoof of Lakota'mani, which starts this quest. He has four spawn points.",tp=1},{t="Lakota'mani is level 22, a hard fight at this point. Pull him only at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Hezrul Bloodmark walks a loop round the lake, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Warlord Krom'zar is a level 20 elite and brings two or more Kolkar. Do this one in a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krom'zar is slow to arrive. Give it as much as 3 minutes.",tp=1},{t="You can lead Krom'zar in circles round Regthar Deathgate's building while you attack from range.",tp=1},{t="His banner falls to the ground when he dies. Loot that for the Piece of Krom'zar's Banner.",tp=1},{t="Serena is level 20 and stands among Witchwing Slayers and Windcallers. Clear round her before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Other players hunt the Savannah Patriarchs too, so expect to wait on respawns.",tp=1},{t="Walton's camp is up on the ridge above the Dry Hills. The trail climbs from the south-east.",w=1},{t="Mobs at the wrecked caravan stand close together. A pull often brings two or three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Terry Longdrink's marines attack after about a minute of talk. Wait behind the house so they don't all pull at once.",tp=1},{t="Vrang Wildgore fights at Walton's side, so Walton survives without your help.",tp=1},{t="Seereth talks for a few seconds after this hand-in. The Elder Crone and Shredding Machines show up once he's done.",tp=1},{t="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is inside his cave at the top of Malaka'jin, up the left-hand path.",w=1},{t="Xen'Zilla is inside a hut at Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Mobs in the Boulderslide Ravine cave hit harder than their level and pull together easily.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gogger Rock Keepers' Earth Shock hits very hard. Kill them first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Everything is in the ravine's north cave. The explore credit comes only well inside it.",tp=1},{t="You get Resonite Crystals by attacking the crystals in the cave.",tp=1},{t="Goggeroc, a level 20 elite, waits deeper in the cave than the explore point. Don't go further than you need.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Mor'rogal and Tsunaman stand together, up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="About 50 troggs of 16 to 18 fill the cave, and Goggeroc is a level 20 elite. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Enchanted Resonite Crystal on the Resonite Cask to call Goggeroc.",u=16603},{t="Mor'rogal stands up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks stands at a small goblin hut tucked behind a hill.",w=1},{t="Piznik is inside the Windshear Mine, west of its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine holds about 60 kobolds of 20 to 23, Geomancers among them. Clear a path in and out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kobolds hit Piznik in three waves over 5 minutes, up to four at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The waves land at about 0:15, 2:15 and 3:20, the second with two casters. Eat and drink in the gaps.",tp=1},{t="Ursangous, a strong level 25 mob, patrols the stag and bear grounds. Watch for him between pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Eye of Kilrogg follows you north-west to the main road. Talk to it there to hand in.",tp=1},{t="Mitsuwa and Marukai are inside a hut at Zoram'gar.",w=1},{t="Marukai is inside the hut at Zoram'gar, beside Mitsuwa.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magatha has a short scene after The Elder Crone. Forsaken Aid comes up once it ends.",tp=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Chol'aruk is inside a cave in the Razormane hills east of the Crossroads.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Bruuz is a level 20 elite in the water off Ratchet, hard for one player.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lead Bruuz to Ratchet's guards and they attack him. You need half his damage for the kill to count.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Northwatch Hold is packed with Theramore Marines and Preservers. Work in from the edge, one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gilthares Firebough not here? Another player has taken this quest. Gilthares Firebough is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Gilthares walks you up the coast past the Southsea camps to Ratchet. Stay close to him.",tp=1},{t="Aean Swiftriver, a level 26 rare elite, can be up among the mounds. Keep well clear of him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Twitching Antennae expire 15 minutes after you loot them. Get them in one go and head straight back.",tp=1},{t="Ruga Ragetotem is inside a building at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Dogran's Pendant calls the succubus at the Summoning Circle. Use it there, then kill her.",u=6626},{t="The Summoning Circle is inside a building a short walk south of Gan'rul.",w=1},{t="Taskmaster Fizzule is a level 30 elite and attacks anyone close before he turns friendly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="From well away, target Fizzule, fire the Flare Gun twice, then type /salute. Talk to him once he's friendly.",u=8051},{t="Every Drone, Patroller and Lookout you need is inside the Venture Co. tower north of the Sludge Fen.",tp=1},{t="Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix, a level 23 elite, waits on the tower's top floor.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Open on Gallywix with Ambush for about half his health. Gouge him when you need energy back.",tp=1},{t="Keep Evasion, Thistle Tea and a healing potion for when the fight goes wrong.",tp=1},{t="Use the Samophlange Manual Cover once you hold the five pages.",u=11147},{t="Boss Copperplug, who drops the cover, is at the back of the Boulder Lode Mine.",w=1},{t="Open the Bundle of Reports in your bags to get the three Warsong Reports.",u=16783},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Instant Poison II needs 120 Poisons skill before Ormok can teach it.",tp=1},{t="Anti-Venom removes Touch of Zanzil. Left alone, it lasts 7 days.",tp=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is inside the town hall in Brill.",w=1},{t="Ride the lift down. Raleigh Andrean stands near the foot of the lifts.",w=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is down in the Sepulcher's crypt.",w=1},{t="Yuriv's Tomb lies flat on the ground beside the Sepulcher, so it's easy to walk past.",tp=1},{t="The Charred Remains lie on Fenris Isle, well south of the keep.",w=1},{t="Lumina Windsinger is caged deep inside Fenris Keep, at the north end of the isle.",w=1},{t="Thule Ravenclaw, a level 24 elite, and two rare gnolls (22 and 23) share Fenris Keep. Pull the gnolls out singly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lumina walks out of the keep with you; stay with her until she's safe."},{t="Lumina Windsinger not here? Another player has taken this quest. Lumina Windsinger is back a few minutes after they finish, so wait nearby.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Lumina walks south out of Fenris Keep and down Fenris Isle. Stay close and fight off what attacks her.",w=1},{t="Archmage Ataeric is inside Ambermill's town hall.",w=1},{t="Ataeric's hall is crowded with Dalaran casters. Draw them to the door a few at a time before you take him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Offering Stone stands deep in the cave, at its far end.",w=1},{t="Offering the soul at the stone spawns a hostile Tortured Soul. Clear the mobs around the stone first.",tp=1},{t="Stand at the Offering Stone and use the Tortured Soul from your bags.",u=210713},{t="Valdred Moray walks a patrol among packs of refugees. Wait until he's clear of them, then pull him alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The yeti cave north of the fields holds yetis of 30 to 32. Stay on the road.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Serge Hinott not here? Another player has taken this quest. Serge Hinott is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Hinott needs about half a minute to brew the cure. Wait beside him.",tp=1},{t="Use Hinott's Oil from your bags to wash off Touch of Zanzil.",u=8095},{t="Ott sometimes has the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-hander with +12 Strength.",tp=1},{t="Jailor Marlgen carries the Burnished Gold Key for Tog'thar's lock. He stands by Tog'thar or below the tower.",tp=1},{t="Kris Legace sometimes has Stalking Pants and Wolf Bracers, leather for your legs and wrists.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Jailor Eston carries the Dull Iron Key for Drull's lock. He stands outside Tog'thar's barracks or beside Drull.",tp=1},{t="The tower a short way southwest of Durnholde Keep has more Shadow Mages, plus Syndicate Rogues and Watchmen.",tp=1},{t="Hillsbrad Farmers disarm you, which hurts melee most. Pull them one at a time.",tp=1},{t="Farmer Getz turns up in his house, his barn or out in the field.",w=1},{t="Farmer Ray is under the grapevine or inside his house, on either floor.",w=1},{t="Hunt the Starving Mountain Lions of the fields. The lions to the south-east and up in Alterac are 27 to 34.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="After a short scene Stanley turns into Enraged Stanley and attacks. Hand this in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stanley is at Farmer Ray's farm, at the north end of the fields.",w=1},{t="The farmers, farmhands, peasants and footmen of the fields all drop skulls. No need to go down to the mine.",tp=1},{t="Elder Gray Bears (25-26) and Elder Moss Creepers (26-27) outlevel the rest here. Leave them alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Giant Moss Creepers, 24 to 25, drop Creeper Ichor as well.",tp=1},{t="Masoj is out among level 26 to 28 lions, moss creepers and gnolls. Go in slowly and pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="We don't know yet which peaks the three Apothecary Vials go on. If you place them, tell us where each one is.",a=1},{t="It sends you up three peaks around Hillsbrad. A long climb for its XP.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It sends you up three peaks around Hillsbrad. A long climb for its XP.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) can wander through here. Watch for it and keep clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shallow Grave is just east of Fenris Keep's walls.",w=1},{t="Thule Ravenclaw waits in a large hall inside Fenris Keep.",w=1},{t="Thule is a level 24 elite who calls a minion back and hexes you. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dusty Shelf is in the keep's north-west tower. Turn left at the top of the first stairs.",w=1},{t="Fenris Keep is full of Rot Hides of 18-19, with Thule Ravenclaw (24 elite) among them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is down in the Sepulcher's crypt.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Raleigh Andrean stands near the foot of the lifts.",w=1},{t="Master Apothecary Faranell is in the Apothecarium, with Apothecary Zinge beside him.",w=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is in the Pools of Vision, the cave under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Miles Welsh is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Look for the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-handed axe with +12 Strength. Delgo has few, so it may be sold out.",tp=1},{t="Mangletooth swaps Blood Shards for buffs. Spirit of the Wind gives 5 minutes of extra run speed.",tp=1},{t="Mangletooth is locked in the cage at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Owatanka is a blue thunder lizard that roams east of Camp Taurajo.",tp=1},{t="Owatanka is level 24 and hits hard. Pull him only at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Owatanka drops Owatanka's Tailspike, which starts this quest. He has four spawn points.",tp=1},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. If it isn't up, carry on; this step waits for its head.",tp=1},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Washte Pawne is a red wind serpent with 4 spawn spots south of Camp Taurajo. If he isn't up, move on.",tp=1},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gann Stonespire walks the road north and south. If he's not at the arrow, follow the road.",tp=1},{t="Lok Orcbane is in the building at the top of the ramp.",w=1},{t="The Backstabber drops from Pathfinders and from Stalkers, which move in stealth.",tp=1},{t="Melee: when a Bael'dun Officer takes its defensive stance, its parry chance goes up 50% for 8 seconds.",tp=1},{t="Captain Gerogg Hammertoe, a rare level 27 elite, can be up inside Bael'dun Keep. Check before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dig Rats run inside the Bael Modan dig, among Bael'dun soldiers and riflemen of 23 to 26.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Explosive Stick of Gann on the flying machine up on its platform. It reaches 40 yards.",u=5021},{t="The Outraged Pillager is an elite and fights alongside Encroaching Soldiers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill the Encroaching Soldiers first, then let the fight reset to take the Pillager alone.",tp=1},{t="Slows and stuns work on the Outraged Pillager.",tp=1},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mangletooth is locked in the cage at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Hula'mahi has Flash Powder and the reagents for Instant Poison.",tp=1},{t="The Crate With Holes, Command Stick and Owner's Manual lie beside Mebok. Pick up all three.",w=1},{t="Isha Awak spawns at one of 4 spots along the coast. If she isn't here, try the next.",tp=1},{t="Isha Awak is level 27 and hits hard. Pull her at full health, away from the shore murlocs.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Clear the spiders around Besseleth first, or they join her fight.",tp=1},{t="Besseleth webs you in place for 10 seconds, so you can't run once she has you. Go in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Warlocks: keep Besseleth feared and let your damage-over-time spells wear her down.",tp=1},{t="XT:9 patrols the river's south bank and XT:4 the north bank.",tp=1},{t="Use the Toxic Fogger beneath the sky port platform. You don't need to climb up.",u=5638},{t="Venture Co. Machine Smiths summon Compact Harvest Reapers, so each fight gains an extra mob.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gerenzo is on the Venture Co. platform at the top of Windshear Crag. The climb starts on its east side.",w=1},{t="Sorrow Wing, a rare level 27 elite, can spawn at the lake's north end. Keep clear if it's up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Only plain Sap Beasts drop Stonetalon Sap. Corrosive Sap Beasts carry none.",tp=1},{t="Nal'taszar, a level 30 rare elite fey dragon west of the Peak, drops the scale too. Leave him be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dried Mirkweed grows in the water of Mirkfallon Lake.",w=1},{t="Sorrow Wing, a rare level 27 elite, can spawn at the lake's north end. Keep clear if it's up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Bloodfury Slayers can execute you under 20% health, and Ambushers cast a hard shock often. Pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sister Riven, a rare level 28 elite harpy, can be up at the south end of the vale. Steer clear if she is.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Bloodfury Ripper is elite, and attacking her pulls in harpies from far around.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill the harpies near her first. On her own she can be soloed.",tp=1},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is inside his cave at the top of Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Ashenvale Outrunners move in stealth, so you only see them up close.",tp=1},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="If Torek isn't here, someone just ran his escort. He's back within 5 minutes.",tp=1},{t="Torek not here? Another player has taken this quest. Torek is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Let Torek's raiders draw the Sentinels and Warriors before you join in.",tp=1},{t="Duriel Moonfire appears on the balcony after the building. Let Torek's group hit her first and she stays on them.",tp=1},{t="The lake's north shore has Silverwind Refuge's level 40 guards, and a Wandering Protector (35 elite) walks it. Stay out on the water.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stand on the gazebo out on Mystral Lake's water for the scouting credit.",tp=1},{t="Tideress moves around the island and dives underwater. Circle the island if you can't see her.",tp=1},{t="Ursangous walks a patrol from Mystral Lake's west end up into the hills northwest. Follow it if he's not here.",tp=1},{t="A Wandering Protector, a level 35 elite, walks Ursangous's path too. Look before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Astranaar's guards are level 40 and attack the Horde. Keep to the arrow round the town's west side.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About 35 furbolgs of 23 to 24 fill Thistlefur Hold's tunnels. Clear the way to each chest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Troll Charms are in small chests on the ground inside Thistlefur Hold.",w=1},{t="Ruul Snowhoof is at the back of Thistlefur Hold, the cave on the northeast side of the village.",w=1},{t="Ruul Snowhoof not here? Another player has taken this quest. Ruul Snowhoof is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="3 furbolgs ambush you halfway along the tunnel, and 3 more at the village entrance. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Shadumbra walks the road through here, east to Raynewood Retreat. If she's not in sight, follow the road.",tp=1},{t="Two Cenarion Vindicators guard Ordanus, and each can summon 3 Treants. Pull the Vindicators one at a time first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keeper Ordanus stands up on the highest level of Raynewood Retreat's building.",w=1},{t="Ordanus roots you and casts Lightning Bolt, so there's no running from him. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Laughing Sisters, the dryads round Raynewood Retreat, drop the Etched Phial for The Sacred Flame.",tp=1},{t="A Wandering Protector, a level 35 elite, can patrol near the western approach to Night Run. Look before you go in.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Casters: any Felmusk satyr can silence you for 6 seconds, instantly (Overwhelming Stench). Heal early.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Etched Phial at the moonwell to fill it.",u=5867},{t="The Shadethicket treants are 25 to 27, above your level. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You can lead Sharptalon to the Splintertree or Forsaken Camp guards. Deal over half his damage or no claw drops.",tp=1},{t="Yama Snowhoof is inside the inn at Splintertree Post.",w=1},{t="Mitsuwa is inside the hut at Zoram'gar.",w=1},{t="The escort starts the moment you accept, and it's a hard one. Accept at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Muglash not here? Another player has taken this quest. Muglash is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Waves of naga come first, then Vorsha the Lasher, who hits very hard.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Let Muglash hold Vorsha for a few seconds before you join, so she stays on him.",tp=1},{t="Look for the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-handed axe with +12 Strength. Delgo has few, so it may be sold out.",tp=1},{t="Melor Stonehoof is on the Hunter Rise, over the bridge south of the inn.",w=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Miles Welsh is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="General Twinbraid's room, on the keep's lowest level, is packed tight. A careless pull brings several.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pull the room's mobs out to you one at a time before you open the Strongbox.",tp=1},{t="Brave Moonhorn stands at the top of the Great Lift, on the Barrens side.",w=1},{t="The Galak Messenger drops the note. His patrol begins at Splithoof Crag, the centaur camp farther east.",tp=1},{t="The Great Lift goes down from here. Step on and off only while the platform is stopped: a fall from it kills.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Two level 30 Galak Flame Guards stand at the brazier. Go in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ancient Brazier sits at the far end of the cave in Splithoof Crag's cliff.",w=1},{t="Galak Scouts are the scarce ones and you need 12, so kill every Scout you pass.",tp=1},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="With Test of Faith in your log, leap from the very tip of the wooden platform. The fall becomes a teleport.",tp=1},{t="Jump only from the end of the planks. Anywhere else on the needle, it's a real fall.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stormheart, a level 30 elite, walks a long round through these kobold camps east of Freewind Post. Keep out of his way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Alien Egg spawns in one of three places, so it may not be at the first one you check.",tp=1},{t="Windcallers stun everyone within 10 yards for 4 sec, and Screeching Harpies silence for 8. Pull them singly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Grenka Bloodscreech is a tough kill on your own. Bring a group for her.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The foodstuffs call in pack after pack of harpies along with Grenka.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Stolen Freewind Supplies lie on the floor of Roguefeather Den, the harpy cave.",w=1},{t="Achellios the Banished, a level 31 rare centaur with hounds, and Rok'Alim the Pounder, a level 30 elite, roam the canyon between the harpies and Highperch.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Heartrazor, a level 32 rare elite, can be up near Pao'ka. Look before you climb.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pao'ka waits at the top of the path that climbs toward Highperch.",w=1},{t="Pao'ka Swiftmountain not here? Another player has taken this quest. Pao'ka Swiftmountain is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Three Highperch Wyverns spawn once Pao'ka is in the heart of Highperch.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Attack the easternmost wyvern and the other two vanish.",tp=1},{t="The Highperch Wyvern Eggs lie on the ground among the nests across the plateau.",w=1},{t="The Enraged Panther is a hard fight alone. Bring a friend, or open the cage at full health with cooldowns up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Panther Cage Key at the cage to let the Enraged Panther out.",u=12942},{t="Steelsnap has two hyenas with him, so he's a three-mob pull. Go in at full health or bring a friend.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Steelsnap walks this loop counter-clockwise. The arrow goes round the other way, so you meet him head-on.",tp=1},{t="Handing this in sends three Galak Assassins after Kanati. Be at full health first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Frost does nothing to Boiling and Scalding Elementals and Fire barely hurts them. Arcane works.",tp=1},{t="Scald hits for about 150 Fire damage and stuns for 4 sec. Steam Jet makes you miss far more. Pull these one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Incendia Agave grows round the pools, and some of it under the water.",w=1},{t="Melor Stonehoof is on the Hunter Rise, over the bridge south of the inn.",w=1},{t="Magatha Grimtotem is on the Elder Rise, right where the bridges from the central mesa land.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="Rok'Alim the Pounder roams a wide stretch of north-western Thousand Needles, so expect a search.",tp=1},{t="Secret Note #1 is in a Document Chest on top of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",w=1},{t="Secret Note #2 is in the Document Chest in the big tent.",w=1},{t="Secret Note #3 is in the Document Chest in the eastern plateau's tent.",w=1},{t="Clear the Grimtotems around the fire before you light it. Lighting it brings out Arikara.",tp=1},{t="Use the Incendia Powder at the Sacred Fire of Life to light it.",u=12785},{t="The Sacred Fire of Life is on the north-eastern plateau, at the top of the winding path.",w=1},{t="Lakota Windsong not here? Another player has taken this quest. Lakota Windsong is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Two Grimtotems spawn at every platform Lakota reaches.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Run ahead of Lakota and clear the respawns on the next platform before she gets there.",tp=1},{t="If the escort goes wrong, run back the way you came. It fails and you get out alive.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="The Shimmering Flats are 31 to 35, and Vile Sting, a rare elite scorpid of 35, roams them. Keep to the road to the Raceway.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stormheart, a level 30 elite, walks a long round through these kobold camps east of Freewind Post. Keep out of his way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Just the way there. Go any way you like.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="This chain (The Affray, then The Windwatcher) ends in Berserker Stance.",tp=1},{t="Affray Challengers come one at a time, back to back, before Big Will. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The fight starts when you step onto the grate just north of Klannoc.",w=1},{t="Craven Drok walks around the Cleft of Shadow rather than standing in one spot.",tp=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Use the Withered Scarf at the Summoning Circle south of Gan'rul, then kill the incubus.",u=190187},{t="Keldran stands by Orgrimmar's western exit.",w=1},{t="Gornek is inside the Den, a few steps past its door.",w=1},{t="Hraug is at the back of the Den, beside Nartok.",w=1},{t="Nartok is at the back of the Den, past Gornek.",w=1},{t="Reach level 2 on the boars first. The Vile Familiars are a safer fight at level 2.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sarkoth is a level 4 scorpid. Kill boars up to level 2 before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sell your Mottled Boar loot to Duokna before you train. It comes to about 1 silver.",tp=1},{t="Keep your Mottled Boar loot for the vendor. Your next training costs about 1 to 2 silver.",tp=1},{t="Gornek is inside the Den, a few steps past its door.",w=1},{t="Rwag is inside the Den, a little past Gornek.",w=1},{t="Nartok is at the back of the Den, past Gornek.",w=1},{t="Shamans: Kzan sells a Short Staff, a two-hand upgrade, for about 1 silver. Sell your old weapon toward it.",tp=1},{t="Kzan Thornslash is at the back of the Den, past Gornek.",w=1},{t="Hraug is at the back of the Den, beside Nartok.",w=1},{t="Priests: sell your Mottled Boar loot here first. Training and water come to about 50 copper.",tp=1},{t="Use the Foreman's Blackjack on a Lazy Peon while it sleeps.",u=16114},{t="Use the Foreman's Blackjack on a Lazy Peon while it sleeps.",u=16114},{t="Gornek is inside the Den, a few steps past its door.",w=1},{t="Thazz'ril's Pick and Yarrog Baneshadow are both inside the Burning Blade Coven cave.",w=1},{t="The Lost Journal lies on a barrel right beside Zureetha.",w=1},{t="Rwag is inside the Den, a little past Gornek.",w=1},{t="Hraug is at the back of the Den, beside Nartok.",w=1},{t="Nartok is at the back of the Den, past Gornek.",w=1},{t="Drink the Earth Sapta at the shrine, and the Minor Manifestation of Earth appears.",u=6635},{t="Spirit Rock is the shrine south of the valley.",w=1},{t="Lar Prowltusk walks a short beat outside Sen'jin, on the village's west side.",w=1},{t="Vel'rin Fang is inside a hut, just north of Master Gadrin.",w=1},{t="Trayexir sells upgrades for Rogues (Stiletto), Warriors (Large Axe, Tomahawk) and Hunters (Hornwood Recurve Bow).",tp=1},{t="Pa'zula offers this only after you learn Enchanting from her, and that takes one of your two profession slots.",tp=1},{t="Pa'zula is inside the big hut in Sen'jin Village.",w=1},{t="Trayexir is in the big hut, but you can reach him from outside it.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Ukorsbane drops the pack that starts this.",tp=1},{t="Ukorsbane is a level 8 elite and a hard kill alone. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 2 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Sit by Brakk's campfire with /sit. The rest buff the quest asks for comes after about a minute.",tp=1},{t="No credit after sitting? Abandon the quest, take it again from Brakk and sit back down.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Gar'Thok stands inside the bunker. He's in reach from its doorway or its roof too.",w=1},{t="Furl Scornbrow waits on the highest level of the Razor Hill watchtower.",w=1},{t="Warriors, Rogues, Shamans, Warlocks: training here costs about 4 silver. Priests: about 2.",tp=1},{t="Warlord Kolkanis, a level 9 rare, can be up among the Kolkar. Have a Minor Healing Potion ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Valley of Trials plan is on the floor inside a tent.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Pal'juh leaves Kolkar Crag with whoever escorts him, so he may be gone. Wait for him to come back.",tp=1},{t="Pal'juh not here? Another player has taken this quest. Pal'juh is back a few minutes after they finish, so wait nearby.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Rogues: K'waii, the general goods vendor in Sen'jin, sells a Weighted Throwing Axe for your ranged slot.",tp=1},{t="Lar Prowltusk walks a short beat outside Sen'jin, on the village's west side.",w=1},{t="Trayexir is in the big hut, but you can reach him from outside it.",w=1},{t="The Raider's Bow lies on the ground south-west of the keep.",w=1},{t="The Raider's Battleaxe lies in the middle of the keep.",w=1},{t="Watch Commander Zalaphil, a level 9 rare, can be up in Tiragarde Keep. Keep a healing potion on your bar.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lieutenant Benedict is upstairs, on the keep's second floor.",w=1},{t="Open Benedict's Chest with his key, then right-click the Aged Envelope inside.",u=4881},{t="Benedict's Chest is upstairs, a floor above Benedict.",w=1},{t="The Raider's Shield lies by the watchtower north of the keep.",w=1},{t="Gar'Thok stands inside the bunker. He's in reach from its doorway or its roof too.",w=1},{t="Furl Scornbrow waits on the highest level of the Razor Hill watchtower.",w=1},{t="Uhgar has the same Walking Stick as Trayexir in Sen'jin, at the same price.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Thotar is inside the bunker.",w=1},{t="The Gnomish Toolboxes are inside the wrecked boats and on the ground around them.",w=1},{t="The Matriarch is on the small northern isle with the Taillasher eggs. Swim over from the beach.",w=1},{t="The Matriarch is level 9, and Shal'ma, a level 9 tiger, can be beside her. Pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Bloodtalon Taillasher usually stands by each egg. Kill it before you loot.",tp=1},{t="Swim over from the Durotar shore to reach the main island.",tp=1},{t="The Loa Idols sit mostly along the stone walls.",tp=1},{t="Zalazane casts Healing Wave. Save an interrupt or a stun for it.",tp=1},{t="Shamans: Earth Shock interrupts his Healing Wave.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: Gouge him when he starts Healing Wave.",tp=1},{t="Voodoo Trolls cast Healing Wave too. Interrupt it when you can, or the fights drag on.",tp=1},{t="Minshina's skulls lie in Zalazane's circle, right beside him. Kill him (level 10) before you loot one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Disenchant the Hexed Pendants from Hexed and Voodoo Trolls. That gives the Luminous Residue.",tp=1},{t="Pa'zula is inside the big hut in Sen'jin Village.",w=1},{t="The Really Sticky Glue roots a target for 10 seconds. Keep it for getting away from a bad pull.",tp=1},{t="The Faintly Glowing Skull drains 75 to 125 health from a target. Save it for a fight that turns.",tp=1},{t="Vel'rin Fang is inside a hut, just north of Master Gadrin.",w=1},{t="Shamans, Priests, Mages and Warlocks: the Walking Stick here, about 5 silver, is your next staff. Sell your starting weapon toward it.",tp=1},{t="Trayexir is in the big hut, but you can reach him from outside it.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 2 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Gar'Thok stands inside the bunker. He's in reach from its doorway or its roof too.",w=1},{t="Thotar is inside the bunker.",w=1},{t="Thotar is inside the bunker.",w=1},{t="Wuark sells the Mining Pick. Turn on Find Minerals to see Copper Veins on the minimap.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Rough Stone from Copper Veins makes Rough Sharpening Stones, which add 2 damage to a sharp weapon for 30 minutes.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Aim the Taming Rod at a Dire Mottled Boar from its longest range, so the cast ends before it reaches you.",u=15917},{t="Thotar is inside the bunker.",w=1},{t="Dustrunners cast Rejuvenation on themselves and Battleguards have a lot of health. Pull them one at a time.",tp=1},{t="Gar'Thok stands inside the bunker. He's in reach from its doorway or its roof too.",w=1},{t="The trail up to Telf Joolam is a narrow ledge. A fall from it can kill you.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Leave Telf Joolam by the same trail you came up.",tp=1},{t="Fizzle Darkstorm is level 12 and casts from range with his imp beside him. Take him at full health once his friends are cleared; a partner makes it much safer.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Burning Blade Fanatic patrols near Fizzle, and Lightning Hides stand behind him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill the Fanatic and the Lightning Hides, then pull Fizzle back to that cleared spot, away from his friends.",tp=1},{t="Fizzle has an Imp Minion. Kill the imp first.",tp=1},{t="Mages: Polymorph Fizzle while you kill his imp.",tp=1},{t="Shamans: Earth Shock his Soul Siphon.",tp=1},{t="Rogues: Gouge interrupts his Soul Siphon.",tp=1},{t="If it turns bad, drink a Minor Healing Potion or use the Faintly Glowing Skull.",tp=1},{t="Warlocks: if you've trained Create Healthstone, make one before you pull.",tp=1},{t="Warlocks: dismiss your Imp before you drop into Thunder Ridge.",tp=1},{t="Thotar is inside the bunker.",w=1},{t="The Hornwood Recurve Bow is about 2 silver 80. The Laminated Recurve Bow, about 17 silver 50, needs level 11.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Spitelash camp is crowded: Scouts at 9-10, Attendants at 10-11. Pull from its edge, one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Each naga's Spinefin goes to one player only, so a group needs a kill each.",tp=1},{t="Dismiss the boar before you tame a Surf Crawler. You can only hold one beast.",tp=1},{t="Leave the Armored Scorpids alive. Your next tame is one of them.",tp=1},{t="Aim the Taming Rod at a Surf Crawler from its longest range.",u=15919},{t="Thotar is inside the bunker.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dismiss the Surf Crawler first, then tame the scorpid.",tp=1},{t="Aim the Taming Rod at an Armored Scorpid from its longest range.",u=15920},{t="Thotar waits inside the bunker.",w=1},{t="Dustwind Savages and Storm Witches run when hurt and can bring another one back. Finish them before they get away.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dustwind Storm Witches drop the Dull Storm Orb that starts this.",tp=1},{t="Walk out of the ravine through the cave passage. It comes out near Rezlak.",tp=1},{t="Warriors: the Blemished Wooden Staff needs Staves, which Hanashi teaches in Orgrimmar.",tp=1},{t="Hunters: the Hickory Shortbow is worth keeping. Learn Bows in Orgrimmar if you don't have it.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="This quest has a 45-minute timer. Take it so Kor'ghan offers the antidote quest; the guide has you drop it and take it again on the way back.",tp=1},{t="Hunters: the Venomtail Scorpids and Bloodtalon Scythemaws near Rhinag make the hardest-hitting pets around here.",tp=1},{t="Thatog is upstairs in his building.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Nazgrel stands in Thrall's chamber, inside Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="Kor'ghan is in the Cleft of Shadow.",w=1},{t="If Yelmak doesn't offer it yet, give it about 10 seconds.",tp=1},{t="Migi is out behind Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="Thra paces behind Grommash Hold and may not be right at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Smooth Boulders are the orange rocks. There are few of them, and they respawn slowly.",tp=1},{t="Halikor drops the hoof that starts this. He has at least two spawn points in Thunder Ridge.",tp=1},{t="Halikor is a level 12 elite with about 800 health. His hits are moderate, but alone it's a long fight. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Lieutenant's Insignia is a chance drop, so it can take a few Burning Blade.",tp=1},{t="Kron's Amulet doesn't drop often. Expect to kill a fair number of crocolisks.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Aggor the Young walks the shore, so he may be away from the arrow.",w=1},{t="Aggor the Young is a level 11 elite sea giant. Bring two friends; at about 13 a pair can handle him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Gazz'uz drops the Eye of Burning Shadow, which starts this.",tp=1},{t="Gazz'uz, in the Skull Rock cave, is level 14 and brings a Voidwalker and Shadow Bolt. Bring a partner if you can.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Really Sticky Glue roots his Voidwalker so it can't reach you.",tp=1},{t="Break line of sight to stop his Shadow Bolts.",tp=1},{t="With Gazz'uz dead, the water pools in the cave let you get away from the Voidwalker.",tp=1},{t="The Burning Blade Stash is at the far end of the Skull Rock cave, down its right-hand passage.",w=1},{t="The cave holds Burning Blade at 9 to 11, Gazz'uz at 14 with a Voidwalker, and Felweaver Scornn, a rare elite.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kor'ghan is in the Cleft of Shadow.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Urtharo sells the Tabar for about 22 silver. The Quarter Staff, about 30 silver, needs level 11.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The trail up to Telf Joolam is a narrow ledge. A fall from it can kill you.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Drink the Fire Sapta by the shrine so the Minor Manifestation of Fire shows itself.",u=6636},{t="The Dormant Flame's brazier sits atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame, north-east of Telf.",w=1},{t="Leave Telf Joolam by the same trail you came up.",tp=1},{t="The Flawed Power Stone is the purple stone on the ground beside Ak'Zeloth.",w=1},{t="Take a Flawed Power Stone from the stones beside Ak'Zeloth, then go straight to the altar on Dreadmist Peak: the stone lasts 30 minutes."},{t="Rathorian, a level 15 rare, can be up on Dreadmist Peak. Keep Really Sticky Glue and the Faintly Glowing Skull ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Come back down the same trail you climbed.",tp=1},{t="The altar is inside Dreadmist Den, a cave on the summit of Dreadmist Peak.",w=1},{t="Burning Blade at 10 to 12 crowd the trail and the den. Pull them singly on the way up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Burning Blade Crusher (13) and a Toxicologist (14) stand in the den by the altar. Pull them out one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Doras stands at the top of the wind rider tower.",w=1},{t="You can destroy the Lieutenant's Insignia now. Nothing needs it again.",tp=1},{t="Use the Glyphs of Summoning here, then defeat the Voidwalker it calls.",u=7464},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Coleman Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Gretchen Dedmar is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Austil de Mon is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Ageron Kargal is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Cain Firesong teaches from the Brill inn's upper floor.",w=1},{t="The Maggot Eye poster is inside the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is indoors, in the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Deathguard Bartholomew walks around the Brill graveyard, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Use the Executor's Motivator on Deathguards in and near Brill. Any five will do.",u=286176},{t="You can destroy the Executor's Motivator once Discipline is handed in.",tp=1},{t="Dry Branches lie at the foot of the trees around Brill.",tp=1},{t="Each report comes from a dialogue option when you talk to Kristof, Dillinger and Gordo.",tp=1},{t="Hostile Tirisfal Farmers and Farmhands (5-7) work the pumpkin rows, with Farmer Solliden, a level 8 rare.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="When a Scarlet Warrior drops into a defensive stance, it parries much more for a few seconds. Save big hits.",tp=1},{t="Three Scarlet Warriors stand together on the tower's top floor. Expect all three if you pull one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bareth Dawnstone is on the top floor. Once you accept, stay with him until he's clear of the outpost.",w=1},{t="Bareth Dawnstone not here? Another player has taken this quest. Bareth Dawnstone is back a few minutes after they finish, so wait nearby.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Cursed Darkhounds roam among the ones you need, and they're higher level. Look around before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Deathguard Burgess is inside the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="The Captured Scarlet Zealot is in the tavern cellar, toward the back.",w=1},{t="Ulag the Cleaver is level 11 and hits hard. Call him at full health with food ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Carendin Halgar is in the Magic Quarter.",w=1},{t="Anastasia Hartwell is in the Magic Quarter.",w=1},{t="Perrine's Chest sits on the ground right beside Captain Perrine.",w=1},{t="Stand on the Summoning Circle, then use the Runes of Summoning to call the Voidwalker.",u=6284},{t="Any undead at Agamand Mills can drop the letter. Loot every kill there.",tp=1},{t="Nissa Agamand sometimes stands inside the building. Check indoors if she isn't out front.",w=1},{t="Thurman and Gregor Agamand wander around the Mills instead of standing still. Look about for them.",tp=1},{t="Cracked Skull Soldiers in the Mills are level 9 and packed close. Start in the fields to the south and pull singly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The drop from Agamand Mills toward Garren's Haunt is steep enough to hurt. Zigzag down.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Yvette Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Coleman Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is indoors, in the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Dark Cleric Beryl is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Cain Firesong is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Austil de Mon is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Marion Call is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Rupert Boch is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Necrotic Crystal Fragments also lie loose on the ground. Pick those up between kills.",tp=1},{t="Dark Enforcers (level 10-12) hit hard and have an instant strike. Neophytes hit hard too. Fight at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Only Vile Fin Muckdwellers and Minor Oracles drop the skins. Puddlejumpers never do.",tp=1},{t="The crypt's Ancestors respawn fast. Rooms you cleared can fill again behind you, so don't linger.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Captain Dargol, level 13, waits on the crypt's lowest level. Clear the Ancestors in his room first.",w=1},{t="The four weapon racks are on the floor inside the Agamand family crypt.",w=1},{t="Rotting and Wailing Ancestors (levels 9 to 11) fill the crypt and respawn fast. Loot each rack and keep moving.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keep the Slumber Sand from this quest for the day a pull goes wrong.",tp=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is indoors, in the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is indoors, in the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Coleman Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Riptear, a level 13 elite, wanders the west end of Venomweb Vale. Keep to the spiders on its east and south side, and watch for it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Deathguard Burgess is inside the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="The Captured Mountaineer is in the inn cellar, in the same room as the Zealot.",w=1},{t="Dark Cleric Beryl is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Cain Firesong is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Austil de Mon is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Marion Call is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Rupert Boch is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Leonid Barthalomew is on the upper floor of Bandarion Keep.",w=1},{t="Stay by Leonid while he and Danitha Morr talk. The quest completes when they finish.",tp=1},{t="Hilda the Breaker stands outside, south of the keep.",w=1},{t="Ephram Barbaro stands outside, west of the keep.",w=1},{t="The Whispering Horror haunts the north end of the Shadowvale Crypt.",w=1},{t="The Whispering Horror in the crypt's north room is an elite of 11 to 13 that hits hard. Bring a partner, or leave it: nothing else needs it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Its drop starts a quest. Pick it up if you come across it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Whispering Horror drops the Residue that starts this quest.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 2 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Glowing Crystal Fragment lies at the far south end of the Shadowvale Crypt.",w=1},{t="The bones come from the level 9-10 Lurchers and Mystics in the crypt's south half.",tp=1},{t="Bottles of Whispering Elixir lie about the Shadowvale crypt, some on the floor, some up on its walls.",w=1},{t="Deathstalker Erland isn't always at his post. If he's gone, wait for him to come back.",tp=1},{t="Deathstalker Erland not here? Another player has taken this quest. Deathstalker Erland is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Worgs ambush the escort, sometimes several on the same spot. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Eat and drink in each lull between worg attacks.",tp=1},{t="Vile Fin Shredders and Tidehunters on the shore east of here drop Murloc Eyes. Keep 3 for Quinn's Wild Eyes.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) has been seen on the road at the north end of this loop. Keep clear of it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dusty Spellbooks lie upstairs in the house at Valgan's Field. The Remedy of Arugal is in them.",w=1},{t="Quinn Yorick is upstairs in the house at the Ivar Patch.",w=1},{t="Fear doesn't work on the Rot Hide gnolls here.",tp=1},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 25 elite) roams from The Dead Field south to the Moonrage gnolls. Give it a wide berth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) can wander through here. Watch for it and keep clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krethis Shadowspinner (level 15 rare) shields herself and shocks hard. Nothing here needs her, so leave her alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Buy the Wise Man's Belt here, about 14 silver. You can wear it from level 15.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Moonrage Darksouls (level 13-14) enrage when they get low. Keep a cooldown for the end of the fight.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) has been seen among the Moonrage here. Look around before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Quinn Yorick is upstairs in the house at the Ivar Patch.",w=1},{t="Ivar the Foul waits in the barn with two Ravenclaw Slaves. One walks out on a short patrol, so pull it alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ravenclaw Slaves can't be feared.",tp=1},{t="Clear the mobs standing in front of the barn before you go in.",tp=1},{t="Hands of Ravenclaw (up to level 16) stand around the ferry dock and stun melee for 5 seconds. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Corpse Laden Boat is tied up alongside the ferry dock. Click it.",w=1},{t="Dalaran Apprentices (level 13-14) guard the crate. They cast Frostbolt and run when hurt.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Draw the apprentices away one at a time, then open the crate.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 5 minutes. Walk straight to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium, across the slime canal."},{t="Doctor Martin Felben is in the Apothecarium, over the slime canal.",w=1},{t="Master Apothecary Faranell is in the Apothecarium, with Apothecary Zinge beside him.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 2 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Anastasia Hartwell is in the Magic Quarter.",w=1},{t="In Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium, use the Cantation of Manifestation to reveal the Rift Spawns.",u=7308},{t="Once a Rift Spawn is stunned, use the Chest of Containment Coffers on it and loot the coffer. Three in all.",u=7247},{t="Grimson the Pale is inside the Deep Elem Mine, past its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine is full of Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls (13-14). Clear the way in one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Moonrage Bloodhowlers (15-16) stand with Darksouls at the mine's mouth. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dalaran Conjurors and Warders (16-18) hold Ambermill's east end. Keep to the Protectors and Mages west of them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Apothecary Berard is upstairs in Pyrewood's inn. The journal is in Berard's Bookshelf beside him.",w=1},{t="Berard is a level 16 elite, and every villager around him is an elite too. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Deathstalker Faerleia waits inside Pyrewood's chapel.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The council is eight elite councilmen and Lord Mayor Morrison, a level 15 elite. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Pyrewood villager is an elite of 14-15. Take them on with a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Outside the keep the Rot Hides are 16 to 18, inside 18 to 19 with Thule Ravenclaw (24 elite), and Snarlmane, a level 23 rare, roams the island. Pull one at a time at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shallow Grave is just east of Fenris Keep's walls.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mennet Carkad is in the Rogues' Quarter, near the rogue trainers.",w=1},{t="Duskbat Pelts don't drop from every bat. Plan on more kills than the five you need.",tp=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is inside the town hall in Brill.",w=1},{t="Gretchen Dedmar is upstairs in the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Captain Vachon is inside the Scarlet tower.",w=1},{t="Scarlet Friars cast Lesser Heal on themselves and their friends. Kill them first.",tp=1},{t="Riptear is a level 13 elite that wanders Venomweb Vale. Come back two levels above it, or bring a friend.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Captain Melrache and his bodyguards are inside the tower.",w=1},{t="Melrache (level 12) and both Scarlet Bodyguards stand side by side. Expect all three at once.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lake Creepers are 17-18, and the Elder Lake Creepers north of them 18-19. Work the southern ones.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Master Apothecary Faranell is in the Apothecarium, with Apothecary Zinge beside him.",w=1},{t="Ride the lift down. Raleigh Andrean stands near the foot of the lifts.",w=1},{t="Josef Gregorian is in the tailor shop in the Magic Quarter.",w=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Thork and Darsok Swiftdagger stand at the top of the Crossroads tower.",w=1},{t="Thork is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="The keg spawns in several spots across the Barrens. If it isn't here, grab it when you pass another.",tp=1},{t="The supply crates spawn in several places, so one may not be where the arrow points.",tp=1},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Root Samples come from gathering Barrens herbs: Peacebloom, Silverleaf, Earthroot, Mageroyal, Briarthorn, Bruiseweed.",tp=1},{t="Baron Longshore can be at any of the Southsea camps. Check each one.",tp=1},{t="Tazan walks back and forth along a hillside among the Southsea camps.",tp=1},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Thork is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="The Bubbling Fissure is underwater in the pool. Dive down to it.",w=1},{t="Barak Kodobane hits very hard, and the Kolkar Wrangler at his side nets you and shoots from range.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Warriors: Vrang Wildgore also sells the Heavy Spiked Mace, a level 14 two-hander, in limited stock.",tp=1},{t="Two of the valves call out Venture Co. guards when shut, two for one and one for the other. Start each at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Tinkerer Sniggles is inside the building northeast of the control console.",w=1},{t="Darsok Swiftdagger is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="Uthrok's Fine Longbow (level 14) is limited stock. When it's gone, the Reinforced Bow (level 16) is the backup.",tp=1},{t="Instant Poison II needs 120 Poisons skill before Ormok can teach it.",tp=1},{t="Zor Lonetree is inside Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="Pick Lock opens Tazan's Satchel. It needs Thieves' Tools from Rekkul in Orgrimmar.",tp=1},{t="Without Pick Lock, Pick Pocket Gamon in the Orgrimmar inn. He carries the key.",tp=1},{t="Open Tazan's Satchel with the key from Gamon, or Pick Lock it first.",u=7209},{t="The Cats Eye Emerald is a rare drop. It can take 25 kills or more.",tp=1},{t="Boulder Lode Mine mobs stand close enough to pull in pairs, and the tunnels leave little room to run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Work the camp outside the mine entrance. Stay out of the tunnels.",w=1},{t="If the shredder isn't here, someone is on The Escape with it, and it's slow to come back.",tp=1},{t="Venture Co. goblins here are 14 to 18, and a few Lookouts and Patrollers of 22 to 23 stand just north-west. Pull one at a time and keep away from those.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supervisor Lugwizzle paces the platform, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Two level 19 rares, Foreman Grills and Sludge Beast, can be up around The Sludge Fen.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The escort starts the moment you accept. Rest to full first.",tp=1},{t="Wizzlecrank's Shredder not here? Another player has taken this quest. Wizzlecrank's Shredder is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Two Venture Co. Mercenaries jump in when the shredder reaches the high ground.",tp=1},{t="The quest completes after the shredder's closing lines, so stay until it's done talking.",tp=1},{t="If he doesn't show or another player tags him, abandon the quest and take it again from Sergra for a new horn.",tp=1},{t="Blow the Horn of Echeyakee at his lair to call him out.",u=10327},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws in the north run up to level 18 and use Thrash. Take your heads from Lashtails and Screechers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Takk the Leaper, a rare level 19 elite raptor, can spawn just east of the Sludge Fen. Leave him be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Witchwing Slayers cast Execute, a heavy hit once you're under 20% health. Keep your health up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Witchwing Ambushers patrol in stealth, so one can join a fight without warning.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Chol'aruk is built for a group of five. Don't take him on alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Darsok Swiftdagger is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="When Polly the parrot attacks, give her the E.C.A.C. from your bags.",u=7970},{t="The Jewel of the Southsea is on the ship's bottom deck. Opening it takes Lockpicking 70.",w=1},{t="Raise Lockpicking to 70 on the ship's second deck before you go down.",tp=1},{t="The Bubbling Fissure is underwater, on the lakebed in the middle of the oasis.",w=1},{t="Each Kolkar killed at the oasis can bring out Verog. When it's crowded, wait at his spawn point.",tp=1},{t="Laden Mushrooms grow at The Forgotten Pools and at The Stagnant Oasis.",tp=1},{t="Each nest (blue, red and yellow) takes one Sunscale Feather, which the Scytheclaws drop.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws are level 16-18 and Thrash for two extra hits. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Beaten Corpse lies on the ground at a small outpost beside the road south of the Crossroads.",w=1},{t="Mangletooth's Spirit of the Wind costs 10 Blood Shards and speeds you up for 5 minutes.",tp=1},{t="The Grimtotem camp is up a trail that climbs to a bonfire.",tp=1},{t="Kill all six Brutes before you talk to Kaya, so none are left to join her escort.",tp=1},{t="Grundig Darkcloud stands in front of the camp's main tent.",w=1},{t="Kaya Flathoof is indoors, next to Grundig Darkcloud's spot.",w=1},{t="Kaya Flathoof not here? Another player has taken this quest. Kaya Flathoof is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Three Grimtotems attack when Kaya reaches the bonfire. Start the escort at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stay right beside Kaya the whole way.",tp=1},{t="Xen'Zilla is inside a hut at Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Mor'rogal and Tsunaman stand together, up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks is in a small goblin hut, tucked behind a hill.",w=1},{t="Deepmoss Hatchlings can call a level 22 Deepmoss Matriarch into the fight. Kill them fast, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Deepmoss Eggs lie on the ground beside the trees.",w=1},{t="If you have First Aid, keep the Small Venom Sacs for Anti-Venom.",tp=1},{t="Venture Co. Operators are level 19-20. Pull them on their own, away from the Loggers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bristleback Geomancers are level 19-20, the toughest here. Take them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keep the Blood Shards the quilboars drop. Mangletooth at Camp Taurajo trades them for buffs.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws cast Thrash, two extra hits about every 10 seconds. Fight them at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Oasis Snapjaws are in the water as well as on the shore.",tp=1},{t="Humar the Pridelord, a rare level 23 elite lion, can be up among the lions north of Ratchet.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Zhevra drop the Fresh Zhevra Carcass that draws Ishamuhale out. It spoils 30 minutes after you loot it.",tp=1},{t="By the dead tree, use the Fresh Zhevra Carcass. Ishamuhale comes out to eat it.",u=10338},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Grazlix's Mighty Chain Pants are limited stock and a solid leg upgrade.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 45 minutes. The route takes it to Zamah in Thunder Bluff straight away."},{t="Apothecary Zamah is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Clarice Foster is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Miles Welsh is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Check the Heavy Recurve Bow here against the bow you're using.",tp=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Xen'Zilla is inside a hut at Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Seereth talks for a few seconds after this hand-in. The Elder Crone and Shredding Machines show up once he's done.",tp=1},{t="Ruga Ragetotem is inside a building at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Kill Lakota'mani for the Hoof of Lakota'mani, which starts this quest. He has four spawn points.",tp=1},{t="Lakota'mani is level 22, a hard fight at this point. Pull him only at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Chol'aruk is inside a cave in the Razormane hills east of the Crossroads.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Hezrul Bloodmark walks a loop round the lake, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Warlord Krom'zar is a level 20 elite and brings two or more Kolkar. Do this one in a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krom'zar is slow to arrive. Give it as much as 3 minutes.",tp=1},{t="You can lead Krom'zar in circles round Regthar Deathgate's building while you attack from range.",tp=1},{t="His banner falls to the ground when he dies. Loot that for the Piece of Krom'zar's Banner.",tp=1},{t="Serena is level 20 and stands among Witchwing Slayers and Windcallers. Clear round her before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Other players hunt the Savannah Patriarchs too, so expect to wait on respawns.",tp=1},{t="Walton's camp is up on the ridge above the Dry Hills. The trail climbs from the south-east.",w=1},{t="Mobs at the wrecked caravan stand close together. A pull often brings two or three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Terry Longdrink's marines attack after about a minute of talk. Wait behind the house so they don't all pull at once.",tp=1},{t="Vrang Wildgore fights at Walton's side, so Walton survives without your help.",tp=1},{t="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is inside his cave at the top of Malaka'jin, up the left-hand path.",w=1},{t="Mobs in the Boulderslide Ravine cave hit harder than their level and pull together easily.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gogger Rock Keepers' Earth Shock hits very hard. Kill them first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Everything is in the ravine's north cave. The explore credit comes only well inside it.",tp=1},{t="You get Resonite Crystals by attacking the crystals in the cave.",tp=1},{t="Goggeroc, a level 20 elite, waits deeper in the cave than the explore point. Don't go further than you need.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Mor'rogal and Tsunaman stand together, up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="About 50 troggs of 16 to 18 fill the cave, and Goggeroc is a level 20 elite. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Enchanted Resonite Crystal on the Resonite Cask to call Goggeroc.",u=16603},{t="Mor'rogal stands up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks stands at a small goblin hut tucked behind a hill.",w=1},{t="Piznik is inside the Windshear Mine, west of its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine holds about 60 kobolds of 20 to 23, Geomancers among them. Clear a path in and out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kobolds hit Piznik in three waves over 5 minutes, up to four at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The waves land at about 0:15, 2:15 and 3:20, the second with two casters. Eat and drink in the gaps.",tp=1},{t="Ursangous, a strong level 25 mob, patrols the stag and bear grounds. Watch for him between pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Eye of Kilrogg follows you north-west to the main road. Talk to it there to hand in.",tp=1},{t="Mitsuwa and Marukai are inside a hut at Zoram'gar.",w=1},{t="Marukai is inside the hut at Zoram'gar, beside Mitsuwa.",w=1},{t="Aean Swiftriver, a level 26 rare elite, can be up among the mounds. Keep well clear of him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Twitching Antennae expire 15 minutes after you loot them. Get them in one go and head straight back.",tp=1},{t="Ruga Ragetotem is inside a building at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Northwatch Hold is packed with Theramore Marines and Preservers. Work in from the edge, one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gilthares Firebough not here? Another player has taken this quest. Gilthares Firebough is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Gilthares walks you up the coast past the Southsea camps to Ratchet. Stay close to him.",tp=1},{t="Bruuz is a level 20 elite in the water off Ratchet, hard for one player.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lead Bruuz to Ratchet's guards and they attack him. You need half his damage for the kill to count.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Brine is in her hut, up above the watering hole.",w=1},{t="Use the Empty Brown Waterskin at the watering hole below the hut.",u=7766},{t="Stormhides, Hecklefang Stalkers and Greater Thunderhawks of 22-24 roam the watering hole. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dogran's Pendant calls the succubus at the Summoning Circle. Use it there, then kill her.",u=6626},{t="The Summoning Circle is inside a building a short walk south of Gan'rul.",w=1},{t="Taskmaster Fizzule is a level 30 elite and attacks anyone close before he turns friendly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="From well away, target Fizzule, fire the Flare Gun twice, then type /salute. Talk to him once he's friendly.",u=8051},{t="Every Drone, Patroller and Lookout you need is inside the Venture Co. tower north of the Sludge Fen.",tp=1},{t="Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix, a level 23 elite, waits on the tower's top floor.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Open on Gallywix with Ambush for about half his health. Gouge him when you need energy back.",tp=1},{t="Keep Evasion, Thistle Tea and a healing potion for when the fight goes wrong.",tp=1},{t="Use the Samophlange Manual Cover once you hold the five pages.",u=11147},{t="Boss Copperplug, who drops the cover, is at the back of the Boulder Lode Mine.",w=1},{t="Open the Bundle of Reports in your bags to get the three Warsong Reports.",u=16783},{t="If Torek isn't here, someone just ran his escort. He's back within 5 minutes.",tp=1},{t="Torek not here? Another player has taken this quest. Torek is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Let Torek's raiders draw the Sentinels and Warriors before you join in.",tp=1},{t="Duriel Moonfire appears on the balcony after the building. Let Torek's group hit her first and she stays on them.",tp=1},{t="Anti-Venom removes Touch of Zanzil. Left alone, it lasts 7 days.",tp=1},{t="Magatha has a short scene after The Elder Crone. Forsaken Aid comes up once it ends.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Apothecary Zamah is in the Pools of Vision, the cave under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Instant Poison II needs 120 Poisons skill before Ormok can teach it.",tp=1},{t="Ride the lift down. Raleigh Andrean stands near the foot of the lifts.",w=1},{t="Yuriv's Tomb lies flat on the ground beside the Sepulcher, so it's easy to walk past.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is down in the Sepulcher's crypt.",w=1},{t="Archmage Ataeric is inside Ambermill's town hall.",w=1},{t="Ataeric's hall is crowded with Dalaran casters. Draw them to the door a few at a time before you take him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Offering Stone stands deep in the cave, at its far end.",w=1},{t="Offering the soul at the stone spawns a hostile Tortured Soul. Clear the mobs around the stone first.",tp=1},{t="Stand at the Offering Stone and use the Tortured Soul from your bags.",u=210713},{t="Valdred Moray walks a patrol among packs of refugees. Wait until he's clear of them, then pull him alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The yeti cave north of the fields holds yetis of 30 to 32. Stay on the road.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Serge Hinott not here? Another player has taken this quest. Serge Hinott is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Hinott needs about half a minute to brew the cure. Wait beside him.",tp=1},{t="Use Hinott's Oil from your bags to wash off Touch of Zanzil.",u=8095},{t="Fill the Empty Red Waterskin from your bags at Tarren Mill's well, in the middle of town.",u=7768},{t="Ott sometimes has the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-hander with +12 Strength.",tp=1},{t="Jailor Marlgen carries the Burnished Gold Key for Tog'thar's lock. He stands by Tog'thar or below the tower.",tp=1},{t="Kris Legace sometimes has Stalking Pants and Wolf Bracers, leather for your legs and wrists.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Jailor Eston carries the Dull Iron Key for Drull's lock. He stands outside Tog'thar's barracks or beside Drull.",tp=1},{t="The tower a short way southwest of Durnholde Keep has more Shadow Mages, plus Syndicate Rogues and Watchmen.",tp=1},{t="Hillsbrad Farmers disarm you, which hurts melee most. Pull them one at a time.",tp=1},{t="Farmer Getz turns up in his house, his barn or out in the field.",w=1},{t="Farmer Ray is under the grapevine or inside his house, on either floor.",w=1},{t="Hunt the Starving Mountain Lions of the fields. The lions to the south-east and up in Alterac are 27 to 34.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="After a short scene Stanley turns into Enraged Stanley and attacks. Hand this in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stanley is at Farmer Ray's farm, at the north end of the fields.",w=1},{t="The farmers, farmhands, peasants and footmen of the fields all drop skulls. No need to go down to the mine.",tp=1},{t="Elder Gray Bears (25-26) and Elder Moss Creepers (26-27) outlevel the rest here. Leave them alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Giant Moss Creepers, 24 to 25, drop Creeper Ichor as well.",tp=1},{t="Masoj is out among level 26 to 28 lions, moss creepers and gnolls. Go in slowly and pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="We don't know yet which peaks the three Apothecary Vials go on. If you place them, tell us where each one is.",a=1},{t="It sends you up three peaks around Hillsbrad. A long climb for its XP.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It sends you up three peaks around Hillsbrad. A long climb for its XP.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) can wander through here. Watch for it and keep clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shallow Grave is just east of Fenris Keep's walls.",w=1},{t="Thule Ravenclaw waits in a large hall inside Fenris Keep.",w=1},{t="Thule is a level 24 elite who calls a minion back and hexes you. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dusty Shelf is in the keep's north-west tower. Turn left at the top of the first stairs.",w=1},{t="Fenris Keep is full of Rot Hides of 18-19, with Thule Ravenclaw (24 elite) among them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is down in the Sepulcher's crypt.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Raleigh Andrean stands near the foot of the lifts.",w=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is in the Pools of Vision, the cave under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Check the Heavy Recurve Bow here against the bow you're using.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Miles Welsh is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Look for the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-handed axe with +12 Strength. Delgo has few, so it may be sold out.",tp=1},{t="Mangletooth swaps Blood Shards for buffs. Spirit of the Wind gives 5 minutes of extra run speed.",tp=1},{t="Mangletooth is locked in the cage at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Owatanka is a blue thunder lizard that roams east of Camp Taurajo.",tp=1},{t="Owatanka is level 24 and hits hard. Pull him only at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Owatanka drops Owatanka's Tailspike, which starts this quest. He has four spawn points.",tp=1},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. If it isn't up, carry on; this step waits for its head.",tp=1},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Washte Pawne is a red wind serpent with 4 spawn spots south of Camp Taurajo. If he isn't up, move on.",tp=1},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Brine is in her hut, up above the watering hole.",w=1},{t="Gann Stonespire walks the road north and south. If he's not at the arrow, follow the road.",tp=1},{t="Lok Orcbane is in the building at the top of the ramp.",w=1},{t="The Backstabber drops from Pathfinders and from Stalkers, which move in stealth.",tp=1},{t="Melee: when a Bael'dun Officer takes its defensive stance, its parry chance goes up 50% for 8 seconds.",tp=1},{t="Captain Gerogg Hammertoe, a rare level 27 elite, can be up inside Bael'dun Keep. Check before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dig Rats run inside the Bael Modan dig, among Bael'dun soldiers and riflemen of 23 to 26.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Explosive Stick of Gann on the flying machine up on its platform. It reaches 40 yards.",u=5021},{t="The Outraged Pillager is an elite and fights alongside Encroaching Soldiers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill the Encroaching Soldiers first, then let the fight reset to take the Pillager alone.",tp=1},{t="Slows and stuns work on the Outraged Pillager.",tp=1},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mangletooth is locked in the cage at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Hula'mahi has Flash Powder and the reagents for Instant Poison.",tp=1},{t="The Crate With Holes, Command Stick and Owner's Manual lie beside Mebok. Pick up all three.",w=1},{t="Isha Awak spawns at one of 4 spots along the coast. If she isn't here, try the next.",tp=1},{t="Isha Awak is level 27 and hits hard. Pull her at full health, away from the shore murlocs.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Clear the spiders around Besseleth first, or they join her fight.",tp=1},{t="Besseleth webs you in place for 10 seconds, so you can't run once she has you. Go in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Warlocks: keep Besseleth feared and let your damage-over-time spells wear her down.",tp=1},{t="XT:9 patrols the river's south bank and XT:4 the north bank.",tp=1},{t="Use the Toxic Fogger beneath the sky port platform. You don't need to climb up.",u=5638},{t="Venture Co. Machine Smiths summon Compact Harvest Reapers, so each fight gains an extra mob.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gerenzo is on the Venture Co. platform at the top of Windshear Crag. The climb starts on its east side.",w=1},{t="Sorrow Wing, a rare level 27 elite, can spawn at the lake's north end. Keep clear if it's up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Only plain Sap Beasts drop Stonetalon Sap. Corrosive Sap Beasts carry none.",tp=1},{t="Nal'taszar, a level 30 rare elite fey dragon west of the Peak, drops the scale too. Leave him be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dried Mirkweed grows in the water of Mirkfallon Lake.",w=1},{t="Sorrow Wing, a rare level 27 elite, can spawn at the lake's north end. Keep clear if it's up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Bloodfury Slayers can execute you under 20% health, and Ambushers cast a hard shock often. Pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sister Riven, a rare level 28 elite harpy, can be up at the south end of the vale. Steer clear if she is.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Bloodfury Ripper is elite, and attacking her pulls in harpies from far around.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill the harpies near her first. On her own she can be soloed.",tp=1},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is inside his cave at the top of Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Ashenvale Outrunners move in stealth, so you only see them up close.",tp=1},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The lake's north shore has Silverwind Refuge's level 40 guards, and a Wandering Protector (35 elite) walks it. Stay out on the water.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stand on the gazebo out on Mystral Lake's water for the scouting credit.",tp=1},{t="Tideress moves around the island and dives underwater. Circle the island if you can't see her.",tp=1},{t="Ursangous walks a patrol from Mystral Lake's west end up into the hills northwest. Follow it if he's not here.",tp=1},{t="A Wandering Protector, a level 35 elite, walks Ursangous's path too. Look before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stand under the gazebo at the Ruins of Stardust and fill the Empty Blue Waterskin.",u=7767},{t="Astranaar's guards are level 40 and attack the Horde. Keep to the arrow round the town's west side.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About 35 furbolgs of 23 to 24 fill Thistlefur Hold's tunnels. Clear the way to each chest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Troll Charms are in small chests on the ground inside Thistlefur Hold.",w=1},{t="Ruul Snowhoof is at the back of Thistlefur Hold, the cave on the northeast side of the village.",w=1},{t="Ruul Snowhoof not here? Another player has taken this quest. Ruul Snowhoof is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="3 furbolgs ambush you halfway along the tunnel, and 3 more at the village entrance. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Shadumbra walks the road through here, east to Raynewood Retreat. If she's not in sight, follow the road.",tp=1},{t="Two Cenarion Vindicators guard Ordanus, and each can summon 3 Treants. Pull the Vindicators one at a time first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keeper Ordanus stands up on the highest level of Raynewood Retreat's building.",w=1},{t="Ordanus roots you and casts Lightning Bolt, so there's no running from him. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Laughing Sisters, the dryads round Raynewood Retreat, drop the Etched Phial for The Sacred Flame.",tp=1},{t="A Wandering Protector, a level 35 elite, can patrol near the western approach to Night Run. Look before you go in.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Casters: any Felmusk satyr can silence you for 6 seconds, instantly (Overwhelming Stench). Heal early.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Etched Phial at the moonwell to fill it.",u=5867},{t="The Shadethicket treants are 25 to 27, above your level. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You can lead Sharptalon to the Splintertree or Forsaken Camp guards. Deal over half his damage or no claw drops.",tp=1},{t="Yama Snowhoof is inside the inn at Splintertree Post.",w=1},{t="Mitsuwa is inside the hut at Zoram'gar.",w=1},{t="The escort starts the moment you accept, and it's a hard one. Accept at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Muglash not here? Another player has taken this quest. Muglash is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Waves of naga come first, then Vorsha the Lasher, who hits very hard.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Let Muglash hold Vorsha for a few seconds before you join, so she stays on him.",tp=1},{t="Look for the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-handed axe with +12 Strength. Delgo has few, so it may be sold out.",tp=1},{t="Melor Stonehoof is on the Hunter Rise, over the bridge south of the inn.",w=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Miles Welsh is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Check the Heavy Recurve Bow here against the bow you're using.",tp=1},{t="Brine is in her hut, up above the watering hole.",w=1},{t="General Twinbraid's room, on the keep's lowest level, is packed tight. A careless pull brings several.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pull the room's mobs out to you one at a time before you open the Strongbox.",tp=1},{t="Brave Moonhorn stands at the top of the Great Lift, on the Barrens side.",w=1},{t="The Galak Messenger drops the note. His patrol begins at Splithoof Crag, the centaur camp farther east.",tp=1},{t="The Great Lift goes down from here. Step on and off only while the platform is stopped: a fall from it kills.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Two level 30 Galak Flame Guards stand at the brazier. Go in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ancient Brazier sits at the far end of the cave in Splithoof Crag's cliff.",w=1},{t="Galak Scouts are the scarce ones and you need 12, so kill every Scout you pass.",tp=1},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="With Test of Faith in your log, leap from the very tip of the wooden platform. The fall becomes a teleport.",tp=1},{t="Jump only from the end of the planks. Anywhere else on the needle, it's a real fall.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stormheart, a level 30 elite, walks a long round through these kobold camps east of Freewind Post. Keep out of his way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Alien Egg spawns in one of three places, so it may not be at the first one you check.",tp=1},{t="Windcallers stun everyone within 10 yards for 4 sec, and Screeching Harpies silence for 8. Pull them singly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Grenka Bloodscreech is a tough kill on your own. Bring a group for her.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The foodstuffs call in pack after pack of harpies along with Grenka.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Stolen Freewind Supplies lie on the floor of Roguefeather Den, the harpy cave.",w=1},{t="Achellios the Banished, a level 31 rare centaur with hounds, and Rok'Alim the Pounder, a level 30 elite, roam the canyon between the harpies and Highperch.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Heartrazor, a level 32 rare elite, can be up near Pao'ka. Look before you climb.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pao'ka waits at the top of the path that climbs toward Highperch.",w=1},{t="Pao'ka Swiftmountain not here? Another player has taken this quest. Pao'ka Swiftmountain is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Three Highperch Wyverns spawn once Pao'ka is in the heart of Highperch.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Attack the easternmost wyvern and the other two vanish.",tp=1},{t="The Highperch Wyvern Eggs lie on the ground among the nests across the plateau.",w=1},{t="The Enraged Panther is a hard fight alone. Bring a friend, or open the cage at full health with cooldowns up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Panther Cage Key at the cage to let the Enraged Panther out.",u=12942},{t="Steelsnap has two hyenas with him, so he's a three-mob pull. Go in at full health or bring a friend.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Steelsnap walks this loop counter-clockwise. The arrow goes round the other way, so you meet him head-on.",tp=1},{t="Handing this in sends three Galak Assassins after Kanati. Be at full health first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Frost does nothing to Boiling and Scalding Elementals and Fire barely hurts them. Arcane works.",tp=1},{t="Scald hits for about 150 Fire damage and stuns for 4 sec. Steam Jet makes you miss far more. Pull these one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Incendia Agave grows round the pools, and some of it under the water.",w=1},{t="Melor Stonehoof is on the Hunter Rise, over the bridge south of the inn.",w=1},{t="Magatha Grimtotem is on the Elder Rise, right where the bridges from the central mesa land.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="Rok'Alim the Pounder roams a wide stretch of north-western Thousand Needles, so expect a search.",tp=1},{t="Secret Note #1 is in a Document Chest on top of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",w=1},{t="Secret Note #2 is in the Document Chest in the big tent.",w=1},{t="Secret Note #3 is in the Document Chest in the eastern plateau's tent.",w=1},{t="Clear the Grimtotems around the fire before you light it. Lighting it brings out Arikara.",tp=1},{t="Use the Incendia Powder at the Sacred Fire of Life to light it.",u=12785},{t="The Sacred Fire of Life is on the north-eastern plateau, at the top of the winding path.",w=1},{t="Lakota Windsong not here? Another player has taken this quest. Lakota Windsong is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Two Grimtotems spawn at every platform Lakota reaches.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Run ahead of Lakota and clear the respawns on the next platform before she gets there.",tp=1},{t="If the escort goes wrong, run back the way you came. It fails and you get out alive.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="The Shimmering Flats are 31 to 35, and Vile Sting, a rare elite scorpid of 35, roams them. Keep to the road to the Raceway.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stormheart, a level 30 elite, walks a long round through these kobold camps east of Freewind Post. Keep out of his way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Just the way there. Go any way you like.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Part of the Shaman water chain, which runs across several zones. Take it if you want to finish the chain.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="This chain (The Affray, then The Windwatcher) ends in Berserker Stance.",tp=1},{t="Affray Challengers come one at a time, back to back, before Big Will. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The fight starts when you step onto the grate just north of Klannoc.",w=1},{t="Craven Drok walks around the Cleft of Shadow rather than standing in one spot.",tp=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Keldran stands by Orgrimmar's western exit.",w=1},{t="Use the Withered Scarf at the Summoning Circle south of Gan'rul, then kill the incubus.",u=190187},{t="Chief Hawkwind is inside his hut, a short walk north-west of Grull.",w=1},{t="You start with no money. Sell some Plainstrider loot, then come back for Battle Shout.",tp=1},{t="Rockbiter Weapon costs a little, and you start broke. Sell some loot first.",tp=1},{t="The Water Pitcher is on the well itself, a few steps behind Greatmother Hawkwind.",w=1},{t="Chief Hawkwind is inside his hut, a short walk north-west of Grull.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 10 minutes. Light the incense before anything else."},{t="Battleboars (level 3-4) roam the hills round the shrine. Look for one near the fire before you click it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Brave Windfeather walks a short round through the camp, so look around if she isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle waits inside the biggest hut of the Bristleback camp.",w=1},{t="The way into Brambleblade Ravine is a short cave just east of where the Battleboars graze.",tp=1},{t="The Dirt-stained Map lies on the ground just inside the cave on the ravine's south side.",w=1},{t="Brave Windfeather walks a short round through the camp, so look around if she isn't at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Chief Hawkwind is inside his hut, a short walk north-west of Grull.",w=1},{t="At Kodo Rock, drink the Earth Sapta to call up the Minor Manifestation of Earth.",u=6635},{t="Antur Fallow stands at the arch west of Camp Narache. Take the road south out of the camp and round the crater to him.",w=1},{t="Brave Wildrunner walks a short patrol in Bloodhoof Village.",tp=1},{t="Type /sit beside Kaga's campfire. Boosted Rest, the buff it asks for, shows after about a minute.",tp=1},{t="No credit after sitting? Abandon the quest, take it again from Kaga and sit back down.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Novice Warriors stand just east of Krang. Talk to one to start a bout.",tp=1},{t="Ambercorns lie under trees. The Well Stones are on the ground by the Winterhoof Water Well.",tp=1},{t="Use the Tender Strider Meat near Kyle the Frenzied, and he comes over to eat it.",u=287505},{t="Kyle runs laps round Bloodhoof Village, clockwise. Wait on his path rather than chase him.",tp=1},{t="Use the Winterhoof Cleansing Totem beside the Winterhoof Water Well.",u=5411},{t="Use the Tender Strider Meat near Kyle the Frenzied, and he comes over to eat it.",u=287505},{t="Kyle runs laps round Bloodhoof Village, clockwise. Wait on his path rather than chase him.",tp=1},{t="Snagglespear, a level 9 rare, roams near the Palemane camps. He's too much for you at this point. Keep clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A spirit wolf appears to lead the way. Following it is optional.",tp=1},{t="Morin Cloudstalker patrols the road east of Bloodhoof Village.",tp=1},{t="The Sealed Supply Crate is at the centre of the wrecked caravan.",w=1},{t="Perith Stormhoof is inside the cave at Palemane Rock. Lead him out to the cave exit.",w=1},{t="Snarlsnout (level 10) waits in the cave near Perith. Clear the gnolls first and fight him at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Perith Stormhoof not here? Another player has taken this quest. Perith Stormhoof is back a few minutes after they finish, so wait nearby.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Mull talks for a few seconds after Thunderhorn Totem. Thunderhorn Cleansing shows once he's done.",tp=1},{t="Brave Wildrunner walks a short round right beside Baine Bloodhoof.",w=1},{t="Tender Strider Meat drops from Adult Plainstriders.",tp=1},{t="Use the Tender Strider Meat near Kyle the Frenzied, and he comes over to eat it.",u=287505},{t="Kyle runs laps round Bloodhoof Village, clockwise. Wait on his path rather than chase him.",tp=1},{t="Set the Thunderhorn Cleansing Totem down by the well.",u=5415},{t="Venture Co. Laborers and Taskmasters (levels 6 to 8) work around the well. Clear the closest ones first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Bael'dun Appraisers (level 8-9) heal themselves and wounded allies. Kill them first.",tp=1},{t="Use the Prospector's Picks by the dig site's forge to smash them into Broken Tools.",u=4702},{t="Ghost Howl, a level 12 rare, walks the plain between the harpies and the Thunderhorn Water Well. Keep clear of him for now.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Seer Wiserunner is inside a cave. The Windfury harpy grounds start just south of it.",w=1},{t="The Water of the Seers has no use after this. Delete it to free the slot.",tp=1},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It takes 12 Light Leather. Skin it on the way or buy it at the Thunder Bluff Auction House.",tp=1},{t="Use the Bundle of Herbs from your bags. It combines all four parts into Prepared Incense.",u=278079},{t="Hunter's Rise is a sheer mesa and a fall from it can kill. Stand back from the edge.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sprinkle the Prepared Incense at the burner on the south edge of Hunter's Rise.",u=278078},{t="The Interlopers are level 9 and 10, a step above you, and Thornstarter Igleg (level 12) stands by the Ancestral Spirit. Pull the Interlopers one at a time, away from him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Thornstarter Igleg (level 12) stands a few steps from the Ancestral Spirit. Look for him before you walk up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The four parts drop from wolves, cougars, plainstriders and swoops all over Mulgore. Loot as you go.",tp=1},{t="Leftover Prospector's Picks are useless after this turn-in. Delete them.",tp=1},{t="Mull talks for a few seconds after the cleansing. Wildmane Totem shows once he's done.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Cast the Taming Rod from as far away as it reaches, so the cast ends before the beast gets to you.",u=15914},{t="Tame a Prairie Stalker with the rod, cast from as far off as it reaches.",u=15915},{t="Ghost Howl, a level 12 rare, walks the plain between the harpies and the Thunderhorn Water Well. Keep clear of him for now.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Swoop's knockdown interrupts the rod. Use it again right away.",tp=1},{t="If the rod runs out of charges, abandon the quest and take it again for a new one.",tp=1},{t="Tame a Swoop with the rod, cast from as far off as it reaches.",u=15916},{t="Morin Cloudstalker walks the road east of Bloodhoof. Look along it if he isn't at the arrow.",w=1},{t="Herak the Pillager is level 11, and Stormherald Ukta (level 12) stands just north of him. Pull Herak on his own.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Hunters: once you can tame, a Prairie Wolf Alpha teaches your pet Bite (Rank 2).",tp=1},{t="The Venture Co. stand in tight groups at the mine and inside it. Pull them one at a time; inside there's little room to run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Follow the mine's right-hand (east) wall to reach Supervisor Fizsprocket.",tp=1},{t="Fizsprocket (level 12) is deep in the mine among Workers and Supervisors. A bad pull in there is hard to run from.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supervisor Fizsprocket drops the Mulgore Expansion Plans. Right-click them to start this.",tp=1},{t="The carts stand inside the Venture Co. mine and in the camp past its far end. Inside, keep to the upper ledges.",w=1},{t="The Venture Co. Clearclutter, an elite shredder (level 12), works the camp past the mine's far end. Keep away from it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Morin Cloudstalker walks the road east of Bloodhoof. Look along it if he isn't at the arrow.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Thunderheads (20 to 21) and Stormsnouts (18 to 19) graze just outside Camp Taurajo. Stay on the road into the camp.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Everything off this road is level 16 to 19, and Razormane raiders walk it. Keep moving, and run back to Camp Taurajo if one turns on you.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Windfury Cones lie on the ground, mostly under or next to trees.",tp=1},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is on an upper floor in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="Ghost Howl drops the Demon Scarred Cloak that starts this quest.",tp=1},{t="Ghost Howl is a level 12 rare, much stronger than the animals around him. Pull him alone, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About 38 harpies (levels 9 to 11) crowd this camp. Pull from its edge, one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="With 8 Windfury Cones in your bags, grind them into Pine Salve with the Mortar and Pestle.",u=206176},{t="Set the Wildmane Cleansing Totem down by the well.",u=5416},{t="A Venture Co. camp sits just southwest of the well, with Enforcer Emilgund (level 11 rare). Use the totem and move on.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Arra'chea circles northern Mulgore clockwise. Wait on his path if he isn't in sight.",tp=1},{t="Arra'chea is level 11 and The Rake, a level 10 rare, prowls the same ground. Take them one at a time, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Clearclutter is an elite shredder (level 12). Bring two others, or leave this quest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Morin Cloudstalker walks the road east of Bloodhoof. Look along it if he isn't at the arrow.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Use the Cenarion Lunardust by the Moonkin Stone to call Lunaclaw.",u=15710},{t="Lunaclaw (level 12) uses Thrash every 10 seconds, two extra swings at once. Start the fight at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Thunderheads (level 20-21) roam around the Moonkin Stone. Check where they are before you call Lunaclaw.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Buy a Raw Brilliant Smallfish at the Auction House, or catch one in the pond north of Boarton.",tp=1},{t="Fillet the fish with the Knife Set to get the Fish Chunks.",u=206344},{t="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem is on Elder Rise, Thunder Bluff's north-east mesa.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The trail up to Telf Joolam is a narrow ledge, and a fall from it can kill. Take it slowly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Telf Joolam is on a mountaintop in western Durotar. A trail winds up to him.",tp=1},{t="Leave Telf Joolam by the same trail you came up.",tp=1},{t="The trail up to Telf Joolam is a narrow ledge. A fall from it can kill you.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Drink the Fire Sapta by the shrine so the Minor Manifestation of Fire shows itself.",u=6636},{t="The Dormant Flame's brazier sits atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame, north-east of Telf.",w=1},{t="Leave Telf Joolam by the same trail you came up.",tp=1},{t="Austil de Mon is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="The Maggot Eye poster is inside the Brill town hall.",w=1},{t="Ulag the Cleaver is level 11 and hits hard. Call him at full health with food ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Cursed Darkhounds roam among the ones you need, and they're higher level. Look around before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keep the Slumber Sand from this quest for the day a pull goes wrong.",tp=1},{t="Riptear, a level 13 elite, wanders the west end of Venomweb Vale. Keep to the spiders on its east and south side, and watch for it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Captured Mountaineer is in the inn cellar, in the same room as the Zealot.",w=1},{t="Coleman Farthing is inside the Brill inn.",w=1},{t="Deathstalker Erland isn't always at his post. If he's gone, wait for him to come back.",tp=1},{t="Deathstalker Erland not here? Another player has taken this quest. Deathstalker Erland is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Worgs ambush the escort, sometimes several on the same spot. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Eat and drink in each lull between worg attacks.",tp=1},{t="Vile Fin Shredders and Tidehunters on the shore east of here drop Murloc Eyes. Keep 3 for Quinn's Wild Eyes.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) has been seen on the road at the north end of this loop. Keep clear of it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dusty Spellbooks lie upstairs in the house at Valgan's Field. The Remedy of Arugal is in them.",w=1},{t="Quinn Yorick is upstairs in the house at the Ivar Patch.",w=1},{t="Fear doesn't work on the Rot Hide gnolls here.",tp=1},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 25 elite) roams from The Dead Field south to the Moonrage gnolls. Give it a wide berth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) can wander through here. Watch for it and keep clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krethis Shadowspinner (level 15 rare) shields herself and shocks hard. Nothing here needs her, so leave her alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Moonrage Darksouls (level 13-14) enrage when they get low. Keep a cooldown for the end of the fight.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) has been seen among the Moonrage here. Look around before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Quinn Yorick is upstairs in the house at the Ivar Patch.",w=1},{t="Ivar the Foul waits in the barn with two Ravenclaw Slaves. One walks out on a short patrol, so pull it alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ravenclaw Slaves can't be feared.",tp=1},{t="Clear the mobs standing in front of the barn before you go in.",tp=1},{t="Hands of Ravenclaw (up to level 16) stand around the ferry dock and stun melee for 5 seconds. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Corpse Laden Boat is tied up alongside the ferry dock. Click it.",w=1},{t="Dalaran Apprentices (level 13-14) guard the crate. They cast Frostbolt and run when hurt.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Draw the apprentices away one at a time, then open the crate.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Timed: 5 minutes. Walk straight to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium, across the slime canal."},{t="Doctor Martin Felben is in the Apothecarium, over the slime canal.",w=1},{t="Master Apothecary Faranell is in the Apothecarium, with Apothecary Zinge beside him.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Grimson the Pale is inside the Deep Elem Mine, past its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine is full of Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls (13-14). Clear the way in one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Moonrage Bloodhowlers (15-16) stand with Darksouls at the mine's mouth. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dalaran Conjurors and Warders (16-18) hold Ambermill's east end. Keep to the Protectors and Mages west of them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Apothecary Berard is upstairs in Pyrewood's inn. The journal is in Berard's Bookshelf beside him.",w=1},{t="Berard is a level 16 elite, and every villager around him is an elite too. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Deathstalker Faerleia waits inside Pyrewood's chapel.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The council is eight elite councilmen and Lord Mayor Morrison, a level 15 elite. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Pyrewood villager is an elite of 14-15. Take them on with a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) has been seen among the Moonrage here. Look around before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Vile Fin Lakestalkers and Oracles of 18 to 19 walk the lake shore south-east of here. Leave them be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Outside the keep the Rot Hides are 16 to 18, inside 18 to 19 with Thule Ravenclaw (24 elite), and Snarlmane, a level 23 rare, roams the island. Pull one at a time at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shallow Grave is just east of Fenris Keep's walls.",w=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Thork and Darsok Swiftdagger stand at the top of the Crossroads tower.",w=1},{t="The keg spawns in several spots across the Barrens. If it isn't here, grab it when you pass another.",tp=1},{t="Thork is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="The supply crates spawn in several places, so one may not be where the arrow points.",tp=1},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Root Samples come from gathering Barrens herbs: Peacebloom, Silverleaf, Earthroot, Mageroyal, Briarthorn, Bruiseweed.",tp=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Baron Longshore can be at any of the Southsea camps. Check each one.",tp=1},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Thork is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="The Bubbling Fissure is underwater in the pool. Dive down to it.",w=1},{t="Barak Kodobane hits very hard, and the Kolkar Wrangler at his side nets you and shoots from range.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Warriors: Vrang Wildgore also sells the Heavy Spiked Mace, a level 14 two-hander, in limited stock.",tp=1},{t="Two of the valves call out Venture Co. guards when shut, two for one and one for the other. Start each at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Tinkerer Sniggles is inside the building northeast of the control console.",w=1},{t="Darsok Swiftdagger is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="Chol'aruk is built for a group of five. Don't take him on alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Thatog is upstairs in his building.",w=1},{t="If Yelmak doesn't offer it yet, give it about 10 seconds.",tp=1},{t="Zor Lonetree is inside Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="Migi is out behind Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="Thra paces behind Grommash Hold and may not be right at the arrow.",w=1},{t="The Smooth Boulders are small orange rocks lying on the ground.",w=1},{t="The Smooth Boulders are few and slow to respawn, so other players can make this drag.",tp=1},{t="The Cats Eye Emerald is a rare drop. It can take 25 kills or more.",tp=1},{t="Boulder Lode Mine mobs stand close enough to pull in pairs, and the tunnels leave little room to run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Work the camp outside the mine entrance. Stay out of the tunnels.",w=1},{t="If the shredder isn't here, someone is on The Escape with it, and it's slow to come back.",tp=1},{t="Venture Co. goblins here are 14 to 18, and a few Lookouts and Patrollers of 22 to 23 stand just north-west. Pull one at a time and keep away from those.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supervisor Lugwizzle paces the platform, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Two level 19 rares, Foreman Grills and Sludge Beast, can be up around The Sludge Fen.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The escort starts the moment you accept. Rest to full first.",tp=1},{t="Wizzlecrank's Shredder not here? Another player has taken this quest. Wizzlecrank's Shredder is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Two Venture Co. Mercenaries jump in when the shredder reaches the high ground.",tp=1},{t="The quest completes after the shredder's closing lines, so stay until it's done talking.",tp=1},{t="If he doesn't show or another player tags him, abandon the quest and take it again from Sergra for a new horn.",tp=1},{t="Blow the Horn of Echeyakee at his lair to call him out.",u=10327},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws in the north run up to level 18 and use Thrash. Take your heads from Lashtails and Screechers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Takk the Leaper, a rare level 19 elite raptor, can spawn just east of the Sludge Fen. Leave him be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Witchwing Slayers cast Execute, a heavy hit once you're under 20% health. Keep your health up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Witchwing Ambushers patrol in stealth, so one can join a fight without warning.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Darsok Swiftdagger is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="The Bubbling Fissure is underwater, on the lakebed in the middle of the oasis.",w=1},{t="Each Kolkar killed at the oasis can bring out Verog. When it's crowded, wait at his spawn point.",tp=1},{t="Laden Mushrooms grow at The Forgotten Pools and at The Stagnant Oasis.",tp=1},{t="Each nest (blue, red and yellow) takes one Sunscale Feather, which the Scytheclaws drop.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws are level 16-18 and Thrash for two extra hits. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Beaten Corpse lies on the ground at a small outpost beside the road south of the Crossroads.",w=1},{t="Mangletooth's Spirit of the Wind costs 10 Blood Shards and speeds you up for 5 minutes.",tp=1},{t="The Grimtotem camp is up a trail that climbs to a bonfire.",tp=1},{t="Kill all six Brutes before you talk to Kaya, so none are left to join her escort.",tp=1},{t="Grundig Darkcloud stands in front of the camp's main tent.",w=1},{t="Kaya Flathoof is indoors, next to Grundig Darkcloud's spot.",w=1},{t="Kaya Flathoof not here? Another player has taken this quest. Kaya Flathoof is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Three Grimtotems attack when Kaya reaches the bonfire. Start the escort at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stay right beside Kaya the whole way.",tp=1},{t="Xen'Zilla is inside a hut at Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Mor'rogal and Tsunaman stand together, up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks is in a small goblin hut, tucked behind a hill.",w=1},{t="Deepmoss Hatchlings can call a level 22 Deepmoss Matriarch into the fight. Kill them fast, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Deepmoss Eggs lie on the ground beside the trees.",w=1},{t="If you have First Aid, keep the Small Venom Sacs for Anti-Venom.",tp=1},{t="Venture Co. Operators are level 19-20. Pull them on their own, away from the Loggers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Xen'Zilla is inside a hut at Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Seereth talks for a few seconds after this hand-in. The Elder Crone and Shredding Machines show up once he's done.",tp=1},{t="Bristleback Geomancers are level 19-20, the toughest here. Take them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keep the Blood Shards the quilboars drop. Mangletooth at Camp Taurajo trades them for buffs.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws cast Thrash, two extra hits about every 10 seconds. Fight them at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Oasis Snapjaws are in the water as well as on the shore.",tp=1},{t="Humar the Pridelord, a rare level 23 elite lion, can be up among the lions north of Ratchet.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Zhevra drop the Fresh Zhevra Carcass that draws Ishamuhale out. It spoils 30 minutes after you loot it.",tp=1},{t="By the dead tree, use the Fresh Zhevra Carcass. Ishamuhale comes out to eat it.",u=10338},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Grazlix's Mighty Chain Pants are limited stock and a solid leg upgrade.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 45 minutes. The route takes it to Zamah in Thunder Bluff straight away."},{t="Magatha has a short scene after The Elder Crone. Forsaken Aid comes up once it ends.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Apothecary Zamah is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Clarice Foster is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Kill Lakota'mani for the Hoof of Lakota'mani, which starts this quest. He has four spawn points.",tp=1},{t="Lakota'mani is level 22, a hard fight at this point. Pull him only at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Chol'aruk is inside a cave in the Razormane hills east of the Crossroads.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="The Bauble Container lies on the lakebed and can be at any of several spots.",tp=1},{t="Swim on the surface until you're over the container, then dive straight down on one breath.",tp=1},{t="Carry the Shrine Bauble to the tree at the Shrine of Remulos and use it from your bags.",u=15877},{t="The Great Cat Spirit is on a hill above the bridge in southern Moonglade.",w=1},{t="Restless Spirits of 23 guard the relics and attack on sight. The statue's stealth wears off, so don't linger.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Each relic is a small orb beside a cat statue in a wall alcove. The Relic of the Claw is deepest, past a bridge.",w=1},{t="Cast Teleport: Moonglade for the way back to Dendrite. It lands you much closer than the walk north.",tp=1},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Hezrul Bloodmark walks a loop round the lake, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Warlord Krom'zar is a level 20 elite and brings two or more Kolkar. Do this one in a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krom'zar is slow to arrive. Give it as much as 3 minutes.",tp=1},{t="You can lead Krom'zar in circles round Regthar Deathgate's building while you attack from range.",tp=1},{t="His banner falls to the ground when he dies. Loot that for the Piece of Krom'zar's Banner.",tp=1},{t="Serena is level 20 and stands among Witchwing Slayers and Windcallers. Clear round her before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Other players hunt the Savannah Patriarchs too, so expect to wait on respawns.",tp=1},{t="Walton's camp is up on the ridge above the Dry Hills. The trail climbs from the south-east.",w=1},{t="Mobs at the wrecked caravan stand close together. A pull often brings two or three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Terry Longdrink's marines attack after about a minute of talk. Wait behind the house so they don't all pull at once.",tp=1},{t="Vrang Wildgore fights at Walton's side, so Walton survives without your help.",tp=1},{t="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is inside his cave at the top of Malaka'jin, up the left-hand path.",w=1},{t="Mobs in the Boulderslide Ravine cave hit harder than their level and pull together easily.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gogger Rock Keepers' Earth Shock hits very hard. Kill them first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Everything is in the ravine's north cave. The explore credit comes only well inside it.",tp=1},{t="You get Resonite Crystals by attacking the crystals in the cave.",tp=1},{t="Goggeroc, a level 20 elite, waits deeper in the cave than the explore point. Don't go further than you need.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mor'rogal and Tsunaman stand together, up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="About 50 troggs of 16 to 18 fill the cave, and Goggeroc is a level 20 elite. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Enchanted Resonite Crystal on the Resonite Cask to call Goggeroc.",u=16603},{t="Mor'rogal stands up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks stands at a small goblin hut tucked behind a hill.",w=1},{t="Piznik is inside the Windshear Mine, west of its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine holds about 60 kobolds of 20 to 23, Geomancers among them. Clear a path in and out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kobolds hit Piznik in three waves over 5 minutes, up to four at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The waves land at about 0:15, 2:15 and 3:20, the second with two casters. Eat and drink in the gaps.",tp=1},{t="Ursangous, a strong level 25 mob, patrols the stag and bear grounds. Watch for him between pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Eye of Kilrogg follows you north-west to the main road. Talk to it there to hand in.",tp=1},{t="Mitsuwa and Marukai are inside a hut at Zoram'gar.",w=1},{t="Marukai is inside the hut at Zoram'gar, beside Mitsuwa.",w=1},{t="Ruga Ragetotem is inside a building at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Twitching Antennae expire 15 minutes after you loot them. Get them in one go and head straight back.",tp=1},{t="Northwatch Hold is packed with Theramore Marines and Preservers. Work in from the edge, one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gilthares Firebough not here? Another player has taken this quest. Gilthares Firebough is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Gilthares walks you up the coast past the Southsea camps to Ratchet. Stay close to him.",tp=1},{t="Bruuz is a level 20 elite in the water off Ratchet, hard for one player.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lead Bruuz to Ratchet's guards and they attack him. You need half his damage for the kill to count.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Brine is in her hut, up above the watering hole.",w=1},{t="Use the Empty Brown Waterskin at the watering hole below the hut.",u=7766},{t="Stormhides, Hecklefang Stalkers and Greater Thunderhawks of 22-24 roam the watering hole. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Strange Lockbox with the Aquatic Agility half sits in the Sludge Fen's water here.",tp=1},{t="Use the Samophlange Manual Cover once you hold the five pages.",u=11147},{t="Boss Copperplug, who drops the cover, is at the back of the Boulder Lode Mine.",w=1},{t="Open the Bundle of Reports in your bags to get the three Warsong Reports.",u=16783},{t="If Torek isn't here, someone just ran his escort. He's back within 5 minutes.",tp=1},{t="Torek not here? Another player has taken this quest. Torek is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Let Torek's raiders draw the Sentinels and Warriors before you join in.",tp=1},{t="Duriel Moonfire appears on the balcony after the building. Let Torek's group hit her first and she stays on them.",tp=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Magistrate Sevren is inside the town hall in Brill.",w=1},{t="Ride the lift down. Raleigh Andrean stands near the foot of the lifts.",w=1},{t="Yuriv's Tomb lies flat on the ground beside the Sepulcher, so it's easy to walk past.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is down in the Sepulcher's crypt.",w=1},{t="The Strange Lockbox with the Aquatic Endurance half lies in the sea here, off Silverpine's coast.",tp=1},{t="A Reef Shark, a level 21-22 elite, swims by this lockbox. Loot it while the shark is away.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Archmage Ataeric is inside Ambermill's town hall.",w=1},{t="Ataeric's hall is crowded with Dalaran casters. Draw them to the door a few at a time before you take him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Offering Stone stands deep in the cave, at its far end.",w=1},{t="Offering the soul at the stone spawns a hostile Tortured Soul. Clear the mobs around the stone first.",tp=1},{t="Stand at the Offering Stone and use the Tortured Soul from your bags.",u=210713},{t="Valdred Moray walks a patrol among packs of refugees. Wait until he's clear of them, then pull him alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The yeti cave north of the fields holds yetis of 30 to 32. Stay on the road.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Fill the Empty Red Waterskin from your bags at Tarren Mill's well, in the middle of town.",u=7768},{t="Ott sometimes has the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-hander with +12 Strength.",tp=1},{t="Jailor Marlgen carries the Burnished Gold Key for Tog'thar's lock. He stands by Tog'thar or below the tower.",tp=1},{t="Kris Legace sometimes has Stalking Pants and Wolf Bracers, leather for your legs and wrists.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Jailor Eston carries the Dull Iron Key for Drull's lock. He stands outside Tog'thar's barracks or beside Drull.",tp=1},{t="The tower a short way southwest of Durnholde Keep has more Shadow Mages, plus Syndicate Rogues and Watchmen.",tp=1},{t="Hillsbrad Farmers disarm you, which hurts melee most. Pull them one at a time.",tp=1},{t="Farmer Getz turns up in his house, his barn or out in the field.",w=1},{t="Farmer Ray is under the grapevine or inside his house, on either floor.",w=1},{t="Hunt the Starving Mountain Lions of the fields. The lions to the south-east and up in Alterac are 27 to 34.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="After a short scene Stanley turns into Enraged Stanley and attacks. Hand this in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stanley is at Farmer Ray's farm, at the north end of the fields.",w=1},{t="The farmers, farmhands, peasants and footmen of the fields all drop skulls. No need to go down to the mine.",tp=1},{t="Elder Gray Bears (25-26) and Elder Moss Creepers (26-27) outlevel the rest here. Leave them alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Giant Moss Creepers, 24 to 25, drop Creeper Ichor as well.",tp=1},{t="Masoj is out among level 26 to 28 lions, moss creepers and gnolls. Go in slowly and pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="We don't know yet which peaks the three Apothecary Vials go on. If you place them, tell us where each one is.",a=1},{t="It sends you up three peaks around Hillsbrad. A long climb for its XP.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It sends you up three peaks around Hillsbrad. A long climb for its XP.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) can wander through here. Watch for it and keep clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shallow Grave is just east of Fenris Keep's walls.",w=1},{t="Thule Ravenclaw waits in a large hall inside Fenris Keep.",w=1},{t="Thule is a level 24 elite who calls a minion back and hexes you. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dusty Shelf is in the keep's north-west tower. Turn left at the top of the first stairs.",w=1},{t="Fenris Keep is full of Rot Hides of 18-19, with Thule Ravenclaw (24 elite) among them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is down in the Sepulcher's crypt.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Raleigh Andrean stands near the foot of the lifts.",w=1},{t="Master Apothecary Faranell is in the Apothecarium, with Apothecary Zinge beside him.",w=1},{t="With both halves in your bags, join them at the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade.",u=15883},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs.",w=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is in the Pools of Vision, the cave under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Check the Heavy Recurve Bow here against the bow you're using.",tp=1},{t="Look for the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-handed axe with +12 Strength. Delgo has few, so it may be sold out.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mangletooth swaps Blood Shards for buffs. Spirit of the Wind gives 5 minutes of extra run speed.",tp=1},{t="Mangletooth is locked in the cage at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Owatanka is a blue thunder lizard that roams east of Camp Taurajo.",tp=1},{t="Owatanka is level 24 and hits hard. Pull him only at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Owatanka drops Owatanka's Tailspike, which starts this quest. He has four spawn points.",tp=1},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. If it isn't up, carry on; this step waits for its head.",tp=1},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Aean Swiftriver, a level 26 rare elite, can be up among the mounds. Keep well clear of him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Washte Pawne is a red wind serpent with 4 spawn spots south of Camp Taurajo. If he isn't up, move on.",tp=1},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Brine is in her hut, up above the watering hole.",w=1},{t="Gann Stonespire walks the road north and south. If he's not at the arrow, follow the road.",tp=1},{t="Lok Orcbane is in the building at the top of the ramp.",w=1},{t="The Backstabber drops from Pathfinders and from Stalkers, which move in stealth.",tp=1},{t="Melee: when a Bael'dun Officer takes its defensive stance, its parry chance goes up 50% for 8 seconds.",tp=1},{t="Captain Gerogg Hammertoe, a rare level 27 elite, can be up inside Bael'dun Keep. Check before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dig Rats run inside the Bael Modan dig, among Bael'dun soldiers and riflemen of 23 to 26.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Explosive Stick of Gann on the flying machine up on its platform. It reaches 40 yards.",u=5021},{t="The Outraged Pillager is an elite and fights alongside Encroaching Soldiers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill the Encroaching Soldiers first, then let the fight reset to take the Pillager alone.",tp=1},{t="Slows and stuns work on the Outraged Pillager.",tp=1},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mangletooth is locked in the cage at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="The Crate With Holes, Command Stick and Owner's Manual lie beside Mebok. Pick up all three.",w=1},{t="Isha Awak spawns at one of 4 spots along the coast. If she isn't here, try the next.",tp=1},{t="Isha Awak is level 27 and hits hard. Pull her at full health, away from the shore murlocs.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Clear the spiders around Besseleth first, or they join her fight.",tp=1},{t="Besseleth webs you in place for 10 seconds, so you can't run once she has you. Go in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Warlocks: keep Besseleth feared and let your damage-over-time spells wear her down.",tp=1},{t="XT:9 patrols the river's south bank and XT:4 the north bank.",tp=1},{t="Use the Toxic Fogger beneath the sky port platform. You don't need to climb up.",u=5638},{t="Venture Co. Machine Smiths summon Compact Harvest Reapers, so each fight gains an extra mob.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gerenzo is on the Venture Co. platform at the top of Windshear Crag. The climb starts on its east side.",w=1},{t="Sorrow Wing, a rare level 27 elite, can spawn at the lake's north end. Keep clear if it's up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Only plain Sap Beasts drop Stonetalon Sap. Corrosive Sap Beasts carry none.",tp=1},{t="Nal'taszar, a level 30 rare elite fey dragon west of the Peak, drops the scale too. Leave him be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dried Mirkweed grows in the water of Mirkfallon Lake.",w=1},{t="Sorrow Wing, a rare level 27 elite, can spawn at the lake's north end. Keep clear if it's up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Bloodfury Slayers can execute you under 20% health, and Ambushers cast a hard shock often. Pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sister Riven, a rare level 28 elite harpy, can be up at the south end of the vale. Steer clear if she is.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Bloodfury Ripper is elite, and attacking her pulls in harpies from far around.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill the harpies near her first. On her own she can be soloed.",tp=1},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is inside his cave at the top of Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Ashenvale Outrunners move in stealth, so you only see them up close.",tp=1},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The lake's north shore has Silverwind Refuge's level 40 guards, and a Wandering Protector (35 elite) walks it. Stay out on the water.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stand on the gazebo out on Mystral Lake's water for the scouting credit.",tp=1},{t="Tideress moves around the island and dives underwater. Circle the island if you can't see her.",tp=1},{t="Ursangous walks a patrol from Mystral Lake's west end up into the hills northwest. Follow it if he's not here.",tp=1},{t="A Wandering Protector, a level 35 elite, walks Ursangous's path too. Look before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stand under the gazebo at the Ruins of Stardust and fill the Empty Blue Waterskin.",u=7767},{t="Astranaar's guards are level 40 and attack the Horde. Keep to the arrow round the town's west side.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About 35 furbolgs of 23 to 24 fill Thistlefur Hold's tunnels. Clear the way to each chest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Troll Charms are in small chests on the ground inside Thistlefur Hold.",w=1},{t="Ruul Snowhoof is at the back of Thistlefur Hold, the cave on the northeast side of the village.",w=1},{t="Ruul Snowhoof not here? Another player has taken this quest. Ruul Snowhoof is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="3 furbolgs ambush you halfway along the tunnel, and 3 more at the village entrance. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Shadumbra walks the road through here, east to Raynewood Retreat. If she's not in sight, follow the road.",tp=1},{t="Two Cenarion Vindicators guard Ordanus, and each can summon 3 Treants. Pull the Vindicators one at a time first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keeper Ordanus stands up on the highest level of Raynewood Retreat's building.",w=1},{t="Ordanus roots you and casts Lightning Bolt, so there's no running from him. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Laughing Sisters, the dryads round Raynewood Retreat, drop the Etched Phial for The Sacred Flame.",tp=1},{t="A Wandering Protector, a level 35 elite, can patrol near the western approach to Night Run. Look before you go in.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Casters: any Felmusk satyr can silence you for 6 seconds, instantly (Overwhelming Stench). Heal early.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Etched Phial at the moonwell to fill it.",u=5867},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You can lead Sharptalon to the Splintertree or Forsaken Camp guards. Deal over half his damage or no claw drops.",tp=1},{t="Yama Snowhoof is inside the inn at Splintertree Post.",w=1},{t="Mitsuwa is inside the hut at Zoram'gar.",w=1},{t="The escort starts the moment you accept, and it's a hard one. Accept at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Muglash not here? Another player has taken this quest. Muglash is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Waves of naga come first, then Vorsha the Lasher, who hits very hard.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Let Muglash hold Vorsha for a few seconds before you join, so she stays on him.",tp=1},{t="Look for the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-handed axe with +12 Strength. Delgo has few, so it may be sold out.",tp=1},{t="Melor Stonehoof is on the Hunter Rise, over the bridge south of the inn.",w=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Brine is in her hut, up above the watering hole.",w=1},{t="General Twinbraid's room, on the keep's lowest level, is packed tight. A careless pull brings several.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pull the room's mobs out to you one at a time before you open the Strongbox.",tp=1},{t="Brave Moonhorn stands at the top of the Great Lift, on the Barrens side.",w=1},{t="The Galak Messenger drops the note. His patrol begins at Splithoof Crag, the centaur camp farther east.",tp=1},{t="The Great Lift goes down from here. Step on and off only while the platform is stopped: a fall from it kills.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Two level 30 Galak Flame Guards stand at the brazier. Go in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ancient Brazier sits at the far end of the cave in Splithoof Crag's cliff.",w=1},{t="Galak Scouts are the scarce ones and you need 12, so kill every Scout you pass.",tp=1},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="With Test of Faith in your log, leap from the very tip of the wooden platform. The fall becomes a teleport.",tp=1},{t="Jump only from the end of the planks. Anywhere else on the needle, it's a real fall.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stormheart, a level 30 elite, walks a long round through these kobold camps east of Freewind Post. Keep out of his way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Alien Egg spawns in one of three places, so it may not be at the first one you check.",tp=1},{t="Windcallers stun everyone within 10 yards for 4 sec, and Screeching Harpies silence for 8. Pull them singly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Grenka Bloodscreech is a tough kill on your own. Bring a group for her.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The foodstuffs call in pack after pack of harpies along with Grenka.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Stolen Freewind Supplies lie on the floor of Roguefeather Den, the harpy cave.",w=1},{t="Achellios the Banished, a level 31 rare centaur with hounds, and Rok'Alim the Pounder, a level 30 elite, roam the canyon between the harpies and Highperch.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Heartrazor, a level 32 rare elite, can be up near Pao'ka. Look before you climb.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pao'ka waits at the top of the path that climbs toward Highperch.",w=1},{t="Pao'ka Swiftmountain not here? Another player has taken this quest. Pao'ka Swiftmountain is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Three Highperch Wyverns spawn once Pao'ka is in the heart of Highperch.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Attack the easternmost wyvern and the other two vanish.",tp=1},{t="The Highperch Wyvern Eggs lie on the ground among the nests across the plateau.",w=1},{t="The Enraged Panther is a hard fight alone. Bring a friend, or open the cage at full health with cooldowns up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Panther Cage Key at the cage to let the Enraged Panther out.",u=12942},{t="Steelsnap has two hyenas with him, so he's a three-mob pull. Go in at full health or bring a friend.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Steelsnap walks this loop counter-clockwise. The arrow goes round the other way, so you meet him head-on.",tp=1},{t="Handing this in sends three Galak Assassins after Kanati. Be at full health first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Frost does nothing to Boiling and Scalding Elementals and Fire barely hurts them. Arcane works.",tp=1},{t="Scald hits for about 150 Fire damage and stuns for 4 sec. Steam Jet makes you miss far more. Pull these one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Incendia Agave grows round the pools, and some of it under the water.",w=1},{t="Melor Stonehoof is on the Hunter Rise, over the bridge south of the inn.",w=1},{t="Magatha Grimtotem is on the Elder Rise, right where the bridges from the central mesa land.",w=1},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="Rok'Alim the Pounder roams a wide stretch of north-western Thousand Needles, so expect a search.",tp=1},{t="Secret Note #1 is in a Document Chest on top of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",w=1},{t="Secret Note #2 is in the Document Chest in the big tent.",w=1},{t="Secret Note #3 is in the Document Chest in the eastern plateau's tent.",w=1},{t="Clear the Grimtotems around the fire before you light it. Lighting it brings out Arikara.",tp=1},{t="Use the Incendia Powder at the Sacred Fire of Life to light it.",u=12785},{t="The Sacred Fire of Life is on the north-eastern plateau, at the top of the winding path.",w=1},{t="Lakota Windsong not here? Another player has taken this quest. Lakota Windsong is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Two Grimtotems spawn at every platform Lakota reaches.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Run ahead of Lakota and clear the respawns on the next platform before she gets there.",tp=1},{t="If the escort goes wrong, run back the way you came. It fails and you get out alive.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="The Shimmering Flats are 31 to 35, and Vile Sting, a rare elite scorpid of 35, roams them. Keep to the road to the Raceway.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stormheart, a level 30 elite, walks a long round through these kobold camps east of Freewind Post. Keep out of his way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Just the way there. Go any way you like.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Part of the Shaman water chain, which runs across several zones. Take it if you want to finish the chain.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="This chain (The Affray, then The Windwatcher) ends in Berserker Stance.",tp=1},{t="Affray Challengers come one at a time, back to back, before Big Will. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The fight starts when you step onto the grate just north of Klannoc.",w=1},{t="Craven Drok walks around the Cleft of Shadow rather than standing in one spot.",tp=1},{t="Keldran stands by Orgrimmar's western exit.",w=1},{t="Hold Walk on Air for now. Falling With Style needs it soon, and it takes a minute and a half to come back.",tp=1},{t="Blademaster Ren stands inside the watchtower.",w=1},{t="Halaan Hawk-Eye waits atop the watchtower. Take the spiral stairs up.",w=1},{t="Halaan's gift shows you the distant pylon. Move or press Escape to end the view.",tp=1},{t="Myriaal Mistwake stands on the watchtower's top floor, by its ledge.",w=1},{t="A hop on flat ground counts as well, so there's no need to drop from the tower.",tp=1},{t="Xyton Silverwind is in the great tree behind Rorian, at ground level.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Blademaster Ren stands inside the watchtower.",w=1},{t="Akeri Duskblade stands inside the watchtower.",w=1},{t="Cirrusfly Soldiers swarm around the queen. Clear the nearest ones before you pull her.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Skysight is your racial, in your spellbook. Cast it at the convergence the arrow points to (half a second).",tp=1},{t="Next to an Elemental Convergence, Skysight gives 10% run speed for 15 minutes. Elsewhere, 30 seconds.",tp=1},{t="There are Elemental Convergences all over the island. Recast Skysight whenever you pass one.",tp=1},{t="Shamans: the Signet of Akir for Call of Earth drops from these mobs. Loot them all.",tp=1},{t="Drink the Earth Sapta at the Rise of Spirits, then talk to the Minor Manifestation of Earth.",u=6635},{t="Walk back down the south slope. The drop toward the standing stones is a long fall.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="One Raw Windstone can give several clusters. The 15 usually take about 10 stones, 15 at most.",tp=1},{t="With other players farming stones, camp one spawn or circle a few close ones instead of roaming.",tp=1},{t="You pick Herbalism, Mining or Skinning here. A later quest wants 20 skill, so gather as you travel.",tp=1},{t="Read only the book for the profession you picked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Read only the book for the profession you picked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Read only the book for the profession you picked.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Blademaster Ren stands inside the watchtower.",w=1},{t="Xyton Silverwind is in the great tree behind Rorian, at ground level.",w=1},{t="Urs'anah is inside the ursera cave west of Thendal Grove.",w=1},{t="Ursera Scavengers roam the cave around Urs'anah, who is level 5. Pull them away from her one by one.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Equip the weapon Valreaa gave you for Aggressive Encroachment before you fight the thugs.",tp=1},{t="Malduko Cloudcrush is upstairs, on the temple's top floor.",w=1},{t="Keep Small Eggs and Strider Meat. Restocking the Larders wants 3 eggs and 8 Strider Meat.",tp=1},{t="Coriella Calmbreeze runs the village inn.",w=1},{t="Elayaa Easewind trains hunters inside a house.",w=1},{t="Naeluna Swiftmend is inside a house.",w=1},{t="Take this one by clicking the bounty notice on the village's west side.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="An Elemental Convergence sits among the High Order Apprentices. Recast Skysight there.",tp=1},{t="'Badwind' Bennic is deep in the bandits' cave. Its mouth hides behind a waterfall.",w=1},{t="Bennic and his bandits are level 7. Fight them one at a time in the cave.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Elayaa Easewind trains hunters inside a house.",w=1},{t="Naeluna Swiftmend is inside a house.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="No credit after sitting? Abandon the quest, take it again from Raan and sit back down.",tp=1},{t="Sit for about a minute until Boosted Rest shows. Cooking or bandaging meanwhile won't reset the wait.",tp=1},{t="Cook Charred Wolf Meat while you wait. It raises Cooking and leaves your Small Eggs alone.",tp=1},{t="If Boosted Rest still hasn't come after a few minutes, relog and sit by the fire again.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="There's a single Hippogryph Matriarch. Kill her whenever you see her up.",tp=1},{t="The down feathers lie on the ground around the hippogryph nests.",w=1},{t="Vulgara the Insatiable is a level 8 elite. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Vulgara keeps to a hilltop just south-west of Shen'dar Village.",w=1},{t="She respawns slowly. If another group just killed her, expect a long wait.",tp=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 3 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Most well-fed foods also give 5% more kill XP for 15 minutes.",tp=1},{t="Naeluna Swiftmend is inside a house.",w=1},{t="Elayaa Easewind trains hunters inside a house.",w=1},{t="If the Mark of Akir is gone from your buffs, Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village gives it back.",tp=1},{t="Take the stairs inside the house. The Wardrobe stands one floor up.",w=1},{t="Then walk back toward town. A short scene on the way finishes the quest, even if someone else clicked first.",tp=1},{t="An Elemental Convergence lies on the way in from Missionary Jasaan. Recast Skysight there.",tp=1},{t="Equip the reward you picked from Among the Faithful: the Stained Ritual Dagger, Curved Scimitar or Windswept Shortbow.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Peacekeeper Vaaniel is the body lying by the road, northeast of the tower.",w=1},{t="Keep a bag slot free. This quest puts items in your bags.",tp=1},{t="Skypriest Aanders waits on the watchtower's roof, up the spiral stairs inside.",w=1},{t="Walk back down the stairs afterwards, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supply Caches, the small bags on the ground in Falaath, hold the supplies too.",tp=1},{t="Touch a drifting tornado for 40% run speed over 5 minutes. Dealing damage ends it.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Nyalah Brightfire stands inside a house.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Alvarion Windfield is upstairs, one floor up inside the house.",w=1},{t="Valennia Stormfist stands on the tower's top floor. Take the winding stairs up.",w=1},{t="Walk down the tower stairs, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ayessa Dawnsinger is inside the lodge near the skycutter dock.",w=1},{t="An Elemental Convergence is right here. Cast Skysight before you leave for 10% run speed.",tp=1},{t="Ayessa talks for about 75 seconds after you take this. Stay near her until it completes, then hand it in.",tp=1},{t="Nyalah Brightfire stands inside a house.",w=1},{t="Aamelia Windfield walks between two spots in Windfield Orchard, so she may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Hunters: tab to the Hungry Bandits early and Hunter's Mark them, then back off and shoot.",tp=1},{t="Hungry Bandits hide in stealth among the apple trees and open on you up close.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="An Elemental Convergence sits in the orchard. Cast Skysight there for 10% run speed.",tp=1},{t="The Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct drifts a short way east and west, so it may sit off the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Skypriest Faladiel, level 10, stands at the north-west edge of the Al'Aketh camp. Pull him alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Flutterfly that stays put after a swat wasn't caught. Swat it again.",tp=1},{t="Use the Flutterfly Swatter on a Flutterfly, then click the dust it leaves.",u=253666},{t="If you cross the orchard on the way up, stealthed bandits hide among its trees. Expect one to open on you.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Flutterfly Swatter is an uncommon weapon. Equip it if you have it.",tp=1},{t="The Bandit Highwaymen are up on the mountain northwest of the orchard.",w=1},{t="The construct parts lie on this ridge too. Pick them up while you're here.",tp=1},{t="Go down the way you came up. The ridge drops off sharply toward the orchard.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kuramaa knocks you back. Fight with open ground behind you.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kuramaa takes extra fire damage. Put Flametongue Weapon on before you click the stump.",tp=1},{t="When Aamelia stops during the scene, there's time to light a campfire and cook.",tp=1},{t="The Eternal Flame has about 5 minutes to reach Valanaar. Go straight there and avoid fights.",tp=1},{t="When Olariaan's talk ends (about 35 seconds), light your Torch of Eternal Flame at the Brazier of Offering.",u=277329},{t="Alvarion Windfield is upstairs, one floor up inside the house.",w=1},{t="Use the Taming Rod at its longest range, so the tame ends before the crawler gets to you.",u=267272},{t="Windsong Crawlers know Claw (Rank 2). Fight alongside your tamed one to learn it.",tp=1},{t="Use the Taming Rod while still at max range, so the tame ends before it reaches you.",u=267298},{t="Dismiss the last beast you tamed first, or the Taming Rod won't take a new one.",tp=1},{t="Use the Taming Rod while still at max range, so the tame ends before it reaches you.",u=264163},{t="Quel'dora is the pet trainer. Teach your pet Great Stamina and Natural Armor while you're here.",tp=1},{t="The Construct Parts lie deep in the Shriekling Den, on its lowest floor.",w=1},{t="The den's birds only notice you when you're close.",tp=1},{t="Afterwards, Walk on Air glides you from the lower peak down to Urs'endris. Only jump with it ready.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Abandoned Belongings are crates lying round the ruins.",tp=1},{t="Vayn Moongaze stands in the cave mouth northeast of Elegael Thornpaw.",w=1},{t="The same Al'Aketh drop the ears for Mercy Falls on Deaf Ears.",tp=1},{t="Shadowgale Acorns are small seeds on the ground, mostly at the foot of trees.",tp=1},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Look for Lady's Tear Moss on the trees.",tp=1},{t="Vayn Moongaze stands in the cave mouth northeast of Elegael Thornpaw.",w=1},{t="Stand still until each heal finishes. If you move, the druid may not count.",tp=1},{t="Commander Belguilos is indoors, one floor up in a house.",w=1},{t="Valennia Stormfist is up the tower stairs, beside Talaanis Shadowsong.",w=1},{t="Talaanis Shadowsong is up the tower stairs, beside Valennia Stormfist.",w=1},{t="Walk down the tower stairs, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Valennia Stormfist is up the tower stairs, beside Talaanis Shadowsong.",w=1},{t="Hyusaa Quickbreeze is up the steps of the Shrine of Akir.",w=1},{t="Valennia Stormfist is in the inner sanctum, up the spiral staircase.",w=1},{t="Baron Anvillaxx, level 13, and level 12 Malevolent Storms attack during the fight with Lorthuna.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Talaanis Shadowsong is up the tower stairs, beside Valennia Stormfist.",w=1},{t="Walk down the tower stairs, or step off the top only with Walk on Air ready.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Turak Runetotem is on the Elder Rise, across a bridge.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Thatog is upstairs in his building.",w=1},{t="If Yelmak doesn't offer it yet, give it about 10 seconds.",tp=1},{t="Migi is out behind Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="Thra paces behind Grommash Hold and may not be right at the arrow.",w=1},{t="The Smooth Boulders are small orange rocks lying on the ground.",w=1},{t="The Smooth Boulders are few and slow to respawn, so other players can make this drag.",tp=1},{t="Thrall is inside Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="Zor Lonetree is inside Grommash Hold.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="Deathstalker Erland isn't always at his post. If he's gone, wait for him to come back.",tp=1},{t="Deathstalker Erland not here? Another player has taken this quest. Deathstalker Erland is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Worgs ambush the escort, sometimes several on the same spot. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Eat and drink in each lull between worg attacks.",tp=1},{t="Vile Fin Shredders and Tidehunters on the shore east of here drop Murloc Eyes. Keep 3 for Quinn's Wild Eyes.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) has been seen on the road at the north end of this loop. Keep clear of it.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dusty Spellbooks lie upstairs in the house at Valgan's Field. The Remedy of Arugal is in them.",w=1},{t="Quinn Yorick is upstairs in the house at the Ivar Patch.",w=1},{t="Fear doesn't work on the Rot Hide gnolls here.",tp=1},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 25 elite) roams from The Dead Field south to the Moonrage gnolls. Give it a wide berth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) can wander through here. Watch for it and keep clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krethis Shadowspinner (level 15 rare) shields herself and shocks hard. Nothing here needs her, so leave her alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Moonrage Darksouls (level 13-14) enrage when they get low. Keep a cooldown for the end of the fight.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) has been seen among the Moonrage here. Look around before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Quinn Yorick is upstairs in the house at the Ivar Patch.",w=1},{t="Ivar the Foul waits in the barn with two Ravenclaw Slaves. One walks out on a short patrol, so pull it alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ravenclaw Slaves can't be feared.",tp=1},{t="Clear the mobs standing in front of the barn before you go in.",tp=1},{t="Hands of Ravenclaw (up to level 16) stand around the ferry dock and stun melee for 5 seconds. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Corpse Laden Boat is tied up alongside the ferry dock. Click it.",w=1},{t="Dalaran Apprentices (level 13-14) guard the crate. They cast Frostbolt and run when hurt.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Draw the apprentices away one at a time, then open the crate.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 5 minutes. Walk straight to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium, across the slime canal."},{t="Doctor Martin Felben is in the Apothecarium, over the slime canal.",w=1},{t="Master Apothecary Faranell is in the Apothecarium, with Apothecary Zinge beside him.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Grimson the Pale is inside the Deep Elem Mine, past its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine is full of Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls (13-14). Clear the way in one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Moonrage Bloodhowlers (15-16) stand with Darksouls at the mine's mouth. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dalaran Conjurors and Warders (16-18) hold Ambermill's east end. Keep to the Protectors and Mages west of them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Apothecary Berard is upstairs in Pyrewood's inn. The journal is in Berard's Bookshelf beside him.",w=1},{t="Berard is a level 16 elite, and every villager around him is an elite too. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Deathstalker Faerleia waits inside Pyrewood's chapel.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The council is eight elite councilmen and Lord Mayor Morrison, a level 15 elite. Bring a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Every Pyrewood villager is an elite of 14-15. Take them on with a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 4 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Outside the keep the Rot Hides are 16 to 18, inside 18 to 19 with Thule Ravenclaw (24 elite), and Snarlmane, a level 23 rare, roams the island. Pull one at a time at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shallow Grave is just east of Fenris Keep's walls.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Ruins of Lordaeron, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is inside the crypt. Its door faces west, beside Apothecary Renferrel.",w=1},{t="Mennet Carkad is in the Rogues' Quarter, near the rogue trainers.",w=1},{t="Thork and Darsok Swiftdagger stand at the top of the Crossroads tower.",w=1},{t="The keg spawns in several spots across the Barrens. If it isn't here, grab it when you pass another.",tp=1},{t="Thork is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="The supply crates spawn in several places, so one may not be where the arrow points.",tp=1},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Root Samples come from gathering Barrens herbs: Peacebloom, Silverleaf, Earthroot, Mageroyal, Briarthorn, Bruiseweed.",tp=1},{t="Baron Longshore can be at any of the Southsea camps. Check each one.",tp=1},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Thork is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="The Bubbling Fissure is underwater in the pool. Dive down to it.",w=1},{t="Barak Kodobane hits very hard, and the Kolkar Wrangler at his side nets you and shoots from range.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Warriors: Vrang Wildgore also sells the Heavy Spiked Mace, a level 14 two-hander, in limited stock.",tp=1},{t="Two of the valves call out Venture Co. guards when shut, two for one and one for the other. Start each at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Tinkerer Sniggles is inside the building northeast of the control console.",w=1},{t="Darsok Swiftdagger is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="Uthrok's Fine Longbow (level 14) is limited stock. When it's gone, the Reinforced Bow (level 16) is the backup.",tp=1},{t="Chol'aruk is built for a group of five. Don't take him on alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Cats Eye Emerald is a rare drop. It can take 25 kills or more.",tp=1},{t="Boulder Lode Mine mobs stand close enough to pull in pairs, and the tunnels leave little room to run.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Work the camp outside the mine entrance. Stay out of the tunnels.",w=1},{t="If the shredder isn't here, someone is on The Escape with it, and it's slow to come back.",tp=1},{t="Venture Co. goblins here are 14 to 18, and a few Lookouts and Patrollers of 22 to 23 stand just north-west. Pull one at a time and keep away from those.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Supervisor Lugwizzle paces the platform, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="Two level 19 rares, Foreman Grills and Sludge Beast, can be up around The Sludge Fen.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The escort starts the moment you accept. Rest to full first.",tp=1},{t="Wizzlecrank's Shredder not here? Another player has taken this quest. Wizzlecrank's Shredder is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Two Venture Co. Mercenaries jump in when the shredder reaches the high ground.",tp=1},{t="The quest completes after the shredder's closing lines, so stay until it's done talking.",tp=1},{t="If he doesn't show or another player tags him, abandon the quest and take it again from Sergra for a new horn.",tp=1},{t="Blow the Horn of Echeyakee at his lair to call him out.",u=10327},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws in the north run up to level 18 and use Thrash. Take your heads from Lashtails and Screechers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Takk the Leaper, a rare level 19 elite raptor, can spawn just east of the Sludge Fen. Leave him be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Witchwing Slayers cast Execute, a heavy hit once you're under 20% health. Keep your health up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Witchwing Ambushers patrol in stealth, so one can join a fight without warning.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Darsok Swiftdagger is up the Crossroads tower, at its very top.",w=1},{t="When Polly the parrot attacks, give her the E.C.A.C. from your bags.",u=7970},{t="The Jewel of the Southsea is on the ship's bottom deck. Opening it takes Lockpicking 70.",w=1},{t="Raise Lockpicking to 70 on the ship's second deck before you go down.",tp=1},{t="The Bubbling Fissure is underwater, on the lakebed in the middle of the oasis.",w=1},{t="Each Kolkar killed at the oasis can bring out Verog. When it's crowded, wait at his spawn point.",tp=1},{t="Laden Mushrooms grow at The Forgotten Pools and at The Stagnant Oasis.",tp=1},{t="Each nest (blue, red and yellow) takes one Sunscale Feather, which the Scytheclaws drop.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws are level 16-18 and Thrash for two extra hits. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Beaten Corpse lies on the ground at a small outpost beside the road south of the Crossroads.",w=1},{t="Mangletooth's Spirit of the Wind costs 10 Blood Shards and speeds you up for 5 minutes.",tp=1},{t="The Grimtotem camp is up a trail that climbs to a bonfire.",tp=1},{t="Kill all six Brutes before you talk to Kaya, so none are left to join her escort.",tp=1},{t="Grundig Darkcloud stands in front of the camp's main tent.",w=1},{t="Kaya Flathoof is indoors, next to Grundig Darkcloud's spot.",w=1},{t="Kaya Flathoof not here? Another player has taken this quest. Kaya Flathoof is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Three Grimtotems attack when Kaya reaches the bonfire. Start the escort at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stay right beside Kaya the whole way.",tp=1},{t="Xen'Zilla is inside a hut at Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Mor'rogal and Tsunaman stand together, up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks is in a small goblin hut, tucked behind a hill.",w=1},{t="Deepmoss Hatchlings can call a level 22 Deepmoss Matriarch into the fight. Kill them fast, at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Deepmoss Eggs lie on the ground beside the trees.",w=1},{t="If you have First Aid, keep the Small Venom Sacs for Anti-Venom.",tp=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Venture Co. Operators are level 19-20. Pull them on their own, away from the Loggers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Xen'Zilla is inside a hut at Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Seereth talks for a few seconds after this hand-in. The Elder Crone and Shredding Machines show up once he's done.",tp=1},{t="Bristleback Geomancers are level 19-20, the toughest here. Take them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keep the Blood Shards the quilboars drop. Mangletooth at Camp Taurajo trades them for buffs.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws cast Thrash, two extra hits about every 10 seconds. Fight them at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Oasis Snapjaws are in the water as well as on the shore.",tp=1},{t="Humar the Pridelord, a rare level 23 elite lion, can be up among the lions north of Ratchet.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Zhevra drop the Fresh Zhevra Carcass that draws Ishamuhale out. It spoils 30 minutes after you loot it.",tp=1},{t="By the dead tree, use the Fresh Zhevra Carcass. Ishamuhale comes out to eat it.",u=10338},{t="Gazlowe is on the top floor of his building in Ratchet.",w=1},{t="Grazlix's Mighty Chain Pants are limited stock and a solid leg upgrade.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Timed: 45 minutes. The route takes it to Zamah in Thunder Bluff straight away."},{t="Magatha has a short scene after The Elder Crone. Forsaken Aid comes up once it ends.",tp=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Clarice Foster is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Kill Lakota'mani for the Hoof of Lakota'mani, which starts this quest. He has four spawn points.",tp=1},{t="Lakota'mani is level 22, a hard fight at this point. Pull him only at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Aean Swiftriver, a level 26 rare elite, can be up among the mounds. Keep well clear of him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. If it isn't up, carry on; this step waits for its head.",tp=1},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Silithid Harvester spawns rarely. Its head starts this.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Hezrul Bloodmark walks a loop round the lake, so he may not be at the arrow.",tp=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Chol'aruk is inside a cave in the Razormane hills east of the Crossroads.",w=1},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A group quest: it's made for 5 players.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="The Bauble Container lies on the lakebed and can be at any of several spots.",tp=1},{t="Swim on the surface until you're over the container, then dive straight down on one breath.",tp=1},{t="Carry the Shrine Bauble to the tree at the Shrine of Remulos and use it from your bags.",u=15877},{t="Restless Spirits of 23 guard the relics and attack on sight. The statue's stealth wears off, so don't linger.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Each relic is a small orb beside a cat statue in a wall alcove. The Relic of the Claw is deepest, past a bridge.",w=1},{t="Cast Teleport: Moonglade for the way back to Dendrite. It lands you much closer than the walk north.",tp=1},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="Check the Heavy Recurve Bow here against the bow you're using.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Warlord Krom'zar is a level 20 elite and brings two or more Kolkar. Do this one in a group.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Krom'zar is slow to arrive. Give it as much as 3 minutes.",tp=1},{t="You can lead Krom'zar in circles round Regthar Deathgate's building while you attack from range.",tp=1},{t="His banner falls to the ground when he dies. Loot that for the Piece of Krom'zar's Banner.",tp=1},{t="Serena is level 20 and stands among Witchwing Slayers and Windcallers. Clear round her before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Other players hunt the Savannah Patriarchs too, so expect to wait on respawns.",tp=1},{t="Walton's camp is up on the ridge above the Dry Hills. The trail climbs from the south-east.",w=1},{t="Mobs at the wrecked caravan stand close together. A pull often brings two or three.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Terry Longdrink's marines attack after about a minute of talk. Wait behind the house so they don't all pull at once.",tp=1},{t="Vrang Wildgore fights at Walton's side, so Walton survives without your help.",tp=1},{t="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is inside his cave at the top of Malaka'jin, up the left-hand path.",w=1},{t="Mobs in the Boulderslide Ravine cave hit harder than their level and pull together easily.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gogger Rock Keepers' Earth Shock hits very hard. Kill them first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Everything is in the ravine's north cave. The explore credit comes only well inside it.",tp=1},{t="You get Resonite Crystals by attacking the crystals in the cave.",tp=1},{t="Goggeroc, a level 20 elite, waits deeper in the cave than the explore point. Don't go further than you need.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Mor'rogal and Tsunaman stand together, up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="About 50 troggs of 16 to 18 fill the cave, and Goggeroc is a level 20 elite. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Enchanted Resonite Crystal on the Resonite Cask to call Goggeroc.",u=16603},{t="Mor'rogal stands up the path that climbs from Sun Rock's east side.",w=1},{t="Ziz Fizziks stands at a small goblin hut tucked behind a hill.",w=1},{t="Piznik is inside the Windshear Mine, west of its mouth.",w=1},{t="The mine holds about 60 kobolds of 20 to 23, Geomancers among them. Clear a path in and out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kobolds hit Piznik in three waves over 5 minutes, up to four at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The waves land at about 0:15, 2:15 and 3:20, the second with two casters. Eat and drink in the gaps.",tp=1},{t="Ursangous, a strong level 25 mob, patrols the stag and bear grounds. Watch for him between pulls.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Eye of Kilrogg follows you north-west to the main road. Talk to it there to hand in.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mitsuwa and Marukai are inside a hut at Zoram'gar.",w=1},{t="Marukai is inside the hut at Zoram'gar, beside Mitsuwa.",w=1},{t="Ruga Ragetotem is inside a building at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Twitching Antennae expire 15 minutes after you loot them. Get them in one go and head straight back.",tp=1},{t="Northwatch Hold is packed with Theramore Marines and Preservers. Work in from the edge, one pull at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gilthares Firebough not here? Another player has taken this quest. Gilthares Firebough is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Gilthares walks you up the coast past the Southsea camps to Ratchet. Stay close to him.",tp=1},{t="Bruuz is a level 20 elite in the water off Ratchet, hard for one player.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Lead Bruuz to Ratchet's guards and they attack him. You need half his damage for the kill to count.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Brine is in her hut, up above the watering hole.",w=1},{t="Use the Empty Brown Waterskin at the watering hole below the hut.",u=7766},{t="Stormhides, Hecklefang Stalkers and Greater Thunderhawks of 22-24 roam the watering hole. Pull them one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Taskmaster Fizzule is a level 30 elite and attacks anyone close before he turns friendly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="From well away, target Fizzule, fire the Flare Gun twice, then type /salute. Talk to him once he's friendly.",u=8051},{t="Every Drone, Patroller and Lookout you need is inside the Venture Co. tower north of the Sludge Fen.",tp=1},{t="Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix, a level 23 elite, waits on the tower's top floor.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Open on Gallywix with Ambush for about half his health. Gouge him when you need energy back.",tp=1},{t="Keep Evasion, Thistle Tea and a healing potion for when the fight goes wrong.",tp=1},{t="Use the Samophlange Manual Cover once you hold the five pages.",u=11147},{t="Boss Copperplug, who drops the cover, is at the back of the Boulder Lode Mine.",w=1},{t="The Strange Lockbox with the Aquatic Agility half sits in the Sludge Fen's water here.",tp=1},{t="Open the Bundle of Reports in your bags to get the three Warsong Reports.",u=16783},{t="If Torek isn't here, someone just ran his escort. He's back within 5 minutes.",tp=1},{t="Torek not here? Another player has taken this quest. Torek is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Let Torek's raiders draw the Sentinels and Warriors before you join in.",tp=1},{t="Duriel Moonfire appears on the balcony after the building. Let Torek's group hit her first and she stays on them.",tp=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Instant Poison II needs 120 Poisons skill before Ormok can teach it.",tp=1},{t="Anti-Venom removes Touch of Zanzil. Left alone, it lasts 7 days.",tp=1},{t="Magistrate Sevren is inside the town hall in Brill.",w=1},{t="Ride the lift down. Raleigh Andrean stands near the foot of the lifts.",w=1},{t="Yuriv's Tomb lies flat on the ground beside the Sepulcher, so it's easy to walk past.",tp=1},{t="High Executor Hadrec is down in the Sepulcher's crypt.",w=1},{t="The Strange Lockbox with the Aquatic Endurance half lies in the sea here, off Silverpine's coast.",tp=1},{t="A Reef Shark, a level 21-22 elite, swims by this lockbox. Loot it while the shark is away.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Archmage Ataeric is inside Ambermill's town hall.",w=1},{t="Ataeric's hall is crowded with Dalaran casters. Draw them to the door a few at a time before you take him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Offering Stone stands deep in the cave, at its far end.",w=1},{t="Offering the soul at the stone spawns a hostile Tortured Soul. Clear the mobs around the stone first.",tp=1},{t="Stand at the Offering Stone and use the Tortured Soul from your bags.",u=210713},{t="Valdred Moray walks a patrol among packs of refugees. Wait until he's clear of them, then pull him alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The yeti cave north of the fields holds yetis of 30 to 32. Stay on the road.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Serge Hinott not here? Another player has taken this quest. Serge Hinott is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Hinott needs about half a minute to brew the cure. Wait beside him.",tp=1},{t="Use Hinott's Oil from your bags to wash off Touch of Zanzil.",u=8095},{t="Fill the Empty Red Waterskin from your bags at Tarren Mill's well, in the middle of town.",u=7768},{t="Ott sometimes has the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-hander with +12 Strength.",tp=1},{t="Jailor Marlgen carries the Burnished Gold Key for Tog'thar's lock. He stands by Tog'thar or below the tower.",tp=1},{t="Kris Legace sometimes has Stalking Pants and Wolf Bracers, leather for your legs and wrists.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Jailor Eston carries the Dull Iron Key for Drull's lock. He stands outside Tog'thar's barracks or beside Drull.",tp=1},{t="The tower a short way southwest of Durnholde Keep has more Shadow Mages, plus Syndicate Rogues and Watchmen.",tp=1},{t="Hillsbrad Farmers disarm you, which hurts melee most. Pull them one at a time.",tp=1},{t="Farmer Getz turns up in his house, his barn or out in the field.",w=1},{t="Farmer Ray is under the grapevine or inside his house, on either floor.",w=1},{t="Hunt the Starving Mountain Lions of the fields. The lions to the south-east and up in Alterac are 27 to 34.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="After a short scene Stanley turns into Enraged Stanley and attacks. Hand this in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stanley is at Farmer Ray's farm, at the north end of the fields.",w=1},{t="The farmers, farmhands, peasants and footmen of the fields all drop skulls. No need to go down to the mine.",tp=1},{t="Elder Gray Bears (25-26) and Elder Moss Creepers (26-27) outlevel the rest here. Leave them alone.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Giant Moss Creepers, 24 to 25, drop Creeper Ichor as well.",tp=1},{t="Masoj is out among level 26 to 28 lions, moss creepers and gnolls. Go in slowly and pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="We don't know yet which peaks the three Apothecary Vials go on. If you place them, tell us where each one is.",a=1},{t="It sends you up three peaks around Hillsbrad. A long climb for its XP.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It sends you up three peaks around Hillsbrad. A long climb for its XP.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Son of Arugal (level 24-25 elite) can wander through here. Watch for it and keep clear.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Shallow Grave is just east of Fenris Keep's walls.",w=1},{t="Thule Ravenclaw waits in a large hall inside Fenris Keep.",w=1},{t="Thule is a level 24 elite who calls a minion back and hexes you. Bring a partner.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dusty Shelf is in the keep's north-west tower. Turn left at the top of the first stairs.",w=1},{t="Fenris Keep is full of Rot Hides of 18-19, with Thule Ravenclaw (24 elite) among them.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="High Executor Hadrec is down in the Sepulcher's crypt.",w=1},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Raleigh Andrean stands near the foot of the lifts.",w=1},{t="Master Apothecary Faranell is in the Apothecarium, with Apothecary Zinge beside him.",w=1},{t="With both halves in your bags, join them at the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade.",u=15883},{t="Dendrite Starblaze is upstairs in Nighthaven.",w=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is in the Pools of Vision, the cave under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Check the Heavy Recurve Bow here against the bow you're using.",tp=1},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Look for the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-handed axe with +12 Strength. Delgo has few, so it may be sold out.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Wailing Caverns, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Mangletooth swaps Blood Shards for buffs. Spirit of the Wind gives 5 minutes of extra run speed.",tp=1},{t="Mangletooth is locked in the cage at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Owatanka is a blue thunder lizard that roams east of Camp Taurajo.",tp=1},{t="Owatanka is level 24 and hits hard. Pull him only at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Owatanka drops Owatanka's Tailspike, which starts this quest. He has four spawn points.",tp=1},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Washte Pawne is a red wind serpent with 4 spawn spots south of Camp Taurajo. If he isn't up, move on.",tp=1},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Brine is in her hut, up above the watering hole.",w=1},{t="Gann Stonespire walks the road north and south. If he's not at the arrow, follow the road.",tp=1},{t="Lok Orcbane is in the building at the top of the ramp.",w=1},{t="The Backstabber drops from Pathfinders and from Stalkers, which move in stealth.",tp=1},{t="Melee: when a Bael'dun Officer takes its defensive stance, its parry chance goes up 50% for 8 seconds.",tp=1},{t="Captain Gerogg Hammertoe, a rare level 27 elite, can be up inside Bael'dun Keep. Check before each pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dig Rats run inside the Bael Modan dig, among Bael'dun soldiers and riflemen of 23 to 26.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Explosive Stick of Gann on the flying machine up on its platform. It reaches 40 yards.",u=5021},{t="The Outraged Pillager is an elite and fights alongside Encroaching Soldiers.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill the Encroaching Soldiers first, then let the fight reset to take the Pillager alone.",tp=1},{t="Slows and stuns work on the Outraged Pillager.",tp=1},{t="Brontus, a level 27 elite kodo, roams here and drops the liver too. Take it from the plain kodos.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Mangletooth is locked in the cage at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="Hula'mahi has Flash Powder and the reagents for Instant Poison.",tp=1},{t="The Crate With Holes, Command Stick and Owner's Manual lie beside Mebok. Pick up all three.",w=1},{t="Isha Awak spawns at one of 4 spots along the coast. If she isn't here, try the next.",tp=1},{t="Isha Awak is level 27 and hits hard. Pull her at full health, away from the shore murlocs.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Clear the spiders around Besseleth first, or they join her fight.",tp=1},{t="Besseleth webs you in place for 10 seconds, so you can't run once she has you. Go in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="XT:9 patrols the river's south bank and XT:4 the north bank.",tp=1},{t="Use the Toxic Fogger beneath the sky port platform. You don't need to climb up.",u=5638},{t="Venture Co. Machine Smiths summon Compact Harvest Reapers, so each fight gains an extra mob.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Gerenzo is on the Venture Co. platform at the top of Windshear Crag. The climb starts on its east side.",w=1},{t="Sorrow Wing, a rare level 27 elite, can spawn at the lake's north end. Keep clear if it's up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Only plain Sap Beasts drop Stonetalon Sap. Corrosive Sap Beasts carry none.",tp=1},{t="Nal'taszar, a level 30 rare elite fey dragon west of the Peak, drops the scale too. Leave him be.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Dried Mirkweed grows in the water of Mirkfallon Lake.",w=1},{t="Sorrow Wing, a rare level 27 elite, can spawn at the lake's north end. Keep clear if it's up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Bloodfury Slayers can execute you under 20% health, and Ambushers cast a hard shock often. Pull one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sister Riven, a rare level 28 elite harpy, can be up at the south end of the vale. Steer clear if she is.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Jeeda is upstairs in Sun Rock Retreat's inn.",w=1},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Bloodfury Ripper is elite, and attacking her pulls in harpies from far around.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Kill the harpies near her first. On her own she can be soloed.",tp=1},{t="Use the Enchanted Gaea Seeds on each Gaea Dirt Mound in the Charred Vale.",u=16208},{t="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is inside his cave at the top of Malaka'jin.",w=1},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Ashenvale Outrunners move in stealth, so you only see them up close.",tp=1},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The lake's north shore has Silverwind Refuge's level 40 guards, and a Wandering Protector (35 elite) walks it. Stay out on the water.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stand on the gazebo out on Mystral Lake's water for the scouting credit.",tp=1},{t="Tideress moves around the island and dives underwater. Circle the island if you can't see her.",tp=1},{t="Ursangous walks a patrol from Mystral Lake's west end up into the hills northwest. Follow it if he's not here.",tp=1},{t="A Wandering Protector, a level 35 elite, walks Ursangous's path too. Look before you pull.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stand under the gazebo at the Ruins of Stardust and fill the Empty Blue Waterskin.",u=7767},{t="Astranaar's guards are level 40 and attack the Horde. Keep to the arrow round the town's west side.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="About 35 furbolgs of 23 to 24 fill Thistlefur Hold's tunnels. Clear the way to each chest.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Troll Charms are in small chests on the ground inside Thistlefur Hold.",w=1},{t="Ruul Snowhoof is at the back of Thistlefur Hold, the cave on the northeast side of the village.",w=1},{t="Ruul Snowhoof not here? Another player has taken this quest. Ruul Snowhoof is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="3 furbolgs ambush you halfway along the tunnel, and 3 more at the village entrance. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Shadumbra walks the road through here, east to Raynewood Retreat. If she's not in sight, follow the road.",tp=1},{t="Two Cenarion Vindicators guard Ordanus, and each can summon 3 Treants. Pull the Vindicators one at a time first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keeper Ordanus stands up on the highest level of Raynewood Retreat's building.",w=1},{t="Ordanus roots you and casts Lightning Bolt, so there's no running from him. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Laughing Sisters, the dryads round Raynewood Retreat, drop the Etched Phial for The Sacred Flame.",tp=1},{t="A Wandering Protector, a level 35 elite, can patrol near the western approach to Night Run. Look before you go in.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Casters: any Felmusk satyr can silence you for 6 seconds, instantly (Overwhelming Stench). Heal early.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Etched Phial at the moonwell to fill it.",u=5867},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Sharptalon is level 31 and walks a patrol path. Watch for him while you fight nearby.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="You can lead Sharptalon to the Splintertree or Forsaken Camp guards. Deal over half his damage or no claw drops.",tp=1},{t="Yama Snowhoof is inside the inn at Splintertree Post.",w=1},{t="Mitsuwa is inside the hut at Zoram'gar.",w=1},{t="The escort starts the moment you accept, and it's a hard one. Accept at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Muglash not here? Another player has taken this quest. Muglash is back about 1 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Waves of naga come first, then Vorsha the Lasher, who hits very hard.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Let Muglash hold Vorsha for a few seconds before you join, so she stays on him.",tp=1},{t="Look for the Merciless Axe, a level 26 two-handed axe with +12 Strength. Delgo has few, so it may be sold out.",tp=1},{t="Melor Stonehoof is on the Hunter Rise, over the bridge south of the inn.",w=1},{t="Boarton Shadetotem is stealthed. Walk right up to the arrow and he shows.",w=1},{t="Apothecary Zamah is down in the Pools of Vision, under the Spirit Rise.",w=1},{t="Check the Heavy Recurve Bow here against the bow you're using.",tp=1},{t="Brine is in her hut, up above the watering hole.",w=1},{t="General Twinbraid's room, on the keep's lowest level, is packed tight. A careless pull brings several.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pull the room's mobs out to you one at a time before you open the Strongbox.",tp=1},{t="Brave Moonhorn stands at the top of the Great Lift, on the Barrens side.",w=1},{t="The Galak Messenger drops the note. His patrol begins at Splithoof Crag, the centaur camp farther east.",tp=1},{t="The Great Lift goes down from here. Step on and off only while the platform is stopped: a fall from it kills.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Two level 30 Galak Flame Guards stand at the brazier. Go in at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Ancient Brazier sits at the far end of the cave in Splithoof Crag's cliff.",w=1},{t="Galak Scouts are the scarce ones and you need 12, so kill every Scout you pass.",tp=1},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="With Test of Faith in your log, leap from the very tip of the wooden platform. The fall becomes a teleport.",tp=1},{t="Jump only from the end of the planks. Anywhere else on the needle, it's a real fall.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stormheart, a level 30 elite, walks a long round through these kobold camps east of Freewind Post. Keep out of his way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Alien Egg spawns in one of three places, so it may not be at the first one you check.",tp=1},{t="Windcallers stun everyone within 10 yards for 4 sec, and Screeching Harpies silence for 8. Pull them singly.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Grenka Bloodscreech is a tough kill on your own. Bring a group for her.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The foodstuffs call in pack after pack of harpies along with Grenka.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The Stolen Freewind Supplies lie on the floor of Roguefeather Den, the harpy cave.",w=1},{t="Achellios the Banished, a level 31 rare centaur with hounds, and Rok'Alim the Pounder, a level 30 elite, roam the canyon between the harpies and Highperch.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Heartrazor, a level 32 rare elite, can be up near Pao'ka. Look before you climb.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Pao'ka waits at the top of the path that climbs toward Highperch.",w=1},{t="Pao'ka Swiftmountain not here? Another player has taken this quest. Pao'ka Swiftmountain is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Three Highperch Wyverns spawn once Pao'ka is in the heart of Highperch.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Attack the easternmost wyvern and the other two vanish.",tp=1},{t="The Highperch Wyvern Eggs lie on the ground among the nests across the plateau.",w=1},{t="The Enraged Panther is a hard fight alone. Bring a friend, or open the cage at full health with cooldowns up.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the Panther Cage Key at the cage to let the Enraged Panther out.",u=12942},{t="Steelsnap has two hyenas with him, so he's a three-mob pull. Go in at full health or bring a friend.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Steelsnap walks this loop counter-clockwise. The arrow goes round the other way, so you meet him head-on.",tp=1},{t="Handing this in sends three Galak Assassins after Kanati. Be at full health first.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Frost does nothing to Boiling and Scalding Elementals and Fire barely hurts them. Arcane works.",tp=1},{t="Scald hits for about 150 Fire damage and stuns for 4 sec. Steam Jet makes you miss far more. Pull these one at a time.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Incendia Agave grows round the pools, and some of it under the water.",w=1},{t="Melor Stonehoof is on the Hunter Rise, over the bridge south of the inn.",w=1},{t="Magatha Grimtotem is on the Elder Rise, right where the bridges from the central mesa land.",w=1},{t="A buy that helps but isn't needed. Skip it if your money is short.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Wear it if it's better than what you have on.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="Rok'Alim the Pounder roams a wide stretch of north-western Thousand Needles, so expect a search.",tp=1},{t="Secret Note #1 is in a Document Chest on top of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",w=1},{t="Secret Note #2 is in the Document Chest in the big tent.",w=1},{t="Secret Note #3 is in the Document Chest in the eastern plateau's tent.",w=1},{t="Clear the Grimtotems around the fire before you light it. Lighting it brings out Arikara.",tp=1},{t="Use the Incendia Powder at the Sacred Fire of Life to light it.",u=12785},{t="The Sacred Fire of Life is on the north-eastern plateau, at the top of the winding path.",w=1},{t="Lakota Windsong not here? Another player has taken this quest. Lakota Windsong is back about 5 min after they finish, so wait nearby. If someone is about to take it, group up first: the game offers it to the whole group.",tp=1,s="auto"},{t="Two Grimtotems spawn at every platform Lakota reaches.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Run ahead of Lakota and clear the respawns on the next platform before she gets there.",tp=1},{t="If the escort goes wrong, run back the way you came. It fails and you get out alive.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Dorn Plainstalker waits in a small cave up the ramp.",w=1},{t="The Shimmering Flats are 31 to 35, and Vile Sting, a rare elite scorpid of 35, roams them. Keep to the road to the Raceway.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stormheart, a level 30 elite, walks a long round through these kobold camps east of Freewind Post. Keep out of his way.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A dungeon run: it needs a group of five. Settings can leave dungeons out.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Just the way there. Go any way you like.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Part of the Shaman water chain, which runs across several zones. Take it if you want to finish the chain.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="This chain (The Affray, then The Windwatcher) ends in Berserker Stance.",tp=1},{t="Affray Challengers come one at a time, back to back, before Big Will. Start at full health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="The fight starts when you step onto the grate just north of Klannoc.",w=1},{t="Craven Drok walks around the Cleft of Shadow rather than standing in one spot.",tp=1},{t="Keldran stands by Orgrimmar's western exit.",w=1},{t="Both of Rahauro's quests can be shared. Someone in your group may already have them.",tp=1},{t="Thunder Bluff is up on the mesas. The lifts at their foot take you up from Mulgore.",tp=1},{t="The Lieutenant's Insignia is a chance drop off the Burning Blade in Skull Rock.",tp=1},{t="Skull Rock's cave fills up again fast. Bring a friend, or pull from the cave mouth.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="After this hand-in you can destroy the Lieutenant's Insignia.",tp=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker (either one counts).",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="The cave is in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow.",s="classic"},{t="The lava kills a low-level character in moments. Stay off the edges.",s="reported"},{t="Take the paths, not the drops. Jumping down lands you in the middle of the troggs.",s="reported"},{t="Everything in here is elite. Pull one pack at a time, and step round a corner so casters come to you.",s="reported"},{t="Searing Blade Enforcers stun the tank. Never pull two at once.",s="reported"},{t="The Searing Blade cultists and warlocks drop both books. Kill them as you go.",tp=1},{t="He cleaves. Keep him facing away from the group.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Two troggs stand with him. Kill them first.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His Uppercut knocks the tank back. Fight him away from the lava so nobody gets thrown in.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His Fire Nova burns everyone near him. Ranged and healers stand back, melee keep their health up.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Kill the patrols before you pull him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Two adds come with him. Crowd-control one and kill the other, then him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Interrupt his Immolate and remove his curse from the tank.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He swings fast and poisons, and he hits hardest here. Start at full health and mana.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Two cultists stand in front of him. Pull them away first, then fight him alone.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Cure his poison if you can.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="The Bubbling Fissure is under the water at the Forgotten Pools. Swim down to it, then come back.",tp=1},{t="This fissure is on the lake bottom, in the middle of the oasis.",tp=1},{t="Oasis Snapjaws sit along the shore as well as in the water.",tp=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Nalpak is in a hidden cave above the cave mouth. The path up starts at the meeting stone and is easy to miss.",tp=1},{t="Sunscale Scytheclaws Thrash about every 10 seconds, two extra swings at once. Don't take one on at low health.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Ebru stands next to Nalpak in the hidden cave above the cave mouth. Take the path up from the meeting stone.",tp=1},{t="Mad Magglish is in the open caves outside the portal, at one of a few spots. He's slow to respawn.",tp=1},{t="He's stealthed and stands in the narrow spots, so look closely.",tp=1},{t="The portal lies at the back of the open caves behind the cave mouth. The way through runs north, then east and back south to it.",w=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="The cave mouth is under the rock face shaped like a skull, south-west of the Crossroads.",s="classic"},{t="Elites patrol the open caves before the portal. Fight there as carefully as inside.",s="reported"},{t="Some ledges inside are high, and a missed jump can kill.",s="reported"},{t="Deviate Guardians call for help when they're low. Kill them fast.",s="reported"},{t="A rare Deviate Faerie Dragon may wander the caves.",s="reported"},{t="Deviates in the outer caves drop hides too. One run has enough for about three players, so top up outside.",tp=1},{t="Find Herbs shows Serpentbloom on the minimap. A run holds enough for about three players.",tp=1},{t="A snake can come out when you pick one. Clear the area first.",tp=1},{t="She can stand at one of several spots. Look before you pull: at one, a Guardian and a Ravager stand with her.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Interrupt her Healing Touch and her Sleep. Clear the mobs around her before you pull.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Her Thorns Aura hurts anyone who hits her in melee. Use ranged attacks and wands where you can.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He puts a random player to sleep. Don't start a long heal while he can cast.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Three pythons stand with him, and he heals them. Kill them first.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="When he gets low he turns into a big snake and hits harder, but he can't cast in that form. Heal up then.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Optional. He swims the river near the start. Kill him when he comes by, early in the run.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Hardest of the four Fang leaders, and two elites fight with him. Crowd-control them or kill them first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="If he puts the tank to sleep, he turns on the next player for a few seconds. Healers, watch for it.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Optional. His Chained Bolt jumps between players. Spread out and interrupt it.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Nature spells do nothing to him. Turn him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Clear the mobs around him first. Interrupt his Healing Touch, which heals him for a lot.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He puts players to sleep. Interrupt it if you can; Priests can dispel it.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He hits very hard. His Grasping Vines knock down and root everyone near him for 10 seconds.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Optional: he sits by the waterfall past Serpentis, and Naralex doesn't need him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Healers and ranged stand well back, so the vines catch only the tank.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Two waves of oozes and snakes attack on the way, then Mutanus rises from the pool. Keep them off the Disciple.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="His Thundercrack stuns everyone close to him for a few seconds. Healers and ranged stand back.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Tank him away from the Disciple of Naralex.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Warlocks and Shadow priests: Shadow spells do nothing to him. Use Fire, Holy or your wand.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Starts from an item Mutanus the Devourer drops.",s="questie"},{t="Back up the slope beside the meeting stone to the hidden cave where Ebru and Nalpak stand.",w=1},{t="Show the shard to Sputtervalve in Ratchet. He sends you on to Falla Sagewind.",tp=1},{t="Falla Sagewind's hut sits high on the mountain over the caverns.",w=1},{t="Down in the Pools of Vision, the cave under Spirit Rise. Go in by the cave mouth beside the bridge up to the rise.",w=1,s="places"},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Players report the entrance is in the Lordaeron courtyard above Undercity. Alliance get there through Horde land.",s="reported"},{t="If you die inside, you come back as a ghost in the courtyard.",s="reported"},{t="Open ruins with no set path. Bosses go in any order, and packs patrol the streets.",s="reported"},{t="Flesh Golems knock you back. Fight them with your back to a wall, away from other packs.",s="reported"},{t="Two hidden bosses come after waves of undead, at a statue and at a chimney fire.",s="reported"},{t="Fog and drifting shadows hide enemies. Pull packs back to lit, open ground before you fight.",s="reported"},{t="Gargoyles on the walls turn to stone and heal, and then take no physical damage. Use spells on them.",s="reported"},{t="Cure Ghoul Plague at once: it lasts 30 minutes.",s="reported"},{t="Ghoul packs stand close together. Pull one, and kill the Ragged Ghoul first.",s="reported"},{t="Skeletons, Fallen Berserkers, Flesh Golems and Fallen Necromancers drop the limbs. Kill every undead in the ruins as you go: leave packs alive and you can come out short.",tp=1},{t="The crest hangs on a wall at one of several spots: behind a door near the Baron, along Bjork's path, or on a tower top. Everyone clicks their own.",tp=1},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Witherfang walks the whole alley with two spiders. Don't let another pack join the pull.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear the alley first, then pull. Kill the two spiders before Witherfang.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Cure the poison on the tank.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="His Knockout hits the tank very hard and drops the tank's threat.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Groups have died here. A tank below full health can die to one Knockout.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Pull him away from the skeleton packs. Keep stunning him so he can't use Knockout.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Ranged stay back, since he cleaves. Tanks take him back right after a Knockout.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Tank him with your back to a wall, so Knockout can't throw you into a pack.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="To go on, you jump the wall behind him. Hunters and Warlocks, dismiss your pet first.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Optional. Lighting the chimney fire brings five waves of undead with no time to drink.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Then Viktor comes and hits very hard. Tanks at 16 or 17 struggle.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Start it only with full health and mana. Skip him if anyone is unsure.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="A curse in the skeleton waves cuts healing taken by 75%. Remove it fast.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Crossing into Market Street wakes the statue. Three waves of undead come before he does.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="He freezes the group in place, chills anyone who hits him and drains the tank's life.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear the enemies around the statue first, and have full mana for the waves.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Interrupt or stun his Drain Life.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill everything round the statue, the tower too, or he won't come. If a wave stalls, find the stuck enemy and pull it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Bjork patrols a long path. Clear the trash along it before you pull.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="His Anti-Magic Shield blocks spells for 3 seconds. Casters wait or use a wand.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="He's a rare spawn, so he may not be there.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="The last boss. His Flamestrike lands where the tank stands, and it hits hard. Melee step away when he casts.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Interrupt or stun Flamestrike. If it lands, the tank drags him out of the fire at once.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear the ghoul packs before him one at a time. They stand close together.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Edward's body lies by the graves next to Rath'mael. Stand on it.",w=1},{t="Othmar's body is upstairs in the Apothecarium, where the Unfinished Abomination stands.",w=1},{t="Use the Hissing Serum from your bags at Othmar's body.",u=281327},{t="The mine starts in the big house in the middle of Moonbrook. Go in and follow the tunnel down.",w=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Go into the building in the middle of Moonbrook and follow the mine tunnel down to the portal.",s="classic"},{t="Most bosses are level 20 and VanCleef is 21. Under 19, the end of the run is hard on the tank.",s="reported"},{t="Patrols come up behind you after the early bosses. Drink with your back to a cleared room.",s="reported"},{t="Some Defias stun the tank again and again. Pull small.",s="reported"},{t="His Slam stuns the tank for 3 seconds and hits very hard. Keep the tank's health up before every Slam.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Two Defias stand near him. Wait until he moves away from them, then pull him alone.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Defias Miners stand around him and join the pull.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="He's a rare spawn, so he may not be there. Kill the Miners first, then him.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The shredder's Terrify sends a player running. Clear the goblins in the room first, or you'll run into them.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="When the shredder dies, Sneed jumps out and fights on. He disarms the tank. Tank him at once and loot only when he's dead.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Goblin Engineers call golems that keep coming while the engineer lives. Kill or stun the engineer first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="The goblins in his foundry are the hard part. Pull them a few at a time before you take Gilnid.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Two hidden Blackguards jump you at the ship ramp before he charges in. His Smite Slam stuns the tank too.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="At two-thirds and one-third health he stomps and stuns the whole group. Kill his two guards first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="After each stomp he walks to his chest to change weapons. Heal up while he's away.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He runs when he's low and can bring more pirates back. Clear the mobs around him first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His Poisoned Harpoon hurts for a full minute. Druids, Shamans and Paladins can cure it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="He walks the ship's deck. Watch his path so he doesn't join the pack before him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="A caster and a fighter come with him. Crowd-control the Squallshaper and face him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Two Blackguards fight beside him from the start, and two more come at half health.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Crowd-control one guard, and stun him as he nears half health to stop the second pair.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Warlocks only. Its fragments come from two dungeons, this one and Blackfathom Deeps.",y=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="The keep is on the hill above Pyrewood Village, south of the Sepulcher.",s="classic"},{t="Undead in the courtyard silence everyone near them for about 5 seconds, often. Casters stand back.",s="reported"},{t="The Lupine Horror room above the courtyard comes all at once if you rush in. Pull from the door.",s="reported"},{t="The horses in the stables pull together. Hold one while the group kills the rest, one by one.",s="reported"},{t="Trash near the end is level 25. At 20, bring a full group.",s="reported"},{t="The book sits on a shelf in the room where you fight Fenrus the Devourer.",w=1},{t="Vincent lies hurt in the keep's courtyard. High Executor Hadrec doesn't take this one.",w=1},{t="Only the Large Soran'ruk Fragment is in here, from Shadowfang Darksouls. The three small ones are in Blackfathom Deeps.",s="questie"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="His Soul Drain roots you for 10 seconds while it drains you. Pull his two worgs off him first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Once he's dead, talk to your faction's prisoner in the cells. He opens the courtyard door.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Horde: Deathstalker Adamant. Alliance: Sorcerer Ashcrombe.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="A patrol walks past outside his kitchen. Kill it before you pull him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His Veil of Shadow cuts healing on its target by 75% for 15 seconds. Mages and Druids can remove it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="The Wailing Guardsman with him silences everyone near it. Tank it away from the group.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Kill the Haunted Servitor first, then Springvale. Interrupt his Holy Light.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He shields himself when low and heals inside it. Save your interrupt for the Holy Light after.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He howls three times, and each howl makes him and his two bats hit harder. Kill the bats first.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="A rare, the Deathsworn Captain, can stand past Odo. He cleaves: tank him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="When he dies, Arugal sends four Voidwalkers. They heal each other, so focus one down before the next.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His four elite worgs attack before he does, and he calls more during the fight. Start at full health.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Void Bolt can kill a cloth wearer in three or four hits. Interrupt it every time you can.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His curse makes a player a worgen that fights you for 10 seconds. Stop hitting them; fear or polymorph them.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Thundershock stuns everyone near him for 5 seconds.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="He teleports between the raised ledges. Don't chase him; ranged keep shooting, melee wait for him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Each teleport wipes his threat. Hold your damage until the tank has him again.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="The Black Tome lies on the table up the stairs behind Arugal's room.",w=1},{t="Optional. Use it at the Ambermill Leyline Focus, in Ambermill's town hall in Silverpine. It becomes the Tome of Dalaran, which calls a hidden boss in the City of Dalaran.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Doan Karhan takes it once you carry all four fragments, from this run and Blackfathom Deeps.",w=1},{t="A Warlock quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Tsunaman is up the right-hand path in Sun Rock Retreat.",tp=1},{t="The Tide Priestesses in the flooded cave drop the Damp Note too. Hand it in at Zoram'gar before you go in.",tp=1},{t="Warlocks only. Its fragments come from two dungeons, this one and Shadowfang Keep.",y=1},{t="The sapphires are blue crystals on the walls of the flooded cave before the portal.",w=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Experienced Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Ruins in the water off the Zoram Strand, on Ashenvale's west coast. The portal is under water: swim down.",s="classic"},{t="Dive into the pool among the ruins. The cave under the water leads past naga to the portal. Watch your breath.",s="reported"},{t="Threshers in the water below can reach you through the floor of the room above. Keep off the edges.",s="reported"},{t="Some Twilight cultists are level 26 or 27 and can take control of a player. Kill them first.",s="reported"},{t="Argent Guard Thaelrid can repair your gear.",tp=1},{t="Only the three small Soran'ruk Fragments are in here, from Twilight Acolytes. The large one is in Shadowfang Keep.",s="questie"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Looting the Fathom Core spawns Baron Aquanis, and the fight is under water. Get full breath before you loot.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Frostbolt is most of Baron Aquanis's damage. Interrupt it when you can.",tp=1},{t="Every Horde player clicks the Fathom Stone for their own core.",tp=1},{t="Thick armor makes him a slow kill for melee. His Trample hits everyone standing close.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Forked Lightning hits everyone in front of her. Tank turns her away from the group; interrupt it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="She moves around her cave during the fight. Clear it first so she doesn't drag in more naga.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Murlocs in his room run when they're low and bring help, him included. Kill them before they flee.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="When he's dead, gather by the shrine in his room, then one of you clicks it. It gives the Blessing of Blackfathom once.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He stands in one of a few spots, from the tunnel past Gelihast to the first Twilight cultists.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His cave is under water with no air. Without Unending Breath or Water Breathing, leave him alone.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Warlocks (Unending Breath) and Shamans (Water Breathing): cast it on everyone before you swim down.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He heals himself over time. Don't start unless your group can out-damage it.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Once he dies, the altar's four fires open Aku'mai's door. Each brings a wave, so light one and clear it before the next.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Clear his room before you wake him. He puts a player to sleep, often the tank, and Mind Blasts.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Have someone ready to hold him while the tank sleeps.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="She hits very hard and can kill a tank in a few swings. Start at full health and mana.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="She enrages near the end and attacks much faster. Save your cooldowns for it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Her room is wide and she notices you from far off. Pull the last turtles back toward the door, or she joins in.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Her Poison Cloud hurts everyone near her for 15 seconds. Ranged and healer keep their distance. Cure the poison.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Priests: take the Gravestone Scepter. It's a big wand upgrade.",tp=1},{t="Doan Karhan takes it once you carry all four fragments, from this run and Shadowfang Keep.",w=1},{t="A Warlock quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Deathstalker Agent waits beside the Excavation Site's entrance, up the ramp.",w=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Novice Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="An outdoor dungeon. Stay out of the tall grass. Hidden raptors spawn in it and join any fight.",s="reported"},{t="Bring cures. Raptors cause bleeds, spiders poison you, and crocs and spiders spread diseases.",s="reported"},{t="Raptors follow you into the water. A bad pull resets on the wooden planks, not in the water.",s="reported"},{t="Some raptors are stealthed. Move slowly, and keep the healer out of the grass.",s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Saltspine patrols around the swamp and can walk into your fight with a croc pack.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear the crocs near his path, then pull him in the open.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Casters stay 10 yards away. His Dust Storm makes nearby attacks miss.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Two Thicket Hunters come with him. His roar fears the group for 5 seconds.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Feared players run into the tall grass, and hidden raptors join the fight.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="He patrols the raptor path. A screeching roar means he's coming: clear the area before he arrives.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Keep both Hunters out of the fight (Hibernate, roots, Polymorph). Thicket Matriarchs call more raptors when low.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Fear Ward, Tremor Totem or Berserker Rage stop the fear. Save stuns for his enrage at low health.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Don't drag him into the water: he resets.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="It roots everyone near it with Entangling Roots. Healers stand back.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="The Dragonmaw campfires burn anyone within 5 yards, players too.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="It sits in an alcove at the Dragonmaw camp, off the path. Pull it away from the Dragonmaw.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Drag it through the campfires to burn it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Level 31. He hits the tank very hard and may stun the tank for 5 seconds.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="His knockback drops the tank's threat, and he turns on whoever is next.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Click the Archival Panel at his right to wake him, once everyone is ready.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Stay 10 yards out of Thunderclap. Damage dealers ease off after each knockback.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="The Deathstalker Agent is still by the entrance, where he gave you the quest.",w=1},{t="Kirin Tor guards round the city attack Horde, and Alliance players hunt here. Keep to the hills and bring a friend.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Keeper Bel'varil stands beside Magus Voidglare.",w=1},{t="Alina and Dermot are inside the ruin at the marker. Ricter waits outside it.",w=1},{t="The Grimy Key is in the Warden's Footlocker, downstairs in the western building. Kegan Darkmar is on the floor above.",w=1},{t="Kegan Darkmar is on the upper floor of the western building. Go in by its door, then take the stairs up.",w=1},{t="Warden Belamoore (36) stands with Kegan Darkmar. Kill her before you pull him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Shield Guards, Theurgists, Workers and Summoners in these camps drop the tokens.",w=1},{t="Shield Guards raise a violet shield: 8 seconds of 85 damage back for every melee hit. Wait it out.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Use the ruins just north of the Internment Camp, not the ones by the city walls: the Kirin Tor guards there attack Horde.",w=1},{t="The Elemental Slaves you kill for Dalaran Patrols drop the bracers.",w=1},{t="Taking this from Modera gives you the Dalaran Sewer Key. Under 30, have someone with a key open the gate.",tp=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Experienced Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Players report the way in is a sewer grate on the Lordamere Lake shore, on the Silverpine side, by the Image of Archmage Modera.",s="reported"},{t="Almost every enemy is immune to Arcane. Arcane spells, Arcane Shot and Counterspell won't work.",s="reported"},{t="Mana Phantoms Mana Burn your healer. Interrupt them or kill them first.",s="reported"},{t="Some ledges in the city are high enough that the fall kills you.",s="reported"},{t="You get in through a sewer grate by the lake.",s="reported"},{t="The bosses are level 30 to 33. Level 31 is safer.",s="reported"},{t="Fragmented Sentinels smash everyone in front of them. Pull them one at a time.",s="reported"},{t="Fast Arcane Manalings patrol in fives, and Mana Fiends explode for about 250 when they die. Step away from them.",s="reported"},{t="Rexxie Copperclutch gives this just inside, where you arrive.",w=1},{t="The book is in the library at the back of the Silver Enclave.",w=1},{t="The Fragmented Sentinels drop the cores, and rarely. It can take more than one run.",tp=1},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Waves of Fallen and Necromancers come first, then him. He fears.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="He raises skeletons, disarms the tank and speeds up his attacks with Unholy Frenzy.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Pull the three Necromancers round his path one or two at a time while he walks away.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill the skeletons as they come, but let the tank grab them before you hit them all.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Tanks keep a shield on for this fight.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="A hidden boss and a hard one. Shadow Bolt Volley hits the whole group.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Curse of Thorns makes your own attacks hurt you.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Optional. The Tome of Dalaran from Shadowfang Keep summons him. Past Atrexis, go straight on into the side room, not up the ramp, and use it on the circle.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Remove his curse fast and kill the two skeletons he raises.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="No quest needs this boss: kill it for its loot, or go past.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Focal Blast is a beam that sweeps around the room. Standing in it can kill you.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Small adds wait at the room's edge.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Fight inside the circle on the platform so the adds at the edge stay out.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="The beam can turn either way. Watch it and step out of its path.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="It silences everyone in melee range, the tank too.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Manamorph turns a random player into a sheep. Dispel it.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill its two Mana Phantoms first, then hit the Manalings it calls with area damage.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="After a short wind-up, Malfunction hits everyone within 25 yards every 2 seconds for 6 seconds.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Arcing Smash hits everyone in front of him.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Kill the Angry Tomes that come out of the buildings before you pull.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Ranged stay 25 yards away. Melee run out when he winds up. A stun during the wind-up stops it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Fel Timbers leaves a green pool that burns anyone in it for 10 seconds.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Entangle roots two players. Rooted in a pool, you can't step out.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="A barrier blocks Runeweaver Square. Talk to Grindle Firespark to drop it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Step out of green pools at once. Blessing of Freedom and Escape Artist break the roots.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="Debilitate hits everyone within 45 yards and drains 200 mana. The group runs dry fast.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Trash left near him joins the fight.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Clear every pack around him first, then kill him as fast as you can.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="His Drain Vitality keeps hurting the tank. Healers, watch for it.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="New in Forever.",s="client"},{t="His parlor crowns the Violet Citadel. Don't jump off the edge: the fall kills. Take the teleport down.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Bounding Mana flies to one player and back. Anyone in its path takes about 300 and is silenced.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="When his mana runs out, he polymorphs the group and refills with Evocation. Mana Phantoms go for the healer.",d=1,s="reported"},{t="Talk to Archmage Modera at the foot of the Citadel. She opens the way up.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Spread out and keep out of the orb's path. Casters stay 20 yards away from Arcane Explosion.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="Damage dealers kill the Mana Phantoms. Stay inside his room the whole fight, or he resets.",tp=1,s="reported"},{t="The hand-in is back at Dalaran's sewer grate in Silverpine, a long ride for one conversation.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The hand-in is back at Dalaran's sewer grate in Silverpine, a long ride for one conversation.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Image of Archmage Modera stands on the Lordamere Lake shore, by the sewer grate into Dalaran.",w=1},{t="The hand-in is back at Dalaran's sewer grate in Silverpine, a long ride for one conversation.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Once Scooty has set up the Goblin Transponder, step on the pad beside him. It takes you to Gnomeregan and back.",tp=1},{t="Scooty needs about nine seconds to calibrate the transponder. Wait, then hand in.",tp=1},{t="It drops you in the caves outside Gnomeregan's portal.",w=1},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Experienced Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="Take the elevator at the airfield in western Dun Morogh down into the tunnels. The front door is past the Train Depot.",s="classic"},{t="Kill Mobile Alert Systems and Alarm-a-bombs at once. They call elites.",s="reported"},{t="Don't fall off the central structure. Mobs below walk round with about a dozen more.",s="reported"},{t="Techbot, an elite near the start, stuns, roots and calls bugs that heal it. Kill the bugs and treat it as a real fight.",s="reported"},{t="Arcane Nullifier X-21 sends spells back and ignores bleeds and poisons. Dark Iron Agents lay mines.",s="reported"},{t="A rare, the Dark Iron Ambassador, can stand in the tunnel before Tinkers' Court. He casts Fireball and calls a fire add.",s="reported"},{t="Kernobee wanders the Dormitory, next door to the Clean Zone by the way in.",w=1},{t="Walk him back to the Clockwerk Run exit at the start and keep him alive on the way.",tp=1},{t="It needs a Grime-Encrusted Item, a random drop in here, and 3 silver. Skip it if nothing dropped.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Gnomeregan, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Gnomeregan, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Gnomeregan, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only if the Grime-Encrusted Ring dropped for you. Cleaning it costs 3 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Only if the Grime-Encrusted Ring dropped for you. Cleaning it costs 3 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Talking to Emi Shortfuse starts waves of troggs from the tunnels. Keep them off her the whole time.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="When she counts down to blow a tunnel, get out of it. Grubbis and his basilisk come after the last wave.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He looks like the other oozes nearby. Type /target Viscous Fallout to find him.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Bring a poison cure. Each hit on him stacks a debuff that lowers your physical damage.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Chain Bolt jumps between up to three players for heavy damage. Spread out and interrupt it.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His Megavolt hits everyone in front of him. Face him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Crowd Pummel knocks everyone round him back, behind him too. Tank with a wall at your back and keep off the platform's edge.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Arcing Smash hits everything in front of him. The tank turns him away from the group.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Crowd Pummel hits everyone near him and stops their casts, so casters stay back.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He switches on bomb machines on the walls. Their Walking Bombs chase a player and blow up everyone near.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="He knocks the tank away and drops their threat. Taunt him back fast; healers hold still and let the tank pick him up.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Give one player the job of pressing the button on the side of each working machine. It stops the bombs.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Open the safe behind Thermaplugg for the Rig Blueprints. The combination drops from him.",tp=1},{t="Only if the Grime-Encrusted Ring dropped for you. Cleaning it costs 3 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Sparklematic 5200 cleans the ring for 3 silver. It's in the Clean Zone, back by the way in.",tp=1},{t="Only if the Grime-Encrusted Ring dropped for you. Cleaning it costs 3 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can keep the ring as it is, or take it back to its maker.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You can keep the ring as it is, or take it back to its maker.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs a Silver Bar and a Moss Agate, from Mining or the Auction House, and 30 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="It needs a Silver Bar and a Moss Agate, from Mining or the Auction House, and 30 silver.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Crate With Holes, Command Stick and Owner's Manual lie beside Mebok. Pick up all three.",w=1},{t="Ruga Ragetotem is indoors, in one of the buildings at Camp Taurajo.",w=1},{t="You finish it inside Razorfen Kraul, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="The Twitching Antennae expire 15 minutes after you loot them. Collect the five in one go, then head back.",tp=1},{t="You finish it inside Razorfen Kraul, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="You finish it inside Razorfen Kraul, a dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="A Warrior quest: only a part of it is in this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Counts toward the Legacy challenge Experienced Spelunker.",s="client"},{t="Enemies in here hit 20% harder than in Classic, with weapons and spells alike.",d=1,s="client"},{t="In the far south of the Barrens, inside the Razorfen thorns by the Thousand Needles border.",s="classic"},{t="Bats silence you for about 10 seconds. Casters and healers stay back in the bat room.",s="reported"},{t="Many quilboar drop totems, healing ones too. Kill the totems first.",s="reported"},{t="Quilboar packs stun, knock down and heal each other. Pull one pack at a time and interrupt the heals.",s="reported"},{t="Two rares can be here: Earthcaller Halmgar and the Blind Hunter, who silences.",s="reported"},{t="Inside, turn left at the first fork and follow that passage to the big vine. Jump down to the Agam'ar pit beneath it and clear it.",w=1},{t="Open the Crate With Holes down in the pit to call a gopher",u=5880},{t="Point the Command Stick at the gopher so it digs, and loot each tuber it finds, six in all. One crate holds five gophers.",tp=1},{t="He's off the main path, past the first left and across the big vine. He calls a Stone Rumbler to help.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Only this part of the quest is in here. Its other parts are elsewhere, so it isn't handed in after this run.",s="questie"},{t="Part of a quest whose other parts are outside this dungeon.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Interrupt his Chain Heal. He calls a Boar Spirit to help, so hold it or kill it first. Step out of the red on the ground.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="He takes control of a player. Interrupt or dispel it, and never finish off a friend he controls.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Kill his guards first while someone keeps him busy. Interrupt his Shadow Bolts. His guards burn mana.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Two elite Spearhide guards fight with him. Crowd-control them, or tank him while the group kills them.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="His pack runs when it's low. Slow or stun runners before they bring help.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His wall opens once the Ward Guardians and the Seer in the bat room are dead. Then he charges out.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="His Rampage stuns everyone close to him. Healers and ranged keep their distance.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Her Chain Bolt hits up to three players for heavy damage. Spread out so it reaches fewer.",d=1,s="classic"},{t="Stuns don't work on her and Shadow does nothing. Warlocks and Shadow priests: use other spells.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Dispel or purge her Renew. When she shields herself, wait it out: it clears your debuffs on her.",tp=1,s="classic"},{t="Drop down behind Charlga's platform. Willix is in the tent below.",w=1},{t="A big pack of casters stands by the tent. Pull it before you talk to him.",d=1,s="guide"},{t="Stay close to Willix the whole way. Only players near him get credit.",tp=1},{t="Starts from an item Charlga Razorflank drops.",s="questie"},{t="Rau Cliffrunner is at Freewind Post. Bring him the Tattered Note from Charlga Razorflank.",w=1},{t="Camping 101: Mining, from the adventurer near your first town: at skill 20 your trainer teaches you the Lodestone, a camp feature for your campfire (1 Rough Stone and 1 Copper Bar).",s="client"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Copper Vein (skill 1), Poor Copper Vein (skill 1, new in Forever). About 99 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 6-12.",s="questie"},{t="Journeyman: it needs skill 50 and level 10, as players saw in the beta.",s="author"},{t="Tin Vein (skill 65), Copper Vein (skill 1). About 33 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75), Bronze (a point every time until 65, none from 115).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 11-25.",s="questie"},{t="Camping 101: Mining, from the adventurer near your first town: at skill 20 your trainer teaches you the Lodestone, a camp feature for your campfire (1 Rough Stone and 1 Copper Bar).",s="client"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Copper Vein (skill 1), Poor Copper Vein (skill 1, new in Forever). About 99 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 5-11.",s="questie"},{t="Journeyman: it needs skill 50 and level 10, as players saw in the beta.",s="author"},{t="Tin Vein (skill 65), Copper Vein (skill 1). About 33 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75), Bronze (a point every time until 65, none from 115).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 11-25.",s="questie"},{t="Camping 101: Mining, from the adventurer near your first town: at skill 20 your trainer teaches you the Lodestone, a camp feature for your campfire (1 Rough Stone and 1 Copper Bar).",s="client"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Copper Vein (skill 1). About 99 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 5-28.",s="questie"},{t="Journeyman: it needs skill 50 and level 10, as players saw in the beta.",s="author"},{t="Tin Vein (skill 65), Copper Vein (skill 1). About 33 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75), Bronze (a point every time until 65, none from 115).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 11-25.",s="questie"},{t="Camping 101: Mining, from the adventurer near your first town: at skill 20 your trainer teaches you the Lodestone, a camp feature for your campfire (1 Rough Stone and 1 Copper Bar).",s="client"},{t="It teaches a camp feature for your campfire. Handy, but your skill-ups don't need it.",y=1,s="auto"},{t="Copper Vein (skill 1). About 99 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="wowhead"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 5-11.",s="questie"},{t="Journeyman: it needs skill 50 and level 10, as players saw in the beta.",s="author"},{t="Tin Vein (skill 65), Copper Vein (skill 1). About 33 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Copper (a point every time until 25, none from 70), Tin (a point every time until 50, none from 75), Bronze (a point every time until 65, none from 115).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 11-25.",s="questie"},{t="Tin Vein (skill 65), Copper Vein (skill 1), Silver Vein (skill 75). About 22 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Stonetalon Mountains is nearly as good for this.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Bronze (a point every time until 65, none from 115).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 11-25.",s="questie"},{t="Tin Vein (skill 65), Silver Vein (skill 75), Copper Vein (skill 1). About 73 nodes on a 10-spot loop.",s="questie"},{t="Silverpine Forest is nearly as good for this.",s="questie"},{t="Smelting also raises Mining: Bronze (a point every time until 65, none from 115), Silver (a point every time until 100, none from 125).",s="client"},{t="Enemies here are usually level 11-30.",s="questie"},{t="Expert: it needs skill 125 and level 20, as players saw in th