For the whole step: about 42 crafts, 84 Silk Cloth.",s="client"},{t="Taught by Manual: Mageweave Bandage, sold by Deneb Walker in Arathi Highlands.",s="client"},{t="Taught by Manual: Mageweave Bandage, sold by Balai Lok'Wein in Dustwallow Marsh.",s="client"},{t="For the whole step: about 18 crafts, 18 Mageweave Cloth.",s="client"},{t="Every Legacy challenge counts for your whole account. A dungeon counts when you kill its last boss.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Bazzalan. Opens at level 13.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Bjork. Opens at level 15.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Mutanus the Devourer. Opens at level 15.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Edwin VanCleef. Opens at level 17.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Archmage Arugal. Opens at level 20.",s="client"},{t="The credit comes from Relic Guardian. Opens at level 26.",s="client"}},
quests={[2]={t="Sharptalon's Claw",lv=30,min=20,pre1={6383},si=16305,ot="Bring Sharptalon's Claw to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.",st="The mighty hippogryph Sharptalon has been slain, with the claw of the felled beast serving as a testament to your victory.  Senani Thunderheart at the Splintertree Post will no doubt be interested in seeing this trophy as proof of your deeds."},[8]={t="A Rogue's Deal",lv=5,min=1,nx=590,si=7628,ot="Deliver the Nondescript Letter to Innkeeper Renee in Tirisfal Glades.",st="Hey, mate! Do a favor for a young man who's been fighting more than his fair share of mindless zombies and spiders?$B$BI got this here letter that needs to go to Brill... to an innkeeper named Renee something-or-other. Don't really matter none what her last name is.$B$BAnyway, it's a nice cozy little place full of victims of the plague trying to make their way in the world. And it be a great spot for you to rest too if the need arises. You should check it out... you do and I'll pay you well."},[23]={t="Ursangous's Paw",lv=24,min=20,pre1={6383},si=16303,ot="Bring Ursangous's Paw to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.",st="<The paw of the mighty bear Ursangous is your trophy for this part of the Ashenvale Hunt.  On the paw is a small quarter-crescent emblem; the significance of the emblem remains a mystery.$B$BThe paw should be brought to Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post to prove that you have bested the mighty creature and completed this portion of the hunt.>"},[24]={t="Shadumbra's Head",lv=27,min=20,pre1={6383},si=16304,ot="Bring Shadumbra's Head to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.",st="The once swift Shadumbra now lies still as you claim victory over it.  The head of the slain nightsaber is a fitting trophy for this fight of the Ashenvale Hunt.  Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post will want to see such a trophy to award you credit for this part of the Ashenvale Hunt."},[25]={t="Stonetalon Standstill",lv=25,min=23,ot="Dispatch 12 Befouled Water Elementals at Mystral Lake, due east of the Talondeep Path and southwest of Splintertree Post.$B$BScout the gazebo on Mystral Lake that overlooks the nearby Alliance outpost.$B$BReturn to Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.",st="If you want to be useful, then why don't you do something about the situation near Talondeep Path?$B$BThe transports between Ashenvale and Stonetalon are at a standstill because of the lake coming alive and attacking anything that gets close... which means anyone on the path.  What'd be even more useful than just putting the hammer down on the water elementals there is someone scouting the gazebo on Mystral Lake - the one that has a solid view of the Alliance outpost there.$B$BYou up for being useful?",how={{"kill",3917}}},[27]={t="A Lesson to Learn",lv=16,min=16,nx=28,ot="Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.",st="$n, I have been following your progress with much delight.  You are most assuredly developing yourself into a valued protector of nature.$B$BThe time has come for you to learn more about one of the various animal aspects that Cenarius has blessed us with the ability to change into - one that affords you command and mastery of the water.  For this, you must travel to the village of Nighthaven in Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle there.  He will guide you further."},[28]={t="Trial of the Lake",lv=16,min=16,pre1={27},nx=30,si=15877,ot="Find a Shrine Bauble in Lake Elune'ara, and take it to the Shrine of Remulos in northwestern Moonglade.  Once there, use the Shrine Bauble.$B$BYou must speak with Tajarri at the shrine afterwards in order to complete the trial.",st="For your first trial, search the depths of Lake Elune'ara to locate a Shrine Bauble.  It decays rapidly, so proceed with it to the Shrine of Remulos post haste.  Use the bauble at the shrine, and then speak with Tajarri there; she is one of Moonglade's most trusted wardens.$B$BYou only have a set amount of time to complete the task, and you may be competing against other druids searching for baubles themselves.  Mental and physical dexterity will be critical to your success.$B$BGood luck, $n.",how={{"click",15885}}},[30]={t="Trial of the Sea Lion",lv=16,min=16,pre1={28},nx=31,ot="Find the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility and the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance.  Speak with the residents of Moonglade to learn clues as to where these items may be located.$B$BForm the Pendant of the Sea Lion from the two pendant halves.  You need to be in proximity of the Shrine of Remulos to do this.$B$BBring the joined pendant to Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.",st="For the second trial, you'll need the two halves that make the Pendant of the Sea Lion.  One half draws power from the agility of the sea lion aspect, gliding through water; the other draws power from the incredible endurance of the sea lion aspect.  Druids draw on both these traits equally to embody the aspect of their aquatic form.$B$BSpeak with the locals of Moonglade to learn where the parts may lie, and bring both here to join them together.  Once formed, take the pendant to Dendrite Starblaze.",how={{"open",15885,{15885}}}},[31]={t="Aquatic Form",lv=16,min=16,pre1={30},si=15885,ot="Return to Thunder Bluff and show Turak Runetotem the Pendant of the Sea Lion.",st="You have completed the necessary lessons all young druids are taught before they can adopt an aquatic aspect.  Go now back to your trainer, Turak Runetotem, in Thunder Bluff.  Show him your pendant and prove to him you are ready to learn what he has to teach you.  He will complete your training, allowing you to become one with the water.$B$BGoodbye, young druid.  We shall speak again."},[63]={t="Call of Water",lv=23,min=20,pre1={220},nx=100,si=7811,ui={6637},ot="Defeat the Corrupt Manifestation of Water and place the Corrupted Manifestation's Bracers along with the Remaining Drops of Purest Water on the Brazier of Everfount in Silverpine Forest.",st="Along the coast of Silverpine, west of the Sepulcher, you will find a shrine that has become tainted by the plague. The spirits there no longer speak to our people and it will be up to you to defeat the manifestation and cleanse the pool.$B$BTake the elemental's bracers, along with the remaining drops of Brine's potion, and place them on the brazier. The ritual should be enough to summon a pure spirit for you to communicate with.$B$BBring me proof the task is done, and I will reward you with your totem.",how={{"loot",7812,{5894}}}},[99]={t="Arugal's Folly",lv=15,min=9,pre1={424},nx=98298,ot="Bring 6 Pyrewood Shackles to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.",st="As my understanding of Arugal's magic grows so does my disdain for the hapless fool.  I am close to completing my research on his so called remedy.$b$bMy knowledge will be complete when I learn what enchantment is causing the strange behavior going on in Pyrewood Village.  By day, the peasants appear to be Human.  But when the sun goes down the townsfolk turn into Moonrage Worgen.$b$bI need to draw energy from the enchanted shackles Arugal cast on them.  Bring to me six enchanted Pyrewood Shackles, $n.",how={{"loot",3218,{1891,1892,3531}}}},[216]={t="Between a Rock and a Thistlefur",lv=24,min=21,nx=6621,ot="Take down 12 Thistlefur Avengers and 12 Thistlefur Shaman; most are located east of Zoram Strand in Thistlefur Village.  Once completed, return to Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.",st="The Thistlefur furbolgs are threatening our expansion!  Thistlefur Village to our east blocks the way between us here and the Splintertree Post.  It's a path that would circumvent the village of Astranaar; without it, we give the Alliance an extra expansion path.$B$B$n, we must not allow... an expansion path gap!$B$BProceed to Thistlefur Village and thin out the furbolgs.  You will be given compensation for this task, but more importantly you will be doing your duty for the Horde!",how={{"kill",3925},{"kill",3924}}},[220]={t="Call of Water",lv=23,min=20,pre1={1534},si=7810,ot="Bring the Vial of Purest Water to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.",st="Islen will have one more task for you before rewarding you with your next totem. The vial of water I've given you is necessary for whatever that task is.$B$BGo now and find her. We shall meet again some day."},[247]={t="The Hunt Completed",lv=30,min=20,pre={2,23,24}},[264]={t="Until Death Do Us Part",lv=15,min=12,si=6145,ot="Place Clarice's Pendant on Yuriv's Tomb in Silverpine.",st="Filthy scum! Leaves me for his damn crusade. Because \"the Light is the most important thing we have against the threats the undead pose.\"$B$BWell, what about his children?! What about ME?! Night after night I sat patiently waiting for him... always second to his blasted duty!$B$BWell, witness what \"justice\" brings you, $n! He's dead and I'm bearing the very thing he was trying to stop!$B$BTake this piece of junk and put it on his tomb at the Sepulcher. I want nothing to do with it anymore... or him!"},[354]={t="Deaths in the Family",lv=11,min=7,ot="Bring Gregor's Remains, Nissa's Remains and Thurman's Remains to Coleman Farthing in Brill.",st="The Agamand family was the most prosperous family in Tirisfal Glades.  I used to work their mills...before the Plague.$B$BWhen the Scourge first came, the Agamands fortified their home and convinced those in their employ to remain and help them defend.  We were fools, but at least we were loyal fools.$B$BThe Agamands, in their pride, doomed us to undeath.  And now they are minions of the Scourge!$B$BServe the Forsaken by defeating the Agamands who fell to the Plague.  Serve me by bringing me their remains.",how={{"loot",2829,{1654}},{"loot",2828,{1655}},{"loot",2830,{1656}}}},[355]={t="Speak with Sevren",lv=10,min=7,pre={354,362},nx=408,ot="Speak with Magistrate Sevren in Brill.",st="You have given me the remains of the Agamands, and satisfied my desire for revenge.  But the Agamand Mills hold a threat to all the Forsaken, not just to me.$B$BI have spoken to Magistrate Sevren of your exploits against the Agamands, and he wishes to speak with you."},[356]={t="Rear Guard Patrol",lv=11,min=6,nx=99156,ot="Kill 8 Bleeding Horrors and 8 Wandering Spirits, then report back to Linnea at her camp.",st="The defenders on The Bulwark protecting Tirisfal from the Plaguelands are on constant alert. But sometimes Scourge will slip past them.$B$BOur success at the Bulwark depends on a one-front battle - we cannot allow an attack from the rear, nor can we allow our defenders' supply line to be cut.$B$BAssist the Bulwark. Patrol east and slay any Scourge you find. Spend particular effort at the Balnir Farmstead to the east. It has become a haven for interloping Scourge.",how={{"kill",1529},{"kill",1532}}},[357]={t="The Lich's Identity",lv=8,min=5,pre1={405},nx=366,ot="Bring the Lich's Spellbook to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.",st="There is a lich who dwells on the island in Brightwater Lake to the north.  Although he is a free-willed Forsaken, he believes all other Undead are Scourge slaves and has his minions attack anyone who approaches him.$B$BBut because he is Forsaken, the Queen will want him.  And if he is skilled in Necromancy, then his knowledge would be...quite useful to us.$B$BTo discover his identity and his talents, I must see his spellbook.  Steal into his camp and acquire it, then return to me.",how={{"open",2833,{1165}}}},[358]={t="Graverobbers",lv=8,min=4,ot="Kill Rot Hide Graverobbers and Rot Hide Mongrels.  $B$BBring 8 Embalming Ichors to Magistrate Sevren in Brill.",st="The Mass Graves, southwest of Garren's Haunt to the north, were made to accommodate the...impressive...number of deaths Tirisfal suffered when the Plague first came.  $B$BThe bodies in these graves have so far been spared an undeath, but the Scourge now send Rot Hide Gnolls to gather the corpses and use them to bolster their armies.  This cannot be allowed!$B$BYour task is twofold: slay the Rot Hides at the Mass Grave and Garren's Haunt, and gather from them the Embalming Ichor that gives them life.",how={{"kill",1941},{"kill",1675},{"loot",2834,{1941,1674,1675}}}},[359]={t="Forsaken Duties",lv=9,min=6,pre1={358},nx=360,ot="Speak with Deathguard Linnea.",st="I need a fresh report from our Deathguard waystation to the east.$B$BI must know if more Scourge forces have slipped past The Bulwark and into Tirisfal.  Our vigilance on the border to the Plaguelands must be maintained - we can't let the Scourge get a stronger foothold here!$B$BTravel south along the road, then east at the fork to the waystation.  Speak with Deathguard Linnea.  She has the information I need."},[360]={t="Return to the Magistrate",lv=9,min=6,pre1={359},ot="Return to Magistrate Sevren in Brill.",st="Now return to Magistrate Sevren with the information I gave you.  He'll want it as soon as possible, so be swift.$B$BAnd if you see any Scourge on your way back, take them down - we can't let them wander our lands unchallenged."},[361]={t="A Letter Undelivered",lv=7,min=4,si=2837,ot="Find Yvette Farthing, and deliver to her the letter from Thurman Agamand.",st="This is a letter written by Thurman, the eldest son of Gregor Agamand.  It is addressed to an Yvette Farthing, though it does not appear to have reached her..."},[362]={t="The Haunted Mills",lv=10,min=7,ot="Slay Devlin Agamand, and bring Devlin's Remains to Coleman Farthing in Brill.",st="Devlin Agamand was the younger of two sons in the Agamand family, and in life the two could not be more different.  Thurman was tall and gentle while his younger brother was weak and sharp tongued.$B$BWhen Agamand Mills fell to the Plague, I was not surprised to hear that Devlin was quick to succumb.  His mad chattering can still be heard near the road leading to the Agamand Mills.$B$BI'm collecting the remains of the Agamands, and I want poor Devlin.  Find him, destroy him, and bring me his bones.",how={{"loot",2831,{1657}}}},[363]={t="Rude Awakening",lv=1,min=1,nx=364,bc=364,ot="Speak with Shadow Priest Sarvis.",st="About time you woke up. We were ready to toss you into the fire with the others, but it looks like you made it.$b$bI am Mordo, the caretaker of the crypt of Deathknell. And you are the Lich King's slave no more.$b$bSpeak with Shadow Priest Sarvis in the chapel at the base of the hill, he will tell you more of what you must know."},[364]={t="The Mindless Ones",lv=2,min=1,ot="Shadow Priest Sarvis wants you to kill 8 Mindless Zombies and 8 Wretched Zombies.",st="We Forsaken are at war with the Lich King's army of the Scourge: necromantically raised armies of the undead, foul beasts of the north, and tormented spectres.$b$bThe northern part of the village has become overrun with the Mindless Ones, and they must be destroyed. Destroy them, show them no mercy, our former brothers and sisters as they might be. The Fallen are nothing but The Lich King's slaves.",how={{"kill",1501},{"kill",1502}}},[365]={t="Fields of Grief",lv=7,min=4,nx=407,ot="Steal 10 pumpkins from the farm to the west, just north of Deathknell and take them to Apothecary Johaan in Brill.",st="What have we here?  You look like a fledgling $c.  If you hope to prove yourself to The Dark Lady, you need to learn the ways of The Forsaken.$b$bTo the west you'll find a farm.  Humans infest the land like mold on a rotting corpse.  And worse yet, the Scarlet Crusade patrols nearby from their tower.  Teach those scum a lesson and steal 10 of their precious pumpkins.$b$bOnce you have 10, take them to Apothecary Johaan in Brill.",how={{"open",2846,{375}}}},[366]={t="Return the Book",lv=8,min=5,pre1={357},nx=409,si=3016,ot="Return Gunther's Spellbook to him, on the island of Gunther's Retreat.",st="Long ago Gunther and I, along with the now Scourge Necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, were friends and students within the Kirin Tor - a society of mages in Dalaran.$B$BGunther and I both fell to the Plague, but I thought he either remained dead, or was raised into the ranks of the Lich King.  It is good to know he is free.$B$BWe must have him.  I have placed a spell on his book that, when he sees it, will show him that I too am free of the Lich King.  After knowing this, it is my hope that he will join us."},[367]={t="A New Plague",lv=6,min=6,nx=368,ot="Apothecary Johaan in the town of Brill wants you to collect 5 Vials of Darkhound Blood.",st="Lady Sylvanas has called upon the Royal Apothecary Society. The Dark Lady believes our knowledge coupled with the newfound magic will provide the key to Arthas's demise.  She has challenged us to concoct a new plague, a plague deadlier than any ailment on Azeroth. This new disease will bring Arthas's Scourge Army to ruin.$b$bMy studies show that the blood of beasts might prove to be the key. Bring to me 5 vials of darkhound blood so I can test my theory.",how={{"loot",2858,{1547,1548,1549}}}},[368]={t="A New Plague",lv=9,min=6,pre1={367},nx=369,ot="Apothecary Johaan of the town of Brill needs 5 Vile Fin Scales from Murlocs in Tirisfal Glades.",st="While you were collecting samples for me, my experiments led me to realize that more reagents will be required for this new disease to spread properly. Poisoning some hapless victim is child's play. Plaguing an entire world proves to be a bit more complicated.$b$bI will need 5 Vile Fin Scales from Murlocs in the vicinity.  You will find the creatures along the coast to the north or to the west.",how={{"loot",2859,{1545,1544,1543}}}},[369]={t="A New Plague",lv=11,min=6,pre1={368},nx=492,ot="Apothecary Johaan in the town of Brill wants you to bring him 4 samples of venom from a Vicious Night Web Spider.",st="While you were out gathering, I uncovered some old text in one of my tomes that indicates that an ancient plague wiped out thousands of innocent victims.  Later it was discovered that the deadly agent in the plague was preserved through the venom of Night Web Spiders.$b$bBring me some venom from a Vicious Night Web Spider to complete this experiment.  I want to see if the contagious element from the venom will work with my new concoction.  Rumor has it the spiders can be found in Eastern Tirisfal Glades.",how={{"loot",2872,{1555}}}},[370]={t="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",lv=9,min=5,pre1={427},nx=371,ot="Executor Zygand in Brill wants you to kill Captain Perrine, 3 Scarlet Zealots and 3 Scarlet Missionaries.",st="The strategic documents from Executor Arren contain all the details we need to wipe the human infestation from the lands.  According to the information, The Scarlet Crusade has assigned Captain Perrine and a brigade to the ruined tower southwest of Brill.$b$bKill Perrine along with 3 Zealots and 3 Missionaries and report back to me.",how={{"kill",1662},{"kill",1537},{"kill",1536}}},[371]={t="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",lv=10,min=5,pre1={370},nx=372,ot="Executor Zygand in Brill has commissioned you to slay Captain Vachon and 5 Scarlet Friars.",st="We are still at war and the Scarlet Crusade grows in strength.  The report Executor Arren sent me indicates Scarlet Crusaders have been raiding from the ruined tower in southeastern Tirisfal near the Balnir Farmstead under the command of Captain Vachon.$b$bKill Vachon along with 5 Scarlet Friars. It should prove to be a devastating blow to the Crusade!",how={{"kill",1664},{"kill",1538}}},[372]={t="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",lv=12,min=5,pre1={371},ot="Executor Zygand in the town of Brill wants you to assassinate Captain Melrache and his two bodyguards.",st="Scarlet Crusaders have been raiding from the ruined tower in northern Tirisfal, past Faol's Rest.  According to the information we have, a ruthless commander named Captain Melrache is in charge of this evil crew.$b$bI am entrusting you now with a special and dangerous mission.  Slay Melrache and his two bodyguards, in the name of The Dark Lady.",how={{"kill",1665},{"kill",1660}}},[374]={t="Proof of Demise",lv=7,min=5,pre1={427},ot="Bring 10 Scarlet Insignia Rings to Deathguard Burgess in Brill.",st="Executor Zygand tells me you've been out killing Scarlet Crusaders. Tirisfal Glades is crawling with them.$b$bVarimathras, lieutenant to The Dark Lady, is seeing to it personally that the scum of Azeroth, the Human race, gets wiped into oblivion. Here in Tirisfal Glades we face a particularly annoying breed of humans: The Scarlet Crusade.$b$bVenture forth and wage an offensive on the Scarlet Crusade, $c. Bring me back 10 Scarlet Insignia Rings as proof of your loyalty to Varimathras and The Dark Lady.",how={{"loot",2875,{1537,1538,1664}}}},[375]={t="The Chill of Death",lv=8,min=7,ot="Bring five Duskbat Pelts and some Coarse Thread to Gretchen Dedmar in Brill.",st="It's so cold, now.  The Plague of Undeath crawls through my veins like an icy serpent.  The Mindless State will be upon me soon.  But no doomed destiny will prevent me from serving our Dark Lady.  When the call arose I sewed body bags for the fallen soldiers of Sylvanas's mighty army.$b$bNow my hands shake from the chill.  If you would bring me five Duskbat Pelts and some Coarse Thread I could sew myself a blanket.  Help me, $n, so that I can continue to serve the cause.",how={{"loot",2876,{1553,1554}},{"buy",2320,{2118,4561,4577}}}},[376]={t="The Damned",lv=2,min=2,ot="Novice Elreth requires 6 Scavenger Paws and 6 Duskbat Wings.",st="My duties include tending to our wounded warriors, tailoring armor and clothes, and assisting Shadow Priest Sarvis with whatever else he might need.$b$bFrom the look of it, you'll be enlisted in his service also... hunting the Mindless Ones, if I know his mind. Well, if you'd like to stay in one piece--and I've no doubt you do--perhaps I can help. I'm running out of paws and wings, and if you bring me some, I'll find some armor for you. You'll find a good number of wolves and bats to the south.",how={{"loot",3265,{1508,1509}},{"loot",3264,{1512,1513,10716}}}},[380]={t="Night Web's Hollow",lv=4,min=2,pre1={376},nx=381,ot="Executor Arren wants you to kill 10 Young Night Web Spiders and 8 Night Web Spiders.",st="One of our greatest struggles is obtaining the natural resources we need to survive. Gold was scarce even in the height of the Alliance's power.$b$bThere is a gold mine to the northwest that has been overrun with spiders. We need gold from the mine, but we can't very well get it while the spiders are crawling around in there. I've not much manpower to commit to the task, so we'll just have to do it little by little.$B$BGet up there and see what you can do for us, $n.",how={{"kill",1504},{"kill",1505}}},[381]={t="The Scarlet Crusade",lv=4,min=2,pre1={380},nx=382,ot="Bring Executor Arren 12 Scarlet Armbands from Scarlet Converts and Scarlet Initiates.",st="You'll be happy to know we appear to be making progress in the mine, thanks in no small part to your efforts.  We can now turn our eyes to other concerns.$b$bMy scouts have reported that a detachment of the Scarlet Crusade is setting up a camp southeast of here. The Scarlet Crusade is a despicable organization that hunts us, and they will not rest until every undead--Lich King's Scourge or no--is destroyed. We must strike first!$b$bBe careful, their unholy zeal makes them dangerous adversaries.",how={{"loot",3266,{1506,1507,1667}}}},[382]={t="The Red Messenger",lv=5,min=2,pre1={381},nx=383,ot="Kill Meven Korgal, the messenger, at the Crusader camp, then return any information you find to Executor Arren.",st="Reports from my superiors in Brill indicate that an agent of the Scarlet Crusade was dispatched from the Scarlet Monastery and sent here to Deathknell. According to the reports, the messenger possesses important information on his person. I do not have further details, but whatever it is, we must have it!$b$bYou're the most qualified person I have to send, $n. Find that messenger and bring me whatever information you can find.",how={{"loot",2885,{1667}}}},[383]={t="Vital Intelligence",lv=5,min=2,pre1={382},si=2885,ot="Deliver the Scarlet Crusade Documents to Executor Zygand in Brill.",st="These will need to be taken to my superior, Executor Zygand, in Brill. With this information, we'll be able to deal a decisive blow to the Scarlet Crusade. Your services have been useful here in Deathknell, but I need someone to deliver this to Zygand, and I believe he'll be able to find you more appropriate work.$b$bTake the road north out of Deathknell. Soon after entering Tirisfal proper, you'll hit a crossroads. Take the eastern fork, and keep going east. You'll pass Cold Hearth Manor along the way."},[398]={t="WANTED: Maggot Eye",lv=10,min=6,ot="Kill Maggot Eye and return to Executor Zygand in Brill with his paw for a reward.",st="Wanted: Maggot Eye!$b$bA foul beast, even by Gnoll standards, Maggot Eye has been sentenced to death for his crimes against The Forsaken.  This despicable villain has been stealing corpses for use by the Lich King's army.  Maggot Eye was last seen pillaging the lands near Garren's Haunt to the north of Brill.$b$bThe town of Brill hereby offers a reward to the capable soul who can carry out the execution.  Show Executor Zygand the villain's paw once the deed is done.$b$bMercy is for the weak.",how={{"loot",3635,{1753}}}},[404]={t="A Putrid Task",lv=6,min=4,nx=426,ot="Bring 7 Putrid Claws to Deathguard Dillinger in Brill.",st="Scourge have trickled into Tirisfal Glades and have infested the area west of Brill, near the old bridge.$B$BGo there and beat back the rotting dead and ravaged corpses you find.  Scatter their bones and bring back their putrid claws, and the Deathguards will reward you.",how={{"loot",2855,{1525,1526}}}},[405]={t="The Prodigal Lich",lv=8,min=5,pre1={358},nx=357,si=3017,ot="Present Sevren's Orders to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.",st="Bethor Iceshard, a high-ranking and powerful mage in the Undercity to the south, commands me to send him an agent with proven worth against the Scourge.  You, $n, will be that agent.$B$BPresent these orders to Bethor.  He will then instruct you on your mission.  I don't know its details, but it deals with recruiting a wayward Lich.  And it will be dangerous.$B$BSo ready yourself, $C.  You must not fail.$B$BYou may find Bethor in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity."},[407]={t="Fields of Grief",lv=7,min=4,pre1={365},si=3035,ot="Take the Laced Pumpkin to the Captured Scarlet Zealot who is being held in the cellar of the Gallow's End Tavern.",st="Harmless pumpkins, right?  Or so it would seem.  If we are to defeat Arthas's advances from the North and the Human infestation from the South we need to start realizing the full potential of our gift of undeath.$b$bWith a little ingenuity a simple pumpkin becomes an agent for our Dark Lady.  This pumpkin, laced with my latest formula, will prove to be quite a treat.$b$bYet another Scarlet Zealot has been captured and is being kept in the cellar of the Gallow's End Tavern.  Take this pumpkin to the fool."},[408]={t="The Family Crypt",lv=13,min=7,pre1={355},ot="Kill 8 Wailing Ancestors and 8 Rotting Ancestors.$B$BKill Captain Dargol, and bring his skull to Magistrate Sevren in Brill.",st="The Agamand Mills area has become a foothold for the Scourge.  Their strongest point is the Agamand Family Crypt where their local military leader, a skeleton named Captain Dargol, has headquartered.  With Necromancy he has raised the ancestors of the Agamands and plans to use them against us.$B$BThis cannot pass, and you must stop it.  Travel to the Agamand Family Crypt and defeat the raised Agamand ancestors.$B$BAnd, bring me the skull of Captain Dargol.",how={{"kill",1534},{"kill",1530},{"loot",3082,{1658}}}},[409]={t="Proving Allegiance",lv=12,min=5,pre1={366},nx=411,ot="Obtain a Candle of Beckoning.$B$BSummon Lillith Nefara and kill her.$B$BReturn to Gunther on his island.",st="You say you are not bound by the will of the Lich King, and the enchantment Bethor placed upon my book corroborates this.  But before I believe you I must have proof that you are enemy to the Scourge.$B$BThere is an old, bloody altar just off the southern coast of this island.  it is used by a powerful Scourge agent, Lillith Nefara.$B$BTake a Candle of Beckoning from this crate here.  Light it on the altar and Lillith will awake.  Destroy Lillith, and I will believe you are the Lich King's foe.",how={{"kill",1946}}},[411]={t="The Prodigal Lich Returns",lv=12,min=5,pre1={409},si=3081,ot="Bring the Nether Gem to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.",st="Take this Nether Gem to my old comrade Bethor.  It will let us communicate ... and I have much to tell him."},[421]={t="Prove Your Worth",lv=10,min=12,nx=422,ot="Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher wants you to kill 5 Moonrage Whitescalps.",st="Lady Sylvanas has charged Varimathras with the conquering of the human and dwarven lands to the south.$b$bBut that fool, Arugal -- charlatan of Dalaran and now cursed beast of Shadowfang Keep -- let his reckless magic wreak havoc with the strategic stronghold of Silverpine Forest.$b$bI need someone skilled in the ways of combat to help clean up Arugal's mess.  Prove yourself to me by killing 5 Moonrage Whitescalps.  The wretched beasts can often be found just off the road, down the hill below.",how={{"kill",1769}}},[422]={t="Arugal's Folly",lv=11,min=9,pre1={421},nx=423,ot="Retrieve the Remedy of Arugal for Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.",st="How Arugal gained acceptance within the Kirin Tor is beyond me.  His spell-casting knowledge seemed as transparent as a blown glass bauble.$b$bWhat's important now is learning exactly what magic Arugal used so that I can turn it against him and secure Silverpine Forest for the Dark Lady.$b$bArugal first stayed at the wheat farm just north of the bridge.  One of the Deathstalkers reported seeing some spellbooks but could not secure them.  Retrieve for me the spell labeled Remedy of Arugal from those books.",how={{"open",3155,{1571}}}},[423]={t="Arugal's Folly",lv=14,min=9,pre1={422},nx=424,ot="Bring 6 Glutton Shackles and 3 Darksoul Shackles to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.",st="After examining Arugal's work my worst suspicions were confirmed.  The old hack was not qualified to clean chamber pots in Dalaran let alone represent the Kirin Tor in its most dire hour.  Fools!$b$bArugal used enchanted items to reinforce his weak magic.  I need to examine these items first hand.  Travel forth and slay Moonrage Gluttons and Moonrage Darksouls until you have collected enough of their enchanted shackles for my research.  The foul creatures have been seen to the north and east.",how={{"loot",3156,{1779}},{"loot",3157,{1782}}}},[424]={t="Arugal's Folly",lv=15,min=9,pre1={423},nx=99,ot="Kill Grimson the Pale and bring his head to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.",st="It will indeed take me longer than I had thought to uncover the dark secrets behind the enchantments Arugal was using.$b$bBut in the meantime I need you to take care of a slight problem our Darkstalkers have discovered.  It seems that Arugal let his magic spread to the Deep Elem Mine in the hills to the southeast.$b$bThe mine would prove to be quite a resource for Varimathras's advance.$b$bI want you to behead the tainted foreman of the mine, Grimson the Pale.  With his death, the mine shall be ours.",how={{"loot",3634,{1972}}}},[425]={t="Ivar the Foul",lv=12,min=10,pre1={91921},ot="Kill Ivar the Foul, and bring Ivar's Head to Rane Yorick at the Ivar Patch.",st="My brother Quinn and I were tasked to recon Silverpine Forest and report to High Executor Hadrec.  But we didn't get far -- when moving through this farm we were attacked by the ghoul Ivar the Foul.$B$BWe escaped from Ivar, but he seriously mauled Quinn.  He's healing from the potion you gave him, but Ivar may return before Quinn recovers.$B$BKill Ivar so Quinn will have time to heal.  Ivar is usually in the barn yonder, waiting for my guard to drop.",how={{"loot",3621,{1971}}}},[426]={t="The Mills Overrun",lv=8,min=6,pre1={404},ot="Gather 5 Notched Ribs and 3 Blackened Skulls, then return to Deathguard Dillinger in Brill.",st="The Scourge are trying to form a base at the Agamand Mills.  If they do, then they can stage further attacks within Tirisfal.$B$BThe orders have been given.  The Scourge in the Mills must be destroyed.$B$BGo to the Mills.  Collect Notched Ribs from Rattlecage and Cracked Skull Soldiers, and Blackened Skulls from Darkeye Bonecasters.$B$BTo get to the Mills, follow the road west.  After crossing the bridge, take the next fork north then keep going north.  When you see windmills, the battle will begin.",how={{"loot",3162,{1523,1520}},{"loot",3163,{1522,260432}}}},[427]={t="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",lv=8,min=5,nx=370,ot="Executor Zygand of Brill wants you to kill 10 Scarlet Warriors.",st="The documents Executor Arren provided are just the break we needed in our battle with the wretched Scarlet Crusade.  We now know their exact locations throughout Tirisfal Glades.$b$bBut the Deathguard has larger concerns.  The Lich King's army grows in number each night.  We need someone with \"initiative\" like yourself to drive the Scarlet Crusade to the grave.$b$bProve to me you are capable of serving The Dark Lady by travelling west to the tower past the Solliden Farmstead and slay 10 Scarlet Warriors.",how={{"kill",1535}}},[429]={t="Wild Hearts",lv=11,min=10,nx=430,ot="Gather 3 discolored worg hearts and bring them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",st="My brother Quinn was badly hurt by the ghoul, Ivar the Foul, and I don't know if he will heal properly without alchemical aid.  Although I am not an apothecary, I do know that our apothecaries can make healing potions from the discolored hearts of worgs.$B$BGather such hearts and take them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher to the south.  Then return here with the potion.$B$BYou can find plenty of worgs between here and Malden's Orchard to the east.",how={{"loot",3164,{1766}}}},[430]={t="Return to Quinn",lv=11,min=10,pre1={429},nx=91920,si=3165,ot="Bring Quinn's potion to Quinn Yorick at the Ivar Patch, north of the Sepulcher.",st="Here is the potion to aid in Quinn Yorick's recovery.$B$BNow if you will excuse me, I have very important work to continue..."},[435]={t="Escorting Erland",lv=11,min=10,nx=449,ne=1,ot="Escort Erland through the wolves, to Rane Yorick.",st="The wolves outside won't leave, and they eye me evilly every time I step foot out that door.  They must be incredibly hungry to think I'm worth eating.$B$BI have to report to my teammate, the Deathstalker Rane Yorick.  And to get to Rane, I'll need help against those wolves.$B$BPlease escort me!  And there are a lot of wolves out there, so we'll have a better chance if you have friends who can help...",how={{"kill",1765}}},[437]={t="The Dead Fields",lv=14,min=10,nx=438,ot="Kill rot hide gnolls at the Dead Fields.$B$BWhen Nightlash appears, kill her.$B$BBring the Essence of Nightlash to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.",st="Our initial scouting reports of Silverpine show the rot hides have a base at an old farm to the north, the Dead Fields.  We have sent small assaults against them, but each time they are reinforced by the banshee Nightlash, who uses her magic to rout our forces.$B$BWe want Nightlash destroyed.$B$BGo to the Dead Fields and assault the rot hides.  If you don't see Nightlash then kill the rot hides until she appears, then defeat her.$B$BHer essence will turn to dust.  Bring me that dust as proof.",how={{"loot",3622,{1983}}}},[438]={t="The Decrepit Ferry",lv=16,min=10,pre1={437},nx=439,ot="Go to the Decrepit Ferry.$B$BSearch for the reason the Scourge are there.",st="$n, we've discovered a new hive for the Scourge: the Decrepit Ferry.  The ferry lies east of the Sepulcher, and is heavily patrolled by rot hides and other undead.$B$BThere must be a reason for the Scourge's occupation of the area.  Go to the Decrepit Ferry and find out why the Scourge are there."},[439]={t="Rot Hide Clues",lv=16,min=10,pre1={438},nx=443,si=3234,ot="Bring Deliah's Ring to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.",st="Among the corpses a hand protrudes, unwrapped.  It is the hand of a woman, pockmarked from the plague but relatively fresh.  $B$BOn the hand is a ring.  Removing the ring and inspecting it reveals an engraving:$B$B\"For Deliah\""},[440]={t="The Engraved Ring",lv=16,min=10,pre1={439},nx=441,si=3234,ot="Bring Deliah's Ring to Magistrate Sevren in Brill.",st="If you want to find the husband or beloved who gave Deliah her ring... then speak with Magistrate Sevren in Brill.  He should have records of recent deaths and, with luck, can discover who Deliah is.$B$BBut I wouldn't hope.  Whoever gave her the ring is probably dead.  Or if he's undead he probably no longer cares about Deliah."},[441]={t="Raleigh and the Undercity",lv=16,min=10,pre1={440},nx=530,si=3234,ot="Bring Deliah's Ring to Raleigh.",st="Deliah had a husband, Raleigh, who now dwells in the Undercity.  If the Deliah who lived in Brill is the one who owned this ring, then Raleigh will know.$B$BRaleigh is in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity."},[442]={t="Assault on Fenris Isle",lv=24,min=10,pre1={448},ot="Bring Thule's Head to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.",st="Now is the time to assault the Scourge's place of strength in Silverpine: Fenris Isle.$B$BYou must again go to the Isle and destroy Thule Ravenclaw.  I want his head!$B$BThis mission is as dangerous as it is vital, $n.  You must not fail.",how={{"loot",3623,{1947}}}},[443]={t="Rot Hide Ichor",lv=17,min=10,pre1={439},nx=444,ot="Bring 8 bottles of rot hide ichor to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",st="Before we launch an assault on Fenris Isle, we must determine who is behind the rot hide gnolls.  Our apothecaries believe their origin lies within the strange fluid that flows through their bodies.$B$BGo to Fenris Isle, east of the Decrepit Ferry, and collect rot hide ichor from the gnolls you find there.  Bring it to Apothecary Renferrel, stationed outside the Sepulcher.",how={{"loot",3236,{1940,1939}}}},[444]={t="Rot Hide Origins",lv=17,min=10,pre1={443},nx=446,si=3237,ot="Bring the Sample Ichor to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.",st="I have reduced the ichor you brought me and separated it into its base components.  My findings are not conclusive, but I have determined that warlock and necromantic magics were used in the ichor's creation.$B$BWhile I continue to study the ichor, I want you to take a sample to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.  Bethor is not an apothecary, but his knowledge of magic may help to unravel the mystery of the rot hides.$B$BGo.  You will find Bethor in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity."},[445]={t="Delivery to Silverpine Forest",lv=10,min=9,si=3238,ot="Take Apothecary Johaan's findings to Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine Forest.",st="Time is a luxury that is not afforded to those of us under the employ of Lady Sylvanas.  Surely you know this by now.$b$bAs a member of the Royal Apothecary Society it is my duty to share my knowledge with my colleagues so that our collective efforts might one day provide The Dark Lady with the New Plague she so badly desires.$b$bTake these findings to Apothecary Renferrel who is stationed at The Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.  Follow the roads to the south from Brill.  From the Undercity go southwest."},[446]={t="Thule Ravenclaw",lv=16,min=10,pre1={444},nx=448,si=3250,ot="Bring Bethor's Scroll to Apothecary Renferrel at the Silverpine Sepulcher.",st="This Ichor was crafted by an old colleague of mine: Thule Ravenclaw.  He was a young, promising mage before the great war, but when the Lich King rose to power, he betrayed his brethren and allied with the Scourge.$B$BI did not realize he still lives, nor that he leads the Rot Hides in their forays against us!$B$BI know many of his spells, and can help concoct a potion to counter them.  Take this scroll back to Apothecary Renferrel.  It has the incantations needed for the potion."},[447]={t="A Recipe For Death",lv=12,min=9,nx=450,ot="Collect 6 Grizzled Bear Hearts and 6 samples of Skittering Blood and deliver them to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",st="Arthas's numbers are overwhelming. But with a New Plague we could eradicate both the Scourge Army and the Human infestation once and for all.$b$bMy studies have proven that spider blood combined with a toxin derived from a grizzled bear heart results in a deadly elixir. Collect samples from the spiders in the Skittering Dark to the northwest and from the bears wandering throughout Silverpine Forest. Deliver the reagents to Master Apothecary Faranell of the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity.",how={{"loot",3253,{1797,1778,12432}},{"loot",3254,{1780,1781,12433}}}},[448]={t="Report to Hadrec",lv=16,min=10,pre1={446},nx=442,ot="Report to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.",st="Before you launch an assault on Fenris Isle, report to High Executor Hadrec.  He may have additional information or equipment you'll need."},[449]={t="The Deathstalkers' Report",lv=11,min=10,pre1={435},nx=3221,si=3252,ot="Bring the Deathstalker Report to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.",st="Although Quinn's wounds are mending, I want to get our report to High Executor Hadrec as quickly as possible.  It has information that is vital to the Forsaken's occupation of Silverpine."},[450]={t="A Recipe For Death",lv=15,min=9,pre1={447},nx=451,ot="Retrieve Apothecary Berard's journal from Pyrewood Village and take it to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",st="You can be of further service to the Royal Apothecary Society, $n.$b$bWhen Arugal cast his wretched magic on the forest, he cursed one of our most promising members, Apothecary Berard.  Now a mindless servant of Arugal, Berard is useless to us.  But his findings might prove to be of worth.  He was studying an ancient plague that killed off all the aquatic life in Lake Lordamere ages ago.$b$bRetrieve Berard's Journal from his study in the Pyrewood Village Inn and take it to Apothecary Renferrel.",how={{"open",3255,{1594}}}},[451]={t="A Recipe For Death",lv=18,min=9,pre1={450},ot="Bring 6 samples of Lake Creeper Moss, 6 samples of Lake Skulker Moss and a Hardened Tumor to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",st="According to Berard's Journal the moss from Lake Skulkers and Creepers might prove useful for our quest to brew a new plague.  Those beasts dwell on the islands in Lake Lordamere to the east.$b$bHe also mentions a very rare Hardened Tumor that he discovered on a Vile Fin murloc.  Apparently the tumor is so rare Berard was only able to obtain one.$b$bCollect samples of the moss as well as the rare hardened tumor and take them to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",how={{"loot",3256,{1953,1954}},{"loot",3257,{1955}},{"loot",3258,{1958,1957}}}},[452]={t="Pyrewood Ambush",lv=15,min=12,ne=1,ot="Help Deathstalker Faerleia kill the Pyrewood Council.",st="You got here just in the nick of time, $n!$b$bThe Pyrewood Council will be returning any moment.  Arugal has other matters to tend to in the keep.  He uses the Council as mere puppets to keep the mindless minions of Pyrewood under his control.  But I believe that without the guidance of the Pyrewood Council, the sons of Arugal will turn against their master.$b$bI cannot handle them all by myself.  I need you to help me.  Together we can lay waste to the Council for Lady Sylvanas.",how={{"kill",2060},{"kill",2061},{"kill",2062},{"kill",2063},{"kill",2064},{"kill",2065},{"kill",2066},{"kill",2067},{"kill",2068}}},[460]={t="Resting in Pieces",lv=17,min=12,nx=461,si=3317,ot="Bring Alaric's Head to his grave.",st="You don't look like a rot hide.  Good.  I had lost hope...$B$BMy name is Alaric, and I was once Thule's head servant and bodyguard.  He used his magic to \"protect\" me from the Plague of Undeath, but instead his spell gave me an unlife from which I cannot escape.  And after creating the cursed rot hide gnolls, Thule beheaded me... and gave my head to the gnolls as a plaything!$B$BPlease, take me to my body.  I believe the gnolls buried it here in Fenris Keep, near the stable, in an unmarked grave."},[461]={t="The Hidden Niche",lv=18,min=12,pre1={460},nx=491,si=3318,ot="Take Alaric to the hidden alcove.",st="I know of a hidden niche within the keep that holds an item dear to Thule, and his old colleagues.  It also holds something you might find useful.  Take me there!$B$BThe alcove is in the southwestern tower of the keep, behind a dusty shelf.$B$BTake my body, but leave my boots.  They never fit me anyway..."},[477]={t="Border Crossings",lv=14,min=10,nx=478,ot="Retrieve the contents of one of the Dalaran wizards' crates. You will find Pyrewood Village to the south.",st="As you may know, the town of Ambermill remains a source of human opposition, mainly through the support they receive from the wizards of Dalaran.$b$bI don't know what their plan is, but for them to show interest in a backwater village like Ambermill indicates that it must have some greater importance.$b$bThey've been shipping crates by the wagon from Hillsbrad. Many of those supplies end up at a small camp north of Pyrewood Village. Retrieve the contents of a crate and return them to me."},[478]={t="Maps and Runes",lv=14,min=10,pre1={477},nx=481,si=3353,ot="Bring the strange pendant to Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.",st="<You quickly remove the pendant from the crate and replace the lid.>"},[479]={t="Ambermill Investigations",lv=16,min=10,pre1={482},nx=480,ot="Obtain 8 Dalaran Pendants for Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.",st="Dalar is attempting to locate the source of the wizards' spellcasting. For now, we'll have to slow their progress in any way we can...$b$bThe conjurers, mages and protectors are no doubt carrying the pendants. Remove and retrieve them.$b$bTake the main road south and the eastern fork into Ambermill.",how={{"loot",3354,{1912,1914}}}},[480]={t="The Weaver",lv=22,min=10,pre1={479},ot="Kill the Dalaran archmage, then retrieve his staff for Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.",st="An archmage of great power is overseeing the reactivation of the ley energy node. With the progress they have made, our only hope of stopping them is by killing him. It will be difficult, he is no doubt protected by many other mages and warders.$b$bYou must go, and you must dispatch him quickly. When he is dead, retrieve his staff for me. Go now.",how={{"loot",3515,{2120}}}},[481]={t="Dalar's Analysis",lv=14,min=10,pre1={478},nx=482,si=3353,ot="Take the rune-inscribed pendant to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.",st="Take the pendant to Dalar Dawnweaver, perhaps he can shed some light on the wizards' plans."},[482]={t="Dalaran's Intentions",lv=14,min=10,pre1={481},nx=479,ot="Speak with Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.",st="Of course! How could I have forgotten?$b$bAmbermill was one of the sites earmarked by the Kirin Tor, noted because it houses a dormant ley energy node. The wizards must be planning to reactivate the node and use its energies for some greater purpose.$b$bWe cannot allow this to happen...$b$bIt will take a great amount of power to activate the area's ley energies, we can stall them by taking the pendants away from the wizards.$b$bRelay this information to Allister, he will decide a course of action."},[492]={t="A New Plague",lv=11,min=6,pre1={369},si=3460,ot="Bring Johaan's Special Drink to the Captured Mountaineer.",st="According to the Deathguard, another one of those foolish Dwarven Mountaineers has just been captured.  The Deathguard likes to use the cellar of the Gallows End Tavern as a holding cell until prisoners can be \"properly\" dealt with.$b$bWhy don't you go see how the Captured Mountaineer enjoys this special drink I made for him?  It contains a subtle hint of what The Dark Lady has planned for the rest of Azeroth."},[493]={t="Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills",lv=20,min=19,si=3468,ot="Deliver Apothecary Renferrel's findings to Apothecary Lydon in the town of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",st="The Royal Apothecary Society is under extreme pressure from the Dark Lady to develop a New Plague.  We are working diligently and have made much progress.  It is our belief that the success will be achieved much faster if we share information amongst the Society.$b$bFor that reason I want you to deliver my latest findings to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, a small town nestled in the Hillsbrad Foothills.  The journey will be a long one.$b$bHead south and stick to the roads.  Follow the signs closely!"},[494]={t="Time To Strike",lv=20,min=19,ot="Travel to Tarren Mill to deliver Deathstalker Lesh's message to High Executor Darthalia.",st="Be silent and pay attention, $c.$b$bI was sent to this position in order to survey the town of Hillsbrad.  My mission is one of reconnaissance.  It is imperative that you send word to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill at once.  Let her know that I, Deathstalker Lesh, send the following message:$b$b\"The raven's cry from the west doth beckon.\"$b$bFollow the road to the east and pay close attention to the signs.  Now, hurry!  Off you go to Tarren Mill, and with urgency I might add!"},[496]={t="Elixir of Suffering",lv=22,min=19,nx=499,ot="Apothecary Lydon of Tarren Mill wants 10 Gray Bear Tongues and some Creeper Ichor.",st="Ah, another wretched day in Tarren Mill.  All of this clean air puts me in such a foul mood, $n.$b$bThe sooner we can plague the humans here, the better.  I've been conducting intense studies on possible killing agents to use in my concoctions but I haven't the time to collect them all.$b$bIf you want to make yourself of use, procure the following items for me:  10 Gray Bear Tongues and the very rare and hard to find, Creeper Ichor.  You'll find both bears and creepers just outside of Tarren Mill.",how={{"loot",3476,{2351,2354,2356}},{"loot",3477,{2350,2349,2348}}}},[498]={t="The Rescue",lv=22,min=17,nx=533,ot="Krusk in Tarren Mill needs you to free Drull and Tog'thar from Durnholde Keep.",st="Me and some other warriors were sent by the Warchief to retrieve an object from Durnholde and to investigate this so-called Syndicate.$b$bWe went to Durnholde to take a look around, but we were taken by surprise by a large number of the humans. We fought bravely, but their sheer numbers were enough to defeat us. They took a few of us captive, but I was able to escape.$b$bDurnholde is just southeast of here, across the river. Drull and Tog'thar are being held there, you must go and rescue them.",how={{"click",1721},{"click",1722}}},[499]={t="Elixir of Suffering",lv=22,min=19,pre1={496},si=3495,ot="Give Umpi the Elixir of Suffering.",st="It will take but a moment for me to mix these components into what I have deemed an Elixir of Suffering.$b$bThere we go!  Ah, nothing brightens a gloomy day in these miserable foothills like bringing a little suffering into the world.$b$bLet us see if our little potion has achieved its desired effect.$b$bGive my assistant Umpi a taste of what the Dark Lady has planned for both humans and Scourge alike."},[501]={t="Elixir of Pain",lv=24,min=21,nx=502,ot="Bring 10 vials of Mountain Lion Blood to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",st="Oh, $n. . .the flowers are blooming in Hillsbrad and the air is so fresh and brisk.  I can't help but to wallow in the misery of it all.  I look out my grimy window and long for the day when our New Plague brings this world the death it deserves.$b$bAs much as I would love to sit and brood all day, my duty to the Dark Lady calls.  Help me, would you?  My research leads me to believe I can make the most splendid death-brew with the blood of a Mountain Lion.  Bring some to me and we'll have a little fun.",how={{"loot",3496,{2384}}}},[502]={t="Elixir of Pain",lv=24,min=21,pre1={501},si=3497,ot="Feed the Elixir of Pain to Stanley.",st="Ah, nothing like the smell of fresh blood in the foothills!$b$bNow we'll mix in a touch of this and a little of that and let the real fun begin!  What I have created with this blood, I like to call an Elixir of Pain.  If my calculations are correct this concoction could be the start of something very beautiful for Lady Sylvanas.  But what we need is a test.$b$bTake this elixir out to the northern farm in Hillsbrad Fields to the southwest.  Let's see how Farmer Ray's little dog Stanley likes this \"treat.\""},[516]={t="Beren's Peril",lv=21,min=16,ot="Locate Beren's Peril, then kill 6 Ravenclaw Drudgers and 6 Ravenclaw Guardians, then return to Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.",st="I have received reports that a group of undead are holing up to prepare for an attack against us. Armed with this information, we can turn the tables and attack them first, nipping their little plan in the bud.$b$bUnfortunately, my information is spotty, at best. They are reported to be hiding in a location known as Beren's Peril. The exact location is unknown, but it appears to be a cave in the hills, near a pocket of Dalaran wizards.$b$bI trust your resourcefulness. Find them, and put them down.",how={{"kill",1974},{"kill",1973}}},[527]={t="Battle of Hillsbrad",lv=24,min=19,nx=528,ot="Kill 6 Hillsbrad Farmhands, 6 Hillsbrad Farmers, Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.",st="Stand at attention while addressing me, $c.$b$bI am under direct command of Varimathras.  We are to quell the human infestation until our apothecaries can develop the new plague.$b$bOur information leads us to believe that the town of Hillsbrad is vulnerable to attack.  Your first assignment is aimed at disrupting their food supply and infrastructure.$b$bTravel west.  Raid the northernmost farms of Hillsbrad Fields.  Make sure that the landowners, Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz, are executed as well.",how={{"kill",2266},{"kill",2360},{"kill",232},{"kill",2403}}},[528]={t="Battle of Hillsbrad",lv=25,min=19,pre1={527},nx=529,ot="Kill 15 Hillsbrad Peasants and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.",st="Word of the attack on the northern farms has the townsfolk panicked.  Most excellent.$b$bOur Deathstalkers report peasants fleeing to the fields in southern Hillsbrad.  The fools think they can hide in the orchards and escape their doom.$b$bProve them wrong, $n.  Return to Hillsbrad Fields and seek out the cowering peasants.  Lay waste to them in the name of our Dark Lady.$b$bDismissed!",how={{"kill",2267}}},[530]={t="A Husband's Revenge",lv=20,min=10,pre1={441},ot="Kill Valdred Moray.$B$BBring his hands to Raleigh Andrean in the Undercity.",st="Valdred, once my good friend, was my wife's murderer.  Although I am incapable of grieving, I do yearn for revenge.  If you kill Valdred and bring me his cursed hands, then I will reward you.$B$BI last heard he was at the Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine, trying to flee into the kingdom of Gilneas.",how={{"loot",3613,{2332}}}},[544]={t="Prison Break In",lv=33,min=30,ot="Find the traitors and recover their artifacts, then return to me, $n.",st="I came to Tarren Mill to research, but now must resolve a crisis. You see, four Forsaken fled the Undercity a few months ago. They turned their backs on their brethren, but what's worse...they stole from the Dark Lady.\r\n\r\nThese thieves broke into a secure vault and stole four artifacts, items our apothecaries required in certain studies. Sylvanas would have these artifacts returned.\r\n\r\nThe thieves fled the Undercity to Dalaran, and those wizards quarantined them in the Lordamere Internment Camp.",how={{"loot",3691,{2413}},{"loot",3689,{2411}},{"loot",3690,{2412}},{"loot",3688,{2414}}}},[545]={t="Dalaran Patrols",lv=35,min=30,pre={544,93680},ot="Kill $1oa Dalaran Summoners and $2oa Elemental Slaves, then return to Magus Voidglare in Tarren Mill.",st="Before it mysteriously vanished, there was an enormous magical barrier around the newly-reconstructed city of Dalaran. I care not what caused such a magical marvel to fail, but I do care that the newly exposed outskirts of their city may hide valuable magical treasures. Vestiges of the ruins on which the new city is built. $B$BBut the area is patrolled by the wizards and their elemental slaves.$B$BSo hunt them, and return when their numbers are sufficiently reduced.",how={{"kill",2358},{"kill",2359}}},[546]={t="Souvenirs of Death",lv=25,min=20,pre1={527},ot="Deathguard Samsa of Tarren Mill wants 30 Hillsbrad Human Skulls.",st="I hear you were enlisted by Darthalia to wage war on the humans of Hillsbrad.  So jealous I am. . .$b$bWhile you're off having all the fun -- slaying humans, pillaging the town, terrorizing innocent people -- I am stuck standing guard here in Tarren Mill.$b$bPerhaps you'll take pity on an old Deathguard like myself?  You see I am collecting human skulls.  And you will be fighting humans for quite some time.  Over the course of your long battle, bring me 30 skulls and I will make it worth your while.",how={{"loot",3692,{2266,2360,2268,2267}}}},[549]={t="WANTED: Syndicate Personnel",lv=22,min=17,nx=566,ot="Kill 10 Syndicate Rogues and 10 Syndicate Watchmen. Return to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill for your reward.",st="By the authority of Lady Sylvanas, all members of the organization known as the Syndicate are wanted dead. Those brought into custody or taken prisoner will be summarily executed. They are currently known to be amassing in the ruins of Durnholde Keep, to the southeast of Tarren Mill.$b$bA handsome reward is offered to all who bring proof of their deeds to High Executor Darthalia.",how={{"kill",2260},{"kill",2261}}},[556]={t="Stone Tokens",lv=33,min=30,nx=557,ot="Bring 10 Worn Stone Tokens to Keeper Bel'varil in Tarren Mill.",st="A notable talent of the wizards of Dalaran is their familiarity with elementals: powerful creatures from other dimensions.  The wizards use magical tokens as a means to control these elementals.  Magus Voidglare would like some of these tokens to study.$B$BEnter the territories of the Dalaran wizards, west of Hillsbrad, and gather the tokens.$B$BYou might find the tokens on any citizen of Dalaran, but I suggest hunting at the internment camp.  It's safer than Dalaran itself.",how={{"loot",3714,{2271,2272,2415}}}},[557]={t="Bracers of Binding",lv=33,min=30,pre1={556},ot="Bring 4 Bracers of Earth Binding to Keeper Bel'varil in Tarren Mill.",st="The Magus will be busy studying those stone tokens you gathered, but I know he'll eventually want examples of their counterpart: bracers of binding.  These are set around the wrists of actual elementals, and bind them into the mage's service.$B$BHunt elementals in the ruins of Dalaran and gather their Bracers of Earth Binding, and the Magus will be pleased.",how={{"loot",3715,{2359}}}},[590]={t="A Rogue's Deal",lv=5,min=1,pre1={8},ne=1,ot="Defeat Calvin Montague in Deathknell.",st="What?$B$BWhat?!$B$BYou want money? I don't owe you any money.$B$BLetter? What letter? Oh, you wanna fight then? All right, mate... let's do this! Owe you any money..."},[743]={t="Dangers of the Windfury",lv=8,min=5,ot="Bring 8 Windfury Talons to Ruul Eagletalon in Bloodhoof Village.",st="Thank you for taking the time to speak to me, $n. I am Ruul, warrior and teacher.$B$BYou have obviously reached an age when you must prepare for your trials if you are to adventure much further out of Mulgore.$B$BIf you wish a test of your strength, start by seeking out the Windfury harpies to the southeast. They nestle along the mountain's edges away from the road.$B$BThey are one of our natural enemies here in Mulgore and will be a good gauge of your skill.",how={{"loot",4751,{2963,2962}}}},[744]={t="Preparation for Ceremony",lv=11,min=7,ot="Collect 6 Azure Feathers and 6 Bronze Feathers, and bring them to Eyahn Eagletalon in Thunder Bluff.",st="$n, my brother soon stands before Chief Bloodhoof, and it is my honor to make his headdress for him.$B$BI want to ask a favor of you while I finish tanning these leather straps. There is not time for me to find enough feathers, and I was wondering, would you gather more for me?$B$BYou can find feathers of the correct size from the harpies residing far to the north and northwest of Thunder Bluff. I need only 6 azure and 6 bronze feathers to complete the design.",how={{"loot",4752,{2964}},{"loot",4753,{2965}}}},[745]={t="Sharing the Land",lv=8,min=1,ot="Kill 10 Palemane Tanners, 8 Palemane Skinners, and 5 Palemane Poachers, then return to Baine Bloodhoof in Bloodhoof Village.",st="$n, there are many conflicts that wound this land. It is my hope that you will not bear witness to as many of them as I have. Yet there is one that I would ask you to seek out. It will give you some sense of how terrible, if left unchecked, even a small threat can be to the land.$B$BPalemane gnolls have settled to the south of Bloodhoof and in a cave to the west. They disrespect our attempts to communicate with them, and they slay the wildlife of Mulgore unbridled.$B$BWords are no longer the answer.",how={{"kill",2949},{"kill",2950},{"kill",2951}}},[746]={t="Dwarven Digging",lv=8,min=6,si=4702,ot="Collect 5 Prospector's Picks.$B$BAt a forge, smash the Prospector's Picks to create Broken Tools.$B$BBring 5 Broken Tools to Baine Bloodhoof in Bloodhoof Village.",st="There are dwarves preparing a dig site to the northwest.  They think secrets lie in the earth, and that is true, but hollowing and defiling the land is no way to earn its teachings.$B$BCollect the dwarven tools of digging, smash them, and return to me with the dwarves' broken tools.$B$BYou can smash the tools at a forge.  You will find one in Thunder Bluff, but any forge -- even a forge at the dwarven camp -- will suffice.",how={{"open",4703,{17190}}}},[747]={t="The Hunt Begins",lv=2,min=1,rwc={[11]=1},ot="Grull Hawkwind in Camp Narache wants you to bring him 7 Plainstrider Feathers and 7 pieces of Plainstrider Meat.",st="You have a promising air about you, and will prove yourself to the tribe. Perhaps someday soon you will be welcomed into the great city of Thunder Bluff. But before that can happen you must prove yourself to my father, Chief Hawkwind.$b$bUp here on Red Cloud Mesa we pride ourselves on keen hunting skills. Tauren hunt out of necessity and for sport. Our supply of meats has run low and we require feathers for clothing. Hunt the nearby plainstriders and prove yourself by resupplying the village.",how={{"loot",4739,{2955}},{"loot",4740,{2955}}}},[748]={t="Poison Water",lv=5,min=4,nx=754,ot="Bring 6 Prairie Wolf Paws and 4 Plainstrider Talons to Mull Thunderhorn in Bloodhoof.",st="Goblins and their servants have tainted our sacred water wells! We cannot allow this.$B$BTo cleanse each well, I must create a cleansing totem, then you must bring the totem to the well and perform a cleansing ritual.$B$BFirst we will create a cleansing totem for the Winterhoof Water Well. To do this, the land must offer its aid. Hunt prairie wolves for their paws and adult plainstriders for their talons. They are to the southwest.$B$BReturn to me with the paws and talons, $n.",how={{"loot",4758,{2958}},{"loot",4759,{2956}}}},[749]={t="The Ravaged Caravan",lv=8,min=5,nx=751,ot="Morin Cloudstalker wants you to examine the contents of a supply crate at the Ravaged Caravan.",st="A few days ago, we found a Venture Co. caravan traveling under guard on the northern shore of Stonebull Lake. We'd lost two of our number in an earlier battle, so we were quick to attack and lay waste to the caravan.$b$bWe left their supply crates, thinking that our torches would destroy anything of value, but given that Venture Co. salvagers have been spotted near the burned wagons, maybe we were wrong.$b$bPerhaps you could go to the caravan and examine the contents of the crates."},[750]={t="The Hunt Continues",lv=3,min=1,pre1={747},nx=780,ot="Grull Hawkwind in Camp Narache wants you to bring him 10 Mountain Cougar Pelts.",st="A tauren skilled in the ways of the hunt knows that his prey is not for mere trophy. The beasts of the plains provide us with a means of survival. You will make quite an impression on the elders if you can bring back some highly valued Mountain Cougar Pelts. You can find the beasts lurking in the hills to the south.$b$bOur children need clothing and our tents need mending.",how={{"loot",4742,{2961}}}},[751]={t="The Ravaged Caravan",lv=8,min=5,pre1={749},si=4834,ot="Return the Venture Co. Documents to Morin Cloudstalker near Bloodhoof Village.",st="Prying open the lid reveals a tightly packed assortment of ore and minerals, more evidence of the Venture Co.'s mining operation in Mulgore. On the top of the ore and minerals you remove a tightly bound sheaf of papers.$b$bUp in the foothills to the east, you can barely hear the sounds of work, and see smoke rising from a large fire."},[752]={t="A Humble Task",lv=2,min=1,nx=753,bc=753,ot="Chief Hawkwind wants you to search for his mother near the water well to the southeast of Camp Narache.",st="All members of the tribe share in the harmony of life. We live together and work together.$b$bOur commitment to one another carries with it a high degree of responsibility. I ask of you now a humble task.$b$bMy mother set out this morning to fetch water from the well to the southeast of Narache. It has been quite some time now. Perhaps you could check on her for me while I attend to tribal matters here?"},[753]={t="A Humble Task",lv=3,min=1,nx=755,ot="Take a Water Pitcher from the water well.$b$bReturn the pitcher to Chief Hawkwind in Camp Narache which is northwest from the water well.",st="I have traveled many paths through life and these old legs lack the vigor they once had. I can still perform my duties to the tribe. Sometimes it just takes an old woman a little longer to do the task.$b$bBut you look like an eager $c. Let's put some of that youthful vitality to the test. Take a water pitcher from the well and bring it to my son, the Chief, in Camp Narache.$b$bRemember that even the most humble task can gain the recognition of elders.",how={{"open",4755,{2907,337}}}},[754]={t="Winterhoof Cleansing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={748},nx=756,si=5411,ot="Use the Winterhoof Cleansing Totem at the Winterhoof Water Well, then return to Mull Thunderhorn.",st="I have crafted the totem to cleanse the Winterhoof Water Well. Now, you must take it to the well and perform a cleansing ritual. You will find it to the southeast, guarded by foul goblins!$B$BThis will not be an easy task, but you must do it if we are ever to use its waters again.$B$BFortune to you, $n."},[755]={t="Rites of the Earthmother",lv=3,min=1,pre1={753},nx=757,ot="Travel to Seer Graytongue who lives in the hills directly south of Camp Narache.",st="Your willingness to perform a humble task for the tauren of Narache and your eagerness to learn are noble traits, $n. I believe one day you will be heralded in Thunder Bluff as a $c of greatness.$b$bBefore that you must embark on the Rites of the Earthmother, of which there are three.$b$bThe first test is the Rite of Strength. Travel to Seer Graytongue and tell him Chief Hawkwind has sent you.$b$bYou will find the seer's abode directly to the south of Camp Narache, tucked away in the hills."},[756]={t="Thunderhorn Totem",lv=7,min=4,pre1={754},nx=758,ot="Bring 6 Stalker Claws and 6 Cougar Claws to Mull Thunderhorn.",st="To create the Thunderhorn Cleansing Totem, you must gather the claws of the predators of the Mulgore plains. Hunt prairie stalkers for their stalker claws and flatland cougars for their cougar claws, then return to me.$B$BYou will find the prairie stalkers and flatland cougars to the east and west.",how={{"loot",4801,{2959}},{"loot",4802,{3035}}}},[757]={t="Rite of Strength",lv=4,min=1,pre1={755},nx=763,ot="Kill Bristlebacks in Brambleblade Ravine and bring 12 Bristleback Belts to Chief Hawkwind in Camp Narache.",st="The Rites of the Earthmother are the steps a young tauren needs to take to gain respect in Thunder Bluff.$b$bFirst you must pass the Rite of Strength. In this test you must prove your bravery by slaying enemies of the tribe.$b$bBristlebacks of Brambleblade Ravine to the east are encroaching on our tribal lands. They ambush our hunting parties and steal from the village by dark.$b$bShow your valor by slaying these villains and return to the Chief in Camp Narache with their belts as proof of your deeds.",how={{"loot",4770,{2952,2953}}}},[758]={t="Thunderhorn Cleansing",lv=8,min=4,pre1={756},nx=759,si=5415,ot="Use the Thunderhorn Cleansing Totem at the Thunderhorn Water Well, then return to Mull.",st="The totem is ready, $n. And again, it is your task to perform the ritual of cleansing.$B$BGo to the Thunderhorn Water Well, north of the village, and use the Thunderhorn Cleansing Totem in your ritual. After you do this, return to me.$B$BMay the spirits guide you."},[759]={t="Wildmane Totem",lv=10,min=4,pre1={758},nx=760,ot="Bring 8 Prairie Alpha Teeth to Mull Thunderhorn in Bloodhoof Village.",st="There is but one water well left to cleanse, named after the Wildmane clan. For this well to be pure, the land must offer the teeth of a fierce predator, the prairie wolf alpha. Find the alphas to the north, then return to me when your hunt is finished.$B$BAlphas often wander around the base of our mighty city, Thunder Bluff.",how={{"loot",4803,{2960}}}},[760]={t="Wildmane Cleansing",lv=10,min=4,pre1={759},nx=98435,si=5416,ot="Use the Wildmane Cleansing Totem at the Wildmane Water Well, then return to Mull Thunderhorn.",st="Your cleansing of the Winterhoof and Thunderhorn wells is spoken among the spirits, young $n. The Wildmane Totem is made, and your last task lies ahead.$B$BThe Wildmane Water Well lies north of Thunder Bluff. Perform the ritual! Heal the land of the goblins' poisons! Let clean water flow once again!"},[761]={t="Swoop Hunting",lv=6,min=4,ot="Bring 8 Trophy Swoop Quills to Harken Windtotem in Bloodhoof Village.",st="The swoop is a cunning bird, and difficult to find and hunt.  A collection of Swoop Quills is a badge of cleverness and determination for a hunter.$B$BIf you are willing to take up this task, then enter the plains and hunt the swoop.$B$BBring me their quills, and bring honor to your clan.$B$BThe swoops may be found anywhere in Mulgore, but your eyes must be sharp to spot them, and your hooves must be quick to catch them.",how={{"loot",4769,{2971,2970,2969}}}},[763]={t="Rites of the Earthmother",lv=5,min=1,pre1={757},nx=767,bc=767,si=4783,ot="Take the Totem of Hawkwind to Baine Bloodhoof in Bloodhoof Village. Follow the road out of Camp Narache.",st="For you to continue with the Rites of the Earthmother you must pass two more tests. It is time for you to broaden your experience, $n.$b$bTravel to Bloodhoof Village and seek out the Chief, Baine Bloodhoof, son of Cairne. There you may continue your journey and earn the acceptance of the elders of Thunder Bluff.$b$bTake this totem to Baine. He will recognize my carvings and help you on your path.$b$bFollow the road out of Camp Narache and travel with haste. Do not stray or you will lose your way."},[764]={t="The Venture Co.",lv=10,min=5,pre1={751},ot="Kill 14 Venture Co. Workers and 6 Venture Co. Supervisors for Morin Cloudstalker at Bloodhoof Village.",st="This explains the buildup of Venture Co. employees and equipment we've seen in Mulgore. Those goblins... their company is expanding too quickly for their own good. It's how they say, show a goblin something, and you can hear the scales in the background.$b$bGreedy little things, they are. Unfortunately for their business enterprise, we tauren cannot allow them to conduct their operations in our lands. Go to their mine northeast of the ravaged caravan and send them a message.",how={{"kill",2978},{"kill",2979}}},[765]={t="Supervisor Fizsprocket",lv=12,min=5,pre1={751},ot="Kill Supervisor Fizsprocket and return his clipboard to Morin Cloudstalker at Bloodhoof Village.",st="According to the documents you salvaged from the caravan, the Venture Co. created many plans to attempt to drive us from our lands here, so that they could have free reign to plunder our lands.$b$bThe depths that they would sink to accomplish their goals disgusts and appalls me. I want the mastermind behind their plans killed. His name is Supervisor Fizsprocket, you will find him at the Venture Co. mine east of the ravaged caravan. Bring me his clipboard, we shall see if we find out anything useful.",how={{"loot",4819,{3051}}}},[766]={t="Mazzranache",lv=8,min=5,ot="Bring a Prairie Wolf Heart, Flatland Cougar Femur, Plainstrider Scale and Swoop Gizzard to Maur Raincaller at Bloodhoof Village.",st="My grandfather told me stories about his battles with a strider named Mazzranache. He told me of its demonic red eyes, razor-sharp talons and venomous bite.$b$bAs fortune would have it, while traveling across the plains, I encountered it, and it took a nasty bite from my shoulder. He was as terrible as my grandfather described. I will need some hard-to-find animal parts to clean the infection from his bite: a wolf heart, cougar femur, plainstrider scale and swoop gizzard.$b$bHurry, time is of the essence.",how={{"loot",4804,{2960,2959,2958}},{"loot",4805,{3035}},{"loot",4806,{2957,2956,3068}},{"loot",4807,{2971,2970,2969}}}},[767]={t="Rite of Vision",lv=6,min=3,nx=771,ot="Speak with Zarlman Two-Moons in Bloodhoof Village.",st="The Rite of Vision, one of the Rites of the Earthmother, will help guide you toward earning the respect of the elders of Thunder Bluff.$b$bOur people have learned that the land is our most holy provider. In order to take part in the ritualistic vision, you must speak with the spiritual leader of the village, Zarlman Two-Moons."},[768]={t="Gathering Leather",lv=8,min=4,ot="Bring 12 pieces of Light Leather to Veren Tallstrider in Thunder Bluff.",st="Greetings, young one.  You have a gleam in your eye; I can tell you are eager to venture back to the plains for the hunt.  May you bring honor to your clan!$B$BI work with the skins of beasts, fashioning them into clothes and armor for the people of Thunder Bluff.$B$BIf you hunt beasts and bring me their skins, then I will fashion something for you.",how={{"loot",2318}}},[769]={t="Kodo Hide Bag",lv=10,min=4,ot="Bring 4 Light Leather and 4 Coarse Thread to Veren Tallstrider in Thunder Bluff.",st="The kodo beasts of Mulgore are strong and sturdy -- traits much respected among us.  If you are skilled in leatherworking and wish the knowledge to make a Kodo Hide Bag, then bring me supplies for my trade.$B$BDo this, and I will share my knowledge with you.",how={{"loot",2318},{"buy",2320,{8363,3005,3081}}}},[770]={t="The Demon Scarred Cloak",lv=12,min=6,si=4854,ot="Find someone who knows of Ghost Howl.",st="The ragged hide of Ghost Howl still bears a terrible wound, gained from the wolf's battles against the Burning Legion.$B$BPerhaps someone in Bloodhoof Village should know of Ghost Howl's demise...."},[771]={t="Rite of Vision",lv=7,min=3,pre1={767},nx=772,ot="Collect 2 Well Stones and 2 Ambercorn and bring them back to Zarlman Two-Moons in Bloodhoof Village.",st="In order to pass through the Rite of Vision, you must gather the reagents needed to make the Water of the Seers.$b$bI will need well stones, which can be found around the water wells in Mulgore. With those I will combine Ambercorn, which fall beneath the mighty trees in our land.$b$bThese reagents contain magical elements, and when brewed and consumed before the tribal fire, will cause you to encounter a vision. Follow it, and it will lead you to the next step of this holy quest.",how={{"open",4808,{2910}},{"open",4809,{2912}}}},[772]={t="Rite of Vision",lv=7,min=3,pre1={771},nx=773,si=4823,ot="Consume the Water of the Seers in front of the tribal fire in Bloodhoof Village and follow the vision once it appears.",st="I now present you with the Water of the Seers.$b$bWhen you are ready, consume the waters near the tribal fire. Once you have ingested the holy waters, it will take a few moments before the vision materializes before the fire.$b$bAt that point, it is up to you to follow it to your destiny...."},[773]={t="Rite of Wisdom",lv=10,min=3,pre1={772},nx=775,ot="Travel to Red Rocks east of Thunder Bluff and speak with the Ancestral Spirit.",st="To gain acceptance amongst the elders of Thunder Bluff you must next complete the Rite of Wisdom.$b$bNow that you have passed the Rite of Vision, the ancestral spirits of Red Rocks will give you the blessing of our ancestors. Only those who have drunk from the Water of Seers can gain the blessing.$b$bTravel east of Thunder Bluff, to Red Rocks and seek out the Ancestral Spirit, $n."},[775]={t="Journey into Thunder Bluff",lv=10,min=3,pre1={773},nx=776,ot="Speak with Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.",st="You will now be revered within our great city. Any $r worthy of completing the Rites of the Earthmother earns that honor.$b$bFor your final quest, seek out our noble leader, Cairne Bloodhoof, who dwells atop the highest mesa in Thunder Bluff."},[776]={t="Rites of the Earthmother",lv=14,min=3,pre1={775},ot="Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff wants you to bring him the Horn of Arra'chea.",st="You have passed the Rites of the Earthmother and earned your place in Thunder Bluff.$b$bBut in order to maintain the spot that you strived so hard to achieve, you must continue to prove your worth to your people.$b$bWe are hunters, $n. Down below in Mulgore there is a mighty kodo named Arra'chea. Show me your skills in the ways of tracking and hunting by bringing me the Horn of Arra'chea.",how={{"loot",4841,{3058}}}},[780]={t="The Battleboars",lv=4,min=1,pre1={750},ot="Grull Hawkwind in Camp Narache wants you to kill Battleboars and bring back 8 Battleboar Snouts and 8 Battleboar Flanks.",st="The Battleboars of Brambleblade Ravine to the east are encroaching on our tribal hunting grounds. They are trained to be malicious by the Bristleback Quilboars with whom we are at war.$b$bGo and slay the vile creatures and bring back some snouts and flanks so that we can make stew for our young.",how={{"loot",4848,{2966,2954}},{"loot",4849,{2966,2954}}}},[781]={t="Attack on Camp Narache",lv=4,min=1,si=4850,ot="Bring the Bristleback Attack Plans to Chief Hawkwind in Camp Narache.",st="After carefully evaluating the map, you realize that what you discovered are the plans made by the Bristleback warchief for an extended siege on Camp Narache.$b$bSurely Chief Hawkwind could use this information!"},[784]={t="Vanquish the Betrayers",lv=7,min=3,nx=825,ot="Kill 10 Kul Tiras Sailors, 8 Kul Tiras Marines and Lieutenant Benedict and return to Gar'Thok in Razor Hill.",st="Led by Admiral Proudmoore, the humans of Kul Tiras encroached on Durotar, violating the Warchief's pact made with Jaina Proudmoore in order to defeat Archimonde years ago.$b$bThe human aggression was repelled and Tiragarde Keep fell. But recently, the Admiral's reserves, led by Lieutenant Benedict, have retaken the keep and once again pose a threat to our homeland. These humans show no respect for diplomacy.$b$bProve your honor and travel south to Tiragarde Keep to eliminate the human invaders.",how={{"kill",3128},{"kill",3129},{"kill",3192}}},[786]={t="Thwarting Kolkar Aggression",lv=8,min=5,rwc={[7]=1},ot="Lar Prowltusk outside of Sen'jin Village wants you to destroy the 3 sets of Attack Plans held within Kolkar Crag.",st="Lower your voice, $c. The Kolkar centaurs lie just over the ridge to the west in Kolkar Crag.$b$bLast night while they were raiding, I snuck into their village and discovered that the dirty beasts have a three-tiered attack planned on the trolls and orcs of Durotar.$b$bWe mustn't let their invasion come to fruition. Perhaps you can muster the might needed to infiltrate Kolkar Crag and destroy their attack plans.$b$bLast I saw, they had divided them up amongst three of their leaders.",how={{"click",3189},{"click",3190},{"click",3192}}},[788]={t="Cutting Teeth",lv=2,min=1,rwc={[7]=2},ot="Kill 10 Mottled Boars then return to Gornek at the Den.",st="The first order of business will be to put a little strength in your backbone. I could send you out to the Barrens to hunt kodo, but well, in all honesty, you're more useful to us alive than dead.$b$bI believe you would find a good match with the mottled boars you'll find to the north of here.",how={{"kill",3098}}},[789]={t="Sting of the Scorpid",lv=3,min=1,pre1={788},rwc={[7]=2},ot="Get 10 Scorpid Worker Tails for Gornek in the Den.",st="Powerful warrior and awkward novice alike have fallen to the venomous sting of the scorpid. You will find large numbers of scorpids northwest of here. Bring me ten of their tails as proof of your prowess in battle.$b$bThe antidote for their sting is actually made from venom extracted from their stingers. We keep large quantities of antidote for scorpid venom on hand to heal young bloods just like you...$b$bBut I'm sure you won't be needing any of that, will you?",how={{"loot",4862,{3124,3281}}}},[790]={t="Sarkoth",lv=5,min=1,nx=804,ot="Kill Sarkoth and bring his claw back to Hana'zua.",st="$C! I thought I would die out here with none to know of it. While I was hunting the scorpids of the Valley, I came across a particularly vicious-looking one. Hurling myself at it, I managed to inflict a massive blow to its claw before it closed around my leg.$b$bI wasn't ready for its stinger though, and it sliced down and into my chest, cutting into my flesh and letting my blood. Please, you must kill the scorpid for me! My honor must be upheld! I fought it up on the plateau to the south.",how={{"loot",4905,{3281}}}},[791]={t="Carry Your Weight",lv=7,min=4,ot="Furl Scornbrow in the Razor Hill watchtower wants 8 Canvas Scraps.",st="Age has rendered me useless in battle. Now I make myself useful in other ways.$b$bFrom this vantage point I watch for invaders. As our strength here grows, I find myself blowing the signal horn less and less.$b$bTo pass the time I fashion goods to help younger, more able warriors defend our homeland.$b$bFor you, I can fashion you a bag for your belongings. If such an item would be of use to you, bring me some canvas, a material common to the humans and centaurs.",how={{"loot",4870,{3129,5809,3128}}}},[792]={t="Vile Familiars",lv=4,min=2,nx=794,ot="Kill 12 Vile Familiars.$B$BReturn to Zureetha Fargaze outside the Den.",st="I trust the Valley of Trials will teach you much, young $c.$B$BI was sent to the Valley to guide you, but I have discovered a growing taint here...$B$BA group that calls itself the Burning Blade has a coven here in the Valley of Trials.  They are skulking in a cave to the northeast, and their Vile Familiars have spilled from its mouth to cause havoc.$B$BAs your first task against the Burning Blade, I bid you, defeat these familiars. Slay many and, if you survive, return to me.",how={{"kill",3101}}},[794]={t="Burning Blade Medallion",lv=5,min=1,pre1={792,1499},nx=805,ot="Bring the Burning Blade Medallion to Zureetha Fargaze, outside The Den.",st="Through my divinations, I see that an item of power hides deep within the Burning Blade Coven, guarded by beasts and black magic.$B$BIt is called the Burning Blade Medallion, and your next task is to find it and remove it from the coven.$B$BBut be wary, for the medallion may be possessed by an agent of the Burning Blade, and if so then the agent's power would be greater than the familiars you have already encountered.$B$BGo, $n.  You will find the coven in a cave, to the north and west.",how={{"loot",4859,{3183}}}},[804]={t="Sarkoth",lv=5,min=1,pre1={790},rwc={[7]=1},ot="Bring the news of Hana'zua's plight to Gornek at the Den.",st="Seeing the deed you have done for me steels my heart. I cannot fall so easily! I must endure!$b$bBut it remains that I cannot make the trek back to the Den unassisted. Please, $n, return to the Den and tell Gornek of my situation. Perhaps he can help me."},[805]={t="Report to Sen'jin Village",lv=5,min=1,pre1={794},ot="Speak with Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.",st="Your trials against the Burning Blade are finished... here in the Valley.  But I want you to report your findings.$B$BGo to the troll village of Sen'jin and seek out Master Gadrin.  Sen'jin Village is east out of the valley, then right at the fork.$B$BTell Gadrin of the Burning Blade, and that they have reached the Valley of Trials.  Discover from him if they have yet reached Sen'jin.$B$BGo, $n, and be swift.  I fear the evil found in the Burning Blade Coven is but the herald of a larger threat..."},[806]={t="Dark Storms",lv=12,min=4,pre1={823},nx=828,ot="Bring Fizzle's Claw to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.",st="We cannot allow the Burning Blade a foothold in Durotar!  We must destroy them before their evil festers!$B$BI have undergone my own investigations and found that a Burning Blade warlock, the goblin Fizzle Darkstorm, has camped within Thunder Ridge to the northwest.  There he and his cultist minions spread chaos.$B$BFind and defeat Fizzle, and bring me his dead claw!",how={{"loot",4869,{3203}}}},[808]={t="Minshina's Skull",lv=9,min=4,ot="Retrieve Minshina's skull from the circle of power on the Echo Isles.$B$BBring it to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.",st="I hear the voice of my brother, Minshina, calling to me in my dreams.$B$BHe was taken by Zalazane, the warlock on the Echo Isles to the east. And he is dead.$B$BBut death is not freedom for my brother. Minshina's spirit was trapped within his own skull by Zalazane's magics. In my dreams I see it with other skulls, in a circle of power on the largest Echo Isle. As long as it remains there my brother's soul is doomed.$B$BPlease, $n. Find the circle and retrieve Minshina's skull. Bring it to me.$B$BFree him!",how={{"open",4864,{3237}}}},[809]={t="Ak'Zeloth",lv=13,min=4,pre1={829},nx=924,ot="Speak with Ak'Zeloth in the Barrens.",st="Since the last great war when the Burning Legion was defeated, I have searched for sources of demonic corruption in orc society.  The collar you brought me confirms my fears.$B$BIt belongs to the Burning Blade, a cult that rallies around an item of demonic power.  It is called the Demon Seed, and it resides in the Barrens atop Dreadmist Peak.  It must be destroyed!$B$BGo to Far Watch Post, on the border of the Barrens to the west, and speak with my assistant, Ak'Zeloth.  He will direct you further."},[812]={t="Need for a Cure",lv=9,min=7,ot="Find Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar and get the Venomtail Antidote. Then bring the antidote to Rhinag near the northwestern border of Durotar.",st="$n... your timing is perfect. I just hope I can compliment your haste as well.$B$BI was careless while fighting a few of the venomtails nearby, and one of them stung me deeply. I can feel its poison weakening me even as we speak. At this rate, I got maybe an hour left to live. But I'll need your help if I'm to do so...$B$BKor'ghan in Orgrimmar knows how to make the antidote. Find him... and hurry, $n. I won't be able to last much longer. He should be in the Cleft of Shadow.",how={{"loot",4904,{3189}}}},[813]={t="Finding the Antidote",lv=9,min=7,ot="Bring 4 Venomtail Poison Sacs to Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar.",st="Venomtails are some of the deadliest scorpids in Durotar. It was unwise for Rhinag to hunt them without having some of the antidote with him, but right now, chastising is the last thing he needs.$B$BBring me a few venomtail poison sacs from any of the venomtails near the entrance of Orgrimmar and I'll make an antidote for him.$B$BMake haste, $n. One of our own needs your help.",how={{"loot",4886,{3127,3226,5823}}}},[815]={t="Break a Few Eggs",lv=8,min=6,ot="Bring 3 Taillasher Eggs to Cook Torka in Razor Hill.",st="Bah! I almost forgot I need to get breakfast ready.$B$B$n, get yourself movin' and get me some taillasher eggs. I'll need at least three of them if I'm going to have enough for tomorrow's meal.$B$BThe Bloodtalon taillashers can be fierce, and protect their eggs to the death more often than not. They sometimes bury their eggs too deep in the earth to uncover safely, but if you head to the Echo Isles to the southeast of Sen'jin Village, you can usually find them all over those islands.",how={{"open",4890,{3240}}}},[816]={t="Lost But Not Forgotten",lv=11,min=8,ot="Bring a sign of Kron's fate to Misha Tor'kren at the farmstead northwest of Razor Hill.",st="$n, please, can you help me? My son Kron went hunting days ago, and he still hasn't returned. He went west towards the Barrens to hunt crocolisks along Southfury River. I fear the worst.$B$BAs strong as he was, his stubborn pride has always drawn him into trouble. I warned him that the crocolisks were powerful and vicious. He grew angry and stormed off.$B$BIf you can't find him, at least bring me a sign of his fate... even if you have to open up the stomach of every crocolisk along the Southfury's banks.",how={{"loot",4891,{3110,3231}}}},[817]={t="Practical Prey",lv=8,min=5,ot="Bring 4 Durotar Tiger Furs to Vel'rin Fang in Sen'jin Village.",st="Many of the hides we use come from Durotar tigers, $n. Blankets, armor, tents: there are a great many reasons we hunt the beasts, and many reasons we let them thrive at the same time.$B$BThe time has come for us to cull the flock, so to speak. Our numbers grow, and our needs are beginning to overwhelm our stocks. I need more hides if I'm to prepare suitable goods for our people.$B$BBring me 4 Durotar tiger furs, and I shall reward you. You can find them on the islands south of here.",how={{"loot",4892,{3121,276198}}}},[818]={t="A Solvent Spirit",lv=7,min=5,ot="Bring 4 Intact Makrura Eyes and 8 vials of Crawler Mucus to Master Vornal in Sen'jin Village.",st="Although my eyes fail me, I still can see clearly enough. More often I must rely on my alchemical skills to aid me in magics that once came easily. But I refuse to take on an apprentice--no troll or orc worthy enough has ever come forward.$B$BAre you worthy? Yes, of course you are... of course you think you are.$B$BI need a few things. Will you get them for me?$B$BI need intact makrura eyes, and vials of crawler mucus. You can find them on any makrura or crawler in Durotar. We shall speak again soon.",how={{"loot",4887,{3103,3104}},{"loot",4888,{3107,3106}}}},[819]={t="Chen's Empty Keg",lv=15,min=11,nx=821,si=4926,ot="Find someone who knows about Chen's Empty Keg.",st="A small placard on one of the ends of the keg says,$B$B\"Chen Stormstout-$B$BMay your spirit be raised and always raise your spirits.\""},[821]={t="Chen's Empty Keg",lv=15,min=11,pre1={819},nx=822,ot="Bring 5 Savannah Lion Tusks, 5 Plainstrider Kidneys, and 1 Thunder Lizard Horn to Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet.",st="Would you like a taste of Chen's namesake? Ahh, the stormstout is a mighty brew. Chen taught the recipe to my mentor, and my mentor passed it on to me. I'll need you to get me a few things, but I can tell you this: the kick is worth it.$B$BBring me 5 savannah lion tusks from any savannah lion, 5 plainstrider kidneys from any plainstrider, and 1 thunder lizard horn from any species of thunder lizard. That should do the trick nicely.$B$BYou can find these ingredients throughout the Barrens.",how={{"loot",4893,{3425,3241}},{"loot",4894,{3245,3246,3244}},{"loot",4895,{3240}}}},[822]={t="Chen's Empty Keg",lv=24,min=11,pre1={821},ot="Bring 5 Lightning Glands, 1 Thunderhawk Saliva Gland and 1 Kodo Liver to Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet.",st="Good stuff, that stormstout, huh?$B$BI have another recipe that I learned from Chen. Would you be interested? It won't take long to make, and it might be useful if you plan on adventuring some more.$B$BBring me 5 lightning glands from any stormhide, 1 thunderhawk saliva gland from greater thunderhawks, and a kodo liver from any of the Barrens' kodos.$B$BLike I said, this stuff has kick; it's the trogg brew that I mentioned to you before.",how={{"loot",4898,{3238}},{"loot",4897,{3249}},{"loot",4896,{5827,3236,3237}}}},[823]={t="Report to Orgnil",lv=7,min=4,nx=806,ot="Speak with Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.",st="We at Sen'jin Village are not without our own troubles, and we thank you for your aid.  But the news you bring regarding the Burning Blade could be trouble for everyone.$B$BThere is an orc stationed at Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar, who polices Durotar from evils such as the Burning Blade!  Go to Orgnil and tell him of our plight, as well as your news from the Valley of Trials.  He will want to know these things.$B$BRazor Hill lies to the north."},[824]={t="Je'neu of the Earthen Ring",lv=27,min=23,pre1={1918},si=16408,ot="Bring the Befouled Water Globe to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.",st="The Earthen Ring is a shamanistic group dedicated to studying and preserving the elements.  They have forgotten more about crazy old gods, ancient legends and lore than most scholars will ever know.$B$BLucky for you, I know someone in the Earthen Ring here in Ashenvale.  Head over to Zoram'gar Outpost on the coast of the Zoram Strand; show Je'neu Sancrea what you found.  If anyone can figure out that globe's significance, it'd be him."},[825]={t="From The Wreckage....",lv=8,min=3,pre1={784},ot="Gar'Thok of Razor Hill wants you to retrieve 3 Gnomish Tools from the wreckage off the coast.",st="One of my most observant scouts brings back word that the wreckage of Proudmoore's fleet still remains off the coast of Durotar, just east of Tiragarde Keep.$b$bIt is no secret that the humans, in alliance with those foul little creatures known as gnomes, have an advanced knowledge of mechanics. We must have a complete understanding of all our potential enemies. And our people will benefit from this new knowledge as well.$b$bSwim through the wreckage, $n, and retrieve for me the tools of the Alliance.",how={{"open",4863,{3236}}}},[826]={t="Zalazane",lv=10,min=4,rwc={[7]=2},ot="Defeat Zalazane.$B$BKill 8 Voodoo Trolls and 8 Hexed Trolls.$B$BBring Zalazane's Head to Gadrin.",st="The witchdoctor Zalazane dwells on the Echo Isles to the east.  They are the isles we once called home.$B$BFrom there he sends his trolls to the mainland, to hex our people and drag more of them under his sway.$B$BHe must be stopped.$B$BDefeat Zalazane and his minions -- former Darkspear trolls, now lost to us.  Bring me his head and I will know his reign of evil is over.",how={{"kill",3207},{"kill",3206},{"loot",4866,{3205}}}},[827]={t="Skull Rock",lv=12,min=4,pre1={828},nx=829,ot="Gather Searing Collars from the cultists in Skull Rock.$B$BBring them to Margoz at his camp.",st="$n.  The Burning Blade has infested the cave east of Orgrimmar known as Skull Rock.  Inside that cave they perform vile rituals, and burn their own flesh with Searing Collars.$B$BBy wearing these collars, I believe the cultists attune themselves to demonic power.  But to confirm this, I must have a collection of the collars to study.$B$BGo to Skull Rock and gather Searing Collars from the cultists you find there.  Bring them to me, and I will uncover their secrets.",how={{"loot",4871,{3195,3196,3199}}}},[828]={t="Margoz",lv=12,min=4,pre1={806},nx=827,ot="Speak with Margoz.",st="One of our Shamans, Margoz, knows more of the Burning Blade's corruption.  He speaks of a cave called Skull Rock in the mountains - just outside Orgrimmar! - that shelters a large band of Burning Blade cultists.$B$BBefore you go to Skull Rock speak with Margoz.  He is wise and his council is valued.$B$BHe is camped to the northeast, between the coast and Drygulch Ravine.$B$BFollow his advice, but whatever Margoz says, $n, I still want you to crush those cultists!"},[829]={t="Neeru Fireblade",lv=12,min=4,pre1={827},nx=809,si=6658,ot="Bring an Example Collar to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.",st="The Searing Collars you brought me are powerful, demonic implements.  Divining their origin is, I'm afraid, beyond my skills as a shaman.  We will need a warlock to study them.$B$BTake a searing collar to Neeru Fireblade.  Although he is a skilled warlock, he professes to use his powers to thwart demons, and claims his research in the occult is benign.  Be that true or false, we may need his aid against the demonic cult in Durotar.$B$BYou may find Neeru in Orgrimmar in the Cleft of Shadow."},[830]={t="The Admiral's Orders",lv=7,min=1,nx=831,si=4883,ot="Take Admiral Proudmoore's Orders to Gar'Thok in Razor Hill.",st="You open the aged and weathered envelope and discover an official looking document. You recognize the seal of Admiral Proudmoore.$b$bThis looks important. Perhaps Gar'Thok, the commander of Razor Hill, would be interested in having this information."},[831]={t="The Admiral's Orders",lv=7,min=1,pre1={830},si=4883,ot="Deliver Admiral Proudmoore's Orders to Nazgrel in Thrall's chamber in Orgrimmar.",st="Humans cannot be trusted. We fought alongside them with a weary heart, knowing they would betray us one day.$b$bAdmiral Proudmoore's death was not enough to stop his legacy of deceit. The human scum had his plans well laid out before he ever met his demise.$b$bHis reign won't even die with Benedict it seems. Who knows how long it will be before the next waves of Proudmoore's men land upon our shores.$b$bWe need to get these orders to Nazgrel in Orgrimmar immediately! He can be found in Thrall's chamber."},[832]={t="Burning Shadows",lv=12,min=4,si=4903,ot="Take this eye to Neeru Fireblade.",st="<Words emanate from the pendant and into your mind.>$B$BGazz'uz?$B$BGazz'uz...report!$B$BThere is word of your discovery in Skull Rock.  You must prepare for an attack!$B$BGazz'uz, I order you to speak!  Speak or I will make sure Neeru Fireblade knows of your presence, and he will descend on you with swift brutality.$B$BDo not test your skills against Neeru...$B$B...Gazz'uz, are you there...?"},[833]={t="A Sacred Burial",lv=10,min=7,ot="Lorekeeper Raintotem wants you to kill 8 Bristleback Interlopers at Red Rocks.",st="Only the most valiant tauren are laid to rest at Red Rocks, our sacred burial ground. It is an honor bestowed upon the great warriors who helped found and defend Thunder Bluff and those who have given their lives for the greater good of their tribes and chieftains.$b$bBut it appears a foul menace has made its way onto our holy land. A band of Bristleback Interlopers is ravaging the grave site and I am too old and past my prime to drive them away.$b$bThey must be driven off with force, $n.",how={{"kill",3232}}},[834]={t="Winds in the Desert",lv=9,min=7,nx=835,ot="Retrieve 5 Sacks of Supplies and return them to Rezlak near Orgrimmar.",st="I'm Rezlak, one of Gazlowe's boys. Boss sent me to help the orcs here in Durotar. Things'd been going good except for the caravans. Can't manage to keep them safe! Makes my job a little harder, you know?$b$bThe last shipment--they promised it'd get through!--was snatched by the Dustwind harpies of...where was it...Razorwind Canyon?$b$bI gotta have those supplies or I'll never get anything done! Follow the big canyon to the south, you'll find the ravine cut right into the west and east sides of the walls.",how={{"open",4918,{3290}}}},[835]={t="Securing the Lines",lv=11,min=7,pre1={834},si=277661,ot="Kill 12 Dustwind Savages and 8 Dustwind Storm Witches for Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.",st="Gazlowe told me once, \"Rezlak. There's one thing you need to know in life, and that's if you want something done well, do it yourself.\"$b$bI can't deal with losing all our caravans, so I'm just going to take matters into my own hands. Drygulch Ravine lies through the eastern part of Razorwind Canyon. If we kill all the harpies there, the routes will be safe.$b$bOf course, there was one other thing that Gazlowe taught me, and that's \"You can get anything done for a price.\" So, going to help me out, $n?",how={{"kill",3117},{"kill",3118}}},[837]={t="Encroachment",lv=10,min=6,ot="Kill 4 Razormane Quilboars, 4 Razormane Scouts, 4 Razormane Dustrunners and 4 Razormane Battleguards for Gar'Thok at Razor Hill.",st="When we arrived, the Razormane quilboars possessed much of the land, and proved a thorn in our sides. Through our efforts we have driven out the largest part of their numbers, but still they remain well-fortified in some areas.$b$bIt has gone on long enough, however. For our own protection, we cannot allow the Razormane any hold in our lands. Their camps can be found to the west of here. Look for the brambles and you will find them. Today we drive them from Durotar, tomorrow, perhaps from all of Kalimdor.",how={{"kill",3111},{"kill",3112},{"kill",3113},{"kill",3114}}},[840]={t="Conscript of the Horde",lv=12,min=10,nx=842,si=4992,ot="Follow the western road from Razor Hill to the Barrens over a bridge.$B$BStop at the orc outpost across the bridge.$B$BGive Kargal Battlescar at the Barrens outpost your recruitment letter.",st="Hmm, you look pretty strong.$B$BListen, my good friend Kargal needs some new recruits for Barrens duty. I know you want to do what's right for the Horde. Well, this is your chance.$B$BTake this recruitment letter to Kargal and see if he'll sign it."},[842]={t="Crossroads Conscription",lv=12,min=10,pre1={840},si=4995,ot="Follow the western road from Kargal's Far Watch Outpost.$B$BAt the T intersection, turn left and follow the road south. $B$BFind Sergra Darkthorn at the crossing of roads within the Crossroads.",st="Take this signed recruitment letter to the Crossroads.$B$BSergra Darkthorn, curse her hide, is in charge there. She's a nasty shaman who will talk your head in circles before she lets you do anything useful. Thrall is convinced she's something special, but I'm not so sure.$B$BYou'll just have to decide for yourself, pup..."},[843]={t="Gann's Reclamation",lv=23,min=17,nx=846,ot="Gann Stonespire wants you to kill 15 Bael'dun Excavators and 5 Bael'dun Foremen.$b$bBring Khazgorm's Journal to Gann Stonespire.",st="In solitude I wander these roads.$b$bThe dwarves of Bael Modan show no respect for my land. Horrendous blasts drive holes deep into the ground as noisy machines rip apart the hills. Lands which once served as home and provider to my tribe are now riddled with destructive dwarves.$b$bAttempts at reaching a diplomatic resolution have failed. Now is the time for decisive action.$b$bDrive the dwarves from the Bael Modan excavation by force and bring to me the journal of their leader, Prospector Khazgorm.",how={{"kill",3374},{"kill",3375},{"loot",5006,{3392}}}},[844]={t="Plainstrider Menace",lv=12,min=10,nx=845,ot="Collect 7 Plainstrider Beaks and return them to Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.",st="Your first prey will be easy.$B$BThe plainstriders to the east have been harassing our food supplies and have become a nuisance.$B$BPut down the plainstriders and return to me with their beaks.",how={{"loot",5087,{3244,3246}}}},[845]={t="The Zhevra",lv=13,min=10,pre1={844},nx=903,ot="Slay Zhevra Runners to collect 4 Zhevra Hooves for Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.",st="The zhevra, although not the fiercest beast in the Barrens, are a shade tougher than the plainstriders.  Don't worry -- we'll send you against bigger prey in good time, but for now your teeth could use a little more cutting.$B$BHunt the zhevra to the north and south, and collect their hooves.  Bring them to me and perhaps we'll next send you against something tougher.",how={{"loot",5086,{3242}}}},[846]={t="Revenge of Gann",lv=26,min=17,pre1={843},nx=849,ot="Gann Stonespire wants you to bring him 6 vials of Nitroglycerin, 6 bundles of Wood Pulp, and 6 samples of Sodium Nitrate.",st="It is clear the prospector depended on explosives and those noisy vehicles to rip the ground apart. We can expect a new foreman to take over soon.$b$bI want to give the dwarves a taste of their own medicine. According to these plans if we combine nitroglycerin with wood pulp and sodium nitrate we can create an explosive charge. The rifleman, soldiers and officers in the Keep are known to have the supplies.$b$bCollect these items and bring them to me. I will fashion a charge that the dwarves won't forget!",how={{"loot",5017,{3376,3377,3378}},{"loot",5018,{3376,3377,3378}},{"loot",5019,{3376,3377,3378}}}},[848]={t="Fungal Spores",lv=15,min=10,nx=853,ot="Bring 4 Fungal Spores to Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads.",st="The oases of the Barrens hide a mystery.  Life energy flows from their waters, invigorating the plants and beasts that drink it.$B$BInvigorating, and altering.$B$BThere is a mushroom that grows near these oases.  Its spores hold properties that we, the apothecaries of Lordaeron, find useful.$B$BBring me these spores and you will earn our gratitude.",how={{"open",5012,{3640}}}},[849]={t="Revenge of Gann",lv=26,min=17,pre1={846},si=5021,ot="Destroy the flying machine at Bael Modan and return to Gann Stonespire.",st="Following Khazgorm's plans it should be no problem to fashion an explosive charge$b$bAh, there we go.$b$bNow, $n, I am going to entrust you with a special task. Take this explosive stick and use it to blow up the flying machine at Bael Modan.$b$bNot only is the flying machine a key part of the site's infrastructure it also serves as a weapon of war. More importantly it is an icon of power and an insult to the memory of my tribe.$b$bMake me proud by completing this heroic task and you shall be rewarded.",how={{"click",3644}}},[850]={t="Kolkar Leaders",lv=16,min=11,nx=851,ot="Bring Barak's Head to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.",st="The centaurs have plagued the Tauren for years.  And recently, the Kolkar centaurs of the Barrens have grown into a real threat.  Normally they were disorganized in these lands, but new leaders have risen among them.  Rallying them.$B$BTo preserve our holdings here, these centaur leaders must be destroyed.$B$BBring me the head of Barak Kodobane.  He camps near the Forgotten Pools to the north.$B$BDefeat him, then return to me.",how={{"loot",5022,{3394}}}},[851]={t="Verog the Dervish",lv=18,min=11,pre1={850},nx=852,ot="Bring Verog's Head to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.",st="The centaur Verog the Dervish wanders the Barrens, and will be difficult to find.  But he is based at the centaur command tent at the Stagnant Oasis to the southeast.  It may be possible to draw him to you.$B$BTravel to the Stagnant Oasis to the southeast and attack centaur near the command tent.  It will be dangerous, but if you can kill enough centaur then they should raise an alarm.  And Verog will come.$B$BBring me his head and I will place it with Barak Kodobane's.",how={{"loot",5023,{3395}}}},[852]={t="Hezrul Bloodmark",lv=19,min=11,pre1={851},nx=4021,ot="Bring Hezrul's Head to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.",st="Hezrul Bloodmark is the leader of the Kolkar centaurs in the Barrens.  He is fierce, brutal and cunning.  Defeating him would disrupt and fracture the Kolkars, greatly reducing their threat to us.$B$BSo kill him.  As with Barak and Verog, bring me Hezrul's Head.$B$BHe leads his people from the Lushwater Oasis, to the south.",how={{"loot",5025,{3396}}}},[853]={t="Apothecary Zamah",lv=15,min=10,pre1={848},si=5027,ot="Bring the Rendered Spores to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff, before the time limit is up.",st="I have rendered the spores you gave me into an emulsion.  I must now send it to my associate, Apothecary Zamah.  If you were to carry this to her, she can offer you something from our stores of alchemical goods.$B$BShe is in the Pools of Vision, a cave beneath the shamans of Thunder Bluff.  The path to this cave is well hidden, but you may find it on the Spirit Rise bluff.$B$BDo hurry.  This emulsion will maintain its potency for only a short time, and must be resealed and processed before then."},[854]={t="Journey to the Crossroads",lv=12,min=9,ex={844},ot="Speak with Thork at the Crossroads in the Barrens.",st="I have foreseen your arrival, young $c. Though perhaps you are not so young anymore.$B$BI think that it is time for you to move deeper into this land. I can sense that you are destined for great things.$B$BIt is the Crossroads that you must seek out, for our lives with the orcs have become intertwined and they need assistance. Continue down this road towards the east and follow it north to the Crossroads. Find Thork within its walls, he has the Earthmother's blessing."},[855]={t="Centaur Bracers",lv=14,min=9,ot="Bring 15 Centaur Bracers to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.",st="The Kolkar are a threat to the Horde's claims in the Barrens; we must reduce the numbers of their troops.  And so, I have a bounty task for you.$B$BWhile in Kolkar territories, slay their warriors and collect centaur bracers.  Return when you have a heap of bracers and the Horde will reward you well.",how={{"loot",5030,{3273,3397,3274,3275,3272}}}},[857]={t="The Tear of the Moons",lv=30,min=22,ot="Feegly the Exiled wants you to retrieve for him the Tear of the Moons.",st="The power was mine! In my very hands! And I want it back! Back I say!$b$bThose dirty excavators uncovered it... so beautiful it was. Deemed the Tear of the Moons, it was the first great discovery we made at Bael Modan.$b$bIt should have been mine! Mine I say!$b$bGeneral Twinbraid grew jealous of the power it gave me. He locked it away in the Keep. Called it cursed, he did! The fool!$b$bOthers wanted it and they had to be stopped! That bastard Twinbraid drove me off.$b$bNow I want it back. Back I say!",how={{"open",5038,{3646}}}},[858]={t="Ignition",lv=18,min=13,nx=863,ot="Get the Ignition Key and bring it to Wizzlecrank.",st="I don't suppose Sputtervalve sent you? I'm in a bind here. I hopped in without realizing that I need a key to unlock the shredder's movement column. One of the other shredder operators asked me if everything was okay, and I panicked! Instead of telling him that I was missing my key, I told him there was some sort of mechanical problem.$b$bWe need to get out of here on the double! Go up to the control room at the top of the derrick, the supervisor should have a key for this shredder.$b$bHelp me out here!",how={{"loot",5050,{3445}}}},[862]={t="Dig Rat Stew",lv=23,min=15,ot="Bring 8 Dig Rats to Grub east of the Crossroads.",st="A $c like you must get pretty hungry out here in The Barrens. Me, I'm starving all day long.$b$bTell you what, I'll fix you up a nice stew. Just need a few dig rats.$b$bSeems those filthy dwarves at Bael Modan are overrun with everyone's favorite feast. Now head on down south to Bael Modan and bring me back some dig rats.$b$bYou can't call yourself a seasoned adventurer until you've spent some time killing rats! Haw!",how={{"loot",5051,{3444}}}},[863]={t="The Escape",lv=18,min=13,pre1={858},ne=1,ot="Protect Wizzlecrank and the stolen goblin shredder on the way to Sputtervalve in Ratchet.",st="I suppose I'll learn as we go... Couldn't be too hard. Just some buttons here, and a lever or two... Well, are you ready to go?",how={{"kill",3282},{"kill",3284},{"kill",6606}}},[865]={t="Raptor Horns",lv=18,min=13,nx=1491,ot="Gather 5 Intact Raptor Horns from Sunscale Scytheclaws, and bring them to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",st="The raptors of the Barrens are smarter than raptors in other lands.  And I think all that smarts is hiding in their horns!  If so, then I could grind their horns into powder and use it to make \"smart drinks.\"  I could sell them for a fortune!!!$B$BAnd you can help me.  Find me intact raptor horns from sunscale scytheclaws.  They roam in the southern Barrens, and in the northern Barrens near the border of Ashenvale Forest.",how={{"loot",5055,{3256}}}},[866]={t="Root Samples",lv=16,min=9,ot="Bring 8 Root Samples to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",st="The herbs of the Barrens are not quite like herbs in other lands.  Their properties are mostly the same, but the oasis water here alters the plants; they are just slightly different.$B$BI want to study those differences... to see if they're exploitable!$B$BIf you are skilled in herbalism, then gather root samples off the herbs you find in the Barrens.  Bring back these samples so that I may compare them with herbs from other regions.",how={{"open",5056,{3729,3726,3730}}}},[867]={t="Harpy Raiders",lv=15,min=12,nx=875,ot="Collect 8 Witchwing talons.$B$BReturn them to Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads.",st="The blasted harpies have been ravaging our caravan supplies for too long. It's time we slit a few of their throats and diminished their numbers.$B$BI've been snooping around their nests and figured out who leads who. The most devastating attack will destroy a good section of their lower chain of command and then we can work our way to the top.$B$BI'll start you off slow, take out Witchwing Harpies and Witchwing Roguefeathers in the Northwest and bring me 8 Witchwing talons. That should be a good start...",how={{"loot",5064,{3276,3277}}}},[868]={t="Egg Hunt",lv=22,min=17,si=5059,ot="Bring 12 Silithid Eggs and the Digging Claw to Korran at the Crossroads.",st="Hey, $n. I been sent to the Crossroads to watch over the land and take note of its happenings for my masters in Orgrimmar.$B$BOne object of my studies are the insect-like creatures found to the south in the Field of Giants. We know little of the creatures, so I be makin' it a point to discover more. They seem to have intelligence to them, more so than any normal animal.$B$BTake this digging claw and collect some of the creatures' eggs from their mounds, but be careful: if alerted, they will attack you.",how={{"open",5058,{3685}}}},[869]={t="Raptor Thieves",lv=13,min=9,nx=3281,ot="Bring 12 Raptor Heads to Gazrog at the Crossroads.",st="Not long ago, a shipment of silver was stolen from our guard tower.  It was meant as payroll to the Crossroads' guards, and we want that silver back.$B$BThe strange thing is... we caught one of the thieves on the night of the theft.  And... it was a raptor!  Unbelievable!$B$BI don't know what raptors would want with silver.  But I don't care -- I want the raptors dead so they won't steal from us again!$B$BHunt raptors in the Barrens.  Collect for me their heads!",how={{"loot",5062,{3255,3254}}}},[870]={t="The Forgotten Pools",lv=13,min=10,nx=877,ot="Report back to Tonga Runetotem with your findings.",st="Long ago, the Barrens was a lush place, teeming with life.  But war and cataclysm raged across the land, scorching it and leaving a dry husk.  Such is the way of things, and it saddens my heart.$B$BBut within the past few years, new oases have formed in the Barrens, and life stirs.  And deep down, we druids sense a power leaking its way to the surface.$B$BWe must find its source.  Travel to the Forgotten Pools, northwest of the Crossroads.  Search its waters for a source of power, then return here."},[871]={t="Disrupt the Attacks",lv=12,min=9,nx=872,ot="Of the Razormane tribe, kill 8 Water Seekers, 8 Thornweavers and 3 Hunters, and then return to Thork in the Crossroads.",st="All the quilboars are our enemies, $n. Some just prove to be more of a nuisance than others.$B$BThe Razormane tribe has been attacking our supply lines from Durotar, causing us no end of annoyance. I have scouts seeking the leader of these raids, but until then, any losses you can inflict on the filthy pig men would aid us.$B$BStart in the northeast towards Durotar. You can always tell their dens from the huge thorny vines that come up from the earth. Seek them out, and slay them.",how={{"kill",3267},{"kill",3268},{"kill",3265}}},[872]={t="The Disruption Ends",lv=15,min=9,pre1={871},ot="Kill 8 Razormane Geomancers, 8 Razormane Defenders, and Kreenig Snarlsnout.$B$BThen bring Kreenig Snarlsnout's Tusk to Thork at the Crossroads.",st="One of my scouts witnessed an attack on a caravan from Durotar, $n. The culprits are indeed the Razormane tribe of quilboars. One of the quilboars in particular is leading the raids: Kreenig Snarlsnout. He was seen northeast of here, just south of the road from Durotar. If the threat is to be ended, then Kreenig must die.$B$BTo be sure the attacks cease, though, I say we add insult to their injury. Kill Kreenig along with more of their tribe, and return to me when you have his tusk.",how={{"kill",3269},{"kill",3266},{"loot",5063,{3438}}}},[873]={t="Isha Awak",lv=27,min=10,pre1={874},ot="Bring the Heart of Isha Awak to Mahren Skyseer.",st="The grand Isha Awak is lord of these waters.  Great is his strength, and solemn his pride.  The humans on the coast fear him, for he has consumed many of their number.$B$BBut I do not fear him.  I am grateful he is here.  He is a worthy challenge, and honorable prey.$B$BIf you are ready, then swim out and search for Isha Awak, the Deep Doom.$B$BHis spirit dwells in his heart, and to hear its beat is to know your fate.",how={{"loot",5104,{3476}}}},[874]={t="Mahren Skyseer",lv=27,min=9,pre1={913},nx=873,ot="Speak with Mahren Skyseer.",st="You have hunted the beasts of the Barrens.  Your spirit is strong.  But a hunter must always be prepared.  A true hunter can stalk prey down any path.  Mountains and swamps will not sway $ghim:her;.$B$BNot even the sea.$B$BFind my sister, Mahren.  She hunts the great water beasts along the coast.  She will be your teacher in their ways.$B$BBut be wary in your search for her, for the Barrens' coast is held by humans."},[875]={t="Harpy Lieutenants",lv=16,min=12,pre1={867},nx=876,ot="Collect 6 Harpy Lieutenant Rings from Witchwing Slayers and return them to Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads.",st="Hahaha, $n. Back for more? Good, I like to hear that.$B$BThis time I want you to assassinate some of the harpy lieutenants in the Dry Hills. Only Witchwing Slayers can be lieutenants, and you can tell them apart by the rings they carry. They are a nasty bunch, but they lead some of the underlings in that area. Taking out 6 of them will be a decisive strike against their matriarchy.$B$BMake sure they die painfully, $n. We want those harpy wenches to know the idiocy of picking fights with the Horde.",how={{"loot",5065,{3278}}}},[876]={t="Serena Bloodfeather",lv=20,min=12,pre1={875},nx=1060,ot="Slay Serena Bloodfeather and return her head to Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads.",st="You did so well with the lieutenants and underlings that I'd like you to do one last thing for me.$B$BSerena Bloodfeather is the sister of a harpy named Bloodfeather who was slain by Rexxar quite a while ago. Apparently, these attacks on the Horde caravans are revenge for her sister's death.$B$BI need you to slit her throat and bring me back her head. I want to place it on the next caravan we send out... Give those harpies something to think about.",how={{"loot",5067,{3452}}}},[877]={t="The Stagnant Oasis",lv=16,min=10,pre1={870},nx=880,si=5068,ot="Return to Tonga at The Crossroads, after investigating the Stagnant Oasis.",st="Like the one you found at the Forgotten Pools, there may be fissures at the other oases in the Barrens.  If so, then perhaps the fissures are the oases' source of life.$B$BWe must test this.$B$BHere, take these seeds.  They are dead and infertile, but take them to the Stagnant Oasis to the southeast.  If there is a fissure there, then place the seeds within it...and observe.",how={{"click",3737}}},[878]={t="Tribes at War",lv=21,min=14,nx=5052,ot="Kill 6 Bristleback Water Seekers, 12 Bristleback Thornweavers and 12 Bristleback Geomancers and return to Mangletooth at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.",st="You must strike my enemies. <snort> You must help Mangletooth and the Razormane by weakening the Bristlebacks. Both tribes are very spiritual--tied to the earth and its power. <snort> It gives us strength in all things... especially war.$B$BIf you want to find out who really causes Thork <snort> and the Horde such anguish, then help Mangletooth! You attack the spiritual leaders of the Bristlebacks to the north; weaken them so the Razormanes can defeat them and rule the Barrens.",how={{"kill",3260},{"kill",3261},{"kill",3263}}},[879]={t="Betrayal from Within",lv=25,min=17,pre1={5052},nx=906,ot="Kill Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane and bring their skulls to Mangletooth at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.",st="Three of my tribe came out of the Kraul to lead the raids against the Horde, $r. <snort> They are ruthless and cunning, and if you defeat them, then your Crossroads and even most of the Barrens will learn peace... <snort> at least from the Razormane tribe. <snort>$B$BNak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane are the ones you seek. They are far to the south  of the Barrens. One is a spell caster, another a tracker, and their leader, the one called Orcbane, <snort> a warrior. Kill them, $r, like they have killed me.",how={{"loot",5074,{3436}},{"loot",5073,{3434}},{"loot",5072,{3435}}}},[880]={t="Altered Beings",lv=16,min=10,pre1={877},ot="Bring 8 Altered Snapjaw Shells to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads.",st="Your findings are incredible, $n.  These oases hold properties that must come from an outside source.  Or perhaps an inside one.$B$BI want to know how these fissures are affecting the beasts who drink from the oases' water.$B$BHunt oasis snapjaws at the Lushwater and Stagnant Oases.  Bring me their shells so I may examine them.",how={{"loot",5098,{3461,209511}}}},[881]={t="Echeyakee",lv=16,min=10,pre1={903},nx=905,si=10327,ot="Bring Echeyakee's Hide to Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads.",st="Whitemist, Echeyakee in the Tauren tongue, is the king of the savannah cats.  He hunts with such stealth, they say he's like a thin, white mist on the earth.  And he kills so fast his prey have no time for fear, or pain.$B$BThe Tauren say he is both mercy and death.$B$BYou will learn if that's true, for I now set you on the path to hunt Echeyakee.  His lair is northeast of the Crossroads, among the bones of giant Kodo$B$BGo.  Blow this horn when you reach his lair.  Blow the horn, and he will come.",how={{"loot",5100,{3475}}}},[882]={t="Ishamuhale",lv=19,min=10,pre1={3261},nx=907,si=10338,ot="Bring Ishamuhale's Fang to Jorn at Camp Taurajo.",st="Ishamuhale, Speartooth, is the fiercest sunscale raptor of the Barrens.  He does not hunt for sport, nor for food.  He hunts because hunting is his passion.  He kills because it is his nature to kill.$B$BAnd you will learn of his nature, $n, for your path now follows the taloned tracks of Ishamuhale.$B$BBegin the hunt.  Slay his favorite prey, a zhevra, then bring its carcass to the dead tree northwest of Ratchet.  Ishamuhale will smell the carcass and be drawn to it.$B$BBe ready when he comes.",how={{"loot",5101,{3257}}}},[883]={t="Lakota'mani",lv=22,min=10,si=5099,ot="Bring the Hoof of Lakota'mani to Jorn at Camp Taurajo.",st="The Hoof of Lakota'mani is a symbol of the strength of the great kodo."},[884]={t="Owatanka",lv=24,min=10,si=5102,ot="Bring Owatanka's Tailspike to Jorn at Camp Taurajo.",st="When touched, sparks fly from the tailspike of Owatanka."},[885]={t="Washte Pawne",lv=25,min=10,si=5103,ot="Bring Washte Pawne's Feather to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo.",st="The feather of Washte Pawne is painful to the touch."},[886]={t="The Barrens Oases",lv=10,min=10,nx=870,bc=870,ot="Speak with Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads.",st="The druids of Thunder Bluff sense a strange power leaking into the Barrens, east of Mulgore.$B$BTonga Runetotem was sent to discover the source of this power, but we fear he will need aid.$B$BTravel to the Barrens and speak with Tonga.  He will be at the Crossroads.  To reach there, take the road east out of Bloodhoof village.  Enter the Barrens, then turn north when the road forks.  Continue north and  you will find the Crossroads.$B$BAnd do not leave the road, $n, for the Barrens is a harsh land."},[887]={t="Southsea Freebooters",lv=14,min=9,nx=890,ot="Kill 12 Southsea Brigands and 6 Southsea Cannoneers for Gazlowe in Ratchet.",st="I sure wish Vice Admiral Grezzlik did a better job of keeping the seas safe for our trading vessels. With all the gold the trade princes have poured into the Trade Fleets, it ticks me off to see so many pirates running willy-nilly, raiding my ships and stealing my goods!$b$bI heard that the Southsea Freebooters have set up a camp just south of here. They've been a real thorn in my side and if Grezzlik won't take care of them, well, maybe you can help me get rid of them.",how={{"kill",3381},{"kill",3382}}},[888]={t="Stolen Booty",lv=16,min=9,pre1={892},ot="Retrieve the Shipment of Boots and Telescopic Lens for Gazlowe in Ratchet.",st="While I'd like to recover all my goods, I'm sure that's not possible. Still, there's a few things that I absolutely must have!$b$bAs you see, my observatory is ready to go, but it needs the smaller of the two lenses. The first arrived by caravan from Durotar, but the second was bound by ship, and never arrived. Also, I never got my boot shipment from Drizzlik in Booty Bay!$b$bHead down to the pirate camp and see if you can find them.",how={{"open",5076,{3767}},{"open",5077,{3768}}}},[890]={t="The Missing Shipment",lv=14,min=9,pre1={887},nx=892,si=5080,ot="Bring Gazlowe's Ledger to Wharfmaster Dizzywig.",st="I've been waiting forever for my last shipment of goods from Booty Bay! I'm pretty sure that it must have been stolen by the Freebooters, but just to make sure, will you go down to the dockside and ask Dizzywig if my goods were already put into my warehouse without my knowledge?$b$bHere, take my ledger down to Dizzywig and have him double check my inventory records against his logs."},[891]={t="The Guns of Northwatch",lv=20,min=13,ot="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun of Ratchet wants you to collect 10 Theramore Medals and slay Captain Fairmount, Cannoneer Whessan and Cannoneer Smythe.",st="Yet another ship from my fleet has been lost to those overzealous humans at Northwatch Hold!$b$bThose bastards must be dealt with. Their paranoia has them in a state of frenzy. Trigger happy, reckless louts are shooting at anything in their sights.$b$bTravel south along the Merchant Coast to the Hold and lay siege to their forces. Bring me the medals of their soldiers as proof. And for the love of my fleet, slay Captain Fairmount and her overzealous cannoneers!",how={{"kill",3393},{"kill",3455},{"kill",3454},{"loot",5078,{3386,3385,3455}}}},[892]={t="The Missing Shipment",lv=14,min=9,pre1={890},nx=888,si=5080,ot="Return Gazlowe's Ledger to Gazlowe in Ratchet.",st="Everything looks square from my records, $n. Go on back and tell Gazlowe he's out of luck. I wouldn't be surprised if it was the pirates that nabbed his goodies.$b$bNothing else I can do for him. Oh... though you could tell him that I've got some things from Undermine for him, when he has the time to come pick them up."},[893]={t="Weapons of Choice",lv=24,min=17,nx=1153,ot="Bring a Razormane Backstabber, a Charred Razormane Wand and a Razormane War Shield to Tatternack Steelforge at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.",st="The Razormane quilboars to the south, beyond the Field of Giants, have no skilled blacksmiths from what I am told, but they've apparently started to develop sturdier weapons. I'd like to get my hands on a few different types to learn their techniques if possible.$B$BIf you wish to help bring honor to the Horde, then bring me examples of their weapons. Find me a dagger from their stalkers, a wand from their seers, and a shield from their warfrenzy. That should do nicely!",how={{"loot",5093,{3456,3457}},{"loot",5092,{3458}},{"loot",5094,{3459}}}},[894]={t="Samophlange",lv=14,min=10,nx=900,si=5088,ot="Access the control console at the Venture Company research site.",st="The Venture Company set up a small research facility far to the north of here, southwest of the Sludge Fen. I don't know very much about what they're doing, but did manage to discover that they're experimenting with something called a \"samophlange\".$b$bNow what the heck is a samophlange? Well, whatever it is, I want to examine it, so I need someone to go get it.$b$bI obtained a copy of their control system operating manual, you should be able to figure out how to disengage the samophlange from it."},[895]={t="WANTED: Baron Longshore",lv=16,min=11,ot="Bring the head of Baron Longshore to Gazlowe in Ratchet.",st="WANTED!$b$bBaron Longshore, Captain of the Heedless$b$bCaptain Longshore of Gilneas leads vessels of the Southsea Freebooters, and is wanted on charges of piracy. Remains must be in identifiable condition!$b$b-- Gazlowe",how={{"loot",5084,{3467}}}},[896]={t="Miner's Fortune",lv=18,min=13,ot="Retrieve the Cats Eye Emerald from one of the Venture Co. Overseers or Enforcers for Wharfmaster Dizzywig at Ratchet.",st="Being Wharfmaster of a busy port like Ratchet, I keep my finger on the pulse of information. I know all about the exchange of goods and money between here and Booty Bay.$b$bThe latest bit of news I've heard is about the Venture Company's Boulder Lode mine northeast of the Sludge Fen. One of the miners discovered an emerald the size of your fist. I know a few buyers who'd be interested in getting their hands on something like that, and I'd be willing to go half and half on its sale.",how={{"loot",5097,{3283,3286}}}},[897]={t="The Harvester",lv=24,min=10,si=5138,ot="Bring the Harvester's Head to Jorn Skyseer.",st="This strange, insect-like creature looks outside of the natural order, as though it does not belong in the Barrens."},[898]={t="Free From the Hold",lv=20,min=13,ne=1,ot="Safely escort Gilthares Firebough back to Captain Brightsun in Ratchet.",st="Finally! Someone to rescue me!$b$bI can't believe you got past the guards. These zealots from Theramore are out of their minds. They sank our ship and imprisoned me, the only survivor. I was called an enemy and threat to the Alliance.$b$bMe! A threat to their great sham of an Alliance? I was a deckhand on a moonshine transport between Ratchet and Booty Bay.$b$bEnough talk. Help me get back to Ratchet will you? Let me know when you're ready and we'll make our break."},[899]={t="Consumed by Hatred",lv=20,min=14,ot="Bring 60 Bristleback Quilboar Tusks to Mankrik at the Crossroads.",st="Perhaps you know the pain of uncertainty, perhaps not, $c. But know this: I stand here every day, from the sun's rising till its decline, scouring the horizon for more of those monsters. I've killed every pig man I've come across since, but my thirst for their blood is far from quenched. Perhaps instead of heading north to the Crossroads I should have headed to Taurajo.$B$BYou, $c--you  could help me.$B$BKill them. Kill as many as you can. Bring me their tusks, and we will celebrate their deaths together.",how={{"loot",5085,{3261,3260,3263}}}},[900]={t="Samophlange",lv=14,min=10,pre1={894},nx=901,ot="Close off the Fuel Control Valve, the Regulator Valve and the Main Control Valve then use the control console again.",st="The three control valves are currently opened. The various readings on the control panel lead you to presume that they must be shut off before the apparatus can be shut off.",how={{"click",4072},{"click",61936},{"click",61935}}},[901]={t="Samophlange",lv=14,min=10,pre1={900},nx=902,ot="Get the Console Key from Tinkerer Sniggles to use on the control console.",st="With the apparatus deactivated, the control panel can be opened up and the samophlange removed from the console. With everything else in place, all that is left is to acquire the key to unlock the console.",how={{"loot",5089,{3471}}}},[902]={t="Samophlange",lv=16,min=10,pre1={901},nx=3921,si=5054,ot="Return the Samophlange to Sputtervalve in Ratchet.",st="Pulling open the face of the control console reveals a dense jumble of wires, tubing and other strange mechanical objects--most of which seem to serve no practical purpose. Pushing them aside and digging deeper into the console, you find the samophlange. A tug removes it from its housing."},[903]={t="Prowlers of the Barrens",lv=15,min=10,pre1={845},nx=881,ot="Collect 7 Prowler Claws from Savannah Prowlers for Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.",st="Now it's time to go after something that really bites.  The prowlers of the Barrens are a tough breed.  Tough, resourceful, sly... and deadly.  You'll find them among the tall grasses.  You'll find many to the southwest of the Crossroads.$B$BBe wary as you hunt them, $n, or you may find yourself no longer the predator, but instead the prey.",how={{"loot",5096,{3425}}}},[905]={t="The Angry Scytheclaws",lv=17,min=10,pre1={881},nx=3261,ot="Kill Sunscale raptors and collect their feathers. Use the feathers on the 3 Scytheclaw nests. Return to Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.",st="Now, $n, the hunt deepens.  Now you must defeat your prey, and then find your way to its lair.$B$BHunt the sunscale raptors to the south.  Slay them and remove the feathers they wear.  Place the feathers on the scytheclaw nests southwest of the Stagnant Oasis. Show their brethren you do not fear them!",how={{"click",6907},{"click",6908},{"click",6906}}},[906]={t="Betrayal from Within",lv=25,min=17,pre1={879},si=5072,ot="Bring Lok's Skull to Thork at the Crossroads in the Barrens.",st="Take Lok's head to Thork in the Crossroads, $r. <snort> He should know what has happened to my tribe without any words--ha, not that he would believe Mangletooth helped in <snort> such things. But I am sure he'll reward you for carrying out such a great deed. <snort>$B$BI will continue to bless you with Agamaggan's power for as long as I remain in this cage, $r. Until then, farewell."},[907]={t="Enraged Thunder Lizards",lv=18,min=10,pre1={882},nx=913,ot="Bring 3 Thunder Lizard Blood to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo.",st="Now, $n, you must face the great thunder lizards.  So large are the beasts, the ground rumbles as they stomp across the plains.  Take care as you fight them, for one false step and you may find yourself beneath their feet.$B$BYou will find the thunder lizards in the southern Barrens.  They are known as Stormsnouts, Stormhides and Thunderheads.  Return to me after you have bested them.",how={{"loot",5143,{3239,3240}}}},[913]={t="Cry of the Thunderhawk",lv=20,min=10,pre1={907},nx=874,ot="Find and slay a Thunderhawk, return its wings to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo.",st="The thunderhawk, $n, is a fierce beast.  It is time for you to face them.  You must find where it roams, and bring me its wings as proof of your successful hunt.$B$BDo this, and your time with me will near its end.",how={{"loot",5164,{3424,3247}}}},[914]={t="Leaders of the Fang",lv=22,min=10,pre1={1490},ot="Bring the Gems of Cobrahn, Anacondra, Pythas and Serpentis to Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff.",st="The druids in the Wailing Caverns, the Druids of the Fang, are an aberration.  They were part of an order of noble druids whose plan was to heal the Barrens, but now seek to remake that land to match their own, twisted dreams.$B$BThe Druids of the Fang have four leaders, and each possesses a dream gem.  Even now their faces haunt me!  Defeat the leaders and bring me their gems, and the Barrens may again know peace.$B$BGo, $n.  You will find them lurking deep within the Wailing Caverns.",how={{"loot",9738,{3669,5791}},{"loot",9739,{3671}},{"loot",9740,{3670}},{"loot",9741,{3673}}}},[924]={t="The Demon Seed",lv=14,min=9,pre1={809},ot="Grab a Flawed Power Stone.  Bring it to the Altar of Fire before the stone expires, then return to Ak'Zeloth.",st="The Demon Seed is a powerful tool for the Burning Legion. It rests in a cave on Dreadmist Peak, above a demonic altar of fire.$B$BI have prepared power stones that when placed near the Seed will disrupt its connection to the Legion.$B$BTake a stone from the table and bring it to the altar of fire atop Dreadmist Peak. Travel west, then north when the road forks. The Peak will be to your left. The safest climb to the top is on its northern face.$B$BAnd hurry--the stone's power will consume itself in time.",how={{"click",3525}}},[926]={t="Flawed Power Stone",lv=14,min=1},[959]={t="Trouble at the Docks",lv=18,min=14,ot="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz in Ratchet wants you to retrieve the bottle of 99-Year-Old Port from Mad Magglish who is hiding in the Wailing Caverns.",st="Oops!$b$bHad a little mishap, as you can see! The morning cargo shipment from Booty Bay was huge. Huge I say! Never seen so many crates. Well, I was trying to expedite things so I started unloading a bit more than I could handle. That's when everything came tumbling down.$b$bBefore I knew what was going on, I saw that menace, Mad Magglish, go running off with a bottle of 99-year-old port. Chased him all the way to Wailing Caverns. No way I was going in there.$b$bMaybe you're brave enough to find him?",how={{"loot",5334,{3655}}}},[962]={t="Serpentbloom",lv=18,min=14,ot="Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff wants you to collect 10 Serpentbloom.",st="The Royal Apothecary Society, based in the great Undercity of Lordaeron, has sent me here for a very specific service, $n. Perhaps you wish to aid me, and in turn The Dark Lady in our efforts to advance the Forsaken.$b$bRecently I studied a rare specimen of flora named Serpentbloom. I believe in greater quantities this herb has great potential.$b$bUnfortunately Serpentbloom can only be found in the darkest recesses of the Wailing Caverns, a dangerous cave system located in the Barrens.",how={{"open",5339,{13891}}}},[1013]={t="The Book of Ur",lv=26,min=16,ot="Bring the Book of Ur to Keeper Bel'dugur at the Apothecarium in the Undercity.",st="$n, Shadowfang Keep holds a book, the Book of Ur, which would be much prized in my collection.  Ur was a great mage of Dalaran before the coming of the Scourge, his studies in other worlds are of much value to ... certain parties among the Forsaken.$B$BEnter Shadowfang Keep and find the book.  Bring it to me, and I will report your service to our Dark Lady...",how={{"open",6283,{36738}}}},[1014]={t="Arugal Must Die",lv=27,min=18,ot="Kill Arugal and bring his head to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.",st="Arugal still resides in Shadowfang Keep. We cannot claim Silverpine as a strategic stronghold for the Dark Lady until Arugal is slain.$b$bI shall see to it that his magic is eradicated, $n. But I leave it in your hands to see that Arugal meets the death he so deserves.$b$bTravel to Shadowfang Keep and put an end to Arugal's foul spells once and for all. Bring to me the vile wizard's head!",how={{"loot",5442,{4275,10000}}}},[1058]={t="Jin'Zil's Forest Magic",lv=26,min=20,ot="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil at Malaka'jin wants 5 portions of Stonetalon Sap, 5 Twilight Whiskers, 30 Courser Eyes and a Fey Dragon Scale.",st="So excited I am!$b$bThree little cages for three little elves! But what shall we do with our lovely tree-hugging friends? Why, let's give them a taste of... what do they call it... forest magic!$b$bI'll need a good mess of Stonetalon sap. From those horrid felines, bring me some twilight whiskers. This calls for plenty of courser eyes, of course -- can never have enough eyes. Oh, and lest we forget, a precious scale from a fey dragon.$b$bHurry to Stonetalon Peak, $n, so I can brew some forest magic!",how={{"loot",5582,{4020}},{"loot",5584,{4067}},{"loot",5585,{4018,4019}},{"loot",5583,{4016,4017,4066}}}},[1060]={t="Letter to Jin'Zil",lv=20,min=15,pre1={876},si=5594,ot="Deliver Darsok's letter to Jin'Zil within his cave in Malaka'Jin, in Stonetalon.",st="You've done so well for me, $n. You're a regular lucky rabbit's foot and there's something I want you to see.$B$BThe harpies are not from around the Barrens. They come from a place called Stonetalon, far to the northwest of here. Though it is probably a dangerous place for you, I need this letter delivered to an old friend of mine who lives there, a witch doctor by the name of Jin'Zil.$B$BHe'll be happy to know that Serena Bloodfeather is dead, and I think you'll find Stonetalon an interesting place."},[1061]={t="The Spirits of Stonetalon",lv=17,min=13,nx=1062,bc=1062,ot="Speak with Seereth Stonebreak in the Stonetalon Mountains.",st="The spirits of the Stonetalon Mountains are angered, for goblins and their servants are plundering and burning the land.  So the land has cried out, and those who listen for such things... have heard.$B$BSeereth Stonebreak, a promising shaman of the Horde, was sent to Stonetalon.  She reports massive deforestation at the hands of the goblins, and requests aid.$B$BMeet Seereth in Stonetalon.  To reach her, follow the road west of the Barrens' Crossroads.  She is camped near the Greatwood Vale."},[1062]={t="Goblin Invaders",lv=19,min=13,ot="Kill 15 Venture Co. Loggers, then return to Seereth Stonebreak on the border of Stonetalon and the Barrens.",st="The goblin-run Venture Company moved into the Stonetalon Mountains, chopping down trees and burning huge stretches of forest.  The spirits of this place are nearly blind with pain and rage.  We must stop the Venture Company!$B$BHead northwest, beyond the Greatwood Vale and into the Windshear Crag.  You will find the goblins and their servants at work -- show them the Horde will not allow the exploitation of Stonetalon.  Show them in the language they best understand...$B$BViolence.",how={{"kill",3989}}},[1063]={t="The Elder Crone",lv=18,min=13,pre1={1062},nx=1064,ot="Speak with Magatha in Thunder Bluff.",st="To truly tend the spirits of Stonetalon we must consult the tauren elders.$B$BI do not know many of their leaders' names, but I do know of one: Magatha.  I have heard that she is very old, and she knows much.  If anyone can marshal spiritual aid from the tauren, it is she.$B$BMagatha resides in the tauren capital of Thunder Bluff, on Elder Rise -- the city's northeastern bluff.  Speak with Magatha, and tell her of the peril of Stonetalon Mountains."},[1064]={t="Forsaken Aid",lv=18,min=13,pre1={1063},nx=1065,ot="Speak with Apothecary Zamah in the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff.",st="The tauren have a bond with the land, and it pains me to hear of Stonetalon's plight.  But I fear that to heal the land, we must first remove the disease upon it.$B$BIs it not fortunate, then, that the Forsaken are allied with us?  They know much of disease.  I believe they can aid us, and by doing so they will strengthen the trust between our people.$B$BSpeak with Apothecary Zamah.  She is a scholar and an emissary of the Forsaken.  You will find her in the Pools of Vision below the Spirit Rise."},[1065]={t="Journey to Tarren Mill",lv=18,min=13,pre1={1064},nx=1066,si=5628,ot="Bring Zamah's Note to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",st="To rid Stonetalon of the Venture Company, we must take extreme measures.  Extreme, but without bloodshed.$B$BA colleague of mine may have just the tool we need.  His name is Lydon; he dwells in the town of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, in the distant land of Lordaeron.$B$BTo reach Hillsbrad, travel by zeppelin to our capital, the Undercity.  Then go north to Tirisfal Glades, southwest to Silverpine, and south to Hillsbrad.$B$BSeek Lydon and bring him this note.  It details our needs to him."},[1066]={t="Blood of Innocents",lv=23,min=13,pre1={1065},nx=1067,ot="Bring 5 Vials of Innocent Blood to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",st="I will create a toxin to bleed the violence from the Venture Company, rendering them weak and docile.  That should fix the Horde's problem in Stonetalon, yes?$B$BBut to create the toxin, I will need the blood of innocents, a difficult ingredient to obtain.$B$BFortunately the Syndicate, a group of human brigands in this area, employ shadow mages... and those mages collect innocent blood for their own, unsavory purposes.$B$BYou can find the Syndicate shadow mages in Durnholde Keep to the southeast.",how={{"loot",5620,{2244}}}},[1067]={t="Return to Thunder Bluff",lv=23,min=13,pre1={1066},nx=1086,si=5588,ot="Bring Lydon's Toxin to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff.",st="Here is the toxin.  If you use it against the Venture Company it should produce favorable, perhaps even contagious, results.  I must say, it is quite exciting to see my work applied in the field!$B$BBut before using it, take it to Apothecary Zamah.  She must create a delivery method for the toxin to maximize its effect."},[1068]={t="Shredding Machines",lv=23,min=13,pre1={1062},ot="Kill the shredders XT:4 and XT:9, then return to Seereth Stonebreak at the border of the Stonetalon Mountains and the Barrens.",st="There is a relation to the spiritual magic of shamans and the natural magic of druids.  This is why we shamans can hear the plea of the spirits of Stonetalon.  Many of their whisperings are lost to me, but one message, one vision, is clear...$B$BI saw a vision of two man-shaped machines in Windshear Crag, northwest of Greatwood Vale, felling trees with impossible speed.  These metal beasts must be stopped!$B$BIn my vision, the machines were marked with strange symbols:$B$BXT:4 and XT:9.",how={{"kill",4073},{"kill",4074}}},[1069]={t="Deepmoss Spider Eggs",lv=20,min=15,ot="Bring 15 Deepmoss Eggs to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",st="Spider egg omelettes are a new fad in Booty Bay!  The problem is... Booty Bay's got no eggs.$B$BI smell an opportunity!$B$BIn Windshear Crag and Sishir Canyon, in the Stonetalon Mountains to the northwest, lives the deepmoss spider.  Bring me its eggs and I'll pay a bundle!$B$BIn Windshear Crag, the eggs will be clustered under what trees remain.$B$BIn Sishir Canyon... well, if you have a weak stomach then maybe you should just collect the eggs at Windshear Crag...",how={{"open",5570,{19541}}}},[1086]={t="The Flying Machine Airport",lv=23,min=13,pre1={1067},si=5638,ot="Bring the Toxic Fogger to the Venture Co. sky port, then return to Apothecary Zamah.",st="The toxin is ready.  All that remains is its delivery.  You, $n, must make that delivery.$B$BThe Venture Company must have a means of sending messages and light cargo between its headquarters and its operations in Stonetalon.  It is likely a small sky port -- not big enough for a zeppelin, but perhaps for a flying machine.  You must search the areas in Stonetalon under control of the Venture Company and find this sky port, if it exists.  If you find it, then place the toxin there.$B$BPlace it, and run.",how={{"click",19594}}},[1087]={t="Cenarius' Legacy",lv=25,min=20,nx=1088,ot="Kill 4 Sons of Cenarius, 4 Daughters of Cenarius and 4 Cenarion Botanists for Braelyn Firehand near Sun Rock Retreat.",st="You cannot imagine the hatred I possess for this wretched land. The ilk of Cenarius and the kaldorei druids at the peak employ their pathetic powers to stifle the flow of magic, even so far south of their pathetic holdings... their beloved forests.$b$bWould that I could return to Jaedenar and exult in the flow of magic, but my master will not allow me to return until my work is done.$b$bI have no doubt you love the night elves and their allies as little as I. Aid me, and both our ends might be satisfied.",how={{"kill",4057},{"kill",4053},{"kill",4051}}},[1088]={t="Ordanus",lv=29,min=20,pre1={1087},nx=1089,ot="Bring Ordanus' head to Braelyn Firehand near Sun Rock Retreat.",st="They thought that they could halt the flow of magic. They were mistaken. They thought that they could hide Ordanus, but I will have his head!$b$bMagic grants me true sight. Yes... there he is. A crossroads... At the top of a great tree in Ashenvale Forest. A name... Raynewood. One of the eldest sons of the forest god. They spirited him away from the peak before I could find him, but his time runs short.$b$bBring it to me and I will share with you a mighty gift.",how={{"loot",5686,{4273}}}},[1090]={t="Gerenzo's Orders",lv=22,min=17,nx=1092,ne=1,ot="Get the mysterious ore from Piznik after he finishes mining it.",st="You know, I was once the second most important person here at this site. That all changed when Gerenzo took over. Fired my boss, Ziz Fizziks, and sent me down to work in the mines. Ziz told me to stay here and gather information, though. His new boss will pay us well if we can find out what Gerenzo's plans are.$b$bAnyways, what I do know is that Gerenzo has ordered large amounts of this gold-green ore to be mined. I can get you a sample to bring to Ziz, but you'll have to watch for patrols while I get it.",how={{"kill",3998}}},[1092]={t="Gerenzo's Orders",lv=22,min=17,pre1={1090},si=5733,ot="Deliver the Unidentified Ore to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",st="I guess I'd better think about getting out of here, also. It won't take long for word of what happened here to spread to the higher ups, and I'm sure they wouldn't take too kindly to meeting me again.$b$bI'll sneak out and meet with Ziz. Hopefully, he'll be able to find me a new job!$b$bI'll try and clean up this mess a little, but you should take the ore sample to Ziz right away. He told me that he'd set up camp somewhere on the western side of Windshear Crag. Good luck."},[1093]={t="Super Reaper 6000",lv=21,min=16,nx=1094,ot="Get the Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints for Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",st="Terrible what the Venture Company has done here, eh? What were they thinking? Goblin company hiring a gnome!$b$bLucky for me, Sputtervalve knows a genius when he sees one. Hired me just after I'd been kicked out!$b$bTells me they built some enormous woodcutting machine, and Sput' wants me to steal the plans for him. Unfortunately, Gerenzo--bloody gnome--wants me dead on sight... maybe you could steal the plans for me? You should be able to find them on one of their operators.",how={{"loot",5734,{3988}}}},[1094]={t="Further Instructions",lv=21,min=16,pre1={1093},nx=1095,si=5735,ot="Deliver the Sealed Envelope to Sputtervalve in the Barrens.",st="This envelope has all the information I was able to snatch as they booted me out the door... Venture Company internal documents, some manuals, technical things... Oh, and of course the Super Reaper 6000 blueprints.$b$bSputtervalve has taken up residence at Ratchet in the Barrens. Shouldn't have much trouble finding him, he's a little green fellow."},[1095]={t="Further Instructions",lv=27,min=16,pre1={1094},nx=1096,ot="Bring the new orders to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",st="The matter of this gnome that has been hired by the Venture Company has caused a bit of a stir in Undermine. The trade princes do not approve of Razdunk's consorting with this Gerenzo.$b$bRiddlevox has asked me to take care of the problem, and I'm sure he was instructed to do so by one or more of the trade princes. Of course, the Director didn't tell me that. Let's just say I have a hunch.$b$bWhatever the case, Gerenzo must be removed, and it would be a fitting test to have Fizziks take care of him."},[1096]={t="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle",lv=27,min=16,pre1={1095},ot="Bring Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle's Mechanical Arm to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",st="I met Gerenzo once, but let me tell you, he's not easy on the eyes. His flesh looks like it's rotting away, and he's grafted metal and gears onto his body, replaced some of his limbs with mechanical ones.$b$bNortheast of here, far above Cragpool Lake, up near the water wheel is where Gerenzo watches over the entire site. There's no way I could fight my way up there, not to mention take on Gerenzo... But you look like you might be able to make it.$b$bIf you kill him for me, I'll make it worth your while!",how={{"loot",5736,{4202}}}},[1098]={t="Deathstalkers in Shadowfang",lv=25,min=18,rwc={[4]=2},ot="Find the Deathstalker Adamant and Deathstalker Vincent.",st="In preparation for an assault on Shadowfang, two deathstalkers were sent to the keep to gather intelligence.  It has been many days and they have not returned, but we must receive their report if we're to have any hope of a successful attack!$B$BSo here is your task, $n.  Go to Shadowfang Keep to the south and find the Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent.  Find them, and if they require aid then give it.$B$BThis mission is as dangerous as is it critical, $n.  Do not fail."},[1102]={t="A Vengeful Fate",lv=34,min=29,si=17008,ot="Bring Razorflank's Heart to Auld Stonespire in Thunder Bluff.",st="Cairne is a noble leader for uniting our people here on Thunder Bluff.$b$bBut I cannot forgive those who drove us from our ancestral lands as easily as some. My people inhabited the southern Barrens for decades. The land was holy to us. But we were driven off by numerous foes.$b$bA vengeful fate awaits the crone, Charlga Razorflank, who musters a foul army from within Razorfen Kraul.$b$bBring me Razorflank's heart and I can die in peace, $n.",how={{"loot",5793,{4421}}}},[1109]={t="Going, Going, Guano!",lv=33,min=30,nx=1113,ot="Bring 1 pile of Kraul Guano to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",st="As you can see, $n, we're up to some very.... interesting experiments at the Royal Apothecary Society.$b$bAs the Master here, it is my job to oversee the most ambitious of our alchemical attempts. So much work and so little time!$b$bYou look well traveled for a $c. Perhaps you can aid me.$b$bI'm in need of a rare substance. It's foul material; it comes from a rare species of bats only found in the muck-hole known as Razorfen Kraul. Bring to me the guano from the Kraul Bats so we can begin our work...",how={{"loot",5801,{4425,4538,4539}}}},[1111]={t="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",lv=36,min=30,nx=1112,si=5799,ot="Bring Kravel's Parts Order to Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.",st="I make it my job to get people what they need, and the gnomes over there need a parts order filled.  Their parts were shipped to Ratchet a week ago, but I haven't been able to make the trip.$B$BSo, are you ready for some legwork?  Go to Ratchet and give this parts order to Wharfmaster Dizzywig -- he'll probably be at the docks.$B$BDo this for me, and I'll have more jobs for you.$B$BJobs, my friend, with serious profit potential..."},[1112]={t="Parts for Kravel",lv=36,min=30,pre1={1111},nx=1114,si=5800,ot="Bring Kravel's Parts to Kravel Koalbeard in the Shimmering Flats.",st="Here's Kravel's package, $n.  And when you deliver it, tell him... if he wants more special orders, then he'll have to pay his tab!"},[1131]={t="Steelsnap",lv=30,min=20,nx=1136,ot="Bring Steelsnap's Rib to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.",st="At times we hunt for food.  At times we hunt for honor.  And at times we hunt to earn the Earthmother's teachings.$B$BBut the hunt I now set upon you is none of these things.  It is to slay a creature outside the Earthmother's blessing.$B$BThe hyena Steelsnap roams the Thousand Needles, south of the Barrens.  He is a tyrant, attracting other hyenas to him and spreading fear and bloodshed among more peaceful beasts.$B$BFind Steelsnap, $n.  Find him, and defeat him.",how={{"loot",5837,{4548}}}},[1144]={t="Willix the Importer",lv=30,min=22,ne=1,ot="Escort Willix the Importer out of Razorfen Kraul.",st="At last, help has arrived!$b$bYou have no clue how long I've been held prisoner here. I can't remember the last time I saw the outside of this place.$b$bYou see, I am an entrepreneur. Always out for a copper, as they say. I caught wind that Mebok Mizzyrix was paying well for Redleaf Tuber from this here pig pen. I figured it would be an easy in, easy out kind of affair. As you can see, I was a bit wrong!$b$bAnyway, if you'd be so kind as to help me get out of here, I'll make it worth your while."},[1145]={t="The Swarm Grows",lv=33,min=29,nx=1146,si=5846,ot="Deliver Korran's Sealed Note to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.",st="Many travelers who've come through the Crossroads helped me gather eggs from the Field of Giants, and many of them have tales of how deadly the creatures are. I've heard enough to consider them insects a much larger threat than my masters first thought.$B$BI need a courier to travel to Orgrimmar to meet Belgrom Rockmaul. It be no simple matter, and someone who would take the task seriously should go.$B$BBelgrom usually be found outside the warriors' guild house."},[1146]={t="The Swarm Grows",lv=33,min=29,pre1={1145},nx=1147,si=5850,ot="Deliver Belgrom's Sealed Note to Moktar Krin in Thousand Needles.",st="So, Korran has come to a similar conclusion about these insects--they seem to be a larger threat than we assumed.$B$BA few days ago a hunter returned to me from Thousand Needles nearly dead. He was with a raiding party sent to drive a dwarven excavation team out of the Shimmering Flats. During the attack, more of these insects erupted from a cave in the dig site and nearly killed the party.$B$BThey were led by Moktar Krin, and they've taken refuge on the border of the Shimmering Flats. Bring him this note."},[1149]={t="Test of Faith",lv=26,min=25,nx=1150,ot="If you have faith, leap from the planks overlooking Thousand Needles.",st="So, you have sought me out, or perhaps destiny brings you to me? No matter. You are here now, and so your journey will begin anew.$B$BMany facets make up a being: the spirit, the body, the mind. Some of these can be measured by a culture's traditions. Others we can only hope exist within ourselves. If you agree, I shall test some of the facets within you.$B$BIf you pass, then you shall become stronger. If you fail, then you will realize the vastness of the Nether.$B$BThe first is a Test of Faith."},[1150]={t="Test of Endurance",lv=30,min=25,pre1={1149},nx=1151,ot="Bring Grenka's Claw to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles.",st="I'm pleased to see your courage remains steadfast in light of what you've already done. Since your faith is intact, the time has come to test your body.$B$BFirst is a test of endurance. Go with friends to the Roguefeather Den west of Freewind Post. Make your way to the depths of their lair and destroy their foodstuffs. By then you should have provoked their fury, and if you are able to survive long enough, Grenka Bloodscreech herself will come for you--kill her and bring me her claw to complete your test.",how={{"loot",5843,{4490}}}},[1151]={t="Test of Strength",lv=30,min=25,pre1={1150},nx=1152,ot="Bring Fragments of Rok'Alim to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles.",st="During the time of the Old Gods, elementals inhabited much of this world. They worshipped the Old Gods, and the Gods, through their power, kept the elementals bound to this world. When the Old Gods were banished, the elementals faded from our world and now only return at the bidding of powerful mages.$B$BThere are exceptions though. Some elementals were powerful enough to remain here on their own. One such elemental is Rok'Alim.$B$BTo test your strength, find Rok'Alim in Thousand Needles and slay him.",how={{"loot",5844,{4499}}}},[1153]={t="A New Ore Sample",lv=29,min=25,pre1={893},ot="Find an Unrefined Ore Sample on a Gravelsnout Digger or Surveyor and bring it to Tatternack Steelforge at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.",st="$C, you have done well in helping me in the past. The warchief is pleased thus far with what I've accomplished, and asks me to continue with renewed determination. My honor dictates that I give you proper recognition to the warchief for all you have done, but first I would ask you for your help again.$B$BTravelers recently came from the south from a place called Thousand Needles. There they killed a kobold who had an unusual ore sample, but they would not sell it. I want a sample of that ore to examine.",how={{"loot",5842,{14427,4113,4116}}}},[1195]={t="The Sacred Flame",lv=25,min=20,nx=1196,si=5867,ot="Return a Filled Etched Phial to Zangen Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.",st="The Galak centaur in the Thousand Needles are protecting an artifact from the time of the centaurs' creation.$b$bWe would like to retrieve it, but we require a phial of water from one of the night elves' moonwells.$b$bTo collect the water, you will first need to obtain one of the phials carried by the dryads near the Raynewood Retreat in the heart of Ashenvale Forest. There is a moonwell near the western bank of the Falfarren River, south of the main road, where you can fill the phial.",how={{"open",5868,{20806}}}},[1196]={t="The Sacred Flame",lv=29,min=20,pre1={1195},nx=1197,si=5868,ot="Deliver the Filled Etched Phial to Rau Cliffrunner at the Freewind Post.",st="Bring the filled phial to Rau Cliffrunner at the Freewind Post in southeastern Thousand Needles. You can get to the Thousand Needles by taking the Great Lift at the southern edge of the Barrens.$b$bI wouldn't be surprised if you can help us out further."},[1197]={t="The Sacred Flame",lv=29,min=20,pre1={1196},si=5868,ot="Retrieve the Cloven Hoof for Rau Cliffrunner at the Freewind Post.",st="Using the water you brought, you will be able to temporarily douse the flame that holds the centaur relic. It will not work permanently, however, so you will have to be quick about it.$b$bYou will find Splithoof Crag, the centaurs' stronghold, to the north of here. The flame is kept in Splithoof Hold, a heavily guarded part of the crag.$b$bBe careful, though, the Galak centaur have great numbers here, and will be rather reluctant to surrender something so dear to them.",how={{"open",5869,{20807}}}},[1221]={t="Blueleaf Tubers",lv=26,min=20,si=6684,ui={5880},ot="Grab a Crate with Holes.$BGrab a Snufflenose Command Stick.$BGrab and read the Snufflenose Owner's Manual.$B$BIn Razorfen Kraul, use the Crate with Holes to summon a Snufflenose Gopher, and use the Command Stick on the gopher to make it search for Tubers.$B$BBring 6 Blueleaf Tubers, the Snufflenose Command Stick and the Crate with Holes to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",st="Blueleaf tubers are a delicacy around the world!  But they're rare, very rare.  The only place to find them is here in the Barrens, deep in the earth, in Razorfen Kraul.$B$BAnd even then, they're impossible to find unless you know just where to look!  That's why I've trained these snufflenose gophers to find them for me.  They have great noses and can smell a tuber from fifty paces away.$B$BIt won't be easy, but if you get me some tubers I'll pay you handsomely.",how={{"open",5876,{20920}},{"open",5880,{21277}},{"open",5897,{21530}},{"open",6684,{68865}}}},[1358]={t="Sample for Helbrim",lv=15,min=10,pre1={1359},si=6016,ot="Bring the Wolf Heart Sample to Apothecary Helbrim in the Barrens.",st="A colleague in Kalimdor, Apothecary Helbrim, is researching the effects of Lordaeron toxins on the beasts of Kalimdor.  He would be very interested in a sample of the wolf hearts Renferrel sent me.$B$BHelbrim is stationed in the Barrens, in a village known as the Crossroads.  To reach him, you must travel via zeppelin to the orc capital of Orgrimmar, then travel south, by foot, to Durotar.  Head west into the Barrens, and you will soon reach the Crossroads."},[1359]={t="Zinge's Delivery",lv=15,min=10,pre1={3221},nx=1358,si=10283,ot="Bring the Wolf Heart Samples to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity.",st="The wolf hearts you acquired possess a quality unseen in similar specimens.  There is a toxicity to them that should be deadly to the very wolves in which the hearts beat!$B$BIt's quite incredible, and we must study it further.  I kept a few samples of the hearts acquired.  Take them to my colleague, Apothecary Zinge.  You will find her in our headquarters in the Undercity."},[1431]={t="Alliance Relations",lv=30,min=30,nx=1432,ot="Speak to Keldran in Orgrimmar.",st="Be still, $c, and allow me to share with you something important to our people, but far from obvious.$B$BWe are a proud race, and the war with the humans tried even Thrall's great patience. You see, our Warchief is wise and prudent, and he continues to put his people first. Ultimately, he is a diplomat, and in his time with the humans he learned much of their ways.$B$BIf the tale I've started piques your interest, then find Keldran near the western exit of the city. His hovel is there."},[1470]={t="Piercing the Veil",lv=3,min=1,ex={1485},ot="Bring Venya Marthand 3 Rattlecage Skulls.",st="Greetings, child. I can see that you are still young in the ways of the warlock, power still eluding your grasp. I can sense your eagerness to learn.$b$bAnd you will learn.$b$bThere is no strength in ignorance. Knowledge is our greatest power. Through its application, we can control the chaotic magics and beings of the void, bending them to our will.$b$bI will show you how to bind a servant to your will, but first you must bring me three skulls of the rattlecage skeletons near the abandoned smithy.",how={{"loot",6281,{1890}}}},[1471]={t="The Binding",lv=10,min=10,pre1={1473},ex={1504},si=6284,ot="Using the Runes of Summoning, summon and subdue a voidwalker, then return the Runes of Summoning to Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",st="Surely you have seen the circle of summoning below us? Only there will you be able to draw forth an unbound voidwalker.$b$bUsing these runes, you will be able to draw it forth, and then you must dominate it through strength of arms and magic.$b$bWhen it is subdued, it will be indentured to you. Come to me then, and I will elucidate the spell of summoning, so that it may serve you to whatever end you wish.",how={{"kill",5676}}},[1473]={t="Creature of the Void",lv=10,min=10,ex={1501},nx=1471,ot="Recover Egalin's Grimoire and bring it to Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned.",st="It seems the consensus that you are ready to learn to summon a voidwalker.$b$bA being created of the chaos that lies beyond, if you summon one but cannot control it, you will be torn asunder.$b$bThe first voidwalker was summoned by Egalin, and in his grimoire is the process explained.$b$bUnfortunately, it was stolen from us by an agent of the Scarlet Crusade who has it secreted away in his base at a tower to the west. Bring it to me, and I will impart the knowledge to you.",how={{"open",6285,{37098}}}},[1478]={t="Halgar's Summons",lv=10,min=10,nx=1473,bc=1473,ot="Speak with Carendin Halgar in the Undercity.",st="Ah, $n! I just received word from Carendin Halgar that he would like to see you for further training.$b$bYou should be proud of yourself, $n. It's not every day that Master Halgar personally sees fit to instruct a young warlock.$b$bYou'll be able to find him in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, near the Temple of the Damned."},[1483]={t="Ziz Fizziks",lv=21,min=16,nx=1093,bc=1093,ot="Speak with Ziz Fizziks in Windshear Crag.",st="The Venture Company stole many of the best goblin minds, but from time to time, we get the opportunity to steal some back.$b$bA while ago, the Venture Company outfit in the Stonetalon Mountains hired Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle--a gnome! Their other engineer, Ziz Fizziks, was so taken aback by this, he pleaded with me to find him new employment with the Tinkers' Union. I set him on a few tasks, but he might need help.$b$bMaybe you could look in on him for me? He's stationed at the western edge of Windshear Crag."},[1485]={t="Vile Familiars",lv=4,min=1,ex={1470},nx=1499,ot="Bring 6 Vile Familiar Heads to Ruzan.",st="Those warlocks who came before us have earned the distrust of the Horde, and while we are tolerated, we are not loved.$b$bThis has not brought the warlocks closer together, however, as many choose to live reclusively, dabbling in their magics alone. I will not seek to lead you down one path or the other, but only help you in your maturation.$b$bBefore I teach you the art of summoning, bring me six heads of the vile familiars from the cave to the northeast.",how={{"loot",6487,{3101}}}},[1486]={t="Deviate Hides",lv=17,min=13,ot="Nalpak in the Wailing Caverns wants 20 Deviate Hides.",st="As Naralex descended deeper into his nightmare, a strange breed of beasts arose from beneath the Barrens into the Wailing Caverns.$b$bThese deviate creatures have strange, otherworldly properties. While evil in nature, it is my opinion that some good can come from their existence here in Kalimdor. I believe their hides will be of particular use in the ways of leatherworking.$b$bIf you feel up to the task, venture into the caves below and retrieve some deviate hides.",how={{"loot",6443,{3631,3633,3630}}}},[1487]={t="Deviate Eradication",lv=21,min=15,ot="Ebru in the Wailing Caverns wants you to kill 7 Deviate Ravagers, 7 Deviate Vipers, 7 Deviate Shamblers and 7 Deviate Dreadfangs.",st="Naralex had a noble goal.$b$bOur great leader aspired to enter the Emerald Dream and help regrow these harsh lands back into the lush forest it once was. But something went terribly wrong.$b$bNaralex's dream turned into a nightmare and corrupt creatures began to inhabit the caverns.$b$bWhile some Disciples of Naralex seek to awake our master, my concern is with ridding these caves of the evil beasts.$b$bBrave the caverns, $n, and eradicate the deviate spawn.",how={{"kill",3636},{"kill",5755},{"kill",5761},{"kill",5056}}},[1489]={t="Hamuul Runetotem",lv=16,min=10,pre1={880},nx=1490,ot="Speak with Hamuul Runetotem",st="The shells you brought me have a taint, one I have never before seen.  I am certain the water of the Oases is the cause, and I can sense the confusion they cause this land.  It is as if the land dreams and cannot awake.$B$BThe Wailing Caverns must be the source of the taint.  But before you go there, speak with Hamuul Runetotem, the elder druid.  I sent word to him of the happenings in the Barrens.  He is wise, and can offer you counsel.$B$BYou will find him in Thunder Bluff, on the Elder Rise."},[1490]={t="Nara Wildmane",lv=16,min=10,pre1={1489},nx=914,ot="Speak with Nara Wildmane.",st="I entered the land of dreams, and dreamed of a cult of druids who dwell in the Wailing Caverns.  I saw that their goals were once noble, but they have lost their way.  They are now servants of the taint seeping through the Barrens.$B$BI am old and my strength fails.  I could not long dwell in that dreaming place and know little more of the tainted druids.  But Nara is young and her spirit is fierce.  She remained in the dreaming when I fled.$B$BSpeak with Nara.  She is in the tent, over yonder."},[1491]={t="Smart Drinks",lv=18,min=13,pre1={865},ot="Bring 6 portions of Wailing Essence to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",st="Ok, so the raptor horns didn't work so well.  But that's all right -- no one got rich on their first try!  And besides, I think I found something that'll work even better in my smart drinks!$B$BThere is a substance called Wailing Essence, and I think it is the cause of the strange plants and animals in the Barrens.  Get me some and I'll try it in my drink!$B$BI heard the essence gathers in ectoplasmic creatures in the Wailing Caverns to the west.  Hunt those creatures and gather the essence.",how={{"loot",6464,{3638,3640,5763}}}},[1492]={t="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",lv=11,min=9,si=6462,ot="Bring the Secure Crate to Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.",st="I have need to send a crate of potions, reagents and other items to my associates in the Old World. Little time I have to actually see them to the dock at Ratchet, and the last caravan has already left.$b$bIf you could, please take this to Wharfmaster Dizzywig. He will ensure that it is placed on the next boat to Blackwater Cove."},[1499]={t="Vile Familiars",lv=4,min=1,pre1={1470,1485},nx=794,ot="Speak with Zureetha Fargaze.",st="Zureetha has been sending novices like yourself to help cull the numbers of the creatures in the cave near where you fought the vile familiars.$b$bI think it would be good for you to gain experience by assisting her. Be sure to tell her that you assisted with the imp problem, she'll probably have a reward for you."},[1501]={t="Creature of the Void",lv=11,min=10,nx=1504,ot="Retrieve the Tablet of Verga for Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.",st="So few warlocks remain... We risk much, but the risks are warranted. You must quickly reach maturity in your ability if you are to be of use to the Horde and to the Warchief.$b$bIt is time that you learned a new summoning spell.$b$bFirst, you must recover the Tablet of Verga, which was stolen by warlocks of the Burning Blade and is now kept at their lair in Skull Rock to the east of the city. With the tablet, I will show you the runes necessary to summoning a voidwalker.",how={{"open",6535,{58595}}}},[1504]={t="The Binding",lv=11,min=10,pre1={1501},si=7464,ot="Using the Glyphs of Summoning, summon and subdue a voidwalker, then return the Glyphs of Summoning to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.",st="Now, observe the Tablet of Verga, for it contains the glyphs you will need for the summoning. Take them to the circle in Neeru Fireblade's tent on the other side of the cavern. There you will be able to call for the voidwalker.$b$bYou must defeat it using whatever physical and magical means you have at your disposal. When this is completed, return to me with the glyphs of summoning and I will demonstrate how you may bind the creature to your will.",how={{"kill",5676}}},[1506]={t="Gan'rul's Summons",lv=10,min=10,nx=1501,bc=1501,ot="Speak with Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.",st="You there. $n, right?$b$bI hope your schedule isn't busy, because Gan'rul wants to see you right away. You'll find him with the senior warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow.$b$bBased on my past dealings with Gan'rul, your summons is either a very good thing or a very bad thing."},[1507]={t="Devourer of Souls",lv=20,min=20,ex={1472},nx=1508,ot="Speak with Cazul in the Cleft of Shadow.",st="The time has come for you to learn more of the summoning magics. You will learn to summon a sayaad, a creature of incredible mental powers. It can lull those of weak minds into its servitude--but have no fear! I feel certain that you will be equal to the challenge.$b$bA sayaad can only be summoned when baited with an item that represents great devotion and love. I leave it to you to find such an object.$b$bA suggestion? Speak with Cazul... There seems to be little the ancient warlock does not know."},[1508]={t="Blind Cazul",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1507},ex={1472},nx=1509,ot="Speak with Zankaja in Orgrimmar.",st="If Gan'rul has sent you to me, it must be that you are to summon a succubus, a female of the sayaad race, and need an object to use for enticement.\r\n\r\nHmm... If you trust a blind man to lead you, $n, then listen. In the bluffs of Orgrimmar, west of the wind rider tower, lives Zankaja. She waits for the return of her mate.\r\n\r\nGo to her."},[1509]={t="News of Dogran",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1508},ex={1472},nx=1510,ot="Speak with Gazrog at the Crossroads.",st="My mate, Dogran, was recently sent to the Crossroads for duty. It was a promotion, and he was very proud.$b$bI was sad, of course, but I didn't let him know that. And worried, too. The Barrens is a more dangerous place than Orgrimmar, and I feared the worst.$b$bNow it's been a week after he should have returned, and I have received no word from him...$b$bPerhaps you could go to the Crossroads and see if they have any news? He worked with Gazrog, who should still be stationed there."},[1510]={t="News of Dogran",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1509},ex={1472},nx=1511,ot="Speak with Ken'zigla at the Malaka'jin.",st="He was stationed at Camp Taurajo, where we've been trying to weed out the quilboar. He led a few grunts to one of their camps, where he was hurt bad. The others made it back and tried to rescue him. He was in bad shape, his wounds festered, so they were afraid to move him without patching him up first.$b$bThey sent a message here, requesting a healing draught from the trolls at the Malaka'jin at the base of the Stonetalon Mountains. We sent someone to get it, but they haven't returned yet."},[1511]={t="Ken'zigla's Draught",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1510},ex={1472},nx=1515,si=6624,ot="Bring Ken'zigla's Draught to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo.",st="I figured there might be another coming to get the draught, so I prepared it anyways.$b$bHere you go, $n. Mind you, you should only give half of it to him! That will give him enough strength to move without bleeding himself dry. Wait a night, then give him the other half.$b$bAnyways, you'll want to bring this to Logmar at Camp Taurajo. From what the first one told me, he should have an idea where this Dogran is."},[1512]={t="Love's Gift",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1515},ex={1472},nx=1513,si=6625,ot="Bring the Dirt-caked Pendant to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.",st="Zankaja is young and beautiful. To be chained to an invalid... I will not allow her to suffer that injustice.$b$bLeave me, $n. And thank you. I may end my life in glorious battle, instead of a lifeless husk.$b$bAnd please, I would ask you not to tell my mate of this... I do not want guilt on her conscience."},[1513]={t="The Binding",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1512},ex={1472},si=6626,ot="Using Dogran's Pendant, summon and subdue a succubus, then return Dogran's Pendant to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.",st="Take this to the summoning circle in Neeru's tent, $n. Summon forth a foul succubus, then show it your mastery. I believe in the strength of your magic. As always, though, be wary, for pride and overconfidence has overcome many a promising warlock.$b$bWhen you have defeated it, return the pendant to me so that I might deliver the news to Zankaja.",how={{"kill",5677}}},[1515]={t="Dogran's Captivity",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1511},ex={1472},nx=1512,si=6624,ot="Bring Ken'zigla's Draught to Dogran in the Barrens.",st="You've made it this far, so if you want to see this through to the end, I won't stop you. I can't spare you any additional manpower though, you'll be on your own.$b$bDogran is being held in a quilboar camp to the north of here. Look for a group of two huts. He'll be heavily guarded--that is, if they haven't killed him yet, or he hasn't succumbed to his wounds.$b$bGood luck."},[1516]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=4,ex={1519,92466},nx=1517,ot="Bring 2 Felstalker Hooves to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials.",st="The time is now, young $c. You've grown strong and your spirit endures like the earth. Following the shaman's path shows you have wisdom before even proving yourself.$B$BThe element of earth will guide your destiny, becoming part of you if you are ready. But you must stand before the earth itself. If you are ready, then you will see things only shaman know of.$B$BSeek out the Felstalkers to the north, and take from them two of their hooves. Return to me then, and we shall speak more of your future.",how={{"loot",6640,{3102}}}},[1517]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=4,pre1={1516,1519},nx=1518,si=6635,ot="Find Spirit Rock and drink the Earth Sapta.",st="A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the strong willed to see the elements as no one else can. Your spirit will be connected to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few shaman know the recipe.$B$BThe sapta is always drunk in a holy place, and never anywhere else--remember that.$B$BSeek out Spirit Rock southwest of here--it is found at the end of the Hidden Path. Drink your sapta there, and... well, you shall see."},[1518]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=4,pre1={1517},si=6656,ot="Bring the Rough Quartz to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials.",st="Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Canaga Earthcaller as proof of our meeting. He will craft a totem for you, and this pebble will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast many others.$B$BBe patient, $n. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you."},[1519]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=4,ex={1516,92466},nx=1520,ot="Bring 2 applications of Ritual Salve to Seer Ravenfeather in Camp Narache.",st="The time has come, young $c. Your body ages and grows strong, and your spirit endures like the earth. I see it within you-you have wisdom already.$B$BThe earth guides our people, and it speaks to us, as it will to you in time. But you must be tested. If you are ready, then you shall see things only our kind know of.$B$BSeek out the Bristleback shamans in their ravine to the east, and take from them a salve they use in their rituals. Return to me only when you have enough for your own potion.",how={{"loot",6634,{2953}}}},[1520]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=4,pre1={1516,1519},nx=1521,si=6635,ot="Find Kodo Rock and drink the Earth Sapta.",st="A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the open minded to see the elements as no one has seen them before. Your spirit will forever be tied to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few of our kind know the secrets of its creation.$B$BThe sapta is always imbibed in a holy place, and never anywhere else.$B$BSeek out the shaman shrine to the east of here and drink of the sapta."},[1521]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=4,pre1={1520},si=6656,ot="Bring the Rough Quartz to Seer Ravenfeather in Camp Narache.",st="Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Seer Ravenfeather as proof of our meeting. She will craft a totem for you, and this pebble will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast mountains.$B$BBe patient, $n. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you."},[1524]={t="Call of Fire",lv=11,min=10,nx=1525,si=6653,ot="Bring the Torch of the Dormant Flame to Telf Joolam in Durotar.",st="You are powerful enough to wield the totem of fire, but that does not mean you are ready.$B$BAlong the Southfury River in Durotar, before the Great Sea, lies a hidden trail to one of the highest peaks in the land. Find your way to the top and you shall find one of our holy shrines watched over by Telf Joolam--the Shrine of the Dormant Flame.$B$BTake this torch to him--it marks that you attempt to tame fire. Return it to me aflame by the brazier at the shrine and I will see you are given the totem of fire."},[1525]={t="Call of Fire",lv=12,min=10,pre1={1524},nx=1526,ot="Bring 1 Fire Tar and 1 Reagent Pouch to Telf Joolam in Durotar.",st="But you did not come here for a history lesson, did you? You came for the Eternal Flame and fire totem.$B$BThe first step is to create a sapta and bind you to the flame.$B$BI can create the fire sapta for you if you bring me two items. The first is fire tar, a simple item usually carried by Razormane spellcasters in eastern Barrens.$B$BThe second item will be more dangerous: a reagent pouch from one of the cultists of the Burning Blade. You can find them in a cave above the ravines northeast of Razor Hill.",how={{"loot",5026,{3268,3267}},{"loot",6652,{3199}}}},[1526]={t="Call of Fire",lv=13,min=10,pre1={1525},nx=1527,si=6653,ui={6636},ot="Defeat the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and place the Glowing Ember in the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame.",st="The fire sapta is finished. The time has come for you to face the flame. Use the sapta at the shrine and head to the top of the mountain to face the manifestation there. He will not attack until you are ready, but he will realize you are able to see him.$B$BStrike him down swiftly, $n, for he shall only grow in power the longer you take to slay him. Once he is defeated, place his glowing embers within the brazier and light the torch.",how={{"loot",6655,{5893,268763}}}},[1527]={t="Call of Fire",lv=13,min=10,pre1={1526},si=6654,ot="Bring the Torch of Eternal Flame to Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.",st="Torch firmly in hand, you turn away from the brazier and look out over Durotar. You feel an excitement tugging at your spirit as the wind picks up and forces the flame to dance violently.$B$BYou start off down the path back to the Barrens in search of Kranal Fiss."},[1530]={t="Call of Water",lv=22,min=20,nx=1535,ot="Find Brine in Southern Barrens.",st="If there is one lesson you must learn of water, it is this: water means rebirth.$B$BIts power flows, erodes, and makes clean all manner of things. You will find its ability to heal and replenish incomparable, but only when it is pure.$B$BWhen you understand that water, when polluted, can devastate all that it touches, you will appreciate how vital a resource it is.$B$BIf you wish the water sapta, find Brine deep in Southern Barrens. Her home is continually molested by the quilboar there."},[1531]={t="Call of Air",lv=30,min=30,ex={1532,96136},ot="Find Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.",st="You be makin' headway now, mon. Your be ready to prove yerself worthy of the air totem, but first, ya must fin' Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles. She be willin' ta tell ya how to get yer air totem if ya treat her wit enough respect.$B$BHead south through the Barrens, and after ya reach Thousand Needles, head east. You'll find her hiddin' in a hole wit' her boyfriend--haha, don' tell her I be dissin' her none--she not take it too kindly."},[1534]={t="Call of Water",lv=23,min=20,pre1={1536},nx=220,si=7767,ot="Fill the Empty Blue Waterskin at the Ruins of Stardust in Ashenvale and return to Brine in the Barrens.",st="Take this waterskin and head deep into the lush forest the night elves call Ashenvale. It is to the far north of the Barrens.$B$BOnce you've entered the forest, travel west. Along the mountains that separate Stonetalon and Ashenvale, and beyond Lake Mystral, you will find a holy place: the Ruins of Stardust. At the center of the lake you will find a small fountain.$B$BBring me a sample of the fountain's water. It will be the final component you'll need before I send you back to Islen.",how={{"open",7770,{107047}}}},[1535]={t="Call of Water",lv=22,min=20,pre1={1530},nx=1536,si=7766,ot="Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the watering hole below Brine's hut and return it to her in the Barrens.",st="To find understanding and gain the sapta from me, you must seek out only the purest forms of water. As you fetch the samples for me, take note of your surroundings. Be aware of the creatures that rely on the water, that protect it. See how it affects forests and deserts. Witness how the very substance that sustains life will force creatures to take lives.$B$BWe shall start with a simple task: down below my hut there is a pond of the precious liquid. Fill this skin with it and return to me.",how={{"open",7769,{107046}}}},[1536]={t="Call of Water",lv=22,min=20,pre1={1535},nx=1534,si=7768,ot="Fill the Empty Red Waterskin at the well in Tarren Mill and return to Brine in the Barrens.",st="Long ago I followed some companions into the Hillsbrad Foothills. We defended ourselves from some tenacious humans who make their home there and we found ourselves in a small town the Forsaken had taken over: Tarren Mill.$B$BIt was there I found a most peculiar thing: in the center of town was a small well of fresh spring water. I'm not sure the plagued citizens of the town even realize its value--it's a small holy vestige in an unhallowed sea.$B$BBring me a sample of that water in this waterskin.",how={{"open",7771,{107045}}}},[1656]={t="A Task Unfinished",lv=5,min=1,si=7626,ot="Bring the Bundle of Furs to Innkeeper Kauth in Bloodhoof Village.",st="$n, please, I beg of you, can you help me? I have not finished my tasks here on the Mesa--I'm in the middle of my Rite of Strength--and my father asked me to deliver these furs to the inn in Bloodhoof.$B$BI'm far from rested enough to complete both my rite and this task for my father. Would you mind going on for me?$B$BThe inn is pleasant and a perfect place to rest during your long travels. I'm sure you'll agree once you see it."},[1718]={t="The Islander",lv=30,min=30,nx=1719,ot="Speak with Klannoc Macleod.",st="Your renown as a warrior grows, $n.  Now it is time to pit yourself against your peers and see where you stand.$B$BThere is an island off the coast of the Barrens, south of Ratchet.  It is called Fray Island and it is a place where warriors meet.$B$BMeet, and fight.$B$BSpeak with the chief warrior of Fray Island, Klannoc Macleod.  If he finds you worthy, then Klannoc will lead you further down the warrior's path.$B$BTo reach Fray Island, search for the sand bar shallows along the Merchant Coast."},[1719]={t="The Affray",lv=30,min=30,pre1={1718},nx=1791,ot="Kill Big Will, then speak to Klannoc Macleod on Fray Island.",st="If you want to learn from me, then you must first pass The Affray.  It is a challenge we on Fray Island like to offer rising warriors who think they're tough, and if you can pass this test then I'll know you are.$B$BTo begin, walk into the middle of that crowd yonder and step on the grate.  That'll tell Twiggy Flathead you're ready, and he'll send challengers against you.$B$BBeat all the challengers and he'll call out Big Will.  Kill Big Will, and return to me in the time we allow.",how={{"kill",6238}}},[1740]={t="The Orb of Soran'ruk",lv=25,min=20,ot="Find 3 Soran'ruk Fragments and 1 Large Soran'ruk Fragment and return them to Doan Karhan in the Barrens.",st="When demons of the Legion fall out of favor, their spirits are imprisoned within orbs and distributed to their mages and warlocks.$b$bMany were carried by their servants in Azeroth. Even fragmented, they still possess the powers of the demons trapped inside.$b$bThe orb of Soran'ruk was broken into two pieces, one was further broken to be used by the acolytes of the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps. The other, larger piece, was possessed by a wizard in Shadowfang Keep. Find them and I can reform it.",how={{"loot",6914,{4809}},{"loot",6915,{3855}}}},[1791]={t="The Windwatcher",lv=30,min=30,pre1={1719},nx=1712,ot="Speak with Bath'rah the Windwatcher.",st="Now that you've learned your berserker's stance, you'll want a nice weapon to use it with.$B$BTalk to Bath'rah the Windwatcher, a troll hermit who lives between the Alterac Mountains and the Western Plaguelands.  He is a skilled weapon maker and a powerful shaman.$B$BTo find Bath'rah, go to the river that flows along Tarren Mill's eastern flank.  Follow it north--Bath'rah is camped near ruins that rest along the river's eastern bank."},[1818]={t="Speak with Dillinger",lv=10,min=10,ex={1498},nx=1819,bc=1819,ot="Speak with Deathguard Dillinger in Brill.",st="I was told Deathguard Dillinger has a job for someone like you.  If you're willing to show your value to the Dark Lady's forces, then report to Dillinger immediately.$B$BDeathguard Dillinger's post is on the west end of Brill, near the graveyard."},[1819]={t="Ulag the Cleaver",lv=10,min=10,ex={1498},nx=1820,ot="Kill Ulag the Cleaver, then speak with Deathguard Dillinger.",st="When the Scourge swept through Tirisfal Glades, we captured one to study.  He had a free mind, and called himself Ulag the Cleaver.  But, although his will was free, he was still enthralled by the Lich King.$B$BWe hoped to find a way to break the king's control over Ulag, but we failed.  Now, finally, it is time to free him.  $B$BFree him, and kill him.$B$BActivate the skull stone trigger near the mausoleum to the north.  This will lift the magical seal that binds him.$B$BThen... be ready, $n.",how={{"kill",6390}}},[1820]={t="Speak with Coleman",lv=10,min=10,pre1={1498,1819},nx=1821,bc=1821,ot="Speak with Coleman Farthing.",st="You have proven your value to the Dark Lady, now perhaps you can prove yourself to one of her subjects.$B$BColeman Farthing awaits a warrior who is willing to be his instrument of revenge against the Forsaken's enemies.$B$BYou will find him in the Gallow's End Tavern in eastern Brill."},[1821]={t="Agamand Heirlooms",lv=11,min=10,pre1={1498,1819},nx=1822,ot="Bring Coleman Farthing the Agamand Family Axe, the Agamand Family Sword, the Agamand Family Mace and the Agamand Family dagger.",st="The Agamand family were my employers in life, and they were the cause of my death!  It is fitting that the Agamands are now mindless minions of the Lich King.$B$BNow I would have their last vestiges of honor.  Go into their family crypt and rob them of their family heirlooms: a sword, an axe, a dagger and a mace.  Bring them to me!$B$BThe Agamand family crypt is at the north end of the Agamand mills, protected by lurking scourge and dead Agamands.",how={{"open",7567,{105170}},{"open",7568,{105171}},{"open",7569,{105172}},{"open",7566,{105169}}}},[1822]={t="Heirloom Weapon",lv=11,min=10,pre1={1821}},[1823]={t="Speak with Ruga",lv=20,min=20,nx=1824,bc=1824,ot="Speak with Ruga Ragetotem.",st="You are a warrior of skill and growing renown.  Perhaps you are ready for Ruga Ragetotem's trial?  If so, then find Ruga in Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.$B$BHe awaits those warriors who answer his call."},[1824]={t="Trial at the Field of Giants",lv=20,min=20,nx=1825,ot="Bring 5 twitching antennae to Ruga Ragetotem at Camp Taurajo",st="To pass this trial, you must travel south to the Field of Giants.  There you will find a host of crawling, insect creatures.  They are new to the Barrens and I do not like what they herald.$B$BBring me their still-twitching antennae, and waste no time, $n, for harvested antennae will not twitch for long.  Bring me the antennae in the time allowed, and you will pass the trial.",how={{"loot",7119,{3252,3251,3250}}}},[1838]={t="Brutal Armor",lv=30,min=20,pre1={1824},nx=1848,si=7587,ot="Bring to Thun'grim Firegaze 15 Smoky Iron Ingots, 10 Powdered Azurite, 10 Iron Bars and a Vial of Phlogiston.",st="I have heard tales of your strength and valor, and wish to make for you a suit of armor, a companion to aid you as tales of your great deeds grow.$B$BBut the fashioning of this armor will be a quest unto itself, $n.  I will need your help, and the help of other smiths of the Horde.$B$BHere, take this scroll.  I spent many nights, struggling with near-blind eyes, writing that which I need for the armor.  Bring me the items on this scroll and I will create for you the first piece of the suit.",how={{"loot",7126,{4003,3999,4004}},{"loot",7127,{2269}},{"loot",3575},{"loot",6841,{6168}}}},[1858]={t="The Shattered Hand",lv=13,min=10,pre1={1963},si=7209,ot="Steal Tazan's key, then use it to open his Satchel and deliver its contents to Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.",st="I'll leave it to you to get Tazan's satchel open, and return to me with its contents. The locking mechanism is complex, so it would probably be easiest if you obtained the key.$b$bAs you didn't find it on Tazan's body, I can only assume that he left the key in the care of another... Ah, yes, that's right. He had an assistant named Gamon. A drunkard, you'll most likely find him at the tavern. Perhaps you could quietly relieve him of the key.",how={{"loot",7295}}},[1859]={t="Therzok",lv=10,min=10,ex={1885},nx=1963,bc=1963,ot="Speak with Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.",st="Lower your voice, $n. Yeah, I know your name. Was told to keep an eye out for an orc by your description.$b$bFrom what we've heard about you, you can handle yourself in combat, and aren't opposed to a little sneakery from time to time.$b$bAm I right?$b$bAnyways, you should go see Therzok in Orgrimmar. He's got an offer for you to hear."},[1881]={t="Speak with Anastasia",lv=10,min=10,ex={1884},nx=1882,bc=1882,ot="Speak with Anastasia Hartwell.",st="$n, Anastasia Hartwell has a task for someone of your talents.  Speak with her in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, and prepare yourself for your first task for the mages of the Forsaken."},[1882]={t="The Balnir Farmstead",lv=10,min=10,ex={1884},ot="Bring Balnir Snapdragons to Anastasia Hartwell in the Mage Quarter of the Undercity.",st="The Plaguelands to the east are an aberration.  Devised by the Lich King, they spread their magic into the soil, corrupting and killing all that live.  Although there is a certain charm to the destructive forces of the plague, we, the mages of the Forsaken, believe it is unruly and must be curtailed.$B$BBut first, we must measure how far it has spread into Tirisfal.  Go to the Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal.  In the garden are flowers--snapdragons.  Gather these and return.",how={{"open",7227,{102985}}}},[1885]={t="Mennet Carkad",lv=10,min=10,ex={1859},nx=1886,bc=1886,ot="Speak with Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity.",st="$n? Not quite what I was expecting, considering Carkad himself has taken an interest to you. Looks can be deceiving though, right?$b$bEither way, you should go see him as soon as possible. You wouldn't want to know what happened to the last few that chose to ignore his summons."},[1886]={t="The Deathstalkers",lv=13,min=10,nx=1898,ot="Get Astor's Letter of Introduction and return it to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter.",st="If you wish to join the Deathstalkers, Lord Varimathras' elite guard, you will have to prove your worth.$b$bI will not lie to you, $n, this task could mean your death.$b$bI have some things that need attending to. I require the personal effects of Astor Hadren, a messenger who travels between Silverpine and the Undercity. I will leave the method of procurement to your discretion.$b$bIt will be better for you if you know less of the nature of this business. Succeed and I shall tell you more.",how={{"loot",7231,{6497}}}},[1898]={t="The Deathstalkers",lv=13,min=10,pre1={1886},nx=1899,si=7231,ot="Speak with Andron Gant in the Undercity.",st="The letter of introduction should be enough to convince Andron that you are the messenger he's been waiting for. I've met Andron before, he doesn't quite have the mental capacity to be that suspicious.$b$bLord Varimathras suspects that Andron has been providing aid to some other group. He wishes to know what organization this is and requires proof of it.$b$bI want you to speak with Andron, and obtain this information. You'll find him at his shop near the Apothecarium."},[1899]={t="The Deathstalkers",lv=13,min=10,pre1={1898},nx=1978,ot="Bring Astor's Ledger to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of Undercity.",st="You'll find the ledger with the information your employers seek on the bookshelf behind me. Deliver it with my regards, and tell them that I would prefer it if they sent you, if they find enough value that they should wish to continue our arrangement.",how={{"open",7294,{103600}}}},[1918]={t="The Befouled Element",lv=27,min=23,nx=824,si=16408,ot="Bring the Befouled Water Globe to Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.",st="The slain elemental has produced an intensely glowing globe of water.  The contents of the globe are, at best, disgusting.  It would be safe to assume that whatever has befouled the water of Mystral Lake is most likely present in the water of the globe.$B$BIt's not exactly common knowledge who might be interested in such a find; perhaps the person who originally sent you out to the lake, Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, might have an idea."},[1960]={t="Investigate the Alchemist Shop",lv=16,min=15,nx=1961,ot="Obtain a Cantation of Manifestation and a Chest of Containment Coffers from behind Anastasia Hartwell.  Bring 3 Filled Containment Coffers, the Chest of Containment Coffers and the Cantation of Manifestation to Anastasia in the Undercity.",st="Algernon's alchemist shop in the Apothecarium is the locus of a strange disturbance.  Invisible creatures, made solely of magic, wander the shop--there must be a reason, and we must find it!$B$BInvestigate the disturbance and capture those creatures.  Take a chest of coffers and a scroll from behind me.  Use the scroll at the shop to make the creatures visible, subdue them with your spells, then throw down a coffer to capture them.  Return with the filled coffers, the empty coffers and the cantation.",how={{"open",7292,{103574}},{"open",7247,{105174}},{"open",7308,{105175}}}},[1961]={t="Gathering Materials",lv=15,min=15,pre1={1960},nx=1962,ot="Bring 10 Linen and 6 Dalaran Mana Gems to Josef Gregorian.",st="It is time for you to don your first mage's robes, $n.  They are a sign of your station, and a testament to your worth.$B$BTo gain the robes, you must gather the mana gems from the Dalaran mages of Silverpine.  Their beliefs are similar to ours and so killing them is somewhat distasteful, but if they lack the strength to resist us, then they do not deserve their lives.$B$BBring the gems and a supply of linen to Josef Gregorian at the Magic Quarter's tailor shop.",how={{"open",2589,{106318,106319,2039}},{"loot",7293,{1912,1867,1914}}}},[1962]={t="Spellfire Robes",lv=15,min=15,pre1={1961}},[1963]={t="The Shattered Hand",lv=13,min=10,nx=1858,ot="Kill Tazan and bring his Satchel to Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.",st="The Warchief is too subtle in his methods. He is cautious to unleash the might of the Horde. Once we were stronger, mighty conquerors all. That pride we must regain, and the Shattered Hand will do so.$b$bWe build strength from the shadows and strike at the exposed, secretly laying our enemies low. A task you must complete for me, to prove your worth.$b$bThe troll Tazan trades with the pirates near Ratchet. He has information I must have. Kill him and bring me his satchel.",how={{"loot",7209,{6494}}}},[1978]={t="The Deathstalkers",lv=13,min=10,pre1={1899},si=7294,ot="Deliver Andron's Ledger to Varimathras in the Hall of the Dark Lady in the Undercity.",st="The Syndicate? I would never have suspected. It seems the lords of Alterac have fallen far in the years since their betrayal.$b$bLord Varimathras will be pleased to learn of this, and as you were so instrumental in this discovery, it would be fitting if you were the one to deliver it to him.$b$bAh, and how could I forget?$b$bWelcome to the Deathstalkers."},[1998]={t="Fenwick Thatros",lv=16,min=16,nx=1999,ot="Kill Fenwick Thatros and bring his head back to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity.",st="Lord Varimathras has just sent me a missive about a threat to the Forsaken that must be immediately removed. His name is Fenwick Thatros, one whom Lord Varimathras believes is a leader of the undead that have taken root in Silverpine Forest.$b$bYour name came to mind immediately, $n. I have faith enough in your abilities that you will carry out this mission flawlessly.$b$bThe latest reports from the Deathstalkers in Silverpine indicate that Thatros can be found near the decrepit dock on Lordamere.",how={{"loot",7306,{6570}}}},[2161]={t="A Peon's Burden",lv=5,min=1,si=7629,ot="Bring Ukor's Burden to Innkeeper Grosk in Razor Hill.",st="Excuse me?  Can you help me?$B$BI have a load of food here.  I walked along the road and braved scorpids and spiders and worse!  I brought the food to the Valley of Trials because I thought they needed it and I like to help out.  But they don't need any food!  Now I have to take it back to Razor Hill and I'm afraid of all the beasts along the way...$B$BCan you take it for me?  I'm just a peon, but you're a hero.  You fear nothing!$B$BTake it to Innkeeper Grosk at the Razor Hill inn.  Thank you!"},[2378]={t="Find the Shattered Hand",lv=16,min=16,ex={2380},ot="Journey to Orgrimmar and speak with Shenthul at the Cleft of Shadow.",st="You have served the Deathstalkers well, $n, but perhaps it is time for you to venture outward. While you have shown aptitude in the ways of stealth and deception, you still require much training.$B$BThe Deathstalkers have allies within the Shattered Hand. Seek out those that would assist us - find Shenthul in Orgrimmar."},[2379]={t="Zando'zan",lv=16,min=16,nx=2382,ot="Speak with Zando'zan at the Cleft of Shadow.",st="Your determination alone is not enough to overcome the obstacles that lay ahead of us.$B$BSpeak with Zando'zan to begin your training as an operative of the Shattered Hand.$B$BIt is only when you have mastered the practices of stealth and thievery that you may take the next step towards your destiny."},[2381]={t="Plundering the Plunderers",lv=18,min=16,pre1={2382},si=7970,ot="Bring the Southsea Treasure back to Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet. Do not forget to get an E.C.A.C. and Thieves' Tools from Wrenix's Gizmotronic Apparatus. You will need both of these items to complete your mission.$B$BShould you be attacked by any unusually hostile parrots, use your E.C.A.C.!",st="I don't mean to scare you, $n, but the last five thieves I sent to steal the southsea treasure came back to me in pieces.$B$BSouth along the coast you'll find Tide Razor, the southsea freebooter's ship. Nestled in the hold is the payoff - the southsea treasure. On the second level of that ship is the pirate's den, a place where they train all of their thieves.$B$BBoard that ship, steal the treasure, and bring it back to me. Use the pirate's den if you need to practice your thievery, but be careful!",how={{"loot",7968,{7168}}}},[2382]={t="Wrenix of Ratchet",lv=16,min=16,pre1={2379},nx=2381,ot="Travel to Ratchet and speak with Wrenix the Wretched.",st="Zando'zan has seen it! Yes, the day comes! Thrall's death... the dagger in his back, poison seeping through to his every vein... Zando'zan has said too much.$B$B$n! Zando'zan has a task for $n! $n must travel to Ratchet, east of the Crossroads, and speak with Wrenix the Wretched. Go!"},[2383]={t="Simple Parchment",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=12635,ot="Read the Simple Parchment and speak to Frang in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the warrior trainer Frang. He would have words with you when you're ready. You'll find him outside the Den, taking cover in the shade."},[2458]={t="Deep Cover",lv=20,min=20,pre1={2460},nx=2478,si=8051,ot="Travel to the Venture Co. Tower, north of the Sludge Fen and contact the Shattered Hand's covert operative, Taskmaster Fizzule.$B$BWhen the tower is in sight, use the Flare Gun to signal your arrival to Taskmaster Fizzule. Fire off TWO flares, then approach Taskmaster Fizzule and perform the Shattered /Salute.$B$BThese actions must be performed in the correct order, as Fizzule will attack and terminate any person he does not recognize.",st="The Venture Company... Perhaps you have heard of them?$B$BFor one year we have worked on planting an agent deep within their ranks. Through much hard work and careful planning, we succeeded.$B$BRecently we received word that the Venture Co. are planning something on a grand scale. Go north of the Sludge Fen to the Venture Co. tower and contact our undercover agent, Taskmaster Fizzule.$B$BWhen you find the tower, use this flare gun, then approach Fizzule and show him the salute of the Shattered Hand."},[2460]={t="The Shattered Salute",lv=20,min=20,nx=2458,ot="Perform the Shattered Salute on Shenthul.",st="As a rogue of the Shattered Hand, it is imperative that you learn the Shattered Salute. It is the only way to truly identify another member of the Hand.$B$BWatch, learn, repeat."},[2478]={t="Mission: Possible But Not Probable",lv=24,min=20,pre1={2458},nx=2479,ot="Steal Silixiz's Tower Key from Foreman Silixiz, then kill two Mutated Venture Co. Drones, two Venture Co. Patrollers, and two Venture Co. Lookouts.$B$BAssassinate Grand Foreman Gallywix and take his head, then pick the lock on Gallywix's lockbox and steal the Cache of Zanzil's Altered Mixture. Take the Cache and Gallywix's Head back to Shenthul in Orgrimmar for further instruction.",st="You will need to steal the tower key from Foreman Silixiz, $n. Once you've got the key in your possession, hold on to it - I may need it later.$B$BRemember, the poison has weakened everything in this tower. Use your abilities to bring chaos and destruction to its inhabitants. Slay them all -- show no mercy!$B$BOnce everything inside lays in a bloodied heap, pick Gallywix's lockbox and steal the cache of Zanzil's mixture held inside. Take both the head of Gallywix and the mixture to Shenthul in Orgrimmar.",how={{"kill",7310},{"kill",7307},{"kill",7308},{"loot",8074,{7288}},{"loot",8072,{7287}},{"open",8073,{129127}}}},[2479]={t="Hinott's Assistance",lv=26,min=20,pre1={2478},nx=2480,si=8087,ot="Travel to Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills and deliver the Sample of Zanzil's Mixture to Serge Hinott.$B$BTo get to Tarren Mill, take the Zeppelin to the Undercity and follow the road south through Silverpine and towards Hillsbrad. Follow the signs!",st="Take a sample of the mixture to Serge Hinott in Tarren Mill.$B$BIf anyone can cure you, it's Serge. Live long enough and Serge will show you the ways of poison creation and use."},[2480]={t="Hinott's Assistance",lv=20,min=20,pre1={2479},ot="Wait for Serge Hinott to complete the cure.",st="I have never seen such wondrous results from a poison! Zanzil you say? Never heard of him, however, I must commend him on the creation of this concoction.$B$BSo, I am to cure you of this and then teach you how to make use of the poison?$B$BGive me a few moments to examine the toxin, $n."},[2841]={t="Rig Wars",lv=35,min=25,ot="Retrieve the Rig Blueprints and Thermaplugg's Safe Combination from Gnomeregan and bring them to Nogg in Orgrimmar.",st="Gnome technology - two years ago its most common use was as a punch line. Times certainly have changed. Now they've got a new rig built that's better than all our shredder models combined. I need the blueprints, $n!$B$BUnfortunately, the plans are locked away in a safe near Mekgineer Thermaplugg. To make matters worse, the combination to the safe is only known by Mekgineer Thermaplugg.$B$BDo whatever you have to do to get that combination, $n. Then crack open that safe and bring back those blueprints!",how={{"open",9153,{142477}},{"loot",9299,{7800,218969,218971}}}},[2842]={t="Chief Engineer Scooty",lv=35,min=20,nx=2843,ot="Speak with Scooty in Booty Bay.",st="As soon as we got word from Kernobee about the new gnomish rig, Scooty and I began work on the Transpolyporter 6000: The fastest and most reliable way to Gnomeregan.$B$BIt's finally ready for passengers to board, $n. If you want to give it a try, go to Booty Bay and talk with Scooty at the wind rider roost. To get to Booty Bay, take the boat from Ratchet.$B$BOf course, you could always try and make the run to Gnomeregan through the dwarf infested mountains of Dun Morogh!"},[2843]={t="Gnomer-gooooone!",lv=35,min=20,pre1={2842},ot="Wait for Scooty to calibrate the Goblin Transponder.",st="As long as you have the transponder in your possession, all you need to do is step on the pad and you'll be teleported to Gnomeregan.$B$BYou may experience some unusual side effects, but none of those should be permanent... anymore.$B$BI almost forgot the most important part - getting back. When you're ready to come back, just step on the transpolyporter pad in Gnomeregan!$B$BNow to calibrate the transponder to your size and weight."},[2904]={t="A Fine Mess",lv=30,min=20,ne=1,ot="Escort Kernobee to the Clockwerk Run exit and then report to Scooty in Booty Bay.",st="<Kernobee groans.> Wha.. What happened?$B$BThe last thing I remember is being captured by a group of dark iron dwarves, beaten to within an inch of my life and then thrown in here with these filthy troggs.$B$BGet me out of here, $n!$B$BHere's the plan: Lead me to the exit; if we make it out alive, you go to Booty Bay and let Scooty know that I went to Ratchet to warn Tinkerwiz of the dark iron's involvement in the making of that super rig.$B$BLet's get going!"},[2945]={t="Grime-Encrusted Ring",lv=34,min=28,si=9326,ot="Figure out a way to remove the grime from the Grime-Encrusted Ring.",st="You have uncovered what appears to be a ring from the corpse of one of the Dark Iron dwarves.  It is difficult to tell what kind of ring it is, however; dirt and hardened residue cake the item completely, making wearing it impossible.  You think you can make out the slight luster of precious metal and maybe even the glint of a gem under the residue.$B$BIf you are going to make use of this ring, you are going to need to find something to get the hardened residue off of it."},[2949]={t="Return of the Ring",lv=34,min=28,pre1={2945},nx=2950,si=9362,ot="You may either keep the ring, or you may find the person responsible for the imprint and engravings on the inside of the band.",st="Opening the box produced by the Sparklematic 5200 reveals a shiny ring!  Donning the ring, you feel magic power surge through your body.$B$BInside the band is a small but nonetheless discernable imprint of the seal of Orgrimmar.  Engraved letters are next to it, but only the first three stand out even after cleaning: \"NOG...\"$B$BThis may signify either the initials of the previous owner, or perhaps the initials of the ring's crafter.  Keep the ring... or find \"NOG\" - decisions, decisions..."},[2950]={t="Nogg's Ring Redo",lv=35,min=28,pre1={2949},si=9362,ot="Bring the Brilliant Gold Ring, a Silver Bar, a Moss Agate, and 30 silver coins to Nogg in Orgrimmar.",st="No, no, no - I'm not all of the sudden saying that the ring is mine.  I normally don't do this, but your information about the Dark Irons was very useful.  I'll improve your ring for you, better than whomever made this simple little thing could have ever done.  Probably some gnome...$B$BIf you bring me a bar of silver, a moss agate, and thirty silver coins for my trouble, I'll add a silver and agate lattice to the ring that will strengthen the magic inside of it.  Interested?",how={{"open",2842,{106319}},{"open",1206,{1732,2849,1733}}}},[2951]={t="The Sparklematic 5200!",lv=30,min=25,ex={4601,4602},ot="Insert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.",st="This contraption stands out amongst the gnomes holding out against the madness outside the room.  A small plaque on the device reads \"The Sparklematic 5200\", followed by some text:$B$B\"Grime and residue ruining your sparklies?  The Sparklematic 5200 puts the shine back in shine-tastic!  Insert the item you wish to clean and deposit three silver coins in the coin slot.  Give the Sparklematic 5200 a moment for operation, and voila!  Your valuables will emerge clean and shiny!\"",how={{"loot",9308,{6213,6209,6210}}}},[2952]={t="The Sparklematic 5200!",lv=30,min=25,pre1={2951,4601,4602},ex={4605,4606}},[2983]={t="Call of Fire",lv=10,min=10,ex={1522,1523,2984,97243},nx=1524,bc=1524,ot="Find Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.",st="It's been some time since you were tested last, $n. You've been patient thus far in your studies, but it's time for you to learn about greater powers... it's time you learn real power. The element of fire is yours if you're prepared to pay for it.$B$BSeek out Kranal Fiss in the Barrens. He lives in a small dwelling north of the Crossroads, but be mindful, if you've reached the blasted night elf lands, you've gone way too far."},[2984]={t="Call of Fire",lv=10,min=10,ex={1522,1523,2983,97243},nx=1524,bc=1524,ot="Find Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.",st="Long has it been since you were last tested, $n. You have shown patience thus far in your studies, but the time has come for you to learn more. The time has come for you to learn about destruction... and chaos. The element of fire is yours for the understanding, if you're prepared to pay for it.$B$BSeek out Kranal Fiss in the Barrens. He lives in a small dwelling north of the Crossroads, but be mindful, if you've reached the night elf lands, you've gone too far."},[3065]={t="Simple Tablet",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=6488,ot="Read the Simple Tablet and speak to Frang in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the warrior trainer Frang. He would have words with you when you're ready. You'll find him outside the Den, taking cover in the shade."},[3082]={t="Etched Tablet",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=9564,ot="Speak to Jen'shan in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the hunter trainer Jen'shan. She would have words with you when you're ready."},[3083]={t="Encrypted Tablet",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=9554,ot="Read the Encrypted Tablet and speak to Rwag in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the rogue trainer Rwag. He would have words with you when you're ready."},[3084]={t="Rune-Inscribed Tablet",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=9562,ot="Speak to Shikrik in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the shaman trainer Shikrik. She would have words with you when you're ready."},[3085]={t="Hallowed Tablet",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=9561,ot="Read the Hallowed Tablet and speak to Ken'jai outside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the priest trainer Ken'jai. He would have words with you when you're ready."},[3086]={t="Glyphic Tablet",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=9575,ot="Read the Glyphic Tablet and speak with Mai'ah near the entrance to the Den in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the mage trainer Mai'ah. She would have words with you when you're ready."},[3087]={t="Etched Parchment",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=9553,ot="Read the Etched Parchment and speak to Jen'shan in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the hunter trainer Jen'shan. She would have words with you when you're ready."},[3088]={t="Encrypted Parchment",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=9560,ot="Read the Encrypted Parchment and speak to Rwag in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the rogue trainer Rwag. He would have words with you when you're ready."},[3089]={t="Rune-Inscribed Parchment",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=9568,ot="Read the Rune-Inscribed Parchment and speak to Shikrik in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the shaman trainer Shikrik. She would have words with you when you're ready."},[3090]={t="Tainted Parchment",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=9579,ot="Read the Tainted Parchment and speak to Nartok inside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BI usually avoid dealing with warlocks if I can help it, but I think you should read it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from your newly-appointed trainer Nartok. He would have words with you when you're ready."},[3091]={t="Simple Note",lv=1,min=1,pre1={747},si=9547,ot="Read the Simple Note and speak to Harutt Thunderhorn in Camp Narache.",st="Just a moment ago a messenger was looking for you, $n. I believe she was sent by the warrior trainer Harutt. If this note is from Harutt, I wouldn't take long in reading it's contents."},[3092]={t="Etched Note",lv=1,min=1,pre1={747},si=9565,ot="Read the Etched Note and speak to Lanka Farshot in Red Cloud Mesa.",st="Just a moment ago a messenger was looking for you, $n. I believe she was sent by the hunter trainer Lanka. If this note is from Lanka, I wouldn't take long in reading it's contents."},[3093]={t="Rune-Inscribed Note",lv=1,min=1,pre1={747},si=9552,ot="Read the Rune-Inscribed Note and speak to Meela Dawnstrider in Camp Narache.",st="Just a moment ago a messenger was looking for you, $n. I believe she was sent by the shaman trainer Meela. If this note is from Meela, I wouldn't take long in reading it's contents."},[3094]={t="Verdant Note",lv=1,min=1,pre1={747},si=9581,ot="Read the Verdant Note and speak to Gart Mistrunner in Camp Narache.",st="Just a moment ago a messenger was looking for you, $n. I believe she was sent by the druid trainer Gart. If this note is from Gart, I wouldn't take long in reading its contents."},[3095]={t="Simple Scroll",lv=1,min=1,pre1={364},si=9546,ot="Read the Simple Scroll and speak to Dannal Stern in Deathknell.",st="Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the warrior trainer Dannal. I would take some time to read it before heading out again."},[3096]={t="Encrypted Scroll",lv=1,min=1,pre1={364},si=9559,ot="Read the Encrypted Scroll and speak to David Trias in Deathknell.",st="Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the rogue trainer David Trias. I would take some time to read it before heading out again."},[3097]={t="Hallowed Scroll",lv=1,min=1,pre1={364},si=9569,ot="Read the Hallowed Scroll and speak to Dark Cleric Duesten in the church in Deathknell.",st="Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the priest trainer Duesten. I would take some time to read it before heading out again."},[3098]={t="Glyphic Scroll",lv=1,min=1,pre1={364},si=9574,ot="Read the Glyphic Scroll and speak to Isabella in the church in Deathknell.",st="Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the mage trainer Isabella. I would take some time to read it before heading out again."},[3099]={t="Tainted Scroll",lv=1,min=1,pre1={364},si=9578,ot="Read the Tainted Scroll and speak to Maximillion in Deathknell.",st="Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the warlock trainer Maximillion. I would take some time to read it before heading out again."},[3221]={t="Speak with Renferrel",lv=12,min=10,pre1={449},nx=1359,ot="Speak with Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",st="While you were out helping our deathstalkers, Apothecary Renferrel sent you a summons.  He did not give me details, but he wanted to speak with you about the wolf hearts you had given him."},[3261]={t="Jorn Skyseer",lv=18,min=10,pre1={905},nx=882,ot="Speak with Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo.",st="Your time with me is over, $n.  To learn more, you must go to Camp Taurajo to the south and speak with Jorn Skyseer.  He will continue your guidance."},[3281]={t="Stolen Silver",lv=18,min=9,pre1={869},ot="Bring the Stolen Silver to Gazrog in the Crossroads.",st="You may have killed the raptors, but the silver they stole must be recovered!  I have reports that the raptors have a large grouping of nests south of Ratchet, known as the Raptor Grounds.  It is likely that they brought our stolen silver there.$B$BGo to this raptor haven and search for the stolen silver.  When you find it, return it to me.",how={{"open",5061,{147557}}}},[3301]={t="Mura Runetotem",lv=15,min=10,pre1={880},si=10414,ot="Speak with Mura Runetotem in the Sepulcher.",st="My clanmate, Mura Runetotem, traveled to Silverpine so that she might aid our undead allies.  Silverpine is an ailing forest, a dying forest, and it was Mura's hope to bring it new life.  Perhaps the strange life found here in the Barrens can help her work in Silverpine.$B$BTake a sample of the shells you gathered, and bring it to Mura in Silverpine.  She is staying at the Sepulcher.  With luck, studying the shell will give her the insight she needs to heal that dying place."},[3369]={t="In Nightmares",lv=25,min=10,pre1={6981},si=10649,ot="Bring the Nightmare Shard to Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise.",st="This shard holds great secrets; it is the pure essence of the Emerald Dream. However, what I see in this shard is not a dream; one would call this sort of a vision a nightmare.$B$BI do not wish to alarm you, $n, but I think it is best if you deliver this shard into the hands of a wise druid as soon as you can.$B$BHamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise is who you need to find. Head to Thunder Bluff. I cannot say more."},[3376]={t="Break Sharptusk!",lv=5,min=3,ot="Bring the head of Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle to Brave Windfeather in Red Cloud Mesa.",st="$n - I have heard of you, newcomer.  Perhaps it is you that will help us, where others have failed.$B$BWe tauren have carved a home out of this land, but not without a cost.  The Bristleback quilboars of Brambleblade Ravine, led by Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle, have made our lives difficult with their continued war against us.  I charge you to bring me the chief's head!$B$BHe will be found in the ravine to the east in their makeshift village.",how={{"loot",10459,{8554}}}},[3901]={t="Rattling the Rattlecages",lv=3,min=1,pre1={364},ot="Kill 12 Rattlecage Skeletons, and then return to Shadow Priest Sarvis in Deathknell when you are done.",st="You've shown your potential to the Forsaken under normal circumstances $n - now let's see you under pressure.$B$BThe Rattlecage skeletons, more mindless minions of the Lich King, are a tougher foe than the zombies you have faced thus far.  Again, thin their numbers and prove yourself to the Forsaken.  Do not tarry - when you are done, speak to me again.",how={{"kill",1890}}},[3902]={t="Scavenging Deathknell",lv=3,min=2,pre1={376},ot="Search Deathknell and the vicinity for 6 pieces of Scavenged Goods, and return them to Deathguard Saltain.",st="You there!  If you're looking for something to make yourself useful, then listen up!$B$BWe need fresh out-of-the-ground recruits to head into Deathknell and search for any sort of useful equipment.  Most likely, they'll be in stacks of boxes.  We expect more recruits to be rising soon, and unless we want them to stumble about naked we had better get to scavenging!$B$BWell get to work, you miserable bag of bones!  I'm not going to reward those without some hustle.",how={{"open",11127,{164662}}}},[3921]={t="Wenikee Boltbucket",lv=14,min=10,pre1={902},nx=3922,si=11142,ot="Bring the Broken Samophlange to Wenikee Boltbucket.",st="I think I might have broken that Samophlange.  That's not good, because I already told some colleagues in Undermine about it and they were very intrigued.  We must find a way to fix it!$B$BTake the broken samophlange to Wenikee Boltbucket, just south of Mor'shan Rampart, the horde outpost between the Barrens and Ashenvale.  She is very clever and inquisitive.  If you show her the samophlange I bet she'd jump at the chance to fix it."},[3922]={t="Nugget Slugs",lv=15,min=10,pre1={3921},nx=3923,ot="Bring 15 Nugget Slugs to Wenikee Boltbucket in the Barrens.",st="I want to fix this samophlange, but to do that I'm going to need some supplies.  I ran out of seventeen-point-five gauge nugget slugs and I'm going to need a bunch of those for the work ahead.$B$BThe closest place to get them is the Sludge Fen to the east.  The Venture Company usually keeps them in their tool buckets.  Go to the Sludge Fen and look in the tool buckets you find there, then return to me when you've gathered enough nugget slugs.",how={{"open",11143,{161752}}}},[3923]={t="Rilli Greasygob",lv=18,min=10,pre1={3922},nx=3924,si=11146,ot="Bring the Broken and Battered Samophlange to Rilli Greasygob in Orgrimmar.",st="Well, that didn't work.  I put some extra gauges on the samophlange to measure its structural integrity, and they read the integrity at an all-time low.  I could add some more dials and maybe a lever or two to try and fix it, but... I think that might make things even worse.$B$BYou should take the samophlange to Rilli Greasygob.  He used to work for the Venture Company -- if anyone knows how to fix it, it's Rilli.$B$BYou can find him at Nogg's Machine Shop in Orgrimmar, in the Valley of Honor."},[3924]={t="Samophlange Manual",lv=19,min=10,pre1={3923},ot="Bring the Samophlange Manual to Rilli Greasygob in Orgrimmar.",st="I think I can fix the samophlange, but I'm going to need the user's manual first.  When I was in the Venture Company I had a rival, Boss Copperplug, who hoarded the secrets of the samophlange, giving out small bits of knowledge on the device to those he trusted.  I wasn't one of the trusted few...$B$BBoss Copperplug used to stay at the Boulder Lode Mine in northeastern Barrens.  Get the manual from him, and if he's given pages from it to anyone, you'll have to collect them too.",how={{"kill",3283},{"kill",3286},{"kill",9336}}},[4021]={t="Counterattack!",lv=20,min=11,pre1={852},ot="Bring a Piece of Krom'zar's Banner to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.",st="The Horde commends your successes against the Kolkar, but the Kolkar themselves are maddened.  I have reports that a contingent of Kolkar has traveled to the Barrens from their home in Desolace, to seek vengeance.  My latest report was that, even now, they move against these bunkers, from the west!$B$BFace the Kolkar invaders, and end their threat in the Barrens.  Kill them until their leader, Warlord Krom'zar, appears.  Defeat him and bring me a piece of his banner as proof.$B$BWe're counting on you, $n.",how={{"open",11227,{164690}}}},[4402]={t="Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise",lv=3,min=1,pre1={788},ot="Bring Galgar 10 Cactus Apples. You remember him saying that they could be found near cactuses.",st="It sure gets hot out here in the Valley of Trials.$B$B<Galgar wipes his brow.>$B$BIf only I had some cactus apples, I could make my famous cactus apple surprise! Nothing cools you off faster than a piece of that delicious treat.$B$BI'll tell you what, $n. If you bring me 10 cactus apples, I'll make you a few portions of cactus apple surprise to take with you on your adventures, and a free training manual, too. If you're interested, you can find cactus apples growing near the cactus plants around here.",how={{"open",11583,{171938}}}},[4542]={t="Message to Freewind Post",lv=25,min=23,nx=4841,bc=4841,si=11886,ot="Bring the Urgent Message to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post.",st="Brave traveler, the centaurs have increased their attacks in this area. Freewind Post must know about this renewed harassment immediately! Seek Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post to the southeast and give him this urgent message.$b$bBe warned, avoid the Grimtotem Clan nearby... they have been acting strange toward us lately."},[4641]={t="Your Place in the World",lv=1,min=1,nx=788,bc=788,ot="Speak with Gornek. You recall Kaltunk marking your map with his location and mentioning that Gornek resided in the Den, a building to the west.",st="Finally, you are of age, $n... of age to battle in the name of the Horde. To conquer for the glory of the Warchief.$B$BYes...$B$B<Kaltunk looks you over.>$B$BYou will do nicely.$B$BNo doubt you wish to find a great dragon or demon and strangle it with your bare hands, but perhaps it would be wise to start on something less... dangerous.$B$B<Kaltunk laughs.>$B$BReport to Gornek, he should be able to assign a task better suited to a young $c. You will find Gornek in the Den, to the west."},[4767]={t="Wind Rider",lv=29,min=25,ot="Bring 10 Highperch Wyvern Eggs to Elu in Freewind Post.",st="I've been tasked to recruit more wyverns for the master wind riders. Their numbers are growing and I myself hope to become a wind rider one day. However, we cannot train enough wyverns to keep up with the demand. Perhaps you can help me, $n.$B$BI need you to travel to Highperch to gather some wyvern eggs. From here, head northwest along the canyon walls to a ramp that will lead you into Highperch. Be careful, wyverns are very protective over their eggs and they will not be kind to intruders.",how={{"open",12356,{175384}}}},[4770]={t="Homeward Bound",lv=29,min=25,ne=1,ot="Escort Pao'ka Swiftmountain from Highperch, and then talk to Motega Firemane in Whitereach Post.",st="Please help me, $c! I've been hiding here in Highperch for some time now and it's been days since I've seen a friendly face. I came here to study the wyvern and I think I got a little too close. After being chased away from one of the nests I got lost.$B$BI need to get back to Whitereach Post! Motega does not know that I am missing and will be furious to know that I ventured into Highperch by myself.$B$BWhitereach Post is just east of here... please take me there!"},[4821]={t="Alien Egg",lv=26,min=24,nx=4865,ot="Return the Alien Egg to Hagar Lightninghoof in Freewind Post.",st="A rumor has surfaced about an alien egg here in Thousand Needles. Those that report seeing this egg have failed to even get close enough to examine it in detail. Serpents guard the egg as if it's one of their own.$B$BI want you to seek out this alien egg and bring it to me so that I may examine it. Reports say the egg is located within a serpent den, but there are several serpent dens along the base of the cliff walls south and northeast of Freewind Post.",how={{"open",12467,{175565}}}},[4841]={t="Pacify the Centaur",lv=25,min=23,nx=5064,ot="Kill 12 Galak Scouts, 10 Galak Wranglers, and 6 Galak Windchasers, and then return to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post.",st="$n, I entreat you to hunt these centaur down. They shall feel the wrath of our revenge. Attack the centaur camp to the north of Freewind Post!  Let wrath guide your hand!",how={{"kill",4094},{"kill",4093},{"kill",4096}}},[4865]={t="Serpent Wild",lv=26,min=24,pre1={4821},nx=5062,ot="Report your findings to Motega Firemane.",st="If I did not see that with my own eyes I would never have believed it to be true. Vengeance has come to Thousand Needles!$B$B<Hagar wipes his brow.>$B$B$n, you must act quickly! Go now and seek out Motega Firemane; he is located at Whitereach Post just northwest of Freewind Post along the road. He will know what to do!"},[4881]={t="Assassination Plot",lv=28,min=23,nx=4966,ot="Warn Kanati Greycloud at Whitereach Post of the plot to kill him.",st="The Tauren, Kanati Greycloud is bold to set up a hunting camp in Thousand Needles. We must kill him to rid this hunting camp and all who may follow him. We will converge at the small post Southwest of the Great Lift."},[4904]={t="Free at Last",lv=29,min=25,ne=1,ot="Escort Lakota Windsong from the Darkcloud Pinnacle, and then talk to Thalia Amberhide at Freewind Post.",st="Arnak thinks we're going to be married... but after I declined his offer he came back that night and kidnapped me. My brother tried to stop him, but Arnak was too strong. He... he slew my brother and then brought me here.  My poor brother...$B$B$n, could you escort me out of the Darkcloud Pinnacle?  Please... I need to get back to Thalia! She must be worried sick about me."},[4921]={t="Lost in Battle",lv=20,min=14,ot="Find Mankrik's wife and then return to him in the Crossroads.",st="We battled in a small tauren camp when we were separated--she held three of the Bristlebacks off by herself. But the odds began to overwhelm us. I led some away only to see her overwhelmed by newcomers. In my rage, I turned to face my enemies, but they brought me down easily with their vast numbers.$B$BI awoke to a tauren druid tending my wounds--he had come across me on the Gold Road as I fell.$B$BPlease, $c, find some sign of my wife.",how={{"talk",10668}}},[4966]={t="Protect Kanati Greycloud",lv=28,min=23,pre1={4881},ne=1,ot="Protect Kanati Greycloud from the centaur attack.",st="But, there may be more centaur than I thought, I ask you, $n, to fight with me against these vile assassins.",how={{"kill",10720}}},[5041]={t="Supplies for the Crossroads",lv=14,min=9,ot="Find and return Crossroads' Supply Crates to Thork in the Barrens.",st="That attack on the caravan contained supplies we desperately needed.$B$BYou've been brave enough to take on the Razormane tribe so far, and I will ask you to do so again, but this time, I wonder if I could ask you to keep your eyes open for some of our lost supplies. You can probably find them throughout their camps, the quilboar getting fat off their dishonorable acts.$B$BThe people of the Crossroads would be in your debt.",how={{"open",12708,{175708}}}},[5052]={t="Blood Shards of Agamaggan",lv=21,min=14,pre1={878},nx=879,ot="Bring a Blood Shard to Mangletooth in Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.$B$BCollect more Blood Shards if you want him to bless you with Agamaggan's power.",st="Along with the thorns, the blood affected <snort> other aspects of the earth: blood red stones mixed in with other minerals. The Bristleback dig up these shards and carry them as totems <snort> for strength in battle and as totems for their magics. <snort>$B$BI know the secrets of that magic.$B$BBring Mangletooth one of these blood shards to show you understand. Bring Mangletooth many of the shards, and he will bless you with quilboar magic--the magic of Agamaggan! <snort>",how={{"loot",5075,{3258,3260,3261}}}},[5062]={t="Sacred Fire",lv=27,min=24,pre1={4865},nx=5088,ot="Gather 10 bushels of Incendia Agave, and then consult Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise in Thunderbluff.",st="Arikara is a deadly creature that must be dealt with swiftly. In order to hunt her down you will need to light the sacred fire of life - this will summon Arikara.$B$BGo now and harvest the rare Incendia agave plant. Once you have harvested enough agave, seek council with Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. She is a powerful shaman that can enchant the agave plant to create a powder that will light the fire.$B$BTravel northeast to the Boiling Pool and gather Incendia Agave.",how={{"open",12732,{175928}}}},[5064]={t="Grimtotem Spying",lv=28,min=24,pre1={4841},ot="Locate and retrieve the three Secret Notes in Darkcloud Pinnacle.",st="$n, you have served us well in the past, so I now entrust to you an important mission. The Grimtotem Clan is up to something secretive. Three agents of unknown origin were seen visiting the Grimtotem over the recent weeks. We discovered that separate chests in Darkcloud Pinnacle hold these guarded messages.$b$b$n, if you succeed in this dangerous mission, I will reward you in kind.",how={{"open",12765,{176344}},{"open",12766,{190483}},{"open",12768,{190484}}}},[5088]={t="Arikara",lv=28,min=24,pre1={5062},si=12785,ot="Slay Arikara. Bring her remains and the Incendia Powder to Motega Firemane in Whitereach Post as proof of your deed.",st="Take this refined and purified Incendia Powder to Thousand Needles and toss it on the sacred fire of life. It is located in the Darkcloud Pinnacle on an isolated needle where they bury their dead.$B$BThe enchantment that I have weaved into the Incendia powder will summon Arikara to you, $n.$B$BI fear she may be stalking Cairne Bloodhoof; too much Tauren lore has changed, and I fear this has angered Arikara. Move quickly before all is lost, $c!",how={{"click",175944},{"loot",12925,{10882}}}},[5147]={t="WANTED: Arnak Grimtotem",lv=29,min=25,ot="Slay Arnak Grimtotem and bring proof of your deed to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post.",st="Wanted: Arnak Grimtotem$B$BArnak the outcast is wanted for the heinous crimes of murder and kidnapping. Handsome rewards will be given to those brave enough to bring this criminal to justice.$B$BArnak was last seen on the cliffs near the Darkcloud Pinnacle. Show the proof of your deed to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post in order to claim the reward.",how={{"loot",12884,{10896}}}},[5151]={t="Hypercapacitor Gizmo",lv=30,min=24,si=12942,ot="Slay the beast and bring back the Hypercapacitor Gizmo and Panther Cage Key to Wizlo Bearingshiner.",st="I am the only survivor from our caravan attack by the centaur! A rare yet mighty panther is guarding my best gizmo, which is around his neck. Hah! Even the centaur tremble in the presence of this ferocious beast!$B$BHere is the key to the cage. They took everything there, but left him alone. Slay this beast and bring back my hypercapacitor, and I shall reward you.$b$bThe wrecked caravan is just north of here.",how={{"loot",12946,{10992}}}},[5441]={t="Lazy Peons",lv=4,min=3,nx=6394,si=16114,ot="Use the Foreman's Blackjack on Lazy Peons when they're sleeping.  Wake up 5 peons, then return the Foreman's Blackjack to Foreman Thazz'ril in the Valley of Trials.",st="Cursed peons!  They work hard gathering lumber from the trees of the valley, but they're always taking naps!  I need someone to help keep the peons in line.$B$BYou look like the right $r for my task.  Here, you take this blackjack and use it on any lazy peons you find sleeping on the job.  A good smack will get them right back to work!  Return the blackjack when you're done.$B$BLousy slacking peons...",how={{"talk",10556}}},[5481]={t="Gordo's Task",lv=5,min=5,nx=5482,ot="Collect 3 Gloom Weed and deliver them to Junior Apothecary Holland in the Brill graveyard.",st="Master want weeds. Us gots big hands and not good at picking. You help us and we not hurt you. Us need gloom weed. Many weeds around here and near road.$b$bWhen you have gloom weed you take to Master Holland in Brill graveyard.",how={{"open",12737,{175566}}}},[5482]={t="Doom Weed",lv=6,min=5,pre1={5481},nx=99142,ot="Collect 10 Doom Weed and deliver them back to Junior Apothecary Holland.",st="So you can see the predicament that I'm in, $n. That thing is out there collecting the wrong weeds! I'll make it worth your while to gather what I need. Bring back to me enough doom weed and I'll give you a suitable reward.$B$BIt is my understanding that they like to plague the flora near the mass gravesite, to the north of the Brill graveyard. Hurry and be mindful of the gnolls in the area.",how={{"open",13702,{176753}}}},[5642]={t="Shadowguard",lv=20,min=20,ex={5643,5680},ot="Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.",st="Something important is up in Orgrimmar, $n.$B$BThe normal messengers that come through here looking for troll priests usually are very casual. This time, they seemed to be in much more a hurry. Don't dally too long in Thunder Bluff. I'd return to the Valley of Spirits as soon as possible."},[5644]={t="Dark Sacrifice",lv=20,min=20,ex={5646,5679},ot="Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity.",st="Ah, a wonderful day for you, $n. I can see by the lessons you've learned that the time has come to send you back to Aelthalyste. There are things only she can teach you, and even then, only if you prove worthy.$B$BI will not spoil the surprise for you, but I remember when I was a young priest learning about true power... divine power. Yes, those were the days.$B$BGo back to Aelthalyste in the Undercity, $n. She will be awaiting you in the War Quarter."},[5648]={t="Garments of Spirituality",lv=4,min=5,ot="Find Grunt Kor'ja and heal her wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant her Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Tai'jin at Razor Hill.",st="You be ready for your first test, $n. South of Razor Hill, just outta town, one of our grunts be hurt fightin' off some o' Proudmoore's old troops. She not doin' too well, an' she benefit much if one of our kind could help her. Find her--her name be Kor'ja--heal her wounds, an' give her the blessin' of our ancestors.$B$BYou do this, an' me thinks that be sufficient proof that you ready to move on in our ways.",how={{"talk",12430}}},[5649]={t="In Favor of Spirituality",lv=4,min=5,nx=5648,bc=5648,ot="Speak to Tai'jin in Durotar.",st="Aye, mon. Our kind have joined the Horde because they be good for us. They loyal, and they teach us much 'bout tings like honor. But our old ways die hard. The orcs may not approve of all our traditions, but that not mean we can't continue to practice some them in secret.$B$BYou know this, an' that's why I send you to Tai'jin in Razor Hill. She teach you more 'bout our history. She teach you the ways of our tribe. Go to her when you be ready."},[5650]={t="Garments of Darkness",lv=4,min=5,ot="Find Deathguard Kel and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill.",st="Our power comes from darkness and shadow, $n, but that is not your only role. You have acknowledged that there is merit in knowing the healing arts. This is wise. But before you can know the dark, you must also know the light. And for this, I have a test for you.$B$BNorth of the cemetery is a wounded Deathguard--Deathguard Kel. He has protected us from gnolls for some time, and needs healing. But, you must also fortify his body before he can return to duty. Do both with your spells, and then return to me.",how={{"talk",12428}}},[5651]={t="In Favor of Darkness",lv=4,min=5,nx=5650,bc=5650,ot="Speak to Dark Cleric Beryl in Tirisfal Glades.",st="There are many lessons that the Forsaken have learned through experience--things that some races can only begin to fathom. And although our path lies in darkness, you will find that a great many things rely on both the light and the dark. Your lessons shall teach you to use both... and with discretion. But heed my words: never forget we were forged in corruption and left to rot like so much carrion. The Darkness is our home.$B$BSeek out Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill when you're ready to learn more."},[5654]={t="Hex of Weakness",lv=10,min=10,ex={5652,5655,5656,5657},ot="Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.",st="It be time for you to meet with Ur'kyo, $n. He be in the Valley of Spirits in the orc city. Go there and speak to him. It is time you learn more of the old ways of our kind. It time you be brought into the circle and made a true priest of our tribe."},[5658]={t="Touch of Weakness",lv=10,min=10,ex={5660,5661,5662,5663}},[5722]={t="Searching for the Lost Satchel",lv=16,min=9,nx=5724,ot="Search Ragefire Chasm for Maur Grimtotem's corpse and search it for any items of interest.",st="The troggs are not the only thing that interested Magatha in Ragefire Chasm. She has heard word that one of her servants, a Maur Grimtotem, found something peculiar while in the Chasm, but he never made it out to show her what. She'd like Maur's body found--if it still exists--and any signs of what he found while attempting to speak to the troggs.$B$BReturn to Magatha any items of interest, and I'm sure she would be very generous in her reward.$B$BAgain, seek the Chasm in the darkest areas of Orgrimmar."},[5723]={t="Testing an Enemy's Strength",lv=15,min=9,ot="Search Orgrimmar for Ragefire Chasm, then kill 8 Ragefire Troggs and 8 Ragefire Shaman before returning to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.",st="Beneath the city of Orgrimmar, stout creatures known as troggs started coming to the surface from deep below the lava filled tunnels. In her ever-benevolence, Magatha sought to make peace with the creatures, but they turned on her diplomats, killing them. She will not allow such treatment of the tauren people and now consider the creatures a threat to all of the Horde.$B$BShe asks that you put an end to this trogg threat before it overwhelms the Horde from below. Find Ragefire Chasm and destroy them all.",how={{"kill",11318},{"kill",11319}}},[5724]={t="Returning the Lost Satchel",lv=16,min=9,pre1={5722},si=14381,ot="Take the Grimtotem Satchel to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.",st="You find a satchel under the body of the tauren. It is still gripped tightly in his arms as though he was trying to protect it while being attacked by the troggs.$B$BRemoving the satchel from his vice-like grip, you stow it with your own equipment and prepare to make your way out of the tunnels and back to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff."},[5725]={t="The Power to Destroy...",lv=16,min=9,ot="Bring the books Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether to Varimathras in Undercity.",st="Many denizens of the Legion bestow gifts on their followers as you may well know. Some of these gifts the Dark Lady feels would be better off in her hands than in the hands of those with... lesser vision.$B$BA sect of the Shadow Council hidden in caverns below Orgrimmar known as the Searing Blade are a prime example. The Lady tells me that members of the Searing Blade have come into the possession of two powerful spell books--she would like to \"borrow\" these books from them. You will get them for her.",how={{"loot",14395,{11322,11324}},{"loot",14396,{11322,11324}}}},[5726]={t="Hidden Enemies",lv=12,min=9,nx=5727,ot="Bring a Lieutenant's Insignia to Thrall in Orgrimmar.",st="One thing I will not tolerate are traitors in our midst, $n. But I would be a fool to play my hand so early--it would not sufficiently cut the corruption out of our lands and only cause the infection to grow worse.$B$BBut you, a young adventurer, could go places my agents could not... could learn the truth... could find the true head of the beast.$B$BIf you are brave enough, then enter Skull Rock to the east of Orgrimmar, find a lieutenant's insignia off one of the Burning Blade there, and return to me.",how={{"loot",14544,{3197,3198}}}},[5727]={t="Hidden Enemies",lv=12,min=9,pre1={5726},nx=5728,si=14544,ot="Take the Lieutenant's Insignia to Neeru Fireblade and speak to him. Gauge if he believes you are a member of the Burning Blade and then return to Thrall in Orgrimmar.",st="Now let us see if this insignia you found is worth the effort.$B$BThere is a warlock within the city who believes he has my trust. He does not know that I realize where his true loyalties lie. He is in fact the leader of the Burning Blade. But do not rush off to do battle with him; he has a purpose, and we shall use him against our enemies.$B$BTake this insignia to him in the Cleft of Shadow here in Orgrimmar, speak to him and see if he believes you are one of his own, then return to me here.",how={{"talk",3216}}},[5728]={t="Hidden Enemies",lv=16,min=9,pre1={5727},nx=5729,ot="Kill Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker before returning to Thrall in Orgrimmar.",st="Hmm, leaders of the Searing Blade... this concerns me most. If they are the ones of value to Neeru, then those are who we must target first. This satyr... Bazzalan, and the other Neeru mentioned--what was he, a warlock?--must be slain.$B$BReturn to the Cleft of Shadow and enter Ragefire Chasm, $n. Find these two leaders of the Searing Blade, and kill them. But be careful not to let Neeru know it was you who did this. You must retain your identity as one of his $gbrothers:sisters; in arms.",how={{"kill",11519},{"kill",11518}}},[5729]={t="Hidden Enemies",lv=15,min=9,pre1={5728},nx=5730,ot="Speak to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.",st="I think our next step should be to have you placed close to Neeru. If he is as agitated as reports suggest, then we may accomplish two things. One, you may be able to gain some greater knowledge about the Council or at least the Burning Blade, and two, he may just begin to trust you enough that he asks you to start to aid him. He may very well look at you as someone who can fill the void now that some of the leadership is in turmoil.$B$BReturn to the Cleft and speak to him again, but do not be too overt."},[5730]={t="Hidden Enemies",lv=16,min=9,pre1={5729},ot="Speak to Thrall in Orgrimmar and tell him what you've learned.",st="You are one of my lieutenants! Prepare yourself, $c. I will call upon you soon.$B$BMy time spent on the Searing Blade may be all but wasted now, but that does not mean that the Shadow Council's schemes elsewhere must suffer. I will do what I can to minimize the damage here in Ragefire Chasm. In the meantime, I will have my agents in the Barrens and Ashenvale begin work on our newest agenda. Return to me soon."},[5761]={t="Slaying the Beast",lv=16,min=9,ot="Enter Ragefire Chasm and slay Taragaman the Hungerer, then bring his heart back to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.",st="The primary task set upon me by our great Warchief is to root out the creatures responsible for infesting our lord's great city with demonic influence. The Burning Blade is one threat, but there are others; the Searing Blade for instance, who make their home in Ragefire Chasm, secretly attempting to subvert innocent members of the Horde.$B$BIf they are to be stopped, then their leader must be slain--a Felguard named Taragaman the Hungerer.$B$BKill him, and his heart will appease Thrall, of this I'm sure.",how={{"loot",14540,{11520}}}},[5881]={t="Calling in the Reserves",lv=28,min=23,si=16189,ot="Maggran wishes you to deliver a letter to Grish Longrunner at the Great Lift in the Barrens.",st="The Horde does well keeping our troops fresh... since the Great War we have been prosperous here in Kalimdor.$B$BI need you to do me a favor, I have a lad by the name of Grish Longrunner protecting the Great Lift in the southern barrens. Give him this letter; the letter will let him know that I have a reserve warrior coming to relieve him of duty so that he can visit his family. He requested this sometime ago and he would be happy to hear the news."},[5922]={t="Moonglade",lv=10,min=10,nx=5930,ot="Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade.  When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.",st="All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade, tauren and night elf alike.  Keeper Remulos - Moonglade's guardian - keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there.  Now that you're learning the ways of the Claw, I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there.  Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.$B$BAs for your first lesson, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on.  Good luck, young druid."},[5928]={t="Heeding the Call",lv=10,min=10,ex={5926,5927},nx=5922,bc=5922,ot="Speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff.",st="Excuse me, friend...$B$BIt has come to my attention that Turak Runetotem has put out word that he wishes to speak with you.  It seems that your training as a druid is about to take on a new life, and he will be training you personally.  Turak is one of the Arch Druid's assistants; he is known as a wise and patient druid, and he should teach you well.$B$BHe is located in Thunder Bluff, inside the Cenarion Circle's main tent on the Elder Rise."},[5930]={t="Great Bear Spirit",lv=10,min=10,pre1={5922},nx=5932,ot="Seek out the Great Bear Spirit in northwestern Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the bear.  When finished, return to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven, Moonglade.",st="In the northwest part of Moonglade resides the home of a wise and noble being we call the Great Bear Spirit.  For all druids, it has served as a tutor and mentor into the first true natural understanding of the bear.  All druids at one point seek the spirit's wisdom, and you shall be no exception.$B$BGo to the Great Bear Spirit now and learn what it will teach.  When it is satisfied with you, return to me here in Nighthaven.  We will then see if you have truly taken account of the lessons it teaches.",how={{"talk",11956}}},[5932]={t="Back to Thunder Bluff",lv=10,min=10,pre1={5930},nx=6002,ot="Return to Thunder Bluff and speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise.",st="The time has come for us to part ways, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to whom that sent you to me.  Though the tauren are thought to be young in the ways of Cenarius, Turak Runetotem walks with much balance in the presence of nature.  Listen to his instructions, and you will soon complete your first lessons into your role as a protector of balance.$B$BGo now, young one.  We shall meet again."},[6002]={t="Body and Heart",lv=10,min=10,pre1={5932},si=15710,ot="Use the Cenarion Lunardust on the Moonkin Stone between Mulgore and the Barrens to bring forth Lunaclaw.  From there, you must face Lunaclaw and earn the strength of body and heart it possesses.$B$BSpeak with Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff when you are done.",st="On land west of Taurajo in the Barrens - just before it turns into Mulgore - lies a Moonkin Stone.  The moonkin are special beasts, not native to these parts.  Lunaclaw, the stone's defender, will face you when Cenarion Lunardust is applied to it.  Lunaclaw possesses within it a strength that you must use as one of the Claw.$B$BYou've earned the right to use this Cenarion Lunardust, $n... now show me that you've earned the right to possess the strength of body and the strength of heart needed as a druid!",how={{"talk",12144}}},[6061]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,nx=6087,si=15914,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame an Adult Plainstrider. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village.",st="As a tauren, it is important to follow the traditions of our ancestors by fighting mighty creatures. By besting these creatures, we are able to intake their spirits, allowing us to become closer to the Earthmother.$B$BIn the same way, taming a beast to fight alongside us helps us become one with nature around us. Eventually, you will learn to tame a beast of your choosing. But all things take practice, and you have much to learn. Begin by taking this taming rod; you must tame an adult plainstrider.",how={{"kill",2956}}},[6062]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,nx=6083,si=15917,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Dire Mottled Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Thotar in Razor Hill.",st="It is an admirable skill to command one's authority over nature. As a hunter, you must strive to learn to use the force and power inherent to any creature of your choosing.$B$BGaining control of an animal is not an easy feat; it is a task that you must undertake with much determination.$B$BFor your first assignment, take this taming rod and use it to tame a dire mottled boar. You can find them quite close to Razor Hill. Practice your skills in battle with the boar at your side, then return to me.",how={{"kill",3099}}},[6081]={t="Training the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6082},ot="Speak with Ormak Grimshot in Orgrimmar.",st="You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it.$B$BTravel to Orgrimmar. There you must speak to one of our most revered hunters, Ormak Grimshot. He will give you the ability to train your new pet. You will find him near the Hall of the Brave.$B$BGood luck, $n."},[6082]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6083},nx=6081,si=15920,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame an Armored Scorpid. Practice your skills, then return to Thotar at Razor Hill.",st="The final creature you need to tame is one you should strive to emulate; the armored scorpid. It strikes quickly and confidently; to control a force such as this is your fate as a hunter.$B$BWhen you return, I will bestow you with the skills you will need to tame an animal of your choosing; this creature will be yours to command. Under your control, your pet will gain experience alongside you. I will also show you how to call it and dismiss it as you wish.",how={{"kill",3126}}},[6083]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6062},nx=6082,si=15919,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Surf Crawler. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Thotar at Razor Hill.",st="The advantage a pet affords you against your rivals is duly noted, $n. When you gain control over another creature, you are adding to your own strength. Your pet must become an extension of yourself.$B$BThe next task requires you to turn from the land; you will find the next creature in the waters off the coast. Across from Sen'jin Village, near the Echo Isles. look for a spirited crab called the surf crawler. Use the taming rod to tame it, then practice your skills.",how={{"kill",3107}}},[6087]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6061},nx=6088,si=15915,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Prairie Stalker. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village.",st="You have a fiery spirit, hunter, readily awaiting your next challenge.$B$BYour next task is to gain the companionship of a wolf known as the prairie stalker. This creature is swift and fearless; in taking this beast as your pet, you must also take on these qualities.$B$BDuring a battle, you will learn how you and your pet will become a team. In the end you must work as one, muscle to muscle.$B$BHere is the taming rod, $n. Tame a prairie stalker and practice your skills.",how={{"kill",2959}}},[6088]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6087},nx=6089,si=15916,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Swoop. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village.",st="The final task that I have for you requires that you tame a creature that inhabits the sky. The swoop is a difficult opponent, but as your ally, you will acquire its sharp attacks and threatening presence.$B$BBy the will of the Earthmother, when you return I will bestow you with the skills you will need to tame an animal of your choosing to be your companion; this creature will face the challenges you face, and gain experience alongside you. I will also show you how to call it and dismiss it as you wish.",how={{"kill",2970}}},[6089]={t="Training the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6088},ot="Speak with Holt Thunderhorn on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff.",st="You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it.$B$BTravel to Thunder Bluff. There you must speak to one of our most revered hunters, Holt Thunderhorn. If he deems you worthy, he will give you the ability to train your new pet.$B$BHolt has bested the most powerful and feared beasts of Azeroth, and commands many strong creatures of his own. His ties to the Earthmother are strong, and you can learn much from him. Good luck, $n."},[6282]={t="Harpies Threaten",lv=26,min=18,nx=6283,ot="Maggran Earthbinder in Sun Rock Retreat wants you to slay 7 Bloodfury Harpies, 7 Bloodfury Ambushers, 7 Bloodfury Slayers and 7 Bloodfury Roguefeathers.",st="Tauren take pride as the protectors of these lands. Undoubtedly you can guess why I am alarmed with the number of harpies that dwell here in Stonetalon.$B$BThe Bloodfuries are the source of the increasing number of harpies in Kalimdor; they encroach upon all likes of life preventing the innocent from leaving their boundaries.$B$BI need you to cull the harpies, $n!",how={{"kill",4022},{"kill",4025},{"kill",4024},{"kill",4023}}},[6283]={t="Bloodfury Bloodline",lv=26,min=18,pre1={6282},ot="Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat wishes you to slay Bloodfury Ripper and bring her remains as proof of your deed.",st="Limiting the number of Bloodfury Harpies will not be enough. The only true cure for their disease would be to slay their leader, Bloodfury Ripper!$B$BShe is all but a queen to those filthy creatures. Slay her and their numbers will surely diminish.$B$BGo back into the Charred Vale and you will find her along the western hills. She will not be easy to vanquish, but the reward will be great.",how={{"loot",16190,{12579}}}},[6284]={t="Arachnophobia",lv=21,min=15,ot="Kill Besseleth and bring Besseleth's Fang to Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat.",st="Warning: Proceed into Sishir Canyon west of here at your own risk.$B$BBesseleth and her eight-legged children of the forest have claimed this canyon as their webbed lair.$B$BMaggran Earthbinder in Sun Rock Retreat has placed a bounty on Besseleth. Slay her and bring proof of your killing to Maggran; there you will receive your reward for disposing this eight-legged menace.",how={{"loot",16192,{11921}}}},[6301]={t="Cycle of Rebirth",lv=23,min=17,nx=6381,ot="Tammra Windfield at Sun Rock Retreat wants you to gather 10 Gaea Seeds.",st="Industrial greed and continuous war have wrecked the lands of Stonetalon. Only the blessings of the Earthmother can cure such injury.$B$B$n, I will require you to seek a special seed, the Gaea seed. They are only found here in Stonetalon Mountain, north of Sun Rock Retreat at Mirkfallon Lake, near the water's edge.$B$BOnce you bring me the seeds I will imbue them with shamanistic power to speed their growth.",how={{"open",16205,{177926}}}},[6321]={t="Supplying the Sepulcher",lv=10,min=10,nx=6323,si=16209,ot="Bring Podrig's Order to Karos Razok.",st="Executor Hadrec asked me to take stock of our equipment at the Sepulcher.  With the Scourge, and worse, lurking in the woods, he doesn't want the Deathguards to lack gear they might need.$B$BI found that we are, in general, well stocked, but we do need more weapons to replace those lost in the field.$B$BHere is a requisition order of what is needed, for the weapon dealer Gordon Wendham in the Undercity.  Take the order to our bat master, Karos Razok, and speak with him about transport to the Undercity."},[6322]={t="Michael Garrett",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6323},nx=6324,si=16210,ot="Bring Gordon's Crate to Michael Garrett.",st="I have placed the Sepulcher's supplies into this crate.  If you have already visited the Sepulcher and spoken with their bat master, then you may ride a bat back to him.$B$BSpeak with the Undercity's bat master, Michael Garrett.  He can provide you with a bat to the Sepulcher."},[6323]={t="Ride to the Undercity",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6321},nx=6322,si=16209,ot="Buy a bat ride to the Undercity from the bat master Karos Razok, then take Podrig's Order to Gordon Wendham in the Undercity.",st="One of my bats can take you to the Undercity, for a small fee.  Speak with me again when you are ready so that we may arrange your transport.$B$BYou will find Gordon Wendham in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity.  That is the same quarter where my bat will land."},[6324]={t="Return to Podrig",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6322},si=16210,ot="Buy a bat ride to the Sepulcher from the bat master Michael Garrett, then bring Gordon's Crate to Deathguard Podrig in the Sepulcher.",st="The bat master in the Sepulcher is Karos Razok.  If you have already met him, then I can give you a bat to fly back to him.$B$BOur bats will always fly to the Undercity, but to travel to more remote locales their rider must first visit the area and speak with its bat master.$B$BYou have met Karos in the Sepulcher, so you may now fly bats there.  Speak with me again when you are ready."},[6361]={t="A Bundle of Hides",lv=10,min=10,nx=6362,si=16282,ot="Bring the Bundle of Hides to the wind rider master Devrak in the Crossroads.",st="I have a bundle of hides from the animals of the Barrens, and must get them to Thunder Bluff.  A colleague there, Ahanu, will use the hides to create leather goods.$B$BWill you take the hides to him for me?$B$BThe quickest way to Thunder Bluff is on the back of a wind rider.  Bring the bundle of hides to Devrak, our wind rider master in the Crossroads, and speak to him about transport to Thunder Bluff."},[6362]={t="Ride to Thunder Bluff",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6361},nx=6363,si=16282,ot="Buy a wind rider to Thunder Bluff from the wind rider master Devrak, then bring the Bundle of Hides to Ahanu in Thunder Bluff.",st="For a small fee, I will give you a wind rider to Thunder Bluff.  There's no faster way to the city!$B$BIf that is acceptable, speak to me again when you are ready to go.$B$BIf you're taking those hides to Ahanu, then I think he's at Hewa's Armory, at the base of the wind rider tower in Thunder Bluff.  And that's right where you'll land!"},[6363]={t="Tal the Wind Rider Master",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6362},nx=6364,si=16283,ot="Bring Ahanu's Leather Goods to Tal in Thunder Bluff.",st="I have prepared leather goods for Jahan to sell at the Crossroads.  Will you bring them to him?$B$BIf you have already been to the Crossroads and spoken to their wind rider master, then you can fly one of our Thunder Bluff wind riders back to him.$B$BTake the leather goods to Tal, our wind rider master in Thunder Bluff, and speak with him to arrange transport to the Crossroads."},[6364]={t="Return to Jahan",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6363},si=16283,ot="Buy a wind rider to the Crossroads from the wind rider master Tal, then bring Ahanu's Leather Goods to Jahan Hawkwing.",st="In order to fly to a town, you must have already been there and spoken with the wind rider master of that town.  You have been to the Crossroads and spoken to their wind rider master Devrak, so for a small fee you can take a wind rider to him from here.$B$BSpeak with me again when you are ready.  Once at the Crossroads, you can then deliver the leather goods to Jahan Hawkwing."},[6365]={t="Meats to Orgrimmar",lv=10,min=10,nx=6384,si=16306,ot="Bring Zargh's Meats to Devrak in the Crossroads.",st="I have some choice cuts of meat that I want to send to a friend.  Her name is Gryshka, the innkeeper in Orgrimmar.  Will you deliver the meat for me?$B$BThe fastest way to Orgrimmar is on a wind rider.  Take the meats to the Crossroads wind rider master, Devrak, and speak with him about transport to Orgrimmar."},[6381]={t="New Life",lv=25,min=17,pre1={6301},si=16208,ot="Plant 10 Gaea Seeds in Gaea Dirt Mounds, and then return the remaining Enchanted Gaea Seeds to Tammra at Sun Rock Retreat.",st="As you have seen, $c, though the land is in pain, the cycle of life is a powerful thing. Now we must do our part help it along. You must plant these seeds at the center of the destruction, to the west, in the Charred Vale. Beware, for harpies and angry fire elementals still plague the scarred land.$B$B$n, take these enchanted Gaea seeds and plant them in fertile mounds of soil. The cycle of life must go on!",how={{"click",177929}}},[6382]={t="The Ashenvale Hunt",lv=20,min=20,pre1={882},ex={235,742},ot="Speak with Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.",st="Your strength impresses me, $c.  Your willingness to embrace the hunt gives me confidence that you could move on to bigger game... and bigger challenges.$B$BThe forests of Ashenvale represent a vast untamed wild that the Horde seeks to impose its own will upon, both politically and spiritually.  If you seek to prove yourself in an unproven land, seek the guidance of Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post.  The outpost is due north of the path leading from the Barrens."},[6383]={t="The Ashenvale Hunt",lv=20,min=20},[6384]={t="Ride to Orgrimmar",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6365},nx=6385,si=16306,ot="Buy a wind rider to Orgrimmar from the wind rider master Devrak, then bring Zargh's Meats to Gryshka in Orgrimmar.",st="For just a few coins I will have a wind rider bring you to Orgrimmar.  When you get there, you can take Zargh's Meats to Gryshka.  Her inn is in the Valley of Strength, not far from the Skytower, where my wind rider will drop you off.$B$BSpeak with me again when you are ready for the journey."},[6385]={t="Doras the Wind Rider Master",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6384},nx=6386,si=16307,ot="Bring Gryshka's Letter to Doras in Orgrimmar.",st="I've written a letter of thanks to Zargh.  Will you deliver it for me?  If you've already been to the Crossroads and spoken with their wind rider master, then you can fly a wind rider back there.$B$BTake my letter to Doras, the wind rider master of Orgrimmar, and speak with him about transport to the Crossroads."},[6386]={t="Return to the Crossroads",lv=10,min=10,pre1={6385},si=16307,ot="Buy a wind rider to the Crossroads from the wind rider master Doras, then bring Gryshka's Letter to Zargh at the Crossroads.",st="My wind riders are trained to fly to many different places, as long as you have already been to that place and spoken with the wind rider master there.$B$BYou have been to the Crossroads and spoken to their wind rider master Devrak, so now you can fly directly to him from here.  Once you're at the Crossroads, you can deliver Gryshka's letter to Zargh.$B$BSpeak with me when you are ready to go."},[6393]={t="Elemental War",lv=25,min=19,ot="Bring 10 Incendrites to Tsunaman at Sun Rock Retreat.",st="The Tribunal of the Tides has sent me to wage war on the fire elementals here in Stonetalon Mountain. Neptulon the Tidehunter, Lord of all water elementals, has taken a personal interest in seeing our fiery cousins extinguished.$B$B$n, you can help me gain favor with the Tribunal by destroying the fire elementals in Charred Vale. When destroyed, the fire elementals leave Incendrites. Return these to me and be rewarded.",how={{"loot",16312,{4037,4038,4036}}}},[6394]={t="Thazz'ril's Pick",lv=4,min=3,pre1={5441},ot="Bring Thazz'ril's Pick to Foreman Thazz'ril.",st="$n, you are a dependable $r.  Can I count on you for another task?$B$BSome time ago I was surveying the cave to the north for minerals, and I left my favorite pick behind.  When I later returned to retrieve it I found the cave was filled with vicious beasts!  Will you go into the cave, the Burning Blade Coven, and get my pick?$B$BI left it in a chamber with waterfalls.  My pick has a spell on it so you can see it in the dark, so you won't have to worry about finding it... just what's guarding it!",how={{"open",16332,{178087}}}},[6395]={t="Marla's Last Wish",lv=5,min=3,pre1={376},ot="Bring Samuel Fipps' Remains to Marla's Grave, then return to Novice Elreth.",st="My friend Marla Fipps lived with her husband Samuel before the plague, but when the plague came Samuel succumbed and joined the Scourge's ranks.$B$BMarla was spared an undeath only to die at the hands of her now mindless husband.  So strong was her love, however, that her last dying wish was to be buried with her beloved Samuel.$B$BSamuel Fipps roams at a ruined camp along the road northeast of Deathknell.  Defeat him and grant Marla's wish: bury him at her grave, in the first row of our graveyard.",how={{"click",178090}}},[6401]={t="Kaya's Alive",lv=18,min=12,pre1={6523},ot="Tell Tammra Windfield in Sun Rock Retreat the good news.",st="Tell Tammra Windfield, Kaya's aunt who's at Sun Rock Retreat, about the good news! Kaya is alive! We had thought she was lost after the brutal attack on our village. Follow the path to the west to get to Sun Rock Retreat."},[6421]={t="Boulderslide Ravine",lv=18,min=14,nx=6481,ot="Explore deep into the cave at Boulderslide Ravine and bring back 10 Resonite Crystals for Mor'rogal at Sun Rock Retreat to investigate.",st="Something is amiss here in Stonetalon. Can you feel the tension in the air, $n?$B$BSoutheast of here lies a deep cave in Boulderslide Ravine. The kobolds there are frantically mining a rare crystal called Resonite. I need you to bring back some ore samples so that I can understand what's happening in that cave.  I also need you to investigate the depth of that cave.$B$BGo young $c, it's imperative I know what evil lurks under these mountains.",how={{"open",16581,{178105,178104,178106}}}},[6441]={t="Satyr Horns",lv=26,min=21,ot="Collect 16 Satyr Horns for Pixel in Splintertree Post.",st="Heya! I've been traveling through Ashenvale, heading towards Ratchet, and decided to make a stop here at Splintertree. I'm always looking for an opportunity, and it seems that satyr horns are in high demand in Ratchet these days.$B$BAfter asking around here, it seems that the satyrs in Night Run, Satyrnaar, and Xavian all have the type of horns I am looking for. I'm no match for those satyrs... but you look like you might be!$B$BTell you what, you collect the horns for me and I'll make it worth your time.",how={{"loot",5481,{3759,3763,3762}}}},[6442]={t="Naga at the Zoram Strand",lv=19,min=14,ot="Bring 20 Wrathtail Heads to Marukai along the Zoram Strand.",st="There is evil lurking here along the coast, $r.$B$BIt is the resting place of the doomed city of Zoram, long destroyed and submerged beneath the seas.  Lost, and nearly forgotten.$B$BNow, the naga have returned, and for what reason we do not know.  But reason matters little; we must defend the land we have worked so hard to claim as our own.$B$BReturn to me with 20 of their heads! Throw the naga back to the depths!",how={{"loot",5490,{3713,3715,3717}}}},[6461]={t="Blood Feeders",lv=19,min=13,ot="Xen'zilla at Malaka'Jin needs you to kill 10 Deepmoss Creepers and 7 Deepmoss Venomspitters.",st="We Trolls here at Malaka'Jin have prospered from the land; Stonetalon Mountain offers great hunting for us to live on.$B$BLately, we have attracted the wrong dinner guests... the spiders in these mountains have been raiding our camps at night looking to steal our hunt.$B$BIf you were to help us kill off these ghastly beasts we at Malaka'Jin would be in your debt. Spiders are everywhere in Stonetalon - just head north from here and you will see what I am talking about.",how={{"kill",4005},{"kill",4007}}},[6462]={t="Troll Charm",lv=24,min=19,ot="Bring 8 Troll Charms to Mitsuwa at the Zoram'gar Outpost.",st="My kinfolk were traveling here with many sacred troll charms, but the Thistlefur furbolgs attacked and killed them before they reached Zoram'gar!  Those vile Furbolgs!$B$BI miss my brothers and sisters who were killed, but we will meet again in the afterlife.  However, their troll charms hold great value in this world.  It is an outrage that the furbolgs have them!$B$B$n, you must retrieve the charms!  They are in chests in Thistlefur Hold, a cave at the end of Thistlefur Village, north of Astranaar.",how={{"open",16602,{178144}}}},[6481]={t="Earthen Arise",lv=20,min=14,pre1={6421},si=16603,ot="Open the Resonite cask with the Enchanted Resonite Crystal, and then slay Goggeroc. Return to Mor'rogal with the news and Enchanted Resonite Crystal.",st="You have uncovered a dark threat to the land, $c. The Resonite cask you have found in that cave houses a slumbering Earthen by the name of Goggeroc.$B$BI have changed the mixture of the Resonite crystals that you gathered with my shamanistic powers. Take the enchanted Resonite crystal and smash open the Resonite cask, which houses the Earthen.$B$BWhen awakened, Goggeroc will be weakened... Slay him, $n!",how={{"kill",11920}}},[6482]={t="Freedom to Ruul",lv=24,min=19,ne=1,ot="Escort Ruul, then speak with Yama Snowhoof in Spintertree Post.",st="Eh?  Who are you?$B$B$n?  You're no furbolg.  They are cursed!  They thought I was a bear and captured me, and now they starve me!  My strength is failing...$B$BHelp me escape, then speak with my sister Yama at the Splintertree Post to the east.$B$B$n! I must escape!"},[6503]={t="Ashenvale Outrunners",lv=24,min=19,ot="Kill 9 Ashenvale Outrunners, then return to Kuray'bin at Splintertree Outpost.",st="We received reports that Ashenvale outrunners left Silverwing Outpost not long ago, and now sneak near our territories in the forest.  We don't want them gathering intelligence on our defenses!$B$BSneak through the forests south of our post here and east of the Alliance outpost of Silverwing.  Find and slay the outrunners, then return to me.",how={{"kill",12856}}},[6522]={t="An Unholy Alliance",lv=36,min=28,nx=6521,si=17008,ot="Take the Small Scroll to Varimathras in the Undercity.",st="My Lady,$B$BYou know very well what it is we are offering. The opportunity for you to take the Barrens and the lands beyond is a great one. We simply want your aid in return. By aid we mean nothing more than your giving us the freedom to take action in the area.$B$BPlease, allow us to discuss this further. We have great power and are willing to share with those wise enough to join us. I will remain outside Razorfen Downs for the time being.$B$BBest Regards,$BAmbassador Malcin"},[6523]={t="Protect Kaya",lv=18,min=12,nx=6401,ne=1,ot="Escort Kaya Flathoof to Camp Aparaje, and then return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.",st="Thank you for rescuing me! We must leave quickly before they discover that I am free. Please escort me to Camp Aparaje. From there, I know my way.$b$bMy father, Makaba Flathoof, will be desperate to know that I am safe."},[6541]={t="Report to Kadrak",lv=19,min=17,nx=6543,bc=6543,ot="Report to Kadrak at the watch tower in northern Barrens.",st="Have you ever been to Ashenvale, to the north? The horde has recently set up an outpost on the Zoram Strand there, and we can always use some new recruits to help defend our new fronts.$B$BIf you think you are up to it, see Kadrak in the northern Barrens, at the watch tower. He is heading up the Ashenvale campaign and can give you further orders."},[6543]={t="The Warsong Reports",lv=19,min=17,si=16783,ot="Open the Bundle of Reports.  Take the Warsong Reports to the Warsong Scout, Warsong Runner, and Warsong Outrider. Bring back the updates they give you to Kadrak at the northern watch tower in the barrens.",st="I recently deployed a few scouts into Ashenvale and I need a runner to take them their orders, and bring me back a report of what they have observed.$B$BYour first stop should be the Zoram'gar Outpost, along the coast to the west, at the Zoram Strand, to locate the first runner. You also need to stop at Splintertree Post, to the north, and along the road to the east, near Azshara. You will find a scout and an outrider there.$B$BGive them each a report, and from them, get an update on their findings.",how={{"buy",16764,{12862}},{"buy",16763,{12863}},{"buy",16765,{12864}}}},[6544]={t="Torek's Assault",lv=24,min=20,ne=1,ot="Escort Torek on his attack against Silverwing Outpost and Duriel Moonfire, then report to Ertog Ragetusk at Splintertree Post.",st="Hey!  $C!  Come here!$B$BMy raiders and I are about to attack the Silverwing Outpost to the west.  Our target is its leader, Duriel Moonfire.  Scouts report the outpost is defended heavily with sentinels and warriors.  The battle will be glorious!$B$BDo you want to share in the glory, $n, and aid us?  If so, then when it's over you can report our success to my superior, Ertog Ragetusk in Splintertree.$B$BWhat do you say.  Are you with us?",how={{"kill",12860},{"kill",12896},{"kill",12897}}},[6548]={t="Avenge My Village",lv=18,min=12,nx=6629,ot="Kill 8 Grimtotem Ruffians and 6 Grimtotem Mercenaries, and then return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.",st="The Grimtotem Clan raided my village and killed most everyone. I killed all I could, but barely escaped with my life.$b$b$n, all I wish now is that more of them are dead. You will find them just to the west of here.",how={{"kill",11910},{"kill",11911}}},[6561]={t="Blackfathom Villainy",lv=27,min=18,ot="Bring the head of Twilight Lord Kelris to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.",st="Strength has left me. Your help is needed!$b$bLong ago this site was a great temple of Elune. But misfortune led to ruin when the corruption of an Old God seeped up from beneath the earth and tainted the sacred Moon Well.$b$bAku'Mai, servant of the Old God, rose from the waters.$b$bThe Twilight's Hammer cultists have allied with the naga to occupy these grounds. The cultists, led by Kelris, sacrifice innocents to Aku'Mai for power.$b$bSlay Kelris and bring his head to Bashana in Thunder Bluff, $n, please.",how={{"loot",5881,{4832}}}},[6562]={t="Trouble in the Deeps",lv=22,min=17,nx=6563,bc=6563,ot="Speak to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.",st="Je'neu Sancrea is in need of aid. He is at the Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale. The Night elf forest is to the north of the Stonetalon mountains. You can reach it by traveling through Windshear Crag or by heading north through Barrens. Zoram Strand is far to the west of the forest. Be careful, $n. There are forces there that will not take to your presence kindly."},[6563]={t="The Essence of Aku'Mai",lv=22,min=17,pre={6562},ot="Bring 20 Sapphires of Aku'Mai to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.",st="Within the beginning tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps, large sapphire clusters can be found along the cave walls. Recently it was noted that the naga were harvesting the crystals. Until it can be discerned why, I sense we should stop the naga from succeeding. The crystals have great elemental power and if used inappropriately, could make for a powerful arcane component.$B$BWill you help me, $n? Blackfathom Deeps can be found along Zoram Strand to the north of our outpost.",how={{"open",16784,{178186,178184,178185}}}},[6564]={t="Allegiance to the Old Gods",lv=22,min=17,pre1={6562},nx=6565,si=16790,ot="Bring the Damp Note to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.",st="Some poor handwriting is scrawled on the crumpled up note:$B$B\"Yes, tell all the priestesses to bring the crystals to me. The water elemental spirits are strong within them and they will aid our aquamancers greatly in their own summonings.$B$BBy controlling the power within the crystals, we will appease Aku'Mai. One day we will have enough power to bring Aku'Mai back to us and the world will return to its greatest era! An era of rule by the Old Gods!\""},[6565]={t="Allegiance to the Old Gods",lv=26,min=17,pre1={6564},ot="Kill Lorgus Jett in Blackfathom Deeps and then return to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.",st="This Twilight's Hammer follower cannot be allowed to complete his plan. The Twilight's Hammer do not understand the spirits of nature. They believe in the Old Gods--creatures of chaos and destruction that were long ago defeated. This Lorgus cannot be allowed to succeed. You must stop him, $n. I cannot do it myself--I am too weak.$B$BGo into Blackfathom Deeps, find him, and kill him. Return to me here at Zoram'gar when it's done.",how={{"kill",12902}}},[6607]={t="Nat Pagle, Angler Extreme",lv=45,min=35,ot="Nat Pagle wants you to catch the following fish:  Misty Reed Mahi Mahi from the Misty Reed Strand in the Swamp of Sorrows.  A Sar'theris Striker from the Sar'theris Strand in Desolace.  Feralas Ahi from the Verdantis River of Feralas.  Savage Coast Blue Sailfin from the Savage Coast of Stranglethorn Vale.  Return to Nat Pagle when you have reeled them all in!",how={{"open",16967,{400006}},{"open",16970,{400007}},{"open",16968,{400008}},{"open",16969,{400009}}}},[6629]={t="Kill Grundig Darkcloud",lv=18,min=12,pre1={6548},ot="Kill Grundig Darkcloud and 6 Grimtotem Brutes, and return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.",st="$n, you've done a fine job killing Grimtotem. If you dare, Grundig Darkcloud and his personal band of brutes is by far the worst of the lot. He was the one who led the brutal attack on my village.$b$bYou will find him in Grimtotem Post a bit further up the path to the west. Kill him, and I will be forever grateful.",how={{"kill",11858},{"kill",11912}}},[6641]={t="Vorsha the Lasher",lv=23,min=20,ne=1,ot="Keep Muglash safe as he travels to the brazier. Help him by putting the brazier out, then protect him as you fight against the Naga.$B$BIf you are successful, return to the Zoram'gar Outpost and inform the Warsong Runner of the death of Vorsha the Lasher.",st="Vorsha the Lasher... the fiendish hydra that roams the seas...$B$BShe has attacked our outpost, each time unprovoked, laying waste to anything that falls in her path.$B$BBut I am ready, $n. I have prepared to best the hydra and end these attacks on Zoram'gar.$B$BThe naga honor the wicked nature of this beast with a brazier that remains lit on an island just off the coast. I believe that if we put it out, Vorsha will appear in anger.$B$BWe will need help, so be sure to bring some strong allies.",how={{"kill",12940}}},[6921]={t="Amongst the Ruins",lv=27,min=21,ot="Bring the Fathom Core to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.",st="The Twilight's Hammer has moved into the Moonshrine Ruins of Blackfathom Deeps.  Their presence can only serve to coerce the elements into working against us.  If left unchecked, this region will be theirs for good.$B$B$n, go into Blackfathom and find the ruin's fathom stone; it should be somewhere close in the water.  In it is a fathom core - a device that when properly read it will relate a history of all elemental activity.  If I have it, I and the Earthen Ring can maybe do something to stop them!",how={{"open",16762,{177964}}}},[6922]={t="Baron Aquanis",lv=30,min=21,si=16782,ot="Bring the Strange Water Globe to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.",st="The defeated water elemental has left behind a strange water globe.  You surmise that the object somehow fed the beast energy.  Inside the globe, a putrid-looking form of water sloshes about.  The globe itself seems impervious to any sort of physical force.$B$BIf anyone can make any sense of this item, it would be Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring.  He is located at the Horde's Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale."},[6981]={t="The Glowing Shard",lv=26,min=15,si=10441,ot="Travel to Ratchet to find someone that can tell you more about the glowing shard.$B$BThen, deliver the shard as you are directed.",st="The shard is a brilliant green, and although solid, what looks like smoke swirls just below the surface. You can't help staring into the depths of the crystal; at the same time, you know there is something very disturbing about it.$B$BMaybe you should see if anyone in Ratchet can tell you more about this strange shard.",how={{"talk",3442}}},[65601]={t="Love Hurts",lv=20,min=20,pre1={1507},ex={1472},nx=65610,ot="Speak with Magar in Orgrimmar.",st="A sayaad male is known as an incubus. A creature of profound evil and singular mind.\r\n\r\nThe demon must be lured into our world with an item of enticement - an object that represents great love and devotion.\r\n\r\nIf you trust a blind man to lead you, $n, then listen. East from the Cleft of Shadow, along the main drag of Orgrimmar, lives Magar. He longs for the return of his mate, Krilge.\r\n\r\nSeek him out. He'll ask you to search for something precious. That is the key which you must bring to Gan'rul."},[65604]={t="The Binding",lv=20,min=20,pre1={65610},ex={1472},ot="Using the Withered Scarf, summon and subdue an incubus, then return the Withered Scarf to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.",st="Yes... I see. I feel the residual emotions bound within these threads. Love is woven into its stitches. The incubus will not be able to resist.\r\n\r\nTake this to the summoning circle in Neeru's tent, $n. Summon forth a malevolent incubus, then show it your mastery. Do not expect it to be subdued quietly. Ready your magic and prepare yourself for a fight. Underestimating a demon has been many a warlock's final mistake.\r\n\r\nWhen you have defeated it, return the cloth to me. I will let Magar know what you found.",how={{"kill",185335}}},[65610]={t="Wish You Were Here",lv=27,min=20,pre1={65601},ex={1472},nx=65604,ot="Investigate Fallen Sky Lake in Ashenvale and report your findings to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.",st="I met Krilge while making Mooncloth in Ashenvale. He was stationed there to protect civilians from danger, until he disappeared...\r\n\r\nThey've stopped looking for him and consider him a deserter, but I don't believe it.\r\n\r\nWe would often meet at Fallen Sky Lake before it became overrun by those aggressive bog beasts.\r\n\r\nI'm not typically one to ask favors, but if you could go to Ashenvale and look for any sign of him, I'd appreciate it.",how={{"loot",190232,{3782,3784,3931}}}},[76156]={t="Stalk With The Earthmother",lv=10,min=4,nx=76160,si=206159,ot="Sneak into the Venture Company mine southeast of Thunder Bluff and collect 5 Seaforium Mining Charges from carts of blasting supplies, then return them to Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff.",st="I sense in you a hidden talent for the subtle arts, $c. Use this mask to infiltrate the nearby Venture Company mine and steal their supplies. It may not seem like a convincing disguise, but a skilled rogue can slip past any guard with naught but a winning smile and a cunning distraction. I believe this capability lies within you as well.",how={{"open",206157,{403041}}}},[76160]={t="Stalk With The Earthmother",lv=11,min=4,pre1={76156},pre={76156},nx=76240,si=206176,ot="Gather 8 Windfury Cones north of Thunder Bluff, use them with the Mortar and Pestle, then return to Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff with the result.",st="Maybe your skills lie with poisons, not disguises. The Harpies to the north nest in a tree which produces a resin of potent toxicity. Gather the fallen cones around the nests, then crush them into a salve. When applied to a blade this salve will sear your opponent's wounds into their flesh and turn their blood to salt.",how={{"loot",206175}}},[76240]={t="Stalk With The Earthmother",lv=11,min=4,pre1={76160},pre={76160},si=206344,ot="Buy or catch a Raw Brilliant Smallfish, then use the Knife Set to fillet it in front of Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff.",st="I have one last idea that may lead us to success. I still feel there is hidden talent in you, but let us try and coax it out with a less direct approach.\r\n\r\nGo and procure a Raw Brilliant Smallfish, then bring it back here. Use these daggers to clean and fillet it. Do not think too hard - do what comes naturally.",how={{"loot",206345}}},[79360]={t="Elemental Aid",lv=33,min=30,pre1={1531,1532,96136},ot="Defeat Charlga Razorflank in Razorfen Kraul and collect information on the quilboar's plans.",st="Now that you have mastered the elements, you have an obligation to them, and thus to all of Azeroth herself. We call to them for aid, we do not demand their power. It is time you return the favors granted to you. And I think I know how.\r\n\r\nThe quilboar twist the elements for their own ends, and seem to be extending their reach within these borders. Go into their kraul and put an end to whatever they scheme. These lands must be protected.",how={{"loot",274463,{4421}}}},[79364]={t="Eyes on the Sky",lv=33,min=30,pre={79360},ot="Speak with Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.",st="The note you found says the Razormane have burrowed into the Thousand Needles for some sort of unseen ritual. Raging storms and rising tides...\r\n\r\nThe quilboar must be using some cruel sorcery they learned from Hirzek, a shaman who went to great lengths to twist the elements. If they plan to flood the canyon, this would require devastating elemental powers.\r\n\r\nWe are ill equipped to deal with this, but a powerful shaman like you must have an idea. Return to your allies and see if you can't find an answer."},[86576]={t="Bloodfury Trinkets",lv=26,min=18,ot="Bring $1oa Glittering Sunstones to Mor'rogal.",st="In addition to spreading their filth across the Charred Vale, the Bloodfury harpies gather anything shiny that they can find. I'm told that they collect a variety of golden-yellow sunstones for decoration. I have no use for such trinkets, but Mor'rogal has mentioned using them before.\r\n\r\nWhile you're fighting the harpies of the Vale, keep your eye out for Glittering Sunstones. Bring any that you find to Mor'rogal, up on the hills above us.",how={{"loot",277936,{4022,4025,4026}}}},[86784]={t="Sticks and Bones",lv=7,min=4,si=279937,ot="Collect $1oa Dry Branches and bring them to Eleanor Shackleton.",st="My associate Eleanor Shackleton prides herself on traveling the wilds, surviving against weather and monsters. She is currently camped not far from here, in the hills to the west, and I remember a piece of advice that she once gave me: \"When you think you have enough firewood, gather five times more.\"\r\n\r\nIf you have some spare time, you could collect some wood in this basket and take it to her camp. I'm sure she could give you a few tips about the existence of a traveling adventurer.",how={{"open",279991,{671154}}}},[90902]={t="Rediscovering the Light",lv=2,min=2,pre1={364},ot="Heal $1oa Injured Deathguard with your Holy Light ability.",st="I am proud to welcome another newly risen paladin to our ranks. As you begin to reconnect with the light you may notice that certain abilities that were once second nature to you may cause you considerable pain to use now, particularly those involving channeling the light to heal yourself or others. \r\n\r\nThe only way around this problem is--unfortunately--to go through it. Like any other muscle that has atrophied, you must push through the pain and exercise the flesh for it to return to full function.",how={{"talk",259377}}},[91208]={t="Coming to Terms",lv=4,min=4,pre1={90902},ot="Find the Frightened Paladin in Deathknell.",st="Not all of our fellow Paladins who rise again are quick to acclimate to our new reality. Some struggle to reconcile that they are now, in a way, the very thing they spent their lives fighting against.\r\n\r\nThese individuals often simply need a kind gesture and a sympathetic ear. Unfortunately, many others are quick to turn violent. Find the frightened paladin who fled into the hills directly west of this chapel. Extend a hand in friendship. Lead them back into the light if you can.",how={{"talk",246143}}},[91209]={t="Continue Your Training",lv=4,min=4,ot="Follow the road east out of Deathknell to find the town of Brill. Report to Shari Stilwell to continue your training.",st="Lordaeron may not be what it used to be, but our home still needs protection from all manner of threats and it's time for you to go out and face the world. Your next stop should be the town of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades. Go and meet with Shari Stilwell there. She can see to your continued training. \r\n\r\nOne last bit of advice before you go--take extra care as a paladin traveling through Forsaken lands. There are many in the Dark Lady's service who distrust us and our proximity to the light."},[91282]={t="A Second Home",lv=11,min=8,ot="Find the fortress of Bandarion Keep and report to Breton Samuels there.",st="It is encouraging to see my newly risen brothers and sisters thrive as you have. It is only through community and shared faith that we can truly realize our full potential however, and to that end we've begun to form a new paladin order right here in Tirisfal. \r\n\r\nIf you wish to learn more, you should visit our monastery on the edge of the Whispering Woods. It is called Bandarion Keep. It's on the bluffs just northwest of the Solliden Farmstead, and should be hard to miss."},[91285]={t="Murlocs at the Gates",lv=11,min=7,pre={91282},ot="Slay $1oa Vile Fin Attackers and $2oa Vile Fin Seers and report back to Breton Samuels when it is done.",st="Normally we'd show our newcomers a bit more hospitality, but we've got a bit of a murloc problem at the moment.\r\n\r\nA tribe of murlocs used to use the keep as their spawning grounds. They've been a problem since we moved in and kicked them out, but now it's starting to get out of hand. You look like you've seen some action. Do you think you could help us drive back some of these pests? You'll find them lurking in the bluffs along the road to the east, and in the camps around the lake to the west.",how={{"kill",250283},{"kill",250282}}},[91294]={t="Touring the Grounds",lv=11,min=8,pre1={91285},ot="Speak to the residents of Bandarion Keep.",st="Now that the immediate threat of the murloc attacks is under control, I'd encourage you to show yourself around our stronghold. It isn't much yet, but it's home.\r\n\r\nWhen you are done exploring, seek out Danitha Morr, our leader. She can help you get settled in.\r\n\r\nI'm very glad to have met you, $n. May the light be your guide.",how={{"talk",246389},{"talk",246393},{"talk",246394},{"talk",246378}}},[91316]={t="Making Repairs",lv=11,min=8,pre1={91294},ot="Collect 12 pieces of Sturdy Lumber from Shadowvale in Tirisfal Glades.",st="This far from the Undercity, logistics are challenging and we have a dire shortage of building materials needed to help restore this fortress. I'd like your help with that.\r\n\r\nThe ruined village of Shadowvale can be found in the Whispering Forest, just southwest of here. One of the buildings has an old root cellar used to store all sorts of things. There are likely to be usable materials down there. Scavenge what you can and return to us.",how={{"open",246213,{554626}}}},[91317]={t="The Tarnished",lv=12,min=9,pre1={91294},ot="Slay 8 Tarnished Drudges, 6 Tarnished Zealots, and collect the head of Commander Rudolph Gelhardt in Tirisfal Glades.",st="Not all risen paladins have acclimated well to our new existence, as you may have seen yourself already. Some have carried forward their prejudices from life, and continue to visit violence upon their fellow Forsaken.\r\n\r\nAs it stands we are mistrusted by our people who remember well the persecution inflicted by the living in the name of the light, and these attacks do not help. A number of these tarnished have taken up residence at Shadowvale to the southwest. End them and bring me their leader's head.",how={{"loot",270435,{259431}},{"kill",259434},{"kill",259433}}},[91858]={t="Diplomatic Incident",lv=22,min=18,nx=91859,ot="Travel to The Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest and speak with Trevan Rol about the missing Earthen Ring travelers.",st="A most unfortunate turn of events in Silverpine has presented a unique opportunity for us to prove our worth in the eyes of the horde.\r\n\r\nA pair of dignitaries from the Earthen Ring went missing in Silverpine Forest en route to Tarren Mill. We don't know much else but rumors say that this is becoming quite the diplomatic incident. If we can recover these missing persons, it could help gain us the legitimacy we so dearly need.\r\n\r\nWe have a man at The Sepulcher, Trevan Rol. Travel there and speak with him."},[91859]={t="A Curious Pair",lv=22,min=18,pre1={91858},pre={91858},nx=91860,ot="Speak with Deathguard Baldren about the mysterious Earthen Ring travelers who recently passed through The Sepulcher.",st="Cutting straight to it, these \"dignitaries\" are no ordinary diplomats. One was a Tauren. Ordinary enough for the Earthen Ring, but the other--and you'll scarcely believe this--was an elf. A *high* elf. They were cloaked, but I've seen quel'dorei before and I'd bet my good pinky finger that's what I saw.\r\n\r\nWhy was an elf accompanying a Tauren through horde territory? Well, your guess is as good as mine. That's as much as I know, so I'd suggest speaking with Deathguard Baldren near the entrance to town."},[91860]={t="A Grim Fate",lv=22,min=18,pre1={91859},pre={91859},nx=91861,ot="Investigate Fenris Isle to the east and learn the fate of the Earthen Ring traveling party.",st="Out on patrol last night I spotted a group of gnolls dumping a very large body onto a pyre on the shores of Fenris Isle. I didn't see an elf or any smaller corpses, but I'd say this doesn't bode well for them.\r\n\r\nIf you are brave or stupid you are welcome to charge into Fenris Isle to learn more, but if you ask me, it's a lot of work to find some snooty elf that's probably long dead.\r\n\r\nI know you paladins love swearing oaths and taking on lost causes, but this one isn't worth it. Trust me.",how={{"click",566037}}},[91861]={t="Into Fenris Keep",lv=22,min=18,pre1={91860},pre={91860},nx=91862,ot="Investigate Fenris Keep to the north and attempt to locate the missing member of the Earthen Ring party.",st="<The fact that you found only one body is a hopeful sign. Perhaps the High Elf that Trevan and Hadrec described is still alive somewhere deeper inside the nearby fortress?>"},[91862]={t="Lumina Windsinger",lv=22,min=18,pre1={91861},pre={91861},nx=96204,ot="Retrieve the Fenris Isle Key from the Rot Hide Gnolls and use it to free Lumina Windsinger.",st="Quel'dorei? No, I am no \"quel'dorei\". I am Lumina Windsinger and I am shen'dorei. One of the Windshaper Skyborne.\r\n\r\nI came to these lands as a guest of the Earthen Ring. My companion Banon and I were passing through Silverpine to reach the Arathi Highlands so that we could study the elemental convergences there. Clearly, we didn't make it.\r\n\r\nWe have no time for this now though. Kill the gnolls nearby. Retrieve the key to this cage and free me. I will tell you the rest once we are safely away.",how={{"loot",267412,{1942,1943,1944}}}},[91920]={t="Wild Eyes",lv=11,min=10,pre1={430},nx=91921,ot="Gather 3 murloc eyes and bring them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",st="I wouldn't dare to question the effectiveness of Apothecary Renferrel's formulae, however I would be lying if I said that the potion made any noticeable difference.\r\n\r\nAlong the shore of Lake Lordamere are a swarm of murlocs, and of note, murlocs have eyes. I suspect the apothecary's willingness to try new things is suppressed by his recent obsession with hearts. Bring him a few.\r\n\r\nIf my choice is to inevitably die a second death or have Renferrel kill me for questioning his methods, I choose the latter.",how={{"loot",730,{1767}}}},[91921]={t="Return to Quinn (Again)",lv=11,min=10,pre1={91920},nx=425,si=248930,ot="Bring Quinn's potion to Quinn Yorick at the Ivar Patch, north of the Sepulcher.",st="Here is the new potion to aid in Quinn's recovery, made with love extracted from six whole hearts.\r\n\r\nNow, please excuse me before your presence necessitates more paperwork."},[92401]={t="A Frightened Request",lv=22,min=15,ot="Investigate the disappearance of Edward Heartweaver in the Ruins of Lordaeron.",st="It's my husband Edward...\r\n\r\nHe has not returned from his weekly journey to the graveyard in the Lordaeron ruins. Our son was lost when Arthas razed the city, and my dear Edward is still filled with guilt and sorrow that we never found his body. I've tried to warn him against searching those overrun ruins, but he refuses to give up. I try not to worry, but it's been days.\r\n\r\nThere are things there I cannot contend with but if you are willing, I need to know the fate of my husband."},[92421]={t="Light's Justice",lv=22,min=15,ot="Collect $1oa Intact Limbs within The Ruins of Lordaeron for Morbin Lightbane in the Undercity.",st="As a paladin of the Forsaken, it is my duty to exact the will of our Dark Lady while tending to our people's needs. We are fortunate with an opportunity to accomplish both.\r\n\r\nAbove the Undercity, the scourge still roam unchecked in great numbers. Our forces dwindle trying to reclaim our land, and decaying flesh cannot be reknit. Not without replacements.\r\n\r\nWould that our glorious captain Garek Bandarion still be with us, I know what he would wish. To finish what he started and heal our kin. For Lordaeron!",how={{"loot",268580,{250618,250621,250622}}}},[92422]={t="The Wrath of Rath'mael",lv=22,min=15,pre1={99156},ot="Kill Rath'mael in the Ruins of Lordaeron for Deathguard Kristof in Brill.",st="Reports have come in from the Lordamere Overlook deep within the Ruins of Lordaeron. An unholy fog has taken over the streets and graveyard, affording the scourge up there some measure of stealth. \r\n\r\nOur scouts indicate they're being conjured by a new power within their ranks, a necromancer known as Rath'mael. We do not have the luxury of waiting this one out, $n.\r\n\r\nIf you have allies, summon them and their aid to the Forsaken. Drive this creature out of our lands.",how={{"kill",250657}}},[92434]={t="Blood in the Streets",lv=34,min=30,pre1={545,93680},pre={544,93680},si=279469,ot="Find a way into Dalaran along the Lordamere Lake.",st="Whatever caused Dalaran's barrier to lower has left the city in turmoil. With you having dealt with their patrols, there is no better time than now to make our way inside and discover their secrets.\r\n\r\nTake the key you found at the internment camp and seek out their sewers along the northern border of the city. With luck, those mages had no reason to put a ward over such a... disagreeable point of entry."},[92460]={t="Coming of Age",lv=1,min=1,nx=92461,ot="Speak with Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.",st="Look at you, bright eyed and ready for adventure! We need all the help we can get here in Thendal Village and your arrival is most welcome. I imagine you are brimming with nerves for what is to come. After all, you only get to come of age once in a lifetime.\r\n\r\nGo, seek out our village leader Rorian the Dayseeker at the entrance to the greatfather tree just west of here. He will get you started on your journey."},[92461]={t="Harmony in Balance",lv=1,min=1,pre1={92460},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Slay 8 Vuldren Juveniles in Thendal Grove.",st="We live in times of great uncertainty for our people. We face unprecedented challenges that may require bold solutions, but we also must contend with the ordinary and mundane here in Thendal Grove. Take, for example, the recent unsustainable rise in the vuldren population.\r\n\r\nThe vuldren are a vital part of our ecosystem. However, imbalances must be corrected to maintain the delicate harmony that all creatures in Thendal Grove share.\r\n\r\nHead east and cull some of the vuldren there.",how={{"kill",250873}}},[92462]={t="Infestation Investigation",lv=2,min=1,pre1={92460},nx=92463,ot="Slay 8 Pesky Cirrusflies in Thendal Grove.",st="One of our rangers recently reported an infestation of cirrusflies here in Thendal Grove. \r\n\r\nCirrusflies can be dangerous if the swarm is allowed to grow too large, so please head to the eastern end of the Grove and exterminate as many as you can.",how={{"kill",251169}}},[92463]={t="The Cirrusfly Queen",lv=3,min=2,pre1={92462},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[7]=3,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Destroy the Cirrusfly Queen in Thendal Grove.",st="If the forest is as thick with these insects as it sounds, simply killing the workers won't be enough.\r\n\r\nGo deeper into the forest and find the queen. She'll be close to the hive and surrounded by bigger and more aggressive soldiers, so be careful.\r\n\r\nPut her down and return here when it's done. That'll be one less problem to think about around here.",how={{"kill",251404}}},[92464]={t="Elemental Unrest",lv=3,min=2,pre={92461},ot="Speak to Yala Windwatcher in Thendal Grove.",st="Ever since our elemental benefactors left us, it seems that we are simply moving from one unrest to another. The problem we face now is that the manifestations of the winds near the standing stones to the northeast are agitated.\r\n\r\nNot truly self-aware like the sentient wind spirits that once lived here, these simple sprites respond in kind to forces, emotions, and intentions of the creatures around them. \r\n\r\nMy apprentice Yala Windwatcher went to observe them. Seek her out and discover what she's learned."},[92465]={t="Agitators",lv=3,min=2,pre={92464},nx=92469,ot="Slay $2oa Roiling Winds and $1oa Al'Aketh Converts in Thendal Grove.",st="The Al'Aketh cult is a blight upon this island. These cultists are surely the ones responsible for agitating the simple wind sprites that reside here and turning them violent.\r\n\r\nRegrettably, we'll need to disperse these roiling winds here before they harm someone. We also need to send a clear message to the cult that they are not welcome in the grove.\r\n\r\nWill you lend me your aid, $c?",how={{"kill",251160},{"kill",251143}}},[92466]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=3,pre={92484},ex={1516,1519},nx=92467,ot="Bring a Signet of Akir to Windshaper Boro.",st="While we owe much of our prosperity to the elements of wind, the path we walk requires that we obey the call of all four of the primary elements and undertake a trial for each. Before you begin your first trial in earnest however, you must prove the strength of your resolve.\r\n\r\nTravel to the standing stones to the east. A force of Al'Aketh converts has been spotted there and they must be driven off. Confront the cultists there and bring me one of their signets as proof of your deeds.",how={{"loot",251924,{251160}}}},[92467]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=3,pre1={1516,1519,92466},nx=92468,si=6635,ot="Find the Rise of Spirits and drink the Earth Sapta.",st="A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the strong willed to see the elements as no one else can. Your spirit will be connected to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few shaman know the recipe.$B$BThe sapta is always drunk in a sacred place, and never anywhere else--remember that.$B$BSeek out the Rise of Spirits up the pass east of here. Drink your sapta there, and... well, you will see what you need to see."},[92468]={t="Call of Earth",lv=4,min=3,pre1={92467},si=6656,ot="Bring the Rough Quartz to Windshaper Boros in Thendal Grove.",st="Take this Rough Quartz from me and bring it to the one you call Windshaper Boro as proof of our meeting. He will craft a totem for you, and this shard will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast many others.$B$BBe patient, $n. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what the elements ask of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you."},[92469]={t="Return to Rorian",lv=4,min=3,pre1={92465},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Bring word of the Al'Aketh to Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.",st="You've done enough here, $c. I'll stay and clean up any stragglers down there.\r\n\r\nHead back to the Village and tell Rorian about the cult's presence. He will not be pleased."},[92470]={t="Foul Matriarch",lv=5,min=2,pre1={92471},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=4,[7]=2,[8]=3,[11]=2},ot="Slay 8 Ursera Scavengers and collect the head of the den mother, Urs'anah in Thendal Grove.",st="Rorian informed you that I've been watching you. I now offer you a test of resolve. However, be warned--it will send you into great danger.\r\n\r\nGo to the caves to the west. Thin out the ursera's numbers there, and find their matriarch, one the rangers call \"Urs'anah\". Put her down and bring me proof of her demise. Once you have done that, you will have taken an important step on your path.",how={{"kill",250937},{"loot",252665,{251115}}}},[92471]={t="Aetheen of the Gales",lv=4,min=4,pre={92469},ot="Speak with Aetheen of the Gales in Thendal Grove.",st="You may not realize this but everything you've done has been a trial of sorts. A test for what is to come for you. It's a big island out there, and Zephras needs spirited young adventurers such as yourself if we are to survive the trials our people face.\r\n\r\nThe one called Aetheen of the Gales is one of the leaders of our people here on Zephras Isle, and she has been watching you. She has a task that you must complete. Speak with her to learn more."},[92472]={t="The Next Step",lv=5,min=3,pre1={92470},ot="Report to Constable Aonda in Shen'dar Village.",st="One of the most pervasive threats on Zephras Isle is the Al'Aketh Cult. They are religious zealots devoted to the worship of the supposed elemental ruler of Skywall, Al'Akir the Windlord. They are brutal, single-minded, and their power and ambitions are growing more deadly by the day.\r\n\r\nYour path will soon take you to Shen'dar Village to the south. Present yourself to Constable Aonda when you arrive. The cult threatens Shen'dar and they are in need of aid. Tell Aonda that I sent you."},[92473]={t="Aggressive Encroachment",lv=4,min=3,pre1={92471},pre={92471},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Collect 6 Scrawny Ursera Claws from Scrawny Ursera in Thendal Grove.",st="The ursera den to the southwest is rapidly becoming a problem. Just last week the rangers had to kill an adolescent ursera who wandered too close to the village and attempted to attack a boy playing near the base of the elder tree in the center of the village.\r\n\r\nWe were fortunate that the boy escaped with his life. Hunger and desperation makes these beasts too dangerous to be left unchecked. Go south and put the scrawniest among the ursera down. Bring me their claws as proof when it is done.",how={{"loot",251918,{250926}}}},[92474]={t="Falling With Style",lv=2,min=2,ot="Jump from the top of the watchtower in Thendal Grove and use your Walk on Air ability to slow your fall.",st="Well hello there, $n! Want to play a game?\r\n\r\nAll you've got to do is step up on that ledge... then jump! Use your innate ability to walk on the air to slow your fall and see how far forward you can float.\r\n\r\nThe rules are made up and the points don't matter, but you get bonus points if you can land right in front of Rorian the Dayseeker and startle him! He won't like it but I'll certainly get a good laugh if you can get him all worked up! Hah!"},[92482]={t="The Way of the Hunter",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282421,ot="Read the Scribbled Note and then speak with Tai'ree Farsight in Thendal Grove.",st="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident hunter trainer--Tai'ree Farsight--left this note for you. You can find her just over yonder near the center of the village. Read the note then seek her out."},[92483]={t="At Home in the Shadows",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282422,ot="Read the Simple Note then speak with Akeri Duskblade within the watchtower in Thendal Grove.",st="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident rogue trainer--Akeri Duskblade--has requested to speak with you. He left this note, so read that first, then seek him out inside the watchtower, here in the village.\r\n\r\nHe's a shady fellow, but then again, so are you. I think you'll get along well."},[92484]={t="Embracing the Elements",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282418,ot="Examine the Humming Recall Crystal then speak with Windshaper Boro in Thendal Grove.",st="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident Shaman trainer--Windshaper Boro--left this recall crystal for you. Please examine it, then speak with Boro just over yonder near the center of the village."},[92485]={t="A Student of Nature",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282420,ot="Read the Folded Parchment then speak with Xyton Silverwind in Thendal Grove.",st="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident druid trainer--Xyton Silverwind--left this note for you. Read it as soon as you can, and then seek out Silverwind on the ground floor of this great tree just behind me.\r\n\r\nHeed his words and his counsel, he can teach you much."},[92514]={t="Welcome to Shen'dar Village",lv=6,min=4,ot="Speak with Illaya Amberwind and Coriella Calmbreeze in Shen'dar Village.",st="You've got that \"Windshaper\" air about you. Something about how I can feel a tiny bit of static on my skin when near someone spirit-touched that gives it away. Before I properly put you to work around here, you should check in with our resident Windshaper elder, Illaya Amberwind. She's just outside, near the center of town.\r\n\r\nOh, and check in with Coriella Calmbreeze as well, she runs the local inn and can provide lodging and supplies, should you need them.",how={{"talk",251902},{"kill",254089}}},[92515]={t="The Problem With Prideclaws",lv=6,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Collect 10 Prideclaw Pelts from the Prideclaws in Shen'dar Highlands.",st="As if bandits and mad cultists weren't enough, the hills are thick with prideclaws as well right now. They are starting to encroach on the village borders and growing bolder by the day. It's only a matter of time before someone's pet or child is taken. It would be a mercy for us to cull their numbers now rather than after some tragedy occurs.\r\n\r\nBring me a dozen or so of their pelts. I can turn them into all sorts of goods that will be of aid to the village.",how={{"loot",252670,{251245}}}},[92516]={t="Hippogryph Harassment",lv=7,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Slay 8 Hippogryph Youths, 6 Hippogryph Protectors and a Hippogryph Matriarch in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="A flock of Hippogryph have recently established nesting grounds southeast of Shen'dar Village and they've been wreaking havoc on travelers on the road. I need someone to head down there and thin them out for us.",how={{"kill",251291},{"kill",251284},{"kill",251261}}},[92517]={t="The Criminal Element",lv=7,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},nx=93036,rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[7]=3,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Kill 10 Highlands Bandits and their leader, \"Badwind\" Bennic in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="There's a cave not far to the north, hidden behind a waterfall. It's well known to me that there's a group of bandits that are operating out of that cave. They were a problem for us before the cult arrived, but now they are a real terror. I can't spare the people to go and clear them out, unfortunately.\r\n\r\nI need you to go there and take care of them for me. Kill as many as you can, and if possible, take out their leader, the one they call \"Badwind\" Bennic. That cave is dangerous, so be careful.",how={{"kill",251918},{"kill",255534}}},[92528]={t="Among the Faithful",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92529},rwc={[1]=2,[3]=3,[4]=2,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Look around Falaath Village to learn about the cult's intentions in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="The faithful of Al'Akir grow ever stronger with each eager new recruit like yourself. As you can see, our strength gives form to the storm itself!\r\n\r\nNormally I'd send you straight to Skypriest Aanders for assessment, but he is occupied at present receiving a guest at the inn on the north side of town. Please avoid that place for now. An unshaven recruit like yourself in the presence of such a guest would be inappropriate.\r\n\r\nFor now, just don't get in anyone's way.",how={{"kill",254128}}},[92529]={t="Falaath Village",lv=8,min=5,pre1={93036},nx=92528,ot="Report to Missionary Jasaan near the entrance to Falaath Village.\r\n\r\nIf you lose your Mark of Akir, speak with Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village to regain the effect.",st="It gladdens my heart that you wish to serve Al'Akir. Our current trials as a people stem from our own complacency. We grew prideful and took the bounty of the winds for granted. The stagnation that followed is the reason the spirits of the wind abandoned us.\r\n\r\nOnly through acts of contrition may we feel the wind's caress once more. If you seek the fellowship of like-minded shen'dorei, go to Falaath Village and find Missionary Jasaan there. I will mark you so that the faithful will know you as a recruit."},[92532]={t="The Warrior's Path",lv=2,min=2,pre1={92461},si=282419,ot="Read the Crumpled Note you've been given, then seek out Blademaster Ren inside the Thendal Village watchtower.",st="While you were gone our warrior trainer--Blademaster Ren--requested that we send you their way when you returned. She dropped this note off for you as well.\r\n\r\nGive it a read, then find Blademaster Ren inside the village watchtower."},[92544]={t="Al'Aketh Thugs",lv=5,min=2,ot="Slay 6 Al'Aketh Brutes, 4 Al'Aketh Neophytes, and Malduko Cloudcrush in Thendal Grove.",st="A band of Al'Aketh cult ruffians have taken up residence near the temple ruins just southwest of here, led by a real monster called Malduko Cloudcrush. This rabble has no doubt been dispatched here by High Priestess Lorthuna at the Shrine of Akir to attack travelers and coerce our people into joining the cult.\r\n\r\nI need to stay here at my post to alert travelers leaving the grove of the danger, but I would be grateful if you could do something about those cultists and their leader for me.",how={{"kill",251145},{"kill",251448},{"kill",256935}}},[92550]={t="Havoc in the Highlands",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92528},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[7]=3,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Travel to the ruins of Falaath Village and slay 6 Al'Aketh Stormcallers, 4 Living Lightning and take the head of Commander Cyclas.",st="Our best defense here might just be a strong offense. The advantage we now have is that we expect an attack is coming. What they won't expect is for us to hit them first.\r\n\r\nI've already asked a lot of you, but please head back over to Falaath Village. Kill as many cultists as you can and if you can get close enough, kill the commander and bring me his head. I'll stay here and organize the citizens and our few peacekeepers to prepare a defense... just in case you don't return.",how={{"kill",252068},{"kill",251662},{"loot",252661,{251966}}}},[92551]={t="Stolen Supplies",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92528},ot="Collect 10 packs of Stolen Shen'dar Supplies from Falaath Village in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="I overheard you might be going to Falaath Village? While you are there, please keep an eye out for our stolen supply caches.\r\n\r\nThe Al'Aketh have been raiding our supply caravans carrying various goods such as food and windstones to and from the lowlands for months. They've been blaming the bandits, of course, but we all know that it all ends up in the same place. If there's any of that stuff left in Falaath, it would be a huge help if you could recover it.",how={{"loot",252760,{252068}}}},[92553]={t="Restocking the Larders",lv=6,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Collect $1oa Small Eggs and $2oa Strider Meat from creatures found throughout the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="Up for a bit of work? I could use a bit of muscle from a strong adventuring-type such as yourself. With how dangerous things are getting around here, no one's had much time to hunt or forage of late, and I need someone to get out there and source me fresh eggs and strider meat to keep this village fed.\r\n\r\nI'd be happy to teach you one of my famous recipes if you can bring me what I need. What do you say?",how={{"loot",6889,{251661}},{"loot",5469,{251661}}}},[92579]={t="To Valanaar",lv=8,min=6,pre={92550,93927},nx=92700,rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[7]=3,[11]=3},si=253152,ot="Deliver Aonda's Written Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.",st="For now it seems the pylon and the village are safe, so I'd like you to deliver this report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar, at the southeastern edge of the island. Valennia is the leader of the peacekeepers on the island and she needs to know what happened here.\r\n\r\nThe cult is expanding rapidly and the peacekeepers have avoided direct conflict until now, but those days are over. Valanaar will need to be ready for a fight.\r\n\r\nAt any rate, thank you. You'll always have friends in Shen'dar, $n."},[92595]={t="The Windshapers",lv=6,min=4,nx=94411,ot="Listen to what Illaya Amberwind has to say.",st="<Illaya smiles warmly at you.>\r\n\r\nI am glad you returned to speak with me, child of the winds. I knew it the first moment you walked into my presence, that you were strong in the skysight. Do you find this surprising? Even those who have not trained as a Shaman may possess the gift. \r\n\r\nCome, let us speak about the mandate of the Windshapers, the nature of our struggles on Zephras, and the plight of our people."},[92598]={t="The Gift of Skysight",lv=4,min=2,ot="Use your Skysight racial ability at the Elemental Convergence in Thendal Grove.",st="As a Windshaper, you have the ability to use the sacred skysight gifted to us by the elemental spirits. Travel to the standing stones to the northeast of the village. Find the elemental convergence there and use your gift.\r\n\r\nYou'll find that you may draw upon the skysight anywhere, but its boon is much more powerful if you do so in the presence of an elemental convergence. You may at times receive other bits of wisdom from the spirits that are drawn to such places of power, as well.",how={{"click",460001}}},[92640]={t="Desperate Times",lv=11,min=6,pre1={94568},nx=93065,rwc={[1]=2,[3]=1,[4]=1,[8]=3,[11]=1},ot="Speak with Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar and follow her instructions.",st="Since engaging the cult in the open is not viable, our best chance is going to be to use this opportunity to attack the shrine itself. We can take Lorthuna herself off the board before she can finish her part of this scheme.\r\n\r\nIt so happens that Valennia has been preparing a strategy for a potential assault on the Shrine for some time now. The only problem is, we will need help. \r\n\r\nSpeak with Valennia for the details.",how={{"kill",252383},{"talk",251968},{"kill",252475}}},[92642]={t="Disrupting Logistics",lv=11,min=6,pre1={93320},ot="Slay 4 Al'Aketh Healers and 8 Al'Aketh Brawlers in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="Valennia only sent one person to help repel a full-scale assault... by the winds.\r\n\r\nYou don't look like much but I'll take what I can get. We need to inflict as much damage as possible to stop this soon. My people can't hold out much longer.\r\n\r\nGo down the hill and disrupt their logistics. Their healers are keeping the attackers coming, if we take them out we might be able to rally and push them back. Any other cultists you kill while you are out there are helpful as well.",how={{"kill",254596},{"kill",270201}}},[92643]={t="The Turncoat",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92881},nx=92644,ot="Find the cultist turncoat at the house just inside the highlands northwest of Valanaar.",st="There is a turncoat amongst the Al'Aketh. They claim to know the cult's true intentions for the island and want to come in, but will only do so with assurances of protection.\r\n\r\nThis defector is hiding at a secluded residence just northwest of Valanaar inside the highlands. I need someone who can discreetly go there, find the traitor, and escort him back to us. This might be a trap, but if this information is as important as this traitor claims, it's worth some risk.",how={{"kill",255013},{"kill",253372}}},[92644]={t="Unfortunate News",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92643},nx=94568,rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},si=273852,ot="Deliver the glowing crystal to Talanaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",st="<You reach beneath the still-warm body of the turncoat cultist and recover a small, glowing blue crystal. It appears to be damaged, but it may still be important. High Elder Shadowsong may be interested in this.>"},[92645]={t="Breaking the Breaker",lv=11,min=6,pre1={93320},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},ot="Slay Commander Belguilos in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="This attack is going to be hard to repel unless we can take out the cult commander. Belguilos \"the Breaker\" they call her, and she's a veritable terror. She used to be a peacekeeper before the cult got out of control, and even then she was... off. As a cultist I can only imagine how much worse she could be now.\r\n\r\nI might just be sending you to your death, but someone needs to take Belguilos out if we are going to survive here. You can find her at the villa at the hill's base. Good luck, $c.",how={{"kill",252666}}},[92646]={t="Confront Lorthuna",lv=12,min=7,pre1={93958},nx=93836,ot="Take the portal to the Rohashi Spires overhead and join Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger in their confrontation with the High Priestess Lorthuna.",st="Lorthuna fled up to the spires above using some sort of portal. Ayessa and Elaadrin went in after her. That was just a few moments ago.\r\n\r\nI'm afraid I took one too many hits and this is where I stay. Go through the portal, find Ayessa and help them stop Lorthuna.\r\n\r\nUnless that help that Elaadrin and Ayessa said they sent for arrives soon, you are on your own from here. Good luck, $c."},[92679]={t="Blood Tithe",lv=9,min=5,ot="Listen to what Alvarion Windfield has to say and find Aamelia Windfield at the Windfield Orchard.",st="H--Hello, stranger. You have the look of a capable adventurer about you. I...\r\n\r\n<The Skyborne man winces, clearly suffering terrible pain>\r\n\r\n...I was wondering if you were seeking employment? I came here to Valanaar to recruit fighters to help save my farm. If you are interested, please go find my wife Aamelia Windfield at our orchard to the west of Valanaar, in the lowlands.",how={{"kill",252800},{"kill",252448}}},[92682]={t="Make Yourself Useful",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92679},ot="Gather 10 Ripe Stormapples and slay 5 Hungry Bandits at the Windfield Orchard.",st="Oh, so you've got more courage than sense, then? Fine, I won't argue.\r\n\r\nFerauu and his goons aren't due to pick up their take of the harvest just yet, so I'm going to put you to work for your meals until they arrive.\r\n\r\nHead outside and gather today's batch of stormapples for me. Oh, and the bandits lurking around the stormapple trees... They think they are sneaky. They aren't. Kill them for me. \r\n\r\nLet's see what you've got in a fight.",how={{"open",253591,{578937}},{"kill",252802}}},[92683]={t="Flutterfly Dust",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92679},si=253666,ot="Gather 5 Flutterfly Dust from the Flutterflies around the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="I'm sure you've noticed the giant flutterflies out in the outer fields near the orchard? They are pleasant to look at, but they also have other benefits; namely their wing dust. It can be a mess, but if you can gather it up in large amounts, it has useful household applications.\r\n\r\nTake this Flutterfly Swatter and give the big bugs a good swat for me. They'll usually just get scared and flee, but sometimes they'll take some offense. Either way, they'll give their rumps a shake and drop a pile of dust.",how={{"open",253595,{578959}}}},[92684]={t="Ornery Ornery Galestriders",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92679},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=3,[4]=3,[7]=3,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Gather 7 Lowlands Galestrider Tenderloins from the Ornery Galestriders found throughout the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="As if the harvest wasn't light enough this year already, the galestriders in the area have been getting into the orchard and stealing my stormapples. Think you can head out to the fields and cull them for me?\r\n\r\nTake care though stranger, these lowlands galestriders are bigger and angrier than the highlands variety. Watch yourself. A well-timed kick is all it takes to put you down for good if you aren't paying attention.\r\n\r\nBring me some of their meat and I can make us a hot meal with it as well.",how={{"loot",253597,{251707}}}},[92685]={t="The Hills Have Eyes",lv=9,min=5,pre={92682,92683,92684},nx=92693,si=263329,ot="Loot 7 Blood-Stained Bandit Masks from Highwayman Bandits in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="The bandits have camps all over and there's a small one in the hills just north of here. Head up there and start cracking skulls. If we can catch them off guard and take them out before they come for us, we might just even the odds enough to stand a chance.\r\n\r\nBring me their masks. The bloodier the better.",how={{"loot",253596,{252820}}}},[92693]={t="Standing Our Ground",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92685},nx=92703,si=279981,ot="Speak with Aamelia Windfield when you are ready to confront the bandit leader.",st="You've done a lot to give us a fighting chance. Even if we die today, we'll at least know we gave it our best shot.\r\n\r\nThis is your last chance, stranger. If you want to head back to Valanaar and live another day, I wouldn't blame you.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, if you really have a thing for lost causes just let me know when you are ready to go. We'll walk out there with our heads held high and whatever happens, happens.",how={{"kill",252800},{"kill",252863}}},[92698]={t="What Is My Purpose?",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92679},ot="Speak with Aamelia Windfield about the Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct.",st="<You lean in close to try and hear the words coming from beneath the giant construct's armor plates.>\r\n\r\n...Function error...\r\n\r\n...Question...\r\n\r\n...What is....\r\n\r\n...Function...\r\n\r\n<These fragmented words and phrases seem to just repeat. Maybe someone nearby knows more about this construct?>"},[92700]={t="The Grand Skyseer",lv=9,min=4,pre1={92579},ot="Find Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar.",st="Now that you've arrived in Valanaar, you'll likely want to check in with the other members of the Windshapers here. The current Grand Skyseer and her people operate out of the lodge near the center of Valanaar.\r\n\r\nYou should also be aware, the Windshapers and High Order don't get along very well in these parts. Be careful and give the High Order a good, wide berth. We've got enough to worry about with the cult, I won't tolerate faction violence in the streets of Valanaar."},[92703]={t="Deliver the News",lv=9,min=5,pre1={92693},rwc={[1]=1,[4]=3,[7]=1,[11]=2},ot="Speak with Alvarion Windfield in Valanaar.",st="I guess it doesn't feel quite right to keep calling you stranger after all of this so... thank you, $n. \r\n\r\nIf you wouldn't mind and are back out that way, please let Alvarion know what happened here. Also, tell him that once he's up on his feet he needs to bring a windshaper back here to look at that construct for us to make sure it's safe to have around our... our family.\r\n\r\n<Aamelia touches her belly gently.>\r\n\r\nHe doesn't know about this part. Let's just keep that bit between us for now."},[92706]={t="WANTED: Bruuz",lv=20,min=15,ot="Bring Bruuz's Dorsal Fin to Gazlowe in Ratchet.",st="Calling all anglers!\r\n\r\nA giant shark has been circling the waters near the shipping dock, attacking sailors and small boats. Dockworkers have given it the nickname \"Bruuz\". A hefty reward will be given to whoever brings me its fin!\r\n\r\n-- Gazlowe",how={{"loot",253710,{209797}}}},[92708]={t="A Grand Adventure",lv=12,min=7,pre1={92700},ot="Listen to what Ayessa Dawnsinger has to say.",st="The Windshapers have been hard at work trying to respond to the current crisis on Zephras Isle. We have made several surprising discoveries in our search for the missing wind spirits, and we are developing a plan of action that could help us gain the means to save the island.\r\n\r\nWe'll need strong young adventurers like yourself for this to work however. Please, if you have a moment, let us speak on this further."},[92871]={t="In Service of Zephras",lv=11,min=6,pre1={93746},nx=93320,ot="Report to Valennia Stormfist and let her know that the Windshapers are with them in their fight against the Al'Aketh.",st="Valennia Stormfist and her peacekeepers have ever been the protectors of Zephras, and we've done our best to lend aid where we can. There are rumors of larger-scale cult movements around the island, and they are clearly gearing up for something.\r\n\r\nReport to Valennia and reiterate to her that the Windshapers offer their full support in Valanaar's efforts against the Al'Aketh, should the need arise."},[92880]={t="Return to Valanaar",lv=11,min=6,pre={92642,92645},nx=92881,rwc={[1]=1,[3]=3,[4]=2,[8]=3,[11]=3},ot="Bring Yorna's Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.",st="I suspect it will take a bit of time for us to mop up what's left of the attackers, but our chances are far better now. Head back to Valanaar and let them know that we are stable here now.\r\n\r\nI can't thank you enough for your help. We'd be in much worse shape without you. I asked for reinforcements and it seems that I got a burgeoning hero instead. I'll take that.\r\n\r\nMay the four winds bless you, $c."},[92881]={t="The High Elder's Request",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92880},nx=92643,ot="Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",st="The attacks on both the western and eastern watchtowers are not a coincidence. Based on what you told us about what occurred at the western watchtower with that skypriest, our best guess is that the cult is trying to do something to the anchor pylons.\r\n\r\nPlease speak with High Elder Shadowsong. He will tell you about a lead that could prove to be promising."},[92947]={t="Making Our Move",lv=12,min=7,pre1={93065},nx=93958,ot="Slay $1oa Al'Aketh Guardians, $2oa Al'Aketh Spiritcallers, and $3oa Al'Aketh Blademasters, then report to Hyusaa Quickbreeze at the Shrine of Akir.",st="Everyone is here, good. I've just sent a few of my best fighters in through the front of the shrine to cause a bit of trouble and serve as a distraction, while I lead the the bulk of our forces in from the flank.\r\n\r\nIf all goes well, we should be able to punch through quickly and take out the High Priestess. As for you, get in there and start cracking skulls. Meet my second, Hyusaa Quickbreeze, near the steps to the shrine after you've caused some trouble.\r\n\r\nWinds guide you, $c.",how={{"kill",252762},{"kill",252763},{"kill",252765},{"kill",253576}}},[93036]={t="Infiltrating the Cult",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92517},nx=92529,ot="Speak with Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village.",st="You may or may not be aware of this, but Sania Silverstream over there is a \"missionary\" for the Al'Aketh. They like to play at being a normal religious order and send non-threatening emissaries around to recruit. We've tolerated Sania so far to avoid direct conflict with the cult, but it's obvious the illusion of peace won't last much longer.\r\n\r\nYou are new here and unknown to most, so I'd like to see if you can use Sania to get close to the cult and find out what their plans are for the village."},[93065]={t="Prepare for Battle",lv=12,min=7,pre1={92640},nx=92947,ot="Speak with Valennia Stormfist in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="The Peacekeepers are mobilizing and we are all gearing up to head out. Make whatever preparations you need to make and meet us at the eastern road leading north out of town. We'll have one final check-in with everyone before we move out."},[93090]={t="What Comes Next",lv=13,min=7,pre1={93836},nx=95349,ot="Speak with Ayessa Dawnsinger when you are prepared to leave Zephras Isle.",st="Please extend my thanks to Ayessa for all that the Windshapers and your new friends from this \"Earthen Ring\" have done for Zephras Isle. I'm aware of the plan to take the Windshapers' shamans and leave the island, and your order has my blessing and well-wishes in this expedition.\r\n\r\nI can only hope that whatever solution the Windshapers find can truly provide us with the stability we've lacked these past years.\r\n\r\nWinds be with you, $n."},[93159]={t="The Strange Hermit",lv=13,min=8,ot="Speak with the Strange Hermit in the Shadowgale Forest and learn more about him.",st="Uh, um... h-hello, I mean to say, hi! Greetings, even! I'm sorry... it's um, been so long since I've actually spoken to another person. I'm afraid I'm a bit rusty at this.\r\n\r\n<The strange hooded figure shifts uncomfortably before you.>\r\n\r\nSo er, um... how is your day going?"},[93160]={t="The Forest's Bounty",lv=13,min=8,pre1={93159},ot="Gather $1oa Shadowgale Acorns in Shadowgale Forest.",st="I do appreciate you stopping by to talk with me! I-If you do want to help out, I could use a bit of help gathering up acorns from the forest floor. I've gathered most of the ones close by but there sure are a lot of raptor-bird things in the forest. It's dangerous out there and I'd rather not become a giant bird's lunch!\r\n\r\nSo if you want, you could maybe gather them for me? I'll make us something tasty if you do!",how={{"open",257128,{613238}}}},[93165]={t="Mercy Falls on Deaf Ears",lv=13,min=8,pre1={94484,94493},nx=93459,rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},ot="Collect $1oa Al'Aketh Cultist's Ears from the Al'Aketh cultists in Shadowgale Forest, the Shrine of Akir, or Gustberry Lowlands.",st="The Al'Aketh have visited great tragedy upon our enclave, and blood must be repaid with blood.\r\n\r\nI have an offer for you, stranger. Should you find conflict with these accursed cultists, bring me the ears of those you kill. I will reward you for each that you return with in both coin and, in time, access to the Nightclaw's secrets should you prove yourself to be a true friend.",how={{"loot",258771,{257196,252762,252763}}}},[93172]={t="Free the Hollows",lv=13,min=8,pre1={93159},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},ot="Destroy 10 Wind Hollows in Shadowgale Forest.",st="Most of the elves on this island seem to think that these woods are haunted, and they aren't wrong.\r\n\r\nAt the old ruins to the northeast, a strange type of ghost-like spirits gather. Some nights, you can almost hear them \"singing\". It's not like any song I've heard before, but it's definitely a song and it's... just so sad.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why, but I think something terrible happened there at some point, and the spirits are trapped there somehow. If you are feeling brave, maybe you can help set them free?",how={{"kill",251676}}},[93317]={t="Crab Season",lv=9,min=4,ot="Collect 6 pieces of Windsong Crawler Meat.",st="Are you familiar with Windsong Crawlers? You see, these crabs are native only to Windsong Lake here on Zephras, and they are only able to be harvested a few weeks of the year.\r\n\r\nWith all of the cult activity of late, I've not been able to get out to the lake to harvest them, and our window is rapidly closing. I'd be appreciative if you could go and gather some for me. They can generally be found along the shorelines around the lake and in rivers.\r\n\r\nDo be careful though, they are meaner than they look!",how={{"loot",257941,{254588}}}},[93318]={t="WANTED: Vulgara the Insatiable",lv=9,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},rwc={[1]=1,[3]=1,[4]=1,[7]=1,[8]=1,[11]=1},ot="Kill Vulgara the Insatiable in the Shen'dar Highlands and bring her head to Danarii Bellowveil.",st="By order of Constable Aonda of the Peacekeepers, a bounty is hereby placed upon the scourge of the highlands, Vulgara the Insatiable. Last spotted on a hilltop rise just southwest of Shen'dar Village, the winged vuldren terror is highly dangerous and should be approached with caution.\r\n\r\nDeliver the beast's head to Danarii Bellowveil to receive your reward.",how={{"loot",257942,{254589}}}},[93319]={t="Pilfered Windstones",lv=7,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Collect 10 Pilfered Windstones from the Highlands Bandits in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="We are relying on windstones more and more for day-to-day living here on Zephras so we try and maintain a cache of them in reserve for emergencies. Lately I've noticed some go missing from our stores.\r\n\r\nWe've found windstones on bandits we've captured recently, and I suspect they are behind our shortages.\r\n\r\nIf you find yourself near the bandit cave to the north, mind knocking a few heads together and reclaiming some of our pilfered windstones for me?",how={{"loot",257945,{251918}}}},[93320]={t="Tower Defense",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92860,92871},rwc={[1]=3,[3]=1,[4]=1,[8]=2,[11]=1},ot="Report to Yorana Windyreed at the eastern watchtower in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="I've just received word that the cult is attacking the pylon watchtower just outside of town! I've sent the few extra peacekeepers we have here to try and break through the enemy back line to relieve the defenders, but any additional help could mean the difference between our people there living or dying.\r\n\r\nPlease leave immediately for the east watchtower and provide whatever aid you can.\r\n\r\nMy lieutenant Yorana Windyreed led the relief force. If she still lives she can tell you how best to help."},[93552]={t="Harvesting Windstones",lv=4,min=2,pre1={92461},ot="Collect 15 Windstone Clusters from Raw Windstones in Thendal Grove.",st="Windstones are a critical resource on Zephras Isle as they contain the raw, concentrated energy of the winds themselves. The wind elementals who used to live here on Zephras with us vanished a number of years ago, and since then, the magic that sustains this island is slowly fading. Not without limitations, the windstones are still a reliable energy source, and are incredibly valuable to us.\r\n\r\nYou'll find raw windstones scattered around the grove. Think you can help me harvest them?",how={{"open",258772,{613286}}}},[93680]={t="Key to the City",lv=33,min=30,ot="Acquire the Dalaran Sewer Key for Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill.",st="The Alliance had an army of mages known as the Kirin Tor. While they were powerful, the demonic Burning Legion proved to be even more so. In one fell swoop, the arch demon Archimonde flattened their city like it was a child's plaything. Those who remained were reduced to merely dispossessed vagabonds.\r\n\r\nThat is, until they rebuilt Dalaran. And on the Dark Lady's very doorstep, no less!\r\n\r\nWhile in their camps, search for something that can get us into the city unnoticed. I must know more.",how={{"open",279469,{670427}}}},[93735]={t="The Broken Construct",lv=9,min=4,pre1={92700},nx=93737,ot="Find Riaani Nightwind on the west side of Valanaar.",st="Historically, the Windshapers have seen to the tending of the magical instruments and devices that were gifted to us by the spirits of the wind. This includes the myriad of magical constructs around the island. Since the spirits left us, only a scant few of these are still functional.\r\n\r\nOne of the few remaining working constructs in Valanaar has become damaged. One of our artisans was dispatched to help, but he may be in need of aid. Travel to the west end of the city and offer any assistance you can."},[93736]={t="Unwelcome Spirits",lv=9,min=4,pre1={92700},ot="Gather 10 Wind Hollow Essences from Wind Hollows in the Shadowgale Forest.",st="The paramount concern of the Windshapers is to better understand why the spirits left us, and what we may be able to do to bring them back. One curious fixture of Shadowgale Forest to the north is the presence of a curious form of wind sprite that some call \"hollows\". We know little of them and why they are there, but we do know that they first started to appear after the spirits of the wind left us.\r\n\r\nI need you to go there and disperse them. Gather the remains and bring them back here.",how={{"loot",262357,{251676}}}},[93737]={t="The Broken Construct",lv=9,min=4,pre1={93735},nx=93738,ot="Speak with Riaani Nightwind and listen to what he has to say.",st="Oh, hello. Ayessa sent you to assist me? Very well then. \r\n\r\nNot sure what an obvious novice like yourself can do, but if you give me a moment to pull my head out of this construct's innards I might have a few ideas of things you can do to help.",how={{"talk",256083},{"open",260881,{616468}},{"open",260883,{616466}},{"open",260880,{616467}}}},[93738]={t="The Broken Construct",lv=9,min=4,pre1={93737},nx=93746,ot="Report back to Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar.",st="Brightwish, eh? So the High Order wanted to remove these components for some reason. But why though?\r\n\r\nThe High Order has always been meddlesome, constantly wanting to experiment with the wind spirits' magic. They are too bold by a mile, and we've strictly forbidden them from meddling with knowledge under Windshaper purview, but lately they've been testing our patience.\r\n\r\nI think you should report what you've learned back to Ayessa Dawnsinger. She can instruct you further on what to do."},[93740]={t="Blood for Blood",lv=11,min=6,pre1={93746},ot="Collect 10 Al'Aketh Windstone Charms from the corpses of Al'Aketh cultists in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="A number of our Windshaper novices were found dead in the Highlands this morning. We can't be certain but there is a strong chance that the Al'Aketh are responsible. Windshapers trade blood for blood, every time.\r\n\r\nHead north and kill any Al'Aketh you encounter. Bring me their windstone prayer charms as proof of the deed. We do not forgive and we do not forget.",how={{"loot",255658,{253511,253195,270201}}}},[93746]={t="A Firm Response",lv=9,min=4,pre1={93738},pre={93738},ot="Confront Belathaan Brightwish along the road to the Shrine of Akir.",st="The High Order has been warned of the consequences of meddling with the Windshaper's affairs. I think we need to make an example out of Belathaan and send him back to the High Order with a few bruises and a healthy respect for the boundaries we set.\r\n\r\nBelathaan was seen leaving town, traveling north towards the Shrine of Akir. I don't know why he was going there, but confronting him alone on the road is the safest option. Find him, and put a bit of fear into his heart.",how={{"kill",256247}}},[93836]={t="The Fate of Zephras",lv=12,min=7,nx=93090,ot="Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",st="Muln has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir. Now that the wards that have hidden Zephras from his view are down, we are utterly defenseless. If he chooses to attack us, we stand no chance against him here in his own domain.\r\n\r\nHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it."},[93926]={t="The Western Watch",lv=8,min=5,pre1={92528},nx=93927,ot="Find Peacekeeper Vaaniel at the western watchtower.",st="Whatever reason the cult has for attacking the tower, it's not worth losing our people over.\r\n\r\nI'd like for you to head to the southwest and check in on that watchtower for us. Find the peacekeepers there and tell them to head back to the village. Holding that tower is not worth the lives it would cost and I'd rather concentrate the defenders we do have here to protect our citizens.\r\n\r\nPeacekeeper Vaaniel is in charge; let him know to head back here as quickly as possible. Hurry!"},[93927]={t="A Last Request",lv=8,min=5,pre1={93926},ot="Collect the note you found near the dead peacekeeper and read it to determine your next steps.",st="<As you inspect the body of the dead peacekeeper, a bloody note falls free of his hands. Picking it up and reading it may give you a clue as to how to proceed from here.>",how={{"kill",256966},{"open",254871,{617704}},{"open",263415,{617675}},{"open",263418,{617674}}}},[93948]={t="Deliver the Signet",lv=9,min=6,pre={92550,93927},nx=93949,si=263491,ot="Deliver the Shadowsong Family Signet to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",st="Since you are going to Valanaar anyway, please deliver the signet ring you recovered from the tower to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar. \r\n\r\nHe will want this back, and more importantly, he will want to learn the fate of his nephew. Talaanis is the High Elder of Zephras Isle and more importantly, he is a good man who is well loved by the people, despite our current hardships. It pains me to think of how he will react to this news. Please express my condolences for his loss."},[93949]={t="Bugged",lv=8,min=6,pre1={93948},ot="Kill Skyhoppers in Valanaar until you've eliminated $1oa Enchanted Skyhoppers.",st="We've been bugged.\r\n\r\nIt's skyhopper season in the lowlands, which means the pests are everywhere. One of the High Order mages reported that one of the insects that they killed had an enchantment of some kind placed upon it. When we inspected it closely it seems to be some sort of listening spell.\r\n\r\nWe suspect that the cult is using these enchanted insects as spies. Go and exterminate them for us. You won't be able to tell which are enchanted by looking at them, so you'll just have to kill them all.",how={{"kill",251727}}},[93951]={t="A Little Beauty",lv=7,min=4,pre1={92514,93461},ot="Collect 8 Hippogryph Down feathers in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="The hippogryphs that have taken up residence southwest of the village can be a nuisance, but they also present a rather unique opportunity to obtain their feathers. Many skyborne love to adorn their hair with vibrant plumes and the down feathers of a hippogryph are exceptionally vibrant and, more importantly, silky soft.\r\n\r\nIf you are heading that way, try and gather as many of the fallen feathers as you can from around their nesting grounds. Do be careful, as wild hippogryph are not tolerant of guests.",how={{"open",263493,{617839}}}},[93958]={t="The Inner Sanctum",lv=12,min=7,pre1={92947},ot="Speak with Valennia Stormfist inside the inner sanctum at the Shrine of Akir.",st="Valennia's forces just breached the inner sanctum. The fighting was thick in there at first, but it's grown... unsettlingly quiet. Go in there and do your best to link up with Valennia and her forces... if any of them are left.\r\n\r\nI'll stay here and watch your back."},[94003]={t="The Skybreaker Bulwark",lv=10,min=10,ot="Reclaim the Skybreaker Bulwark from Zaal Stormshield at the Shrine of Akir.",st="I am all that remains of the line of Skybreakers here on Zephras Isle. The rest were murdered by the Al'Aketh.\r\n\r\nThe only thing that outweighs my sorrow is my shame. My family's ancestral shield--the Skybreaker Bulwark--is now in the hands of a cultist named Zaal Stormshield. Family lore holds no harm may befall a worthy wielder of this shield.\r\n\r\nZaal is not worthy, of that I am sure. Find this man at the Shrine of Akir and reclaim my shield from him. Do this and I will teach you the Skybreaker Defense.",how={{"loot",263993,{257196}}}},[94006]={t="The Great Ursera Spirit",lv=10,min=10,nx=94638,ot="Speak with Urs'endris near the falls northeast of Valanaar.",st="Greetings, $n. You have progressed in your druidic studies far enough that I think it is time for you to meet one of the great spirits that reside here on Zephras. Urs'endris is a wise and noble spirit, who has taught druids how to take on the ursera shape for generations. Unfortunately his domain has begun to wither and fall into the sky like many other areas of Zephras.\r\n\r\nTo find him, travel northeast near the waterfall in the shadow of the Shrine of Akir. He should be able to instruct you further."},[94013]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94979},nx=94050,si=264163,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Vuldren Alpha in the Gustberry Lowlands. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.",st="You've returned triumphant from taming two beasts. It's time now for your last trial. The winds of Zephras whisper of greater challenges ahead. \r\n\r\nTake this Taming Rod and journey to the Gustberry Lowlands. There, tame a Vuldren Alpha and prove your mastery. \r\n\r\nComplete this lesson and you'll be ready to learn the deeper ways of the hunter.",how={{"kill",250874}}},[94050]={t="Training the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94013},ot="Speak to Quel'dora Quickgale in Valanaar.",st="You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than my sister, Quel'dora. She will give you the ability to train your new pet. \r\n\r\nGo with the winds, young $c."},[94411]={t="Meddlesome Mages",lv=6,min=4,pre1={92595},ot="Slay 6 High Order Apprentices in Shen'dar Highlands.",st="Be warned, members of the High Order have been seen in the vicinity of the standing stones north of the village. We have warned them time and again to not meddle at our sacred sites, but they are growing more bold in pushing us. Prove your resolve to us by going to the standing stones and dispersing them.\r\n\r\nI am loathe to condone outright bloodshed, but do what you must to drive them off. Return to me when it's done.",how={{"kill",257521}}},[94414]={t="The Anchors of Zephras",lv=2,min=2,ot="Speak with Halaan Hawk-Eye and borrow his gift to view the anchor pylon in the distance.",st="Greetings, young $n. I oftentimes come here to look upon the ancient anchor pylon. Gifts from the spirits of the winds, they bind and sustain our island. Of late however, their magic has grown unstable and inconsistent.\r\n\r\nThey suffer no distress I can see. Their splendor has not changed.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like, I can lend you my gift to look upon them yourself."},[94427]={t="A Lesson in Divinity",lv=12,min=12,nx=94434,ot="Speak to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.",st="A key tenent of being a paladin is the pursuit of divinity. This is not the pursuit of godhood, but merely the pursuit of good itself, for good's sake. We've all arrived at this place due to tragedy of one form or another, and it would be easy to lose that grace that defined us as paladins in life.\r\n\r\nGo to the Undercity and seek out Tanis Alderwood in the Trade Quarter. They are in need, and they could benefit greatly from some grace."},[94434]={t="A Lesson in Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre1={94427},nx=94435,ot="Bring 10 Linen Cloth to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.",st="Wait, you want to... help? Why would a paladin want to help a beggar like me?\r\n\r\nWell, I suppose that you could be of some assistance. \r\n\r\nIt's my wife you see. She, well... she's falling apart. I mean that literally. The apothecaries can stitch her back together right as rain, but they are about the Dark Lady's business and none are available to help. If you could perhaps bring me some fresh cloth then I could at least make her a wrapping to hold her together while we wait for the apothecaries.",how={{"open",2589,{106318,106319,2039}}}},[94435]={t="A Lesson in Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre1={94434},nx=94436,ot="Return to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep.",st="I don't know why you'd go out of your way to help me, but I appreciate it. If someone sent you my way, tell them I appreciate them too. You'll always have a friend in Tanis Alderwood, $c."},[94436]={t="A Lesson in Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre1={94435},nx=94438,ot="Speak with Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.\r\n\r\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.",st="It's time to demonstrate your ability to channel one of the light's greatest gifts.\r\n\r\nThe item I just gave you is called the Symbol of Life. Take care, as it may cause you some discomfort to handle a talisman of the light such as this. The light may be anathema to the force that created us, but it is still our guide and ally. The pain reminds us of this.\r\n\r\nGo see Deathguard Billmuth downstairs. He just arrived and he has petitioned us for aid. Show him and the Forsaken what a true paladin can do."},[94438]={t="A Lesson in Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre1={94436},nx=94440,ot="Take the Symbol of Life and use it to resurrect Deathguard Falgan at Venomweb Vale. \r\n\r\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.",st="Falgan and I were sent on a mission to scout out scarlet activity in Venomweb Vale. We managed to sneak close enough to one of their camps to hear about new orders involving an attack on Brill. Before we could decide what to do next, I stepped on a twig and the noise alerted them to us.\r\n\r\nFalgan yelled at me to run, so I ran. By the time I realized he wasn't with me, I was halfway to Brill. That brave idiot probably stayed behind to hold them off for me.\r\n\r\nPlease, find my friend and help him if you can."},[94440]={t="A Lesson in Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre1={94438},nx=94441,ot="Retrieve the Scarlet Crusade Attack Plans from the Scarlet Crusaders at Venomweb Vale, and return to Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.",st="These Scarlet Crusaders often carry satchels with their deployment orders. We know an attack is coming, but if we can recover their orders, we can warn the rest of the Deathguard and prepare an ambush. \r\n\r\nYou are clearly an impressive paladin. Kill these scarlet animals and retrieve a copy of their orders and bring them back to Deathguard Billmuth. He'll take it from there.",how={{"loot",264693,{1537,1538,259433}}}},[94441]={t="A Lesson in Divinity",lv=12,min=12,pre1={94440},ot="Speak with Danitha Morr in the keep at Bandarion Keep.",st="Please give my thanks to Danitha Morr and tell her that the rest of the Deathguard will hear about the service that the paladins of Bandarion Keep performed for us. \r\n\r\nYou have a lot of promise as a paladin, and I am proud to have those like you among the ranks of the Forsaken. Dark Lady watch over you, $n."},[94484]={t="Unnerving Silence",lv=11,min=8,ex={94493},ot="Find and speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.",st="A moment if you will, $n. Are you headed towards Shadowgale Forest? There is a druid conclave there in a cave to the northeast. I have been waiting on word from them but their correspondence is long overdue.\r\n\r\nWith Ban'aethall in ruins and all the unrest lately I worry something dire may have happened. Please, if you are able, go seek out Elegael Thornpaw and put my mind at ease."},[94485]={t="Tears of the Lady",lv=12,min=8,pre1={94484,94493},ot="Collect $1oa Lady's Tear Moss.",st="If we are to save my fellows in the Nightclaw Den, I am going to need some ingredients for a poultice. The first and most important is a spindly moss called Lady's Tear. It typically grows on the base of the trees here in Shadowgale.\r\n\r\nThis moss secretes a sticky substance that acts as an antiseptic and is perfect for binding open wounds. I have gathered what little I can reach but I know there is more in this forest.\r\n\r\nGo and be swift. We are going to need a lot if the injured I left behind still live.",how={{"open",265105,{619450}}}},[94486]={t="Feathers for Binding",lv=11,min=8,pre1={94484,94493},ot="Collect $1oa feathers from the Shadowgale Shrieklings in Shadowgale Forest.",st="The other ingredient I need for the poultice is feathers from the Shadowgale shrieklings that roam this forest. In their juvenile form, the shrieklings have insulative feathers which would be ideal to put over the moss. These feathers will prevent the antiseptic sap from drying out and will provide at least some protection against the elements.\r\n\r\nBe warned, the shrieklings are normally docile but they have been incredibly hostile of late. Their large talons can easily disembowel you if you aren't careful.",how={{"loot",265140,{256092}}}},[94487]={t="Unwanted and Unworthy",lv=11,min=8,pre1={94484,94493},ot="Collect $1oa Bloodied Heirlooms from Al'Aketh Footsoldiers and Al'Aketh Stormchasers in the Shadowgale Forest.",st="The Al'Aketh Cultists ambushed us with no warning, though their motives remain a mystery to me. I knew these cultists had clouds between their ears, but I never imagined they would upset the delicate balance here on Zephras with such brutality. Go, slay as many as you can and take their heirlooms if they wear any.\r\n\r\n<Elegael spits.>\r\n\r\nThese storm-cursed cultists don't deserve to be called shen'dorei. The beasts of the forest can have their bodies. Their ashes don't deserve the winds.",how={{"loot",265141,{252664,252665}}}},[94488]={t="The Ties That Bind",lv=11,min=8,pre={94485,94486,94487},ot="Kill Commander Haalien and bring his head to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.",st="The reason for cultists' presence here still baffles me, but I smell a familiar scent over the bloodshed.\r\n\r\nOne of our circle druids, Haalien, disappeared months back. It appears he's thrown his sorry hide in with the cultists.\r\n\r\nShow him what happens when he spills the blood of his kin! Take his head and return it to me.",how={{"loot",265475,{253622}}}},[94489]={t="The Wounds of Betrayal",lv=12,min=8,pre={94485,94486,94487},ot="Enter the Nightfang Den and heal $1oa druids and find Jorel Windsinger in Shadowgale Forest.",st="I have finished the poultices. Quickly, take them to the druids in the cave, north just across the clearing. I know my brethren are in much more dire condition than I. They are likely too injured to heal their own wounds. There are so few of us shen'dorei druids that every life is precious.\r\n\r\nBefore you go, I have a selfish request. My mate, Jorel Windsinger was in dire condition when I left. Please, see to his wounds if he still lives.",how={{"kill",258130},{"kill",258134},{"kill",258137},{"kill",258138},{"kill",258275},{"kill",258277},{"kill",258288},{"kill",258289}}},[94490]={t="Ripped Missive",lv=12,min=9,pre={94485,94486,94487},nx=94491,si=265476,ot="Bring the Ripped Missive to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.",st="<Tucked behind one of Haalien's bracers is a note that's been slightly torn and bloodstained in your fight. It looks like it contains useful information about the cultist motivations for the attack on the druid den. Elegael would be interested in this intel.>"},[94491]={t="The Fate of the Den",lv=12,min=8,pre1={94490},si=265782,ot="Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valanaar and tell him what has transpired.",st="It would appear that there is a correspondent hiding somewhere in Valanaar feeding information to the cult. I am clearly in no shape to make the journey, but Lotheluum needs to know what transpired here.\r\n\r\nHe should also know the fate of those who are no longer with us. Thanks to your help I think we can handle the rest of the situation from here, though the damage has been done.\r\n\r\nPlease go swiftly, $n. I hope our paths will cross again someday. Until then, I have cultists to slay."},[94568]={t="The Cult's True Plans",lv=11,min=6,pre1={92644},nx=92640,ot="Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong and observe the conversation.",st="The turncoat clearly was afraid of what the cult had planned, enough so to defect and seek our aid. It's truly unfortunate that he is dead and took his secrets to the grave with him.\r\n\r\nWe must discuss this further to determine our next steps."},[94638]={t="Strength and Mercy",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94006},ot="Find and kill Ur'endra in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="You have come to me in hopes of learning to take a shape of strength. I have a task for you, though it lies heavy on my heart.\r\n\r\nMy mate, Ur'endra, has lost herself to madness and has begun to attack her own kin. Without the magic of the winds, many creatures have begun to lose themselves... Ur'endra included. She makes her lair in a cave to the west of here, in the bluffs along the border between the Shen'dar Highlands and the Gustberry Lowlands.\r\n\r\nEnd her suffering and I shall grant you my blessing.",how={{"kill",258443}}},[94896]={t="Aid For The Refugees",lv=11,min=8,ot="Collect $1oa Abandoned Belongings from the ruins of Ban'aethal.",st="You look like a capable adventurer. Do you happen to be headed towards Shadowgale Forest? Ban'aethal lies deep in the forest; that's where we're all from.\r\n\r\n<Ealaane gestures to the other refugees.>\r\n\r\nWe've recently had to evacuate Ban'aethal, as it began to fall into the sky. It was sudden and in the middle of the night. If you are headed that way, would you please look for any belongings left behind? The forest and village are far too dangerous for us to return to now.",how={{"open",266433,{623295}}}},[94897]={t="The Fate of a Loved One",lv=11,min=8,ot="Find Resaan in the Ruins of Ban'aethal.",st="If you are traveling to Ban'aethal, I have a selfish request. My love, Resaan... I believe is no longer a part of this world. He had tried to go back to get supplies even though I begged him to stay. It has been over a week already and I fear the worst.\r\n\r\nPlease, if you find him, bring him home. If he has perished then I beg you to please bring me his heirloom.",how={{"loot",266434,{259013}}}},[94911]={t="Child of Nature",lv=10,min=10,ot="Speak with Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.",st="Greetings, young $r. I can see that you have much promise in the druidic arts. There is one who you may want to speak with in the city of Thunder Bluff by the name of Turak Runetotem. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, Moonglade. \r\n\r\nYou will be welcomed there, and the druids of the circle will impart their knowledge upon you. \r\n\r\nAs your people would say--go with the wind's blessing, young one. I wish you good fortune in your adventures."},[94913]={t="Moonglade",lv=10,min=10,pre={94911},ot="Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.",st="All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade. Keeper Remulos--Moonglade's guardian--keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.$B$BAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid."},[94978]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,nx=94979,si=267272,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame a Windsong Crawler found near bodies of water. \r\nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.",st="Every hunter begins by learning the bond between beast and master. This is your first challenge. In time, you'll tame creatures from every corner of the world, but for now, start with our rivers and lakes on Zephras. \r\n\r\nTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Windsong Crawler.\r\n\r\nShow that you can earn its trust, and begin your path toward true mastery.",how={{"kill",254588}}},[94979]={t="Taming the Beast",lv=10,min=10,pre1={94978},nx=94013,si=267298,ot="Use the Taming Rod to tame an Ornery Galestrider in the Gustberry Lowlands. \r\nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.",st="You've proven you can tame the river's crawler. Now it's time to test your skill on open ground. The plains of Zephras echo with the cries of the galestrider, a proud, winged hunter that runs like the wind.\r\n\r\nTake this Taming Rod and seek one out. Travel to the lowlands and earn its trust.\r\n\r\nShow you're ready for the trials yet to come.",how={{"kill",251707}}},[95034]={t="The Debt",lv=24,min=18,pre1={96204},pre={96204},nx=95036,ot="Speak with Lumina Windsinger in the Sepulcher.",st="I think you should know that it wasn't actually the Gnolls who attacked us on the road.\r\n\r\nWe were actually attacked by a giant, wolf-like creature that I now know as a \"worgen\". It dispatched our guards and came for me, but Banon threw himself in its path. I managed to get a spell off which startled the creature, causing it to flee, but Banon was already badly bitten. He insisted I leave him there but I refused.\r\n\r\nWe were limping back here when the gnolls found us. What came next was terrifying..."},[95204]={t="Crest of Lordaeron",lv=22,min=16,si=275521,ot="Bring the Crest of Lordaeron to Oran Snakewrithe in Undercity.",st="<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in the Undercity would be very keen to get their hands on this.>"},[95216]={t="The New Plague",lv=22,min=16,pre1={451},ot="Collect the Highly Toxic Strain from Witherfang in Ruins of Lordaeron for Theodore Griffs in Undercity.",st="Welcome to the most vital organ of the Undercity: The Apothecarium! Here we experiment on the most virulent of Azeroth's exotic specimens.\r\n\r\nYou've caught me in a good mood, so I will let you in on my latest investigation. It appears there is a particularly venomous arthropod stalking the ruins above our fair city. Its toxins are said to eat through even undead flesh. How exhilarating!\r\n\r\nI wish to validate these claims. Should you find yourself withering away from its bite, I should love a sample.",how={{"loot",275443,{250483}}}},[95314]={t="That Shadowvale Green Elixir",lv=10,min=7,ot="Collect $1oa Bottles of Whispering Elixir from Shadowvale, then return to Carolai Anise in Brill.",st="Before the Scourge invasion, the reclusive village of Shadowvale was known for its Whispering Elixir. Distilled from herbs found only in Tyr's Fall, the elixir was sought by apothecaries, mystics, and poisoners alike even after being banned in the city.\r\n\r\nI've had requests from a number of buyers eager to get their hands on some elixir. Travel to the ruins of Shadowvale deep in the Whispering Forest to the west. I'm prepared to offer significant compensation if you can recover some bottles for me.",how={{"open",268801,{630885,630871}}}},[95328]={t="Whispering Horror Residue",lv=13,min=7,ot="Deliver Whispering Horror Residue to Father Lankester in the War Quarter of Undercity.",st="Against your better judgement you scrape up and collect the squirming remains of the beast. Someone in Undercity might have a use for them.",how={{"loot",268812,{260396}}}},[95349]={t="The Earthen Ring",lv=13,min=7,pre1={93090},ot="Take the skycutter ship from Zephras Isle to Mulgore and speak with Alaana Stormwalker when you arrive.",st="The recent events with the cult have delayed my plans to travel to Azeroth and I must remain here in Valanaar for a time. You and a handful of other Windshapers will be our vanguard instead. Alaana Stormwalker will be waiting to receive our Windshapers upon arrival in Mulgore, and I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we finish our business here. We will join you soon.\r\n\r\nWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there. \r\n\r\nBanu-Alah, $n."},[95350]={t="Welcome to Azeroth",lv=13,min=7,nx=93739,ot="Travel to Orgrimmar and speak with Thrall in the Valley of Wisdom.",st="It's a big world down here, and our new allies are the key to our survival.\r\n\r\nThe Earthen Ring is a member of the \"Horde\", a proud collection of like-minded peoples. The nearby city of Thunder Bluff is a part of the Horde, and further to the east lies the capital of Orgrimmar.\r\n\r\nSeek out the flight master in the center of Thunder Bluff. They will fly you to Orgrimmar where you will make contact with the Horde warchief--Thrall, on behalf of the Windshapers. Winds guide you, $n."},[95494]={t="Bruised Pride and Lion Hides",lv=18,min=14,nx=95495,ot="Collect 6 Savannah Lion Hides from the Savannah Matriarchs and Savannah Patriarchs in the Barrens.",st="I need someone with a strong sword arm and some extra time on their hands to help me gather some lion hides. It stings my pride to ask a stranger for this aid, but I took an injury to my leg recently. Until I heal, I'm in no shape to go hunting myself but I have obligations to keep.\r\n\r\nThe big ones in this area generally have the best hides, so start with those first.",how={{"loot",269715,{3241,3416}}}},[95495]={t="The Hermit Tanner",lv=18,min=14,pre={95494,95507},si=269718,ot="Bring the Bundle of Hides to the hermit on the ridge overlooking the Dry Hills in the Barrens.",st="These hides are bound for a tanner who I often trade with. He is something of a hermit and he lives alone on the top of the ridge behind me. Climbing up a steep hillside isn't something I can manage easily right now so I'd be in your debt if you could make this delivery for me.\r\n\r\nOh, and about this tanner's... appearance. You need not be alarmed. In spite of his looks, he is no threat. I swear this is true."},[95507]={t="Vrang's Game",lv=18,min=14,ot="Collect 8 Trapped Game from traps found in Sprung Traps in the Barrens.",st="While you are out there, it would be of great help to me if you could check on my traps for me. I've got them strewn all over the valley.\r\n\r\nBring back any small game that I've caught. Keep your eye out for the other wildlife, though. This area can be dangerous if you aren't paying attention.",how={{"open",269719,{640104}}}},[95508]={t="Unwelcome Guests",lv=18,min=14,pre1={95494,95621},ot="Help Walton survive the encounter with Terry Longdrink and the Kul Tiras marines.",st="Yes, I used to be a member of the Kul Tiras navy. After Lord Admiral took Theramore and started his campaign in Durotar, I had... \"objections\" to his methods. Particularly the methods involving executing civilians.\r\n\r\nThere's more to the story but... wait... what's that?\r\n\r\nThere's a group of men coming up the ridge!",how={{"kill",261367}}},[95621]={t="Trouble in the Valley",lv=18,min=14,pre1={95495},ot="Travel to the wrecked caravan and learn more about why the Kul Tirans are here.",st="This morning I spotted a group of humans searching for something in the valley below. I managed to use my rifle's scope for a better look, and it was clear that they were soldiers sporting the livery of Kul Tiras. \r\n\r\nIf you'd be willing to take work from me, travel to where these soldiers made camp near the wrecked caravan to the south. Kill any you find and try to learn why they are here.",how={{"loot",270151,{262119}}}},[95663]={t="Dragonmaw Rumors",lv=31,min=24,ot="Travel to the Wetlands and meet the Deathstalker Agent in the hills above the Dragonmaw camp.",st="The Dragonmaw are a formidable clan.\r\n\r\nThey're known for binding magic strong enough to make dragons serve, and rumor claims they're preparing some display of it in the Wetlands. Whether truth or bluster, the Deathstalkers can't act on half-formed whispers. Broken symbols carried only that much to me.\r\n\r\nA deathstalker agent needs a hand in the hills above the Dragonmaw encampment. Meet her there. She'll reveal the next steps."},[95664]={t="Elder Knowledge",lv=31,min=24,ot="Take the Titan Relic to the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff and look for someone who can tell you more about it.",st="This unusual composite shard scatters light like a living prism. Its nature is uncertain, but its power feels ancient. The most knowledgeable minds for artifacts of this bygone age must reside on the Elder rise in Thunder Bluff.",how={{"loot",270866,{260326}}}},[95682]={t="Open the Maw",lv=31,min=24,pre={95663},ot="Slay the Dragonmaw forces within the Excavation Site and return to the Deathstalker Agent outside with anything you recover.",st="Dragonmaw. <She lets out a dry, amused scoff.>\r\n\r\nThe remnants of the dragon-wrangling clan think they've found something that could lead to them rising to their former power. In the eyes of whom... their false warchief?\r\n\r\nClear out their ragtag clan within the Excavation Sites so our Deathstalkers can move in undetected.\r\n\r\nIf the Dragonmaw carry anything of note upon them, return it to me--this information must stay between us and our royal command.",how={{"kill",275044},{"kill",275045},{"kill",275046}}},[95697]={t="Changing Tastes",lv=31,min=24,ot="Enter the Excavation Sites in the Wetlands and bring back Thicket Raptor Meat.",st="Zamja tells me we need more homestyle cooking.\r\nIf we start selling raptor, she thinks it'll draw in customers who don't usually visit Borstan's Firepit.\r\n\r\nHer idea is not so bad. But I want something that rises above the smells of our birth villages. We're in Orgrimmar! Borstan should serve a grand take on their familiar favorites.\r\n\r\nA hunter recently came back from the Wetlands with a giant talon from the thicket raptors in the Excavation Sites.\r\n\r\nUp for a job?",how={{"loot",271100,{260325,260800,260801}}}},[95774]={t="Her Name Is Olgra",lv=20,min=14,pre={4921},ot="Slay quilboars and collect $1oa of Olgra's Adornments for Mankrik's memorial.",st="The healer who saved me could not save her, and she has died in battle. Her name is Olgra, and I will never forget her.\r\n\r\nYou did not find her adornments on her body? She wore many jewels of polished bone.\r\n\r\nSlay the Razormane Raiders near where she fell, and find her precious works of art!\r\n\r\nI will place them with the memorial that I build in her memory.",how={{"loot",277277,{268624}}}},[95803]={t="A Token of Good Faith",lv=12,min=9,pre1={91317},si=270436,ot="Bring the head of Rudolph Gelhardt to Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity.",st="Now that we've claimed the head of the tarnished commander, I need you to deliver it to the Undercity. Sylvanas Windrunner mistrusts us greatly, and all but openly disparages us.\r\n\r\nDeliver Rudolph Gelhardt's head to the Dark Lady. Show her that we tend to our own house and are devoted to the prosperity of the forsaken."},[95805]={t="Grace of An'she and Mu'sha",lv=4,min=1,pre1={755},si=277199,ot="Carry the Smoldering Incense to the shrine of An'she and Mu'sha in the southeastern hills before the incense burns to ash in ten minutes!",st="The sun and the moon, An'she and Mu'sha, are not part of our world like the elements, yet their light gives us life, guidance, and hope.\r\n\r\nWe pay respect to the spirits of the world, and so we pay respect to the twins as well.\r\n\r\nIf you would show your respect, take this smoldering incense and bring it to a shrine in the hills to the southeast, overlooking the mesa, south of the quilboar. Be quick, so that you can reach the shrine before the incense burns away.\r\n\r\nDon't get it wet!"},[95883]={t="The Tortured Soul",lv=23,min=20,pre1={95884},nx=95885,ot="Collect a Tortured Soul from the nearby undead in Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest.",st="<The preparations for a hastily-assembled ritual are gathered unceremoniously on the altar. According to the scrap of note, everything has been gathered. All that's missing are the offering of blood and the Tortured Soul.\r\n\r\nThe undead around you look tortured enough. They may have what you seek.>",how={{"loot",271350,{1973,1974}}}},[95884]={t="The Offering Stone",lv=23,min=20,nx=95883,ot="Find the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest.",st="<The scrap of note is mostly illegible. What is still readable, however, are notes about preparations for an offering.\r\n\r\nAn offering stone is mentioned, as well as a ritual.\r\n\r\nPerhaps you can find this offering stone nearby.>",how={{"loot",271343,{1974,1973}}}},[95885]={t="The Offering of Blood",lv=23,min=20,pre1={95883},si=210713,ot="Use the Tortured Soul to give an offering of blood at the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril.",st="<All that's left now is the offering of blood.\r\n\r\nThe note scrap mentioned a 'willing sacrifice.'\r\n\r\nAn intense sense of dread washes over you.>",how={{"kill",212753},{"click",645153}}},[95981]={t="Watching the Roads",lv=20,min=10,pre1={482},ot="Slay $1oa Dalaran Wizards and $2oa Dalaran Watchers for Shadow Priest Allister in the Sepulcher.",st="Taking away their pendants is just the first step. If the Kirin Tor really are shipping a steady supply of relics from Dalaran, we must stop them at the source.\r\n\r\nSearch the roads around Ambermill for Dalaran's wizards and watchers. Their presence has allowed free access across our borders for too long. If we can cull their numbers, that should put a stop to these pendants making it into Silverpine Forest in the first place.",how={{"kill",1888},{"kill",1889}}},[96031]={t="Camping 101: Leatherworking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97906,97922,97934,97946,97958,97969},ot="Speak with Gretta Finespindle in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\r\n\r\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels."},[96044]={t="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97900,97916,97928,97939,97952,97964},ot="Speak with Tognus Flintfire in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons."},[96045]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97899,97915,97927,97938,97951,97963},ot="Speak with Vosur Brakthel in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Now that you've taken up Alchemy, I can also teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp once you've learned a bit. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste."},[96047]={t="Camping 101: First Aid",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97903,97919,97931,97942,97955,97965},ot="Speak with Thamner Pol in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives."},[96057]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96102,97925,97937,97950,97961,97972,97973},ot="Speak with Uthrar Threx in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[96058]={t="Camping 101: Engineering",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97902,97918,97930,97941,97954,98285,98287},ot="Speak with Bronk Guzzlegear in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells."},[96059]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={97901,97917,97929,97940,97953,98284,98286},ot="Speak with Thonys Pillarstone in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Now that you've begun your journey into being an enchanter, I reckon I can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp once you've learned the ropes.\r\n\r\nIt's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[96101]={t="The Great Outdoors",lv=6,min=4,pre={96638},ex={95998,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ot="Sit near Raan's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",st="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\r\n\r\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\r\n\r\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",how={{"click",460003},{"click",460003}}},[96102]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96057,97925,97937,97950,97961,97972,97973},ot="Speak with Snang in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[96130]={t="Chakuyak",lv=5,min=4,pre1={757},ot="Defeat Chakuyak and bring back her pelt.",st="Among the prairie wolves that hunt the hills nearby is one that is especially aggressive. We have taken to calling her Chakuyak. She has become a threat to travelers coming from abroad.\r\n\r\nShe stalks the trees west of Stonebull Lake, moving from tree stand to tree stand.\r\n\r\nEnd this threat and bring me her pelt, and I will speak your praises to the chief. Beware, for she is dangerous! You might see other hunters seeking her out there, and perhaps you could work as a team.",how={{"loot",270302,{268558}}}},[96204]={t="The Windshaper's Wrath",lv=22,min=18,pre1={91862},pre={91862},nx=95034,ne=1,ot="Accompany Lumina Windsinger and help her escape Fenris Keep.",st="Now that I'm free I'm going to make these vile creatures regret ever laying eyes on a Windshaper.\r\n\r\nLet's get out of here, $c.",how={{"talk",248755}}},[96604]={t="The Great Outdoors",lv=6,min=4,ex={95998,96101,96605,96606,96607,96608},ot="Sit near Brakk's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",st="Lok-tar, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\r\n\r\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\r\n\r\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",how={{"click",460003},{"click",460003}}},[96605]={t="The Great Outdoors",lv=6,min=4,pre={96659},ex={95998,96101,96604,96606,96607,96608},ot="Sit near Kaga's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",st="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\r\n\r\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\r\n\r\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",how={{"click",460003},{"click",460003}}},[96607]={t="The Great Outdoors",lv=6,min=4,pre={96656},ex={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96608},ot="Sit near Eleanor's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",st="Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\r\n\r\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\r\n\r\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",how={{"click",460003},{"click",460003}}},[96626]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96629,96634,96646,96655,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Tomas in Goldshire to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96629]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96634,96646,96655,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Gremlock Pilsnor in Kharanos to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96634]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96646,96655,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Zarrin in Dolanaar to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96638]={t="The Adventurer",lv=6,min=4,pre1={92470},ex={96627,96628,96630,96652,96656,96659},nx=96101,bc=96101,ot="Speak to Raan Wildwind near Shen'dar Village.",st="More and more adventurers like yourself have been seeking glory and fortune outside of the safety of Thendal Grove. There's one such adventurer who has made a camp outside of Shen'dar Village, along the road leading southwest out of Thendal Grove.\r\n\r\nSeek him out and see what you can learn from him that may help you in your own travels."},[96646]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96634,96655,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Zerril Softbreeze in Shen'dar Village to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96652]={t="The Adventurer",lv=6,min=4,pre1={794},ex={96627,96628,96630,96638,96656,96659},nx=96604,bc=96604,si=275022,ot="Bring the journal to Brakk near Razor Hill.",st="<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.\r\n\r\nThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>"},[96655]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96634,96646,96658,96661},ot="Speak with Cook Torka in Razor Hill to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96656]={t="The Adventurer",lv=6,min=4,pre1={382},ex={96627,96628,96630,96638,96652,96659},nx=96607,bc=96607,ot="Speak to Eleanor Shackleton near Brill.",st="$n, you have proven yourself trustworthy in your endeavors against the Scarlet Crusade so far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.\r\n\r\nI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Brill. Go and see what she's doing."},[96658]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96634,96646,96655,96661},ot="Speak with William Pickman in Brill to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96659]={t="The Adventurer",lv=6,min=4,pre1={757},ex={96627,96628,96630,96638,96652,96656},nx=96605,bc=96605,si=275019,ot="Deliver the Supply Bundle to Kaga Wildhoof near Bloodhoof Village.",st="Wait, $n. I have another ask of you, before you leave us.\r\n\r\nThere is an adventurer by the name of Kaga Wildhoof who has made camp just outside of Bloodhoof Village. She has greatly helped me in the past, and now I see my chance to repay her. Could you deliver these supplies to her?"},[96661]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96626,96629,96634,96646,96655,96658},ot="Speak with Pyall Silentstride in Bloodhoof Village to learn to become a cook.",st="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\r\n\r\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp."},[96779]={t="Syndicate Sabotage",lv=24,min=24,ot="Find Lord Tomas inside Durnholde Keep, in Hillsbrad Foothills, and kill him. Then, return to Myrokos Silentform.",st="Sometimes, $r, a single cut in the right place will drop a foe dead. The same is often true of organizations.\r\n\r\nOur agents have identified a key target among the ranks of the Syndicate: a man by the name of Lord Tomas.\r\n\r\nHe plays an instrumental role in the functions of Durnholde Keep, in Hillsbrad Foothills. If you wish to be of service to Ravenholdt, go to Durnholde and eliminate him. The quicker, and quieter, the better.",how={{"kill",266216}}},[96821]={t="Legging It",lv=6,min=1,ot="Kill 6 Ridgeshade Creepers and 6 Ridgeshade Lurkers in southern Durotar, then report to Gar'thok in Razor Hill.",st="We see fewer and fewer travelers from Razor Hill these days. The scorpids were never much fun, but now I hear there are spiders making their nest along the road.\r\n\r\nIf your travels take you up north, kill some of the spiders on your way. Then, let Razor Hill know the path's a bit safer for them.",how={{"kill",266850},{"kill",266849}}},[96822]={t="For Honor",lv=7,min=3,ot="Collect the Raider's Battleaxe, Raider's Bow, and Raider's Shield from the Tiragarde Keep outskirts, then return them to Turroc in Razor Hill.",st="We lost many brave warriors of the Horde when we sacked Tiragarde Keep. Now that the humans have reinforced the ruins, we cannot collect their remains to properly honor their deaths.\r\n\r\nGo to the ruins surrounding the keep, and search for the weapons left by our fallen kin. We will display them in a place of honor.",how={{"open",275713,{656180}},{"open",275716,{656181}},{"open",275717,{656182}}}},[96825]={t="This Fruit Could Bite Back",lv=6,min=3,ot="Cook Torka in Razor Hill wants you to collect 8 Prickly Pear Fruit from the Razormane Grounds west of town.",st="Our hunters and fishers bring back plenty of savory food for our troops - but it's rare that they get a sweet treat.\r\n\r\nI've seen a cactus that produces a prickly, tasty fruit. But it only grows in the hills to the west, where the wretched quilboars make their camps. Make your way past the quilboars and bring me some of those fruits. And be careful - the fruits are as spiny as the quilboars!",how={{"open",275718,{656177}}}},[96873]={t="A Pain in the Neck",lv=8,min=5,ot="Pa'zula in Sen'jin Village wants you to collect 3 Luminous Residue. Luminous Residue can be obtained by disenchanting Hexed Pendants dropped by trolls in the Echo Isles.",st="The trolls east of here have lost their will to the witchdoctor, Zalazane. He uses many cruel magics to keep hold of his prisoners' minds, but one of his favorite tricks is to make them wear pendants wrapped in evil binding spells.\r\n\r\nPractice your enchanting skills by stripping the magic from these pendants, and bring me the results. And don't accidentally put one around your neck, if you value your freedom!",how={{"loot",247884}}},[96874]={t="This Is Spinal Axe",lv=10,min=6,ot="Ug'thok in Orgrimmar wants you to collect 5 Weathered Spines from beasts in Thunder Ridge, along with 5 Rough Grinding Stones.",st="Have you seen the huge beasts of Thunder Ridge? I keep thinking the spines on their backs would be perfect for crafting the head of a mighty axe. Saru laughed when I told him... but what does he know!?\r\n\r\nAs part of your smithing lessons, you can help me out! Bring me some of those spines, along with grinding stones to sharpen them.",how={{"loot",275719,{3131,266852,3130}},{"loot",3470}}},[96875]={t="Beasts of Thunder Ridge",lv=10,min=6,ot="Kamari in Orgrimmar wants you to collect 5 Rough Lizard Hide from beasts in Thunder Ridge, along with 2 Cured Light Hides.",st="Orgrimmar is always expanding, $c. And when the peons need hides to line the walls and roofs of our new buildings, they come to me!\r\n\r\nThe hides of the lizards in Thunder Ridge are typically too thick for armor, but they make excellent building material. Bring me some of their hides, along with a few lighter cured hides. Let's see your skill with leather!",how={{"loot",275720,{3131,266852,3130}},{"loot",4231}}},[96876]={t="Ukor's Lost Pack",lv=8,min=5,si=275722,ot="Return the pack to Ukor in southern Durotar.",st="The pack has the name \"Ukor\" crudely stitched along the flap."},[96877]={t="Halikor's Hoof",lv=12,min=6,si=275723,ot="Deliver Halikor's Hoof to Orgrimmar.",st="The enormous hoof serves as proof of your victory over the mighty lizard."},[96895]={t="The Argent Emissary",lv=12,min=10,ot="Find the Argent Dawn member near the entrance to the Undercity.",st="Not sure if you heard, but two emissaries of the Argent Dawn just passed through here. I don't mind the Argent Dawn, but I don't like them poking around Tirisfal unsupervised either. They were both Forsaken... but that doesn't make me any less nervous.\r\n\r\nOne of them just passed by here, headed southeast. There's a group of scourge cultists snooping around the outskirts of the city in that direction. If those two heard about them, there's no doubt that would have caught their attention."},[96896]={t="A Righteous Cause",lv=12,min=10,pre1={96899},nx=98545,ot="Observe the conversation between Danitha Morr and Leonid Barthalomew the Revered.",st="Danitha and I fought against the Scourge in the defense of the Undercity when Naxxramas attacked. We lost many good friends that day, including the hero after which this keep was named--Garek Bandarion.\r\n\r\nHe might just have been the first Forsaken to rediscover how to wield the Light as a paladin. I am encouraged to see his legacy and potential live on here with Danitha and her cohort.\r\n\r\nIf only the rest of the Forsaken felt the same way..."},[96897]={t="The Cult of the Damned",lv=12,min=10,pre1={96895},ot="Kill $1oa Dark Neophytes and $2oa Dark Enforcers in Tirisfal Glades.",st="The Scourge are a blight on our lands, and their living servants are the worst of them. The people of Tirisfal have enough to deal with between the mindless dead and the Scarlet Crusade. If you wish to do some good, help me put an end to this scum.",how={{"kill",267006}}},[96898]={t="Remnants of War",lv=12,min=10,pre1={96895},ot="Gather $1oa Necrotic Crystal Fragments in Tirisfal Glades.",st="It wasn't long ago that the citadel of Naxxramas bore down upon this city, intent on wiping the Forsaken off the map. Both the Forsaken and the Argent Dawn lost much that day to secure the future of the Forsaken.\r\n\r\nDuring the battle, the great necrotic focusing crystal mounted atop Naxxramas was shattered and its fragments were scattered all over this area. I suspect that is what the cultists are here for. Help me recover the fragments and deprive the Scourge of them.",how={{"loot",275851,{267006,275437}}}},[96899]={t="Bandarion Keep",lv=12,min=10,pre={96897,96898},nx=96896,ot="Meet Leonid Barthalomew at Bandarion Keep in Tirisfal Glades.",st="You've done a great thing for the cause of the Argent Dawn here today, and I thank you. I don't know how familiar you are with the fortress of Bandarion Keep, but my commander and I were headed that way to meet with the paladins that reside there. That was before we learned of the presence of the Cult of the Damned.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to learn more about the Argent Dawn and our mission, seek out my commander at Bandarion Keep, to the northwest of here. I'll remain here to mop up the rest of this mess."},[96984]={t="Heart of Disruption",lv=33,min=24,pre={92434},si=277507,ot="Collect the Arcane Mote in the City of Dalaran for Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill.",st="You may not have our best interests at heart, but I won't deny an extra pair of hands. And if Dalaran falls, it takes everything with it--including your Undercity.\r\n\r\nSo, your benefactor wants in? Fine. I'll imbue your key to work past my wards so you can enter the city. Once you're in, meet me at the Violet Citadel where this all began. With everything going on the Kirin Tor will be too busy to stop you.\r\n\r\nScavenge what you will, but whatever happens, our first priority is to prevent a catastrophe.",how={{"loot",251961,{246020,250657}}}},[96986]={t="The Grave Knight",lv=33,min=24,ot="Defeat Atrexis the Grave Knight in the City of Dalaran for Melisara in Tarren Mill.",st="Within the underbelly of the mage city to the north is a traitor to our kind. A necromancer of disturbing talent. He raises an army of undeath right under the Kirin Tor's nose.\r\n\r\nI care not for the fate of the mage city, $n, but this grave knight spits in the face of everything we Forsaken stand for. Put an end to him. Show him no one is beyond the reach of the Dark Lady.",how={{"kill",247126}}},[96987]={t="Opportunistic Education",lv=33,min=24,ot="Collect the Founding of Dalaran from the City of Dalaran for Rexxie Copperclutch near the sewer entrance.",st="Well if it ain't a like-minded entrepreneur. Sneakin' into Dalaran durin' such troublesome times? Tsk tsk.\r\n\r\nMy kinda $r!\r\n\r\nWhile our mage friends here are occupied, maybe we could find ourselves some 'misplaced' treasures. They gots whole libraries dedicated to fancy arcane magics. If you could bring me one of their secret tomes, I could sell it for a pretty penny. Split the profits with ya.\r\n\r\nHey hey don't look at me like that. You ain't exactly here on a field trip yourself. You want in or what?",how={{"open",275996,{656681}}}},[96988]={t="Source of Power",lv=33,min=24,ot="Collect $1oa Cracked Sentry Cores in the City of Dalaran for Doctor Martin Felben in Undercity.",st="With the city of Dalaran under siege by their own constructs, this is the perfect opportunity to, let's say, borrow a few samples.\r\n\r\nImagine an army of arcane-powered abominations. The Dark Lady would have no choice but to recognize my alchemical prowess. Maybe even grant me head of the Royal Apothecary Society?\r\n\r\nGo to the city and find the constructs' cores. They are unlikely to give them willingly, so do what you must.",how={{"open",275997,{708078}}}},[97003]={t="Chol'aruk the Ravener",lv=21,min=15,ot="Bring the head of Chol'aruk to Gur'ak in the Barrens.",st="You there, $c. I need your aid. There are rumors of a beast that makes its lair deep in a cave at Thorn Hill, northeast of here. The Razormane call it Chol'aruk or \"The Ravener\". It's supposedly five times the size of a normal quilboar with a thirst for blood that can never be sated.\r\n\r\nMost don't believe the tales. But I do--because I've fought its like before.\r\n\r\nSeek out its lair and slay Chol'aruk. Bring me its head. I warn you though--prepare well and do not go alone.\r\n\r\nBlood and thunder, $c.",how={{"loot",276070,{267307}}}},[97223]={t="Bloodtalon Matriarch",lv=9,min=5,ot="Bring Eggs of the Bloodtalon Matriarch to Xar'Ti in Sen'jin Village.",st="All of the raptors you see before you are ones I have trained myself. They come from all over Kalimdor, but some of the finest come from the Bloodtalon raptors on the isles off our coast.\r\n\r\nOne raptor amongst them, the Bloodtalon Matriarch, is particularly savage and has killed many from our village and has become too dangerous to leave at our borders. If you can strike her down, return with her eggs so that we can raise the hatchlings as allies instead of enemies.",how={{"loot",277128,{268530}}}},[97225]={t="Forgotten Loa Idols",lv=9,min=4,ot="Collect $1oa Forgotten Loa Idols from the Echo Isles. Bring them to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.",st="When we fled the isles that Zalazane and his ilk now inhabit, we left behind many precious idols that help us commune with spirits we worship: our loa. They are of grave importance to our tribe.\r\n\r\nThe followers of Zalazane show no reverence for our loa and have scattered these idols across the largest of the isles.\r\n\r\nThis is an action that will not go unnoticed if we are not able to collect these idols, and offending a loa is a grave matter.\r\n\r\nGo, find as many loa idols as you can and return them to me.",how={{"open",277135,{660647}}}},[97242]={t="Yelmak's Medley",lv=15,min=9,nx=97275,ot="Take some cuttings from the Cattails and Speargrass growing around the water flows in the Valley of Honor and return to Kor'geld in Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions.",st="Yelmak doesn't want his apprentice breaking anything. Well, anything more than he already has.\r\n\r\nHe told me the young mixer in training has too much pride to ask for help when he really needs it. Yelmak wants to give him a taste of a particular home-brewed recipe.\r\n\r\nGather a mix of cattail and speargrass cuttings taken from the plants growing around the water in the Valley of Honor. I'd get them myself, but if I left the shop, Whuut would surely know we're catering to his mood.",how={{"open",277278,{661093}},{"open",277279,{661092}}}},[97243]={t="Call of Fire",lv=10,min=10,nx=97244,si=6653,ot="Bring the Torch of Dormant Flame to Olariaan Swiftburn at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands.",st="Even though we are in the realm of Skywall, this is still the elemental plane. The spirits of all four elements speak to us, if we deign to listen. One among us Windshapers is in particular attunement with the element of fire. A shen'dorei by the name of Olariaan Swiftburn.\r\n\r\nBring this to him at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands. You'll find it tucked away along the edge of the island, west of Valanaar."},[97244]={t="Call of Fire",lv=10,min=10,pre1={97243},nx=97245,ot="Slay Skypriest Faladiel in the Gustberry Lowlands and collect Faladiel's Heart.",st="There is an Al'Aketh Skypriest called Faladiel. He was once a caller of the flame and a stalwart Windshaper. Like so many Al'Aketh, he mortgaged his loyalty for power and his hands are now stained with the blood of his former brothers and sisters.\r\n\r\nYou will find Skypriest Faladiel at the farm to the northeast past Valanaar, just to the south of the Shrine of Akir. Kill the betrayer. Bring me his heart. It is a gruesome task, but it is needed for the ritual we are to perform.",how={{"loot",277267,{268602}}}},[97245]={t="Call of Fire",lv=10,min=10,pre1={97244},nx=97257,ot="Find the home of Kuramaa in the Shen'dar Highlands, and defeat the spirit in combat. Bring Kuramaa's Mask to Olariaan Swiftburn in the Gustberry Lowlands when you are victorious.",st="The residents of the Shen'dar Highlands speak of an ancient forest sprite called Kuramaa. They say it lives inside of a twisted stump at the summit of a hill near the highlands Anchor Pylon.\r\n\r\nGo to the highlands and find this stump. Rap your fist upon the bark and Kuramaa will appear. Best the spirit in combat, and bring me its wooden mask.\r\n\r\nBe warned however, this entity will be exceptionally resistant to much of your magic. Only the touch of flame will lay low the spirit.",how={{"loot",277269,{268605}}}},[97246]={t="Meal Appeal",lv=15,min=5,nx=97249,ot="Visit Borstan's Firepit and tell him Thatog wants you to deliver Migi's lunch to him personally.",st="My son, Migi, always takes off to play with his friends all day. I tell him to pick up a lunch at Borstan's, but I know he almost never does, because he comes home starving. These kids think their games are more important than their own bodies!\r\n\r\nPlease, stop at Borstan's Firepit and tell him you're there to deliver Migi's lunch. You can almost certainly find Migi behind Grommash Hold with the rest of his friends.\r\n\r\nDuties keep me here during the day and I can't watch over his every meal."},[97249]={t="Favorite Food",lv=15,min=5,pre1={97246},nx=97326,si=277284,ot="Bring Migi's Lunch to him behind Grommash Hold.",st="Now that I know his parents worry about how much he's actually filling that belly, I've got an idea. \r\n\r\nThey made me promise not to pack the same meal every day, so Migi grows a taste for more than one thing. Still, whenever the smoker's full and we're making sweetglazed hog belly sandwiches, he always shows up for lunch. We've started crumbling the leftover crispy glazed bits as a topping--something we can add daily. \r\n\r\nTake this to him. Maybe he'll start showing up early and bringing friends!"},[97250]={t="Wrongly Blamed, Justly Corrected",lv=23,min=18,ot="Slay Alliance soldiers encroaching into the Barrens at the border to Dustwallow Marsh, then return to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo.",st="Traveler, have you plans to head toward Dustwallow Marsh? I have heard mutterings that a few human soldiers have taken a stand at its border and are toppling the landmarks left behind by our tauren pathfinders.\r\n\r\nRumor has it that a favored tavern has burned to the ground, and in typical Alliance fashion, they immediately cast their blame onto the Horde! I cannot know whether there is any truth to their claim, but their incursion onto OUR land must not stand.\r\n\r\nKill first, investigate later!",how={{"kill",268622},{"kill",268623}}},[97253]={t="Parts and Pieces",lv=15,min=9,ot="Collect $1oa Handfuls of Complicated Parts from the upper pirate camp south of Ratchet, then return to Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet.",st="Hey, got a sec?\r\n\r\nSo, apparently, nobody I've sent to deal with the recent pirate problem has come back alive. After five or six attempts I thought, \"what if I sent a machine instead?\" Turns out, scimitars double as screwdrivers in a pinch, and before I could redirect it home, it was already in pieces and scattered across their camp!\r\n\r\nI need those parts back, and since this is a quick little retrieval mission, I'd wager your odds for survival are MUCH higher than the others. Whaddya say?",how={{"open",277331,{660930}}}},[97257]={t="Call of Fire",lv=10,min=10,pre1={97245},si=277329,ot="Wait for Olariaan to begin the ritual at the Brazier of Offering and follow his instructions.\r\n\r\nYou must deliver the Eternal Flame to Valanaar before the timer runs out.",st="Now we will perform the ritual. \r\n\r\nI will place the materials onto the altar and call forth the spirits of flame. If the offering is accepted, they will appear and light the Eternal Flame. You will then hold your torch forth and capture the flame.\r\n\r\nCarry the lit torch to Valanaar and place it in the Brazier of Eternal Flames. You must do so quickly, for the flames of the Firelands are quick to dissipate here in Skywall.",how={{"kill",268762},{"kill",268679}}},[97275]={t="Whuut's the Rush",lv=15,min=9,pre1={97242},si=277566,ot="Give Yelmak's Potion to Whuut.",st="Whuut is a prodigy. That much is true. But he doesn't yet have the experience, wisdom, and time on the stirring rod to know how to respect alchemical processes.\r\n\r\nHe is exhausting all of the rarest and most exotic reagents we have available without pausing to practice and refine his basic skills.\r\n\r\nGive him this potion I've brewed with a quick tonic method. He'll reconsider everything he's doing when he learns how local remedies and careful touch are the first true mastery."},[97279]={t="Wayward Weapons",lv=2,min=1,ot="Collect $1oa Abandoned Training Weapons, then return to Kzan Thornslash in the Den.",st="With an influx of new recruits like yourself, it's been hard to keep our weapons supplied. Our weaponsmith, Kzan, is running low on training weapons and I'd like to see what kinds of skills you possess to get an idea of what I have to work with. Luckily for you, I have a solution to both.\r\n\r\nWhile you're out there cutting your teeth on boars, salvage six abandoned training weapons. Our failed recruits left them laying on the ground. Once you do, return them to our weaponsmith Kzan behind me in the Den.",how={{"open",277653,{673476}}}},[97281]={t="A Simmering Storm",lv=11,min=7,nx=97282,ot="Bring the Dull Stormy Orb to Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.",st="<Before you is a strange orb with a dull surface. When picked up a small electrical current seems to vibrate from within. Upon closer inspection, it looks as if a dark mist swirls within and every so often a small electrical spark can be seen.\r\n\r\nIt is clear the harpy was using it for some purpose. Perhaps Rezlak would be interested in this object?>"},[97282]={t="Stormy Potential",lv=10,min=6,pre1={97281},ot="Bring $1oa Charged Thunder Lizard Organs to Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.",st="\"Rezlack, when an opportunity comes knocking make sure you're ready to seize it.\" That's another gem Gazlowe taught me and that's exactly what I intend to do.\r\n\r\nThis orb doesn't seem damaged, it just looks like it's out of juice, but I've the idea to supercharge it back to full strength!\r\n\r\nThere are a bunch of thunder lizards in a gorge west of here. They have organs that hold a strong electrical charge that would be perfect for this.\r\n\r\nGo harvest some and bring them back to me!",how={{"loot",277665,{3131,3130,266852}}}},[97287]={t="Shrewd Negotiations",lv=33,min=24,pre={96984},si=251961,ot="Speak with the Image of Archmage Modera near Dalaran.",st="You have done well to infiltrate the city of mages, but I believe it is time for us to be more... negotiatory.\r\n\r\nAs much as it pains me to admit, there is no other place on Azeroth with such a vast knowledge of the arcane. My brilliant work still pales in comparison to the ancient wisdom the Kirin Tor have amassed over the years. I think it's high time we are granted access to this exclusive order, don't you think?\r\n\r\nTake the mote you acquired. They will surely give anything to get it back. Anything."},[97288]={t="Unending Torment",lv=21,min=16,nx=97289,si=280438,ot="Deliver the Abominable Head to Master Apothecary Faranell within the Undercity.",st="<As the creature falls, its head comes toppling off. It seems as if it has been reattached several times, and the connection gets weaker with each reconnection.\r\n\r\nSomeone in the Undercity would know more about this unique abomination.>"},[97289]={t="Unending Torment",lv=21,min=16,pre1={97288},pre={97288},nx=97290,si=268518,ot="Bring the Head of the Baron to the body of Othmar in the Undercity.",st="We craft abomination heads all the time, but this one is special. It belonged to a Grand Marshal of the Alliance once. A particularly unpleasant one. Othmar, I believe its name was. The Dark Lady had the pleasure of dispatching this one herself.\r\n\r\nOoh the secrets it could tell if it could talk. And it can! If we reattach it to an appropriate host.\r\n\r\nGo ahead and place it next to the available body in the next room. But don't attach it. Not yet."},[97290]={t="Unending Torment",lv=21,min=16,pre1={97289},pre={97289},nx=97291,ot="Report your findings to Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.",st="You... abomination...\r\n\r\nWhy should... help you...\r\n\r\nBe gone..."},[97291]={t="Unending Torment",lv=21,min=16,pre1={97290},pre={97290},nx=97292,ot="Collect a Toxic Skullcap from Tawny Grisette in the Trade Quarter, Blisterweed near the Herbalism Trainer, and Essence of Agony from the poison vendor in the Rogues' Quarter for Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.",st="With the head reattached, all we need now is to bind it to the Dark Lady's will. This should not be a problem. The beast barely has brains left as it is after all the beatings it's taken.\r\n\r\nWe simply need to motivate it.\r\n\r\nFetch me a Toxic Skullcap from Miss Grisette in the Trade Quarter. Oh, and some Blisterweed from our local herbalist trainers, the Alliestars. Feel free to just take some, they owe me. And lastly a bit of Essence of Agony. Any old poison vendor should do.\r\n\r\nWe have a potion to make!",how={{"buy",281246,{4554}},{"open",281300,{673933}},{"buy",8923,{4585,3551,6779}}}},[97292]={t="Unending Torment",lv=21,min=16,pre1={97291},pre={97291},si=281327,ot="Inject the Hissing Serum into the system above Othmar's body for Master Apothecary Faranell.",st="I have concocted a lovely serum that our new guest is sure to find quite... stimulating.\r\n\r\nTake this. Feed it into the workings dripping from above him. Let's see if we can't show him why it's in his best interest to serve loyally.\r\n\r\nAnd try not to drop it. I can't afford a new assistant.",how={{"click",460007}}},[97326]={t="Rocks to Rests",lv=15,min=5,pre1={97249},pre={97249},ot="Return $1oa Smooth Boulders to Thra behind Grommash Hold.",st="Hey! You've got time to help us out! I know you do, I can tell by the way you smiled watching the game we're playing.\r\n\r\nThis spot behind Grommash Hold is nice because it's clear enough for us to set up our figures. But what stinks is we don't have enough rocks for chairs or tables.\r\n\r\nYou're big and strong... d'ya think you could carry back some medium-sized rocks, smooth enough to sit on if we need a rest?",how={{"open",277952,{661448,661446,661449}}}},[97485]={t="Traditions of the Bluff",lv=10,min=3,ot="Purchase a Bundle of Herbs from Nida the herbalist, a Bundle of Cedar Twigs from Nata the enchanting supplier, and Sinew Thread from Mahu the leatherworking supplier and Ceremonial Flint and Tinder from Naal the cooking supplier.\r\n\r\nCombine the items and sprinkle the incense off of Hunter's Rise.",st="Blessings of An'she, friend.\r\n\r\nWe tauren have a tradition of scattering incense to the winds and I was hoping you'd be interested in honoring this tradition.\r\n\r\nYou will need to craft the incense by purchasing herbs from Nida, cedar from Nata, sinew thread from Mahu in the mid rise, and ceremonial flint and tinder from Naal on the upper rise. Once you have these items, combine them and spread them off the south facing cliff of Hunter's Rise.\r\n\r\nYou will find a mat and incense at the ceremonial site.",how={{"loot",278078},{"click",665373}}},[97538]={t="Pigments for Paints",lv=26,min=20,ot="Tah Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff wants $1oa Mirkweed Pods from Mirkfallon Lake.",st="Greetings, friend. I wonder if I may ask a favor of you? I have just run out of red pigment for my paints, and I am looking for one with younger hooves to make the long journey into the Stonetalon Mountains on my behalf.\r\n\r\nIn the middle of the mountain pass there lies a large circular lake, Mirkfallon Lake, that has a unique plant that grows within its waters. The pods of this plant, mirkweed, turn a vibrant red when dried. Gather the pods of this plant for me, and I will reward you well for your efforts.",how={{"open",278201,{667362,667364}}}},[97558]={t="Hides for the Forsaken",lv=11,min=6,ot="Bring Shelene Rhobart $1oa Duskbat Wing Membranes, $2oa Darkhound Hides and $3oa Vile Fin Murloc Skin.",st="One part of undeath no one mentions is what happens when we are injured. How does the skin of an undead heal itself?\r\n\r\nWell, it doesn't.\r\n\r\nOurs is a cursed life, $n. We must take from the living to further our own existence.\r\n\r\nWhen we sustain an injury, we must replace our skin which usually means animal hides. Since different hide thicknesses are better for different places on our bodies a variety is key!\r\n\r\nBring me wing membranes of a duskbat, hides from a darkhound and skin of a Vile Fin murloc.",how={{"loot",278242,{1553,1554}},{"loot",278243,{1548,1547}},{"loot",278244,{1544,1545}}}},[97891]={t="Prompt Potion Runner",lv=16,min=9,si=279020,ot="Bring the Unstable Potion to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium within the time limit.",st="You! Quickly, I need you to bring this potion across the slime canal to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium!\r\n\r\nIt has a very limited shelf life, and no I can't go myself, my knees rattle and pop out if I attempt to run.\r\n\r\nJust another lovely side effect of undeath, apparently.\r\n\r\nBut we're wasting time! Here, take this and go!\r\n\r\n<Alessandro makes a shooing motion.>"},[97899]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96045,97915,97927,97938,97951,97963},ot="Speak with Whuut in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste."},[97900]={t="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96044,97916,97928,97939,97952,97964},ot="Speak with Dwukk in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons."},[97901]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96059,97917,97929,97940,97953,98284,98286},ot="Speak with Jhag in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[97902]={t="Camping 101: Engineering",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96058,97918,97930,97941,97954,98285,98287},ot="Speak with Mukdrak in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells."},[97903]={t="Camping 101: First Aid",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96047,97919,97931,97942,97955,97965},ot="Speak with Rawrk in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives."},[97904]={t="Camping 101: Fishing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96050,97920,97932,97943,97956,97967},ot="Speak with Lau'Tiki near Sen'jin Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that."},[97905]={t="Camping 101: Herbalism",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96055,97921,97933,97944,97957,97968},ot="Speak with Jandi in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate."},[97906]={t="Camping 101: Leatherworking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96031,97922,97934,97946,97958,97969},ot="Speak with Karolek in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\r\n\r\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels."},[97907]={t="Camping 101: Mining",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96046,97923,97935,97948,97959,97970},ot="Speak with Krunn in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess."},[97908]={t="Camping 101: Skinning",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96056,97924,97936,97949,97960,97971},ot="Speak with Thuwd in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up."},[97915]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96045,97899,97927,97938,97951,97963},ot="Speak with Alchemist Mallory in Elwynn Forest near Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste."},[97916]={t="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96044,97900,97928,97939,97952,97964},ot="Speak with Smith Argus in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons."},[97917]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96059,97901,97929,97940,97953,98284,98286},ot="Speak with Betty Quin in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[97918]={t="Camping 101: Engineering",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96058,97902,97930,97941,97954,98285,98287},ot="Speak with Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells."},[97919]={t="Camping 101: First Aid",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96047,97903,97931,97942,97955,97965},ot="Speak with Michelle Belle in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives."},[97922]={t="Camping 101: Leatherworking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96031,97906,97934,97946,97958,97969},ot="Speak with Adele Fielder in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\r\n\r\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels."},[97925]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96057,96102,97937,97950,97961,97972,97973},ot="Speak with Eldrin in the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[97927]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96045,97899,97915,97938,97951,97963},ot="Speak with Kray in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skil