m for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\r\n\r\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels."},[97959]={t="Camping 101: Mining",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96046,97907,97923,97935,97948,97970},ot="Speak with Brom Killian in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess."},[97960]={t="Camping 101: Skinning",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96056,97908,97924,97936,97949,97971},ot="Speak with Rand Rhobart on the road to Undercity from Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up."},[97961]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96057,96102,97925,97937,97950,97972,97973},ot="Speak with Bowen Brisboise on the road to Brill from Deathknell to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[97963]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96045,97899,97915,97927,97938,97951},ot="Speak with Nyassa Swiftdraught in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste."},[97964]={t="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96044,97900,97916,97928,97939,97952},ot="Speak with Aedi Thriceforged in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons."},[97965]={t="Camping 101: First Aid",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96047,97903,97919,97931,97942,97955},ot="Speak with Naleeia Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives."},[97967]={t="Camping 101: Fishing",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96050,97904,97920,97932,97943,97956},ot="Speak with Fenn Fairweather in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that."},[97968]={t="Camping 101: Herbalism",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96055,97905,97921,97933,97944,97957},ot="Speak with Syriel Nightrain in Valanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.",how={{"kill",254345}}},[97969]={t="Camping 101: Leatherworking",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96031,97906,97922,97934,97946,97958},ot="Speak with Indari Sunseam in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\r\n\r\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels."},[97970]={t="Camping 101: Mining",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96046,97907,97923,97935,97948,97959},ot="Speak with Messana Crestwind in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess."},[97971]={t="Camping 101: Skinning",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96056,97908,97924,97936,97949,97960},ot="Speak with Mendalass Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up."},[97972]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96057,96102,97925,97937,97950,97961,97973},ot="Speak with Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[97973]={t="Camping 101: Tailoring",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96057,96102,97925,97937,97950,97961,97972},ot="Speak with Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\r\n\r\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized."},[98024]={t="Journey to the Crossroads",lv=13,min=7,pre1={95350},ot="Report To Thork at The Crossroads in The Barrens.",st="After journeying here from the elemental plane, the problems our lands face may seem small. Rest assured, the dangers the horde faces are very real, and you will grow formidable should you survive your service.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, travel southwest to the vast lands known as the Barrens. There is a settlement there known as the Crossroads. The proud citizens there are ever in need of aid.\r\n\r\nGo with honor, adventurer!"},[98069]={t="Stolen Freewind Supplies",lv=30,min=25,ot="Bring 8 Stolen Freewind Supplies to Jandia in Freewind Post.",st="Those wretched harpies! They attacked the last caravan I had scheduled to deliver supplies to Freewind Post. We have enough supplies for the moment, but without more supplies, we'll run short soon.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what the harpies plan to do with the extra supplies, but I would be grateful if you would recover them for me. They make their lair west of here. They can be found both at the base of the cliffside and inside a cave at the top.",how={{"open",279383,{670338}}}},[98070]={t="Stop the Screeching",lv=30,min=25,ot="Slay $1oa Screeching Harpies, $2oa Screeching Roguefeather Harpies and $3oa Screeching Windcaller Harpies.",st="The Screeching Canyon is home to a local band of harpies known for their ferocious nature and raiding tactics. They have ambushed the last few supply caravans that have been brave enough to traverse this place.\r\n\r\nI fear if something isn't done soon, there will be no caravans that will dare make the trek to Freewind Post.\r\n\r\nGo, slay as many of these harpies as you are able. Return to me once the deed has been done, and I will reward you well for your efforts.",how={{"kill",4100},{"kill",4101},{"kill",4104}}},[98093]={t="Field to Clear",lv=23,min=18,ot="Sulhasa in southern Barrens wants you to clear out $1oa Stormhide lizards and $2oa Hecklefang Stalkers in the area so she can leave the tree safely.",st="I'm so glad you saw me!\r\n\r\nThe weather was lovely this morning, so I walked from Camp Taurajo down the golden road. When it came time to head back, I couldn't--a pack of hyenas started circling, and Stormhide lizards blocked my only escape.\r\n\r\nScrambling up this tree I went, and now there are too many foes about at this hour for me to make the run home through the fields.\r\n\r\nWould you mind clearing out these Stormhide and Hecklefang Stalkers for me?",how={{"kill",4128},{"kill",3238}}},[98094]={t="Scout Support",lv=25,min=19,pre={528},si=279394,ot="High Executor Darthalia wants you to deliver updated orders to Deathstalker Masoj, south of Tarren Mill, outside of Dun Garok.",st="Now that we can trust you to deliver critical information to our forward spies, there's an extra task for you.\r\n\r\nBring this to Deathstalker Masoj almost directly south of us. He'll have more for you to do once you get there and hand this to him. He is posted on elevated terrain north of the rotten vineyard they call Nethander Stead.\r\n\r\nOur plan to take control of these lands continues steadily."},[98095]={t="Valuable Vantages",lv=25,min=19,si=279395,ot="Deathstalker Masoj needs you to place the three Apothecary Vials on peaks around Hillsbrad Foothills and return to him.",st="Our high command inserts strategic troops using bat riders. Key points around the foothills have lost their signaling beacons.\r\n\r\nTake these vials. Uncork them in three locations: the hills bordering Dun Garok, the plateau overlooking Dunholde Keep, and the last on the ridge of the Headland above the town of Hillsbrad. The vapors that emanate will be like a potent tuning rod to the senses of the bat, drawing them to the desired drop-off points once more.\r\n\r\nLook for crushed empty vials and renew our marks."},[98251]={t="Never Coming Back",lv=23,min=18,ot="Kill $1oa Shadowhorn Stag and $2oa Ashenvale Bear and return to Va'xug Firefure northwest of Fallen Sky Lake.",st="Gaaah!\r\n\r\nI'm so angry. They said Ashenvale was easy to follow. Easy for who? The beasts? The birds?\r\n\r\nOne moment I was gathering an herb, the next I'm trapped in this ravine. Do I truly have to circle half the forest to reach where I stood just moments ago?\r\n\r\nWhen I'm like this, my spells grow volatile and behave... differently.\r\n\r\nCould you thin the wildlife nearby? Even their stupid hooves grate on me. I despise this cursed forest.",how={{"kill",3817},{"kill",3809}}},[98252]={t="A Void Path",lv=23,min=18,pre={98251},ot="Show Va'xug's Eye of Kilrogg the way back to the main Ashenvale road.",st="Show my Eye of Kilrogg the way out of this ravine and back to the Ashenvale road. Keep it moving and I'll follow once I see a clear path.\r\n\r\nI'll stay here--one of us should keep our bearings. If you lose the way, I can guide you back through the eye. I will not have us both wandering blind in this malicious forest.\r\n\r\nI can hold the channel for four minutes. No longer. Reach the road before the vision breaks, or return to me and we try again."},[98284]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96059,97901,97917,97929,97940,97953,98286},ot="Speak with Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[98285]={t="Camping 101: Engineering",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96058,97902,97918,97930,97941,97954,98287},ot="Speak with the Strange Hermit in Shadowgale Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="An engineer is ever-resourceful, and if you are in the wilds alone, it's always good to be able to put your trade to use. No good camp is complete without a few helpful constructs!\r\n\r\nYes, come back and see me when you've gained a little bit of experience as an engineer and I can show you how to make something special!"},[98286]={t="Camping 101: Enchanting",lv=6,min=4,pre1={95998,96101,96604,96605,96606,96607,96608},ex={96059,97901,97917,97929,97940,97953,98284},ot="Speak with Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",st="Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\r\n\r\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again."},[98299]={t="Stop the Spread",lv=20,min=9,pre1={99},ot="Slay $1oa Sickly Refugees and $2oa Haggard Refugees for Dalar Dawnweaver in The Sepulcher.",st="If there is one thing we do know, it is that Arugal is responsible for worgen within Silverpine--be it his own machinations or otherwise. What we don't know is how it spreads.\r\n\r\nWhile I research a way to stop the curse, our first priority is to contain it. It appears this affliction cannot infect forsaken, but a large group of humans have gathered by the Greymane Wall.\r\n\r\nGo to the wall and put down these refugees before they have a chance to become servants for Arugal. And try not to get bit, $r.",how={{"kill",2053},{"kill",2054}}},[98340]={t="The Great Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,ot="Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.",st="It would seem that you are ready for the next step in your journey, young druid. Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you, and wishes for you to seek him out in Moonglade once again.\r\n\r\nYou have already learned to call upon the magic to take you to Moonglade, so you should be able to embark immediately if you choose. I would suggest you leave soon, if you wish to continue your druidic training."},[98341]={t="The Great Windborne Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre1={98340,98393},ot="Seek out the Avatar of Saeyleenan in the southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the windborne cat.",st="A spirit of your homeland has recently appeared here and has asked me to guide you to it. This windborne cat spirit has come to tutor and mentor you so that you may take the feline shape of the spirit on Zephras.\r\n\r\nAll druids eventually seek this wisdom, though it seems your homeland has a slightly different shape than our traditional one. If you desire to take this spirit's feline form, you will need to undergo our trial.\r\n\r\nIt can be found in the southern part of Moonglade, south of the twin bridges."},[98342]={t="The Great Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98405},ot="Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Great Cat Spirit.",st="To draw upon my spirit, you will need more than a few words. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\r\n\r\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics of my favor you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\r\n\r\nReturn these relics to me. We will see if you are ready to take my shape.",how={{"open",280502,{672821}},{"open",280679,{673093}},{"open",280680,{673094}}}},[98362]={t="To Thunder Bluff",lv=20,min=20,pre1={98738,98739},ot="Return to Thunder Bluff and speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise.",st="The time has come for us to part ways once again, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to the one who sent you to me. It would seem your instructor, Turak Runetotem, has found a worthy pupil in you. I believe I see one as well. Heed his lessons and you shall soon be able to draw upon the Great Cat Spirit to take its shape.\r\n\r\nGo back to whence you came. When the time is right, we will meet again."},[98389]={t="A Light in the Darkness",lv=4,min=2,pre1={376},ot="Free $1oa Webbed Victims in Night's Web Hollow for Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell.",st="Greetings, $c. Yes, I am a paladin. Not even death can stop the Light.\r\n\r\nThis is something my kind have in common with all Forsaken--we have overcome what the living view as their end. However, some even among our own fear us; they suspect we will smite them as some monstrosity.\r\n\r\nIn truth, our relationship with undeath is complex, but I am not here to hurt our own. Help me show the others this. Venture to Night's Web Hollow to the northwest and free the freshly raised fools trapped by the spiders there.",how={{"talk",271961},{"talk",271968}}},[98404]={t="The Great Windborne Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98341},ot="Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Avatar of Saeyleenan.",st="In order to draw upon my spirit, you will need to undergo a trial. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\r\n\r\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\r\n\r\nReturn these relics to me to pass the druidic trial of these lands.",how={{"open",280502,{672821}},{"open",280679,{673093}},{"open",280680,{673094}}}},[98405]={t="The Great Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98340},ot="Seek out the Great Cat Spirit in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the cat.",st="In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.\r\n\r\nMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.\r\n\r\nGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you."},[98424]={t="Fizsprocket's Notes",lv=10,min=5,nx=98427,si=281031,ot="Collect the rest of Supervisor Fizsprocket's pages inside The Venture Co. Mine and bring them to Morin Cloudstalker near Bloodhoof Village.",st="Some particularly worn papers are held separately, folded in Fizsprocket's inside breast pocket.\r\n\r\nThey seem to detail important information that could be used against the Venture Co. and its operations in the region. It would be prudent to look for more before returning to Morin Cloudstalker.",how={{"open",281035,{673494}},{"open",281036,{673496}},{"open",281037,{673497}}}},[98427]={t="Ceasing Operations",lv=12,min=5,pre1={98424},pre={98424},ot="Bring the Clearcutter Key to Morin Cloudstalker outside Bloodhoof Village.",st="The shredder one of the pages speaks of--I have seen them before in my travels. They can decimate a forest in a fraction of the time that hand and axe can.\r\n\r\nEntire glades--homes to the Earth Mother's children for millennia--erased in days.\r\n\r\nWe will not allow this to happen in our home, a stone's throw from where our young ones take their first steps.\r\n\r\n$n, I must ask you to gather others, go back into the mine to the northeast, and ensure it fells not a single tree more.",how={{"loot",281048,{272173}}}},[98430]={t="The Longwalkers",lv=8,min=1,ne=1,ot="Help Perith Stormhoof escape Palemane Rock, and report his safety to Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.",st="Hail, $c. What brings you deep into such a dark and violent place?\r\n\r\nI was sent here by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof as a part of our efforts to communicate with the gnolls that have taken residence. The rest of my mission must remain a secret, as do all things with the Longwalkers, the trusted scouts of our chieftain.\r\n\r\nAll you must know is our diplomacy was met with violence, and I fear I may be tonight's feast for the gnolls if you do not help me escape.\r\n\r\nAre you up to the task?"},[98435]={t="Thunderhorn's Report",lv=10,min=4,pre1={760},si=281139,ot="Bring Thunderhorn's Report to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.",st="Our elders in Thunder Bluff must know of the progress we have made here, thanks to your aid.\r\n\r\nPlease, take this to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff. You will find him in the Elder Rise, on the east side of the city. You must take the lifts up to the center of the city, then cross the bridges to reach it."},[98512]={t="Al'Aketh Assassins",lv=11,min=6,ot="Kill 10 Al'Aketh Assassins in the Shen'dar Highlands.",st="You there, stranger. Get low and keep quiet. We are not alone here.\r\n\r\nI was on patrol near the border and noticed that there are a number of Al'Aketh skulking around the house just up the hill there to the north. I don't know what they are doing here, but it can't be good.\r\n\r\nIf you want to make yourself useful, get in there and take them out. I'll wait here and watch your back.",how={{"kill",254626}}},[98545]={t="Leonid's Letter",lv=12,min=10,pre1={96896},si=282065,ot="Deliver the Sealed Letter to Glix Xizzix in the Undercity.",st="Since you are here, I'd like you to deliver this letter to an old friend of mine in the Undercity. I'd deliver myself but I have a somewhat colorful history with the Dark Lady, and it would be better if a neutral third party made the delivery.\r\n\r\nYou are looking for a goblin named Glix Xizzix in the Trade Quarter area of the Undercity. I'm sure he'd be happy to compensate you for your time.\r\n\r\n<Leonid lets out a low chuckle as he hands you the letter.>"},[98575]={t="Tainted Tablet",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=282346,ot="Read the Tainted Tablet and speak to Nartok inside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, $n.$B$BI usually avoid dealing with warlocks if I can help it, but I think you should read it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from your newly-appointed trainer, Nartok. He would have words with you when you're ready."},[98576]={t="Glyphic Parchment",lv=1,min=1,pre1={788},si=282380,ot="Read the Glyphic Parchment and speak with Mai'ah near the entrance to the Den in the Valley of Trials.",st="Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the mage trainer Mai'ah. She would have words with you when you're ready."},[98601]={t="A Difficult Path",lv=1,min=1,pre1={364},si=282423,ot="Read the Consecrated Scroll and speak to Aramis Hammerhand in the church in Deathknell.",st="While you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. It reeks of the light, so I imagine it's of some importance to a paladin like yourself.\r\n\r\nRead it before heading out again. Just please--step away when you do. Paladins make me quite uneasy."},[98738]={t="Blessings of the Great Windborne Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98404},ot="Speak to Dendrite.",st="Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately I have little left to teach you for the moment. I do hope you come and visit me in Zephras again someday. I sense promise in you, young shen'dorei.\r\n\r\nMay the shadows forever hide you, your foes easily fall prey to your claws, and the winds guide your steps."},[98739]={t="Blessings of the Great Cat Spirit",lv=20,min=20,pre={98342},ot="Speak to Dendrite.",st="Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further. I do hope we meet again someday.\r\n\r\nMay the shadows forever hide you and your foes easily fall prey to your claws, young one."},[98823]={t="Earthen Echo",lv=31,min=24,pre={95664},si=287958,ot="Bring the Titan Relic to Muln Earthfury at the Skywatcher Plateau in northwest Mulgore.",st="Truly, this is a fascinating object.\r\n\r\nIt shows indications of being much more than a mere carving or sculpture.\r\n\r\nWhile our elders may be interested in observing this artifact, the Earthen Ring are who would carry the most wisdom for our buried ruins and forgotten lands. Seek out Muln Earthfury, a direct approach is fitting for the gravity of what you carry.\r\n\r\nYou can find him and other elders of the Earthen Ring council at the Skywatcher Plateau in northwest Mulgore."},[99048]={t="A Missing Hand",lv=11,min=9,nx=99049,ot="Find Heglan Shadeeye north of Tiragarde Keep.",st="A member of the Shattered Hand, a group of more... subtle fighters, was watching Tiragarde Keep from a distance. Her reports suddenly stopped coming in.\r\n\r\nI doubt the humans would have caught her, so I'm concerned something more dangerous is at play. See if you can find her. Hopefully the messages are just delayed."},[99049]={t="Threat from Below",lv=11,min=9,pre1={99048},nx=99051,ot="Find signs of what attacked Heglan Shadeeye.",st="The nearby area is destroyed with obvious signs of a skirmish. Whatever ambushed Heglan didn't make it out unscathed. There's probably signs nearby of what happened.\r\n\r\nOrgnil will probably want to see any evidence left by the attackers.",how={{"open",286012,{693674}},{"open",286011,{693670}},{"open",286010,{693669}}}},[99051]={t="Threat from Below",lv=11,min=9,pre1={99049},pre={99049},nx=99052,ot="Collect $1oa Naga Spinefins.",st="It wouldn't be the first time those snakes bothered us. They need to be taught that their presence is not tolerated here.\r\n\r\nFind where their scouts are setting up camp and slaughter them. Bring me back their fins as proof. We need to act fast to make sure they understand.",how={{"loot",286008,{275662,275663}}}},[99052]={t="Threat from Below",lv=12,min=10,pre1={99051},pre={99051},ot="Kill the sea giant along Durotar's north coast and bring back proof of your accomplishment.",st="One of my scouts has reported a sea giant followed those naga down here. Not sure if they brought him intentionally or what, but he's dangerous in any case.\r\n\r\nIt's a young one, but it could still rip an orc in half in a heartbeat if they were caught off guard. I need him gone. But I'd suggest you find some help to deal with it.",how={{"loot",286009,{275666}}}},[99079]={t="Longwalker Malah",lv=9,min=4,nx=99081,ot="Find Longwalker Malah Longwind east of Bloodhoof Village, near the edge of Mulgore.",st="The Longwalkers are our people's most trusted scouts. Though their loyalty lies with the High Chieftain alone, young Baine at times seeks their aid.\r\n\r\nThis is one such time. Longwalker Malah was dispatched near our borders to the east and did not return last night after three days. When this occurs, it is our duty to confirm their safety.\r\n\r\nI must ensure the village remains safe. Prove yourself, and seek Malah out. You will know her by her headband and feathered staff, emblematic of the Longwalkers."},[99080]={t="Drive Them Out",lv=9,min=4,pre1={99101},nx=99082,ot="Kill $1oa Galak Centaurs, $2oa Galak Outrunners, and bring the head of Herak the Pillager to Baine Bloodhoof.",st="Hear my words well: we will not yield a single blade of grass to the centaur.\r\n\r\nGo to their camp now, before they have rested and have a chance to ride to our village. Slaughter them all. Ensure none escape to the Barrens to rally others to their aid.\r\n\r\nIf you find the leader of this would-be raiding party, bring me his head so that it may serve as a warning to others who dare tread on our ancestral homeland.",how={{"kill",2967},{"kill",2968},{"loot",286075,{275767}}}},[99081]={t="Grim Tidings",lv=9,min=4,pre1={99079},nx=99101,si=286104,ot="Bring Longwalker Malah's Report to Brave Wildrunner in Bloodhoof Village.",st="You can see what appears to be a new centaur camp in the direction the arrows in Malah's back would have come from. There is a stir of activity, suggesting a small raiding party has made its way into Mulgore.\r\n\r\nThe Longwalker has a report in her still-clenched hand. Brave Wildrunner will want to know of Malah's fate--and her killers."},[99082]={t="The High Chieftain",lv=9,min=4,pre1={99080},ot="Seek audience with High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.",st="Your bravery defending your people demands recognition. Journey to Thunder Bluff to the northwest, our mighty city whose shadow grants us shade in the warmer months, and seek audience with my father.\r\n\r\nIt was he who led the charge with the young Warchief Thrall to reclaim these plains and drive the centaur away for good. As High Chieftain, he will reward you generously for your part in ensuring his own bravery is honored.\r\n\r\nYou must take a lift to reach the High Chieftain, who sits on the central rise."},[99101]={t="Our Ancient Enemy",lv=9,min=4,pre1={99081},nx=99080,si=286104,ot="Bring Longwalker Malah's Report to Baine Bloodhoof.",st="Baine Bloodhoof leads our village. He must know of this incursion at once.\r\n\r\nBring him Longwalker Malah's report. You will find him at the center of town.\r\n\r\nQuickly, now. There is no time to waste!"},[99108]={t="Sparring Match",lv=6,min=4,ot="Defeat 3 other players in duels or Novice Warriors for Tang Stonehoof.",st="Hail, young $c. Though you are not a warrior and I cannot teach you that path, that does not mean you would not benefit from my tutelage.\r\n\r\nBefore you lies the arena. In it, it matters not who you call mother or whether you wield sword or bow. All are equal, and all learn to sharpen their horns in direct combat.\r\n\r\nWill you enter our space, and learn our ways for yourself? You may face any of these novices, or any other willing adversary. I care not which.",how={{"talk",10721}}},[99123]={t="Lost in the Shadows",lv=8,min=4,ne=1,ot="Help Pal'juh escape Kolkar Crag and bring news of your success to Master Vornal in Sen'jin Village.",st="I decided to do a bit of scouting in the crag on my own. Unfortunately my magic ran out at the wrong time and I've been stuck hiding here since.\r\n\r\nIf you could help me escape, I would appreciate it."},[99134]={t="Discipline",lv=6,min=4,si=286176,ot="Punish $1oa Deathguards for Executor Zygand.",st="You are not a member of the Deathguard, and therefore have yet to disappoint me.\r\n\r\nAs a reward for your relative lack of incompetence, you shall punish those that have demonstrated such talents in excess.\r\n\r\nSwiftly now--$n, is it?--or I shall add your name to my ledger for someone else's reward.",how={{"talk",1495},{"talk",1496},{"talk",1519},{"talk",1652},{"talk",1735},{"talk",1736},{"talk",1737},{"talk",1738},{"talk",1739},{"talk",1740},{"talk",1741},{"talk",1742},{"talk",1743},{"talk",1744},{"talk",1745},{"talk",1746},{"talk",2209},{"talk",2210},{"talk",5725},{"talk",251001},{"talk",257655},{"talk",272101},{"talk",275103}}},[99141]={t="Patience",lv=6,min=4,ot="Obtain reports from Deathguard Dillinger, Deathguard Kristof, and Gordo for Executor Zygand.",st="Make no mistake, $c--the Dark Lady demands the perfect execution of her will. As an Executor, it is my duty to see that this happens.\r\n\r\nReports from several of my Deathguards are overdue. Needless to say, my patience has run out. Obtain their reports and bring them to me in the Dark Lady's name.\r\n\r\nYou will find Deathguard Dillinger just west of here, by the graveyard. Deathguard Kristof is stationed at the waystation to the east. And check on the abomination Gordo; he wanders west near Stillwater Pond.",how={{"loot",286200,{1496}},{"loot",286201,{251001}},{"loot",286202,{10666}}}},[99142]={t="Tomb Weed",lv=11,min=5,pre1={5482},ot="Collect $1oa Tomb Weed and deliver them back to Junior Apothecary Holland.",st="If you're heading east, towards the Balnir Farmstead, I have more you might do for me. Good help is ever so hard to find these days, as your run-in with Gordo illuminates ever so clearly.\r\n\r\nAs I acquire doom weed I perform some minor alchemical alterations and replant them on that farmstead to cultivate my ultimate creation. I call it tomb weed, and it shall be the herald of my glorious destiny.\r\n\r\nDo keep an eye on the Scourge in the area while you're there. They seem... drawn... to the weed. Curious.",how={{"open",286204,{694732}}}},[99144]={t="Seeking Refuge",lv=7,min=5,ne=1,ot="Help Bareth Dawnstone escape Crusader's Outpost, and report his safety to Shari Stilwell in Brill.",st="Light bless you for finding me. I was on my way from Bandarion Keep to deliver a message to Shari Stilwell in Brill when these monsters captured me. They wield the Light with a hatred in their hearts that makes what's left of my blood seethe. It goes against all I meditate for... all I strive to protect!\r\n\r\n<Bareth Dawnstone steadies himself.>\r\n\r\nI know some still take issue with my kind, but I assure you our intentions are pure. If you would aid me in escaping this place, I would be forever grateful."},[99152]={t="As Above, So Below",lv=12,min=10,pre1={96896},ot="Collect $1oa Faintly Glowing Bones for Hilda the Breaker.",st="While the Tarnished in Shadowvale to the southwest are definitely a problem, we cannot allow the cellars below the town to fester into a full-blown Scourge uprising on Bandarion Keep.\r\n\r\nI need to get these trainees up to snuff in case that happens. You, however, are going to receive what I like to call a crash course.\r\n\r\nTravel beneath Shadowvale and retrieve some of their wretched bones so we can study them further. I need ones that still retain some of the initial reanimation magic--that's glowing ones.",how={{"loot",286259,{260430,260428,260432}}}},[99153]={t="The One That Got Away",lv=12,min=10,pre1={96896},ot="Find the Hidden Crystal Fragment beneath Shadowvale for Ephram Barbaro.",st="Oi, you! Word travels quickly among our ranks. I heard about the work you did with the cultists around the remnants of the battle with Naxxramas.\r\n\r\nProblem is, one of them cultists got away with a piece of the focusing crystal. Seems to still have some juice in it. Best guess we have is it's somewhere beneath Shadowvale. It's either raising 'em or making 'em stronger, and you don't want either one.\r\n\r\nFind that crystal before this gets out of hand.",how={{"open",286269,{694895}}}},[99156]={t="Rear Guard Patrol",lv=13,min=6,pre1={356},nx=92422,ot="Bring Riptear's Heart to Deathguard Linnea.",st="Damn it all! A new report came in while you were on patrol. There has been a sighting of a rogue abomination wandering Eastern Tirisfal Glades, near Venomweb Vale.\r\n\r\nSomething is wrong. Abominations don't just slip through the Bulwark unnoticed.\r\n\r\nKeep this matter on a strictly need-to-know basis. That said, such a creature will not fall easily; you will need allies if you wish to be more than its next meal.\r\n\r\nSee this through, and you will be duly rewarded. Bring me its heart as proof of the deed.",how={{"loot",286326,{276020}}}},[99411]={t="Kyle's Gone Missing!",lv=7,min=5,ot="Ahab Wheathoof at Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore wants you to feed his prized puppy, Kyle the Frenzied.$B$BFeed Kyle Tender Strider Meat and return to Ahab Wheathoof.",st="Help, $n! My prized puppy, Kyle, has run away! I just know he's running around Bloodhoof Village, lost and hungry.$B$BWill you find him and feed him? Once he eats he will settle down and come home.$B$BTo feed him you will need to find food. His favorite meal is tender strider meat. Just venture east and you should find plenty of striders. Hunt one down and take its succulent meat to Kyle. When you see Kyle in town, put the meat down and he is sure to come to you.",how={{"kill",277154}}}},
